 / [ looks · M mute.\"},{\"line_number\":206,\"content\":\"- `resolution?: Resolution`\"},{\"line_number\":207,\"content\":\"- `aspect?: AspectMode`: `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport at an…\"},{\"line_number\":219,\"content\":\"- `debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption`: Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an…\"},{\"line_number\":245,\"content\":\"function frameView(viewport: Viewport, base: Resolution, aspect: AspectMode, current: Resolution): { framing: Framing; resolution: Resolution }\"},{\"line_number\":248,\"content\":\"The framing and art resolution of a view (PixelRenderer's canvas, or a HeadlessView's viewport):\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"`computeFraming`, and the art size as a resolution. Identity is kept where nothing changed: the\"},{\"line_number\":255,\"content\":\"- `readonly artWidth: number`: Art (internal) resolution actually rendered. Equals `internal` in fixed mode.\"},{\"line_number\":309,\"content\":\"- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\"},{\"line_number\":402,\"content\":\"the art resolution), so quality trades the shadow map size and the number of dynamic\"},{\"line_number\":426,\"content\":\"resolution: 'F7' })`), so a shipped game, which has no hotkeys, gets none back.\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"`scale`, and the scene renders at exactly the art resolution (pixelSize = scale). Every\"},{\"line_number\":439,\"content\":\"- `fixed`: the art resolution is exactly `internal` (16:9); other screen shapes letterbox.\"},{\"line_number\":485,\"content\":\"- `readonly renderer: { readonly mode: RenderMode; readonly baseResolution: Resolution; readonly lookVersion: number; setMode(mode: RenderMode): void; setResolution(resolution: Reso…`\"},{\"line_number\":494,\"content\":\"The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\"},{\"line_number\":593,\"content\":\"- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\"},{\"line_number\":596,\"content\":\"- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\"},{\"line_number\":781,\"content\":\"- `pixelSize: N`: Device pixels per art pixel (uniform). 1 in the art-resolution stage.\"},{\"line_number\":782,\"content\":\"- `texture?(node: N): N`: Render a node into a texture at the current stage's resolution (art-sized in the art stage). Defaults to `convertToTexture` (drawing-buffer sized).\"},{\"line_number\":872,\"content\":\"- `pixel: PixelLook | null`: Pixel-art settings, or null for clean full-resolution rendering.\"},{\"line_number\":896,\"content\":\"full resolution, no pixel art, no outlines, no filters), every plain filter stack\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ef6bf6e8-1d85-4b55-b2b2-030e8f0f97d7-41","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114