2,112,114,111,99,101,100,117,114,97,108,32,108,97,121,101,114,115,46,10,50,56,48,56,58,45,32,96,115,99,97,108,101,63,58,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,96,58,32,73,110,116,101,103,101,114,32,97,114,116,45,112,105,120,101,108,32,115,99,97,108,101,32,40,50,32,61,32,100,111,117,98,108,101,45,115,105,122,101,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,41,46,32,68,101,102,97,117,108,116,32,49,46,10,51,57,52,57,58,116,121,112,101,32,66,101,108,116,77,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,32,61,32,77,101,115,104,84,111,111,110,78,111,100,101,77,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,32,38,32,123,32,47,42,42,32,66,101,108,116,32,115,112,101,101,100,32,40,109,47,115,32,97,108,111,110,103,32,43,117,59,32,110,101,103,97,116,105,118,101,32,114,117,110,115,32,98,97,99,107,41,46,32,42,47,32,115,112,101,101,100,58,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,59,32,47,42,42,32,77,111,118,101,32,116,104,101,32,115,116,114,105,112,101,115,32,111,110,32,98,121,32,96,100,116,96,32,115,101,99,111,110,100,115,32,111,102,32,103,97,109,101,32,116,105,109,101,46,32,42,47,32,97,100,118,97,110,99,101,40,100,116,58,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,41,58,32,118,111,105,100,59,32,125,10,52,53,56,56,58,45,32,96,117,112,100,97,116,101,40,100,116,58,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,44,32,99,101,110,116,101,114,58,32,86,101,99,116,111,114,51,41,58,32,118,111,105,100,96,58,32,80,101,114,32,102,114,97,109,101,32,40,103,97,109,101,32,116,105,109,101,41,58,32,97,100,118,97,110,99,101,32,116,104,101,32,102,97,108,108,32,97,110,100,32,102,111,108,108,111,119,32,96,99,101,110,116,101,114,96,46,10,52,54,54,54,58,45,32,96,102,111,114,107,40,112,117,114,112,111,115,101,58,32,115,116,114,105,110,103,32,124,32,110,117,109,98,101,114,41,58,32,82,110,103,96,58,32,65,32,99,104,105,108,100,32,103,101,110,101,114,97,116,111,114,32,102,111,114,32,111,110,101,32,112,117,114,112,111,115,101,59,32,100,111,101,115,32,110,111,116,32,97,100,118,97,110,99,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,111,110,101,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":151,\"content\":\"- `manual: boolean`: Tooling: the render loop stops driving the game; advance it yourself with `step()`. Frame-exact and independent of how fast the browser renders (filmstrips, replays).\"},{\"line_number\":186,\"content\":\"- `step(n = 1, dt = 1 / 60): void`: Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation, animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\"},{\"line_number\":235,\"content\":\"should run, and advances the schedule so the long-run rate is `maxFps` even when the\"},{\"line_number\":1498,\"content\":\"- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number): void`: Per render frame: pick animation state and advance the mixer.\"},{\"line_number\":2223,\"content\":\"- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number, alpha: number): void`: Per render frame: orient the model, pick and advance animation, then the procedural layers.\"},{\"line_number\":2808,\"content\":\"- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\"},{\"line_number\":3949,\"content\":\"type BeltMaterial = MeshToonNodeMaterial & { /** Belt speed (m/s along +u; negative runs back). */ speed: number; /** Move the stripes on by `dt` seconds of game time. */ advance(dt: number): void; }\"},{\"line_number\":4588,\"content\":\"- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\"},{\"line_number\":4666,\"content\":\"- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3aa417c0-f6f5-4c27-8b30-6fbb6cc52956-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2740→- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\\n- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\\\"float\\\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\\n- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\\n- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is full, 0 for an unknown preset). Inline preset objects share one emitter per distinct content, so `burst({ ...literal }, at)` every…\\n- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\\n- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\\n- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\\n- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n2750→\\n### PARTICLES\\n\\n```ts\\nconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\\\"white\\\" | \\\"mist\\\" | \\\"slate\\\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...; }; sparkle: { ...; }; smoke: { ...; }; impact: { ...; }; }\\n```\\n\\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\\n\\n2760→## 10. HUD\\n\\n### class Hud\\n\\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\\n\\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\\n2770→(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\\n- `visible: boolean`\\n2780→- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\\n- `get height: number`\\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n2790→### type HudAnchor\\n\\n```ts\\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\\n```\\n\\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\\n\\n### type HudColor\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"2740→- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\\n- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\\\"float\\\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\\n- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\\n- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is full, 0 for an unknown preset). Inline preset objects share one emitter per distinct content, so `burst({ ...literal }, at)` every…\\n- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\\n- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\\n- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\\n- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n2750→\\n### PARTICLES\\n\\n```ts\\nconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\\\"white\\\" | \\\"mist\\\" | \\\"slate\\\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...; }; sparkle: { ...; }; smoke: { ...; }; impact: { ...; }; }\\n```\\n\\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\\n\\n2760→## 10. HUD\\n\\n### class Hud\\n\\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\\n\\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\\n2770→(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\\n- `visible: boolean`\\n2780→- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\\n- `get height: number`\\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n2790→### type HudAnchor\\n\\n```ts\\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\\n```\\n\\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\\n\\n### type HudColor\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"offset\":2740,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\\n- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\\\"float\\\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\\n- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\\n- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is full, 0 for an unknown preset). Inline preset objects share one emitter per distinct content, so `burst({ ...literal }, at)` every…\\n- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\\n- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\\n- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\\n- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n### PARTICLES\\n\\n```ts\\nconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\\\"white\\\" | \\\"mist\\\" | \\\"slate\\\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...; }; sparkle: { ...; }; smoke: { ...; }; impact: { ...; }; }\\n```\\n\\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\\n\\n## 10. HUD\\n\\n### class Hud\\n\\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\\n\\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\\n- `visible: boolean`\\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\\n- `get height: number`\\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n### type HudAnchor\\n\\n```ts\\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\\n```\\n\\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\\n\\n### type HudColor\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"1e6b8184-7449-49d8-b516-78a72a88c251"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_25","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Evaluating 5×7 font character widths for layout planning.\n\nAssuming 6px per character for the pixel font. This yields roughly 56 characters per line at 342px width, or about 114 characters across two wrapped lines. The 60-character limit fits comfortably within that space.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1ca23e87-eb77-4337-9b1e-634210246616-46","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040 && node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { Hud, frameView } from \"./pixel-engine.js\";\nconst h = new Hud(null);\nfor (const s of [1, 10, 20, 50, 56, 57, 60]) {\n  const t = \"A\".repeat(s);\n  const m = h.measure(t, 1);\n  console.log(s, m);\n}\nconsole.log(\"space\", h.measure(\" \", 1));\nconsole.log(\"frame 1920\", frameView({width:1920,height:1080,dpr:1}, {width:480,height:270}, \"fill\", {width:480,height:270}));\nconsole.log(\"frame 960\", frameView({width:960,height:540,dpr:1}, {width:480,height:270}, \"fill\", {width:480,height:270}));\nconsole.log(\"frame 1280\", frameView({width:1280,height:720,dpr:1}, {width:480,height:270}, \"fill\", {width:480,height:270}));\n'","description":"Measure HUD glyph width and fill framing"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3811,"output_tokens":623,"cache_read_input_tokens":123392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"9e7b5382-d96a-48b9-a6af-7ac0d505b95f"}
