lice(i-30, i+80)));\\n  i += 2; n++;\\n}\\n'\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Find all zK references in engine bundle\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/terminal/call-82574207-1cc5-4e11-9559-9847a3fd5012-53.log\",\"total_bytes\":1238}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"361bf58b-15d0-4a34-af64-57c52cee9386"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_32","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Beginning to write a JavaScript function named zK.\n\nConfirmed the localStorage fallback logic for missing keys. Will write the main code and install Playwright in the background.\n\nStrains will be deterministic spawn timelines rather than complex AI. The introit tick will manage entity spawning and movement. spawn will be passed from op.js to avoid circular dependencies.\n\nResolved the circular dependency by moving makeEntity into a new entities.js module. Both op.js and strains.js will import from it. The file will also export path helpers, slot builders, cell builders, pathMetrics, KIND_TOOL, and toolFor.\n\nDefined `toolFor` to map plate phases to specific tools. Will write the code now. A `runSim` helper in `src/sim/run.js` is planned for tests and campaigns, though the test loop will call `step` directly.\n\nSettled on `runSim` as the shipped driver for campaigns and tests. A `playOp` wrapper will bundle `createOp` with `runSim`. Will write files directly without Python.\n\nFragment angles will be seeded explicitly in puzzle content for deterministic behavior. A difficulty configuration object is being defined with intern-level settings.\n\nCompleted the difficulty configuration with resident and attending tiers. Hints will be drawn by the view layer via a `hintTarget` function exported from bot.js, respecting both the operation's hint flag and the difficulty setting. Will also add PROGRESS.md at the work root.\n\nConfirmed the `loadPack` signature from ASSETS.md. Will use `buildModel` for busts and verify model exports in a quick import test before importing them into `game.js`. The tool dispatch in `op.js` will be a complete switch statement. The `step()` function will clamp delta time to 0.25 and advance `sim.realT`.\n\nInside `step()`, quiet state is updated first to scale delta time. The simulation time advances by the scaled delta. History is recorded at ten hertz. The look action is evaluated before cursor movement so that restoring a saved state does not overwrite the cursor position.\n\nCursor movement is applied after the look restore so the player's input persists. The step function then updates angles and switches tables. Codeblue phase runs with real time. Massage phase advances vitals, drains composure, ticks the clock, and checks for failure.\n\nThe step function now applies tools, ticks droplets and strains, drains vitals, advances the clock, cold, sob, reveals finished items, advances the stage, and checks for win or fail. After a successful look restore, the function returns early to prevent double-applying tools in that same frame.\n\nDefined the quiet-gift unlock rule: a seat can quiet only if its gift type is quiet and persist.quietUnlocked is true. Mapped seat gifts for story and consult modes. Story ilya gives seat 0 quiet. Story sabine gives seat 0 look. The combined story operation gives seat 0 quiet and seat 1 look, with tag swaps. Consult mode assigns odd seats look and even seats quiet. Started writing a `giftType` helper to compute these assignments.\n\nCompleted the `giftType` helper. Ilya and locked operations default to quiet; Sabine gives seat 0 look and all others quiet; combined story gives even seats quiet and odd seats look. Look is available immediately for Sabine and locked for Ilya until unlock. Consult mode will use a `consult` flag to unlock both gifts for the appropriate seats.\n\nOp 6 gives Sabine the look gift immediately. Op 9 unlocks both gifts. The `createOp` definition will list starting gifts, and `persist` will track which ones are unlocked later. `tryLook` requires a seat with the look gift, a rising edge of that gift, sufficient composure, a recent history sample, and no codeblue state. Composure spent on look is not restored by snapshots, and `lookUses` increments in persist rather than being snapshotted. A five percent penalty applies to the final score if any look was used.\n\nConfirmed that rewinding preserves the five percent look penalty because `lookUses` persists in state. Verified that restoring a snapshot cannot accidentally trigger a win, since code blue disables look and phase restoration returns to play. Noted that stage objects mutate their spawned arrays, so snapshots must explicitly capture `stageIndex` and the current spawned IDs.\n\nSnapshot metadata will capture each stage's spawned IDs and entered status. On restore, these arrays are copied back into the simulation.\n\nThe `needRewind` flag lives in persist state, so it survives a snapshot. After the bot presses look to trigger a rewind, the system must clear `needRewind` and set a rewound flag to prevent repeated look presses.\n\nConfirmed that tryLook restores the simulation to four seconds before the clot, sets rewound to true, and clears needRewind so the bot will not press look again. Verified that gift presses cannot accidentally trigger quiet on a quiet seat because each operation assigns gifts to distinct seats.\n\nThe bot will trigger a one-frame look press by setting a `lookSent` flag on the seat object. This flag is not included in snapshots, so it does not survive a rewind and cannot cause repeated look presses.\n\nThe bot will request the gift every frame while `needRewind` is true, but `lookSent` is only set after a successful look. Because the rising-edge check fires once per press, the bot cannot accidentally trigger look repeatedly.\n\nThe bot will retry look on every frame while holding the gift, but only trigger a restore once per hold. A `lookedThisHold` latch prevents repeated restores during the same press. If history is too short, the restore fails and the bot waits until the next frame to try again.\n\nThe bot will hold the gift for about 0.2 seconds to let the restore latch trigger. History is already long enough by the time `needRewind` appears in operation six, so a second look test will use a custom definition with an immediate look gift instead of relying on that operation. Composure starts at forty, which is below the sixty-point cost of a look, so the bot must earn it through CLEANs before it can afford to use the gift.\n\nThe test will set composure to one hundred before pressing the gift. Operation six has enough steps before the unclamp that three CLEANs will already raise composure above sixty, so the look action will be available.\n\nThe bot will earn enough composure through CLEAN actions to afford the sixty-point look cost. Skill 0.7 mostly yields CLEANs, and skill 1 yields all CLEANs, so the bot should reach one hundred composure before operation six. Quiet requires twenty composure, which is already covered by the forty-point start.\n\nComposure will be clamped between zero and one hundred. Only CLEAN actions add composure; GOOD does not. A streak breaks on any non-CLEAN result, which may lower the skill 0.7 score if noise causes GOODs, but that is acceptable for a rank B target.\n\nNoise is set to `(1-skill) * 0.08`, giving skill 0.7 a mean of 0.024 and skill 0.4 a mean of 0.048. This keeps the suture slot at 0.4 safely above the scalpel CLEAN threshold of 0.12, so skill 0.4 should still CLEAR despite lower noise. The speed formula is `0.55 + 0.45 * skill`, meaning skill 0 starts at 0.55 rather than zero.\n\nSkill 0 is treated as idle input rather than a slow bot. Skill 0.4 runs at roughly 7.3 units per second. The bot will stay responsive without artificial delays so clears remain reliable. Skill 0.7 carries slightly more noise and slower speed, which may produce occasional GOOD ratings and reduce the time bonus, but the rank should still land at B+.\n\nNo intentional SLOPPY states will be added for skill 0.4; the bots should clear normally. The simulation config will be exposed as a reference, and createOp will fall back to getConfig() when no config is passed. Slider tests will mutate global config and must reset it afterward. A hashSim helper is being added to support deterministic snapshot hashing.\n\nThe `hashSim` helper will stringify a `publicState` snapshot and hash it with FNV-1a. `publicState` will include seat positions, tool, score, holding status, and `realT`, while excluding history, events, and functions.\n\nSeat coordinates will be rounded to five decimals in the hash state to avoid floating-point mismatches. Events will be excluded from the public state so the hash does not depend on event draining. The view code will be structured as a single present.js class to speed up implementation once the simulation is complete.\n\nThe screenshot script will use `__GAME__.shot()` to render each arena and screen directly, bypassing the need to win operations. The title screen must paint many pixels because the background is dark but meshes remain visible; a painted coverage test checks that the canvas is not blank.\n\nThe HUD is a separate canvas, so page.screenshot captures both the 3D view and the overlay. The title screen will include a visible lamp pool, table, and large title text to ensure high painted coverage. Tissue will also be painted brightly during surgery shots.\n\nThe launch test will verify the 3D canvas is not blank. The title screen will include visible theatre elements such as teal drapes, a warm lamp, a steel table, and monitor glow. The test will read back pixels directly from the WebGL or WebGPU canvas to ensure the scene renders.\n\nWebGPU is confirmed working. The background will be dark blue rather than pure black, with visible geometry on the title screen to ensure painted coverage. Code will be written in simulation-first order, followed by tests and then the view layer. A test filter will allow running only the simulation suite quickly during development.\n\nI will write a complete about.js now so lint passes, then update its numbers before the final test run. I will also create a short PROGRESS.md. The plan checklist will wait until the file:// boot works. I am starting to generate files in this order: entities.js, config, rng, op.js, strains, bot, ops, story, voice, and tests.\n\nI will write files through the tool to avoid a single giant message failure. The workspace is the work folder, so paths are absolute or relative to it. I will run npm install in parallel and draft op.js content offline inside the write call. The hashSim helper will live in src/sim/hash.js.\n\nA campaign runner is being drafted to play through every scene and operation automatically. It will drive each simulation with the given skill level, collect saves, and halt if any operation fails to reach victory.\n\nThe campaign runner will record each operation's rank, score, and pristine status into the save object. It will then mark the log and credits as complete and return the final save. Tests will assert that the campaign succeeds and that every scene and operation is present. A `writeSave` helper will keep an in-memory copy and also persist to localStorage when available.\n\n`readSave` will read from localStorage when available and fall back to the in-memory copy otherwise. The campaign test at skill 0.7 will also verify time remaining and rank, avoiding duplicate work with the balance test.\n\nThe test suite will run each operation once per skill level. The campaign test will reuse the skill 0.7 results to avoid double-running those operations, while still verifying scene progression and save state.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The kit matches the plan's engine. Next I’ll put the pure sim in place so operations, tools, and the bot can be tested without the browser."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-54","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040 && npm install playwright@1.63.0 --no-fund --no-audit --loglevel=error","description":"Install Playwright 1.63 in the dev folder","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-55","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/package.json","content":"{\n  \"name\": \"the-second-opinion-clinic\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-56","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/rng.js","content":"/** Seeded generator. Gameplay never calls Math.random. */\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\n  return {\n    next() {\n      s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;\n      return s / 4294967296;\n    },\n    float(a, b) {\n      return a + this.next() * (b - a);\n    },\n    int(n) {\n      return Math.floor(this.next() * n);\n    },\n    state() {\n      return s;\n    },\n    set(v) {\n      s = v >>> 0;\n    },\n  };\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-57","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/config.js","content":"/** Live balance values. Dev Mode sliders write these; Reset copies DEFAULTS back. */\nexport const DEFAULTS = {\n  vitalsDrainMul: 1,\n  bleedDrain: 0.35,\n  mistakePenalty: 6,\n  maxMistakes: 5,\n  timeLimitMul: 1,\n  cursorSpeed: 10,\n  steadyFactor: 0.4,\n  aimAssist: 1,\n  toolTol: 1,\n  drainRate: 1.4,\n  laserTime: 0.7,\n  syringeDose: 18,\n  syringeDraw: 0.45,\n  composureGain: 7,\n  quietScale: 0.25,\n  quietDrain: 18,\n  lookCost: 60,\n  lookSeconds: 4,\n  strainSpeed: 1,\n  strainHp: 1,\n  diesBpm: 72,\n  blueZone: 0.2,\n  coopScale: 0.25,\n};\n\nconst live = structuredClone(DEFAULTS);\n\nexport function getConfig() {\n  return live;\n}\n\nexport function applySlider(key, value) {\n  if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(DEFAULTS, key)) {\n    throw new Error(`unknown slider ${key}`);\n  }\n  const n = Number(value);\n  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) throw new Error(`bad slider value ${key}`);\n  live[key] = n;\n  return live[key];\n}\n\nexport function resetConfig() {\n  for (const k of Object.keys(DEFAULTS)) live[k] = DEFAULTS[k];\n  return live;\n}\n\nexport const DIFFICULTY = {\n  intern: { time: 1.4, drain: 0.6, blues: 2, hint: true },\n  resident: { time: 1, drain: 1, blues: 1, hint: true },\n  attending: { time: 0.8, drain: 1.3, blues: 1, hint: false },\n};\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-58","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/meta.js","content":"export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-626fe19c-131f-4ff9-b8af-948545f07e1f-59","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/save.js","content":"const KEY = 'soc:save:v1';\nconst mem = { json: null };\n\nexport function emptySave() {\n  return {\n    version: 1,\n    difficulty: 'resident',\n    scenes: [],\n    ops: {},\n    log: false,\n    credits: false,\n    quiet: false,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function writeSave(save) {\n  const json = JSON.stringify(save);\n  mem.json = json;\n  try {\n    globalThis.localStorage?.setItem(KEY, json);\n  } catch {\n    /* private mode */\n  }\n  return save;\n}\n\nexport function readSave() {\n  try {\n    const s = globalThis.localStorage?.getItem(KEY);\n    if (s) return JSON.parse(s);\n  } catch {\n    /* fall through */\n  }\n  return mem.json ? JSON.parse(mem.json) : null;\n}\n\nexport function clearSave() {\n  mem.json = null;\n  try {\n    globalThis.localStorage?.removeItem(KEY);\n  } catch {\n    /* ignore */\n  }\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":830,"output_tokens":7636,"cache_read_input_tokens":161152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"7b6ede03-cad8-4496-b433-5d0884e5a6c8"}
