44,32,68,114,97,105,110,44,32,70,111,114,99,101,112,115,44,32,83,117,116,117,114,101,44,32,71,101,108,44,32,83,121,114,105,110,103,101,44,32,79,112,32,49,32,112,108,97,121,97,98,108,101,32,111,110,32,112,97,100,44,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,97,110,100,32,107,101,121,115,46,32,77,97,107,101,32,116,104,105,115,32,102,101,101,108,32,119,111,110,100,101,114,102,117,108,32,98,101,102,111,114,101,32,109,111,118,105,110,103,32,111,110,46,10,56,53,56,58,55,46,32,42,42,67,111,110,115,117,108,116,46,42,42,32,67,111,117,99,104,32,102,105,114,115,116,32,40,105,116,32,112,114,111,118,101,115,32,116,104,101,32,115,101,97,116,115,41,44,32,116,104,101,110,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,44,32,99,97,114,100,44,32,110,101,116,44,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,112,97,115,115,101,115,46,10,56,55,50,58,35,35,32,49,54,46,32,68,111,110,101,32,109,101,97,110,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":50,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"## 1. The game\"},{\"line_number\":26,\"content\":\"- **Players:** 1 in the campaign. 1 to 4 in Consult, on one TV (couch) or on separate devices (AI Hub shared world).\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"- **Length:** a first run takes about 80 minutes: 10 story operations plus scenes. One Consult round takes about 4 minutes.\"},{\"line_number\":50,\"content\":\"2. \\\"New Shift.\\\" Storm outside, 3 a.m. Nurse Reyes wakes Ilya with a clipboard to the head: a trawler deckhand has eleven fishhooks in one arm.\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"## 2. World, cast and story\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"### World\"},{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"### Cast\"},{\"line_number\":88,\"content\":\"### Tone rules\"},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"### Story beats\"},{\"line_number\":110,\"content\":\"| 1 | Night shift (OR-7) | Storm. Chief unreachable. \\\"You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.\\\" Deckhand Tomasz Dolan, eleven hooks. \\\"How do you get eleven fishhooks in one arm?\\\" \\\"It was a long net.\\\" | Op 1 |\"},{\"line_number\":119,\"content\":\"| 10 | The stretcher (OR-7) | Hesper arrives dying. She took Mercy first, eleven years ago, so she'd never ask anything of others she wouldn't take herself. Everyone looks at Ilya. \\\"Scrub in.\\\" | Op 10. She feels pain for the first time in eleven years. \\\"Why?\\\" \\\"Because it's my shift.\\\" |\"},{\"line_number\":124,\"content\":\"## 3. Operating: the core game\"},{\"line_number\":126,\"content\":\"### The field and the cursor\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"### Instruments\"},{\"line_number\":164,\"content\":\"### Vitals, clock, mistakes\"},{\"line_number\":173,\"content\":\"### Rating and score\"},{\"line_number\":182,\"content\":\"### The gifts and Composure\"},{\"line_number\":198,\"content\":\"### Code Blue\"},{\"line_number\":209,\"content\":\"## 4. Controls and prompts\"},{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"## 5. The ten operations\"},{\"line_number\":252,\"content\":\"| 1 | Eleven Hooks | Ilya, Tomasz Dolan, deckhand | forearm | 240 s | 85 | .10 | 3 |\"},{\"line_number\":263,\"content\":\"**Op 1, Eleven Hooks.** Tools: Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe.\"},{\"line_number\":318,\"content\":\"**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\"},{\"line_number\":326,\"content\":\"## 6. The strains (bosses)\"},{\"line_number\":362,\"content\":\"**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\"},{\"line_number\":366,\"content\":\"## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\"},{\"line_number\":381,\"content\":\"### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\"},{\"line_number\":422,\"content\":\"### Networking\"},{\"line_number\":432,\"content\":\"- `hub:session` 1\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-players` 1-4\"},{\"line_number\":434,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\"},{\"line_number\":435,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-minutes` 4\"},{\"line_number\":436,\"content\":\"- `hub:webgpu` required\"},{\"line_number\":437,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\"},{\"line_number\":438,\"content\":\"- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\"},{\"line_number\":442,\"content\":\"## 8. Screens and flow\"},{\"line_number\":488,\"content\":\"- A looping reel of real sim segments of 20 to 30 s each, played by the bot with cheats (god vitals, free Composure): a talking-head snippet, Op 1 hooks, Op 2 scan and laser, Op 3 table swaps, Bone Mend, Introit with The Quiet, Second Look rewind, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae with Code Blue, then Pile-Up with four hands.\"},{\"line_number\":502,\"content\":\"## 9. Art direction: what works\"},{\"line_number\":640,\"content\":\"## 10. Audio: everything written in code\"},{\"line_number\":667,\"content\":\"- Op 9's silence, then a swell. Op 10 sparse and gentle. Results fanfare and sad variant. Credits.\"},{\"line_number\":673,\"content\":\"## 11. Architecture\"},{\"line_number\":741,\"content\":\"## 12. Balance\"},{\"line_number\":763,\"content\":\"## 13. Testing\"},{\"line_number\":822,\"content\":\"## 14. Build and packaging\"},{\"line_number\":834,\"content\":\"<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\"},{\"line_number\":842,\"content\":\"- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\"},{\"line_number\":848,\"content\":\"## 15. Order of work\"},{\"line_number\":853,\"content\":\"2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\"},{\"line_number\":858,\"content\":\"7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\"},{\"line_number\":872,\"content\":\"## 16. Done means\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-df130944-d4ff-4874-928d-a33583dfebfb-19","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/meta.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"total_lines\":4}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-df130944-d4ff-4874-928d-a33583dfebfb-20","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Seeded generator. Gameplay never calls Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  return {\\n    next() {\\n      s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n      return s / 4294967296;\\n    },\\n    float(a, b) {\\n10→      return a + this.next() * (b - a);\\n    },\\n    int(n) {\\n      return Math.floor(this.next() * n);\\n    },\\n    state() {\\n      return s;\\n    },\\n    set(v) {\\n      s = v >>> 0;\\n20→    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Seeded generator. Gameplay never calls Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  return {\\n    next() {\\n      s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n      return s / 4294967296;\\n    },\\n    float(a, b) {\\n10→      return a + this.next() * (b - a);\\n    },\\n    int(n) {\\n      return Math.floor(this.next() * n);\\n    },\\n    state() {\\n      return s;\\n    },\\n    set(v) {\\n      s = v >>> 0;\\n20→    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/rng.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/** Seeded generator. Gameplay never calls Math.random. */\\nexport function makeRng(seed) {\\n  let s = (seed >>> 0) || 1;\\n  return {\\n    next() {\\n      s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;\\n      return s / 4294967296;\\n    },\\n    float(a, b) {\\n      return a + this.next() * (b - a);\\n    },\\n    int(n) {\\n      return Math.floor(this.next() * n);\\n    },\\n    state() {\\n      return s;\\n    },\\n    set(v) {\\n      s = v >>> 0;\\n    },\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":22}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-df130944-d4ff-4874-928d-a33583dfebfb-21","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→const KEY = 'soc:save:v1';\\nconst mem = { json: null };\\n\\nexport function emptySave() {\\n  return {\\n    version: 1,\\n    difficulty: 'resident',\\n    scenes: [],\\n    ops: {},\\n10→    log: false,\\n    credits: false,\\n    quiet: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(save) {\\n  const json = JSON.stringify(save);\\n  mem.json = json;\\n  try {\\n20→    globalThis.localStorage?.setItem(KEY, json);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* private mode */\\n  }\\n  return save;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSave() {\\n  try {\\n    const s = globalThis.localStorage?.getItem(KEY);\\n30→    if (s) return JSON.parse(s);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* fall through */\\n  }\\n  return mem.json ? JSON.parse(mem.json) : null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clearSave() {\\n  mem.json = null;\\n  try {\\n40→    globalThis.localStorage?.removeItem(KEY);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* ignore */\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→const KEY = 'soc:save:v1';\\nconst mem = { json: null };\\n\\nexport function emptySave() {\\n  return {\\n    version: 1,\\n    difficulty: 'resident',\\n    scenes: [],\\n    ops: {},\\n10→    log: false,\\n    credits: false,\\n    quiet: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(save) {\\n  const json = JSON.stringify(save);\\n  mem.json = json;\\n  try {\\n20→    globalThis.localStorage?.setItem(KEY, json);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* private mode */\\n  }\\n  return save;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSave() {\\n  try {\\n    const s = globalThis.localStorage?.getItem(KEY);\\n30→    if (s) return JSON.parse(s);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* fall through */\\n  }\\n  return mem.json ? JSON.parse(mem.json) : null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clearSave() {\\n  mem.json = null;\\n  try {\\n40→    globalThis.localStorage?.removeItem(KEY);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* ignore */\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/save.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"const KEY = 'soc:save:v1';\\nconst mem = { json: null };\\n\\nexport function emptySave() {\\n  return {\\n    version: 1,\\n    difficulty: 'resident',\\n    scenes: [],\\n    ops: {},\\n    log: false,\\n    credits: false,\\n    quiet: false,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(save) {\\n  const json = JSON.stringify(save);\\n  mem.json = json;\\n  try {\\n    globalThis.localStorage?.setItem(KEY, json);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* private mode */\\n  }\\n  return save;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSave() {\\n  try {\\n    const s = globalThis.localStorage?.getItem(KEY);\\n    if (s) return JSON.parse(s);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* fall through */\\n  }\\n  return mem.json ? JSON.parse(mem.json) : null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function clearSave() {\\n  mem.json = null;\\n  try {\\n    globalThis.localStorage?.removeItem(KEY);\\n  } catch {\\n    /* ignore */\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":44}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"03a01673-03ca-4d7a-95c5-969426cd5bd0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_45","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":245,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":360,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":730,"limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2139,"output_tokens":225,"cache_read_input_tokens":71552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"6ab97204-ec3e-406c-86bb-efbb8c231715"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-22","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"245→\\n## 5. The ten operations\\n\\nEach op is a data file in `src/content/ops/` (section 11). Tools are introduced gradually; unused wheel slots dim. Numbers are starting points; tune with the balance report.\\n\\n250→| # | Op | Surgeon, patient | Arena | Time | Start vitals | Drain/s | Doses |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Eleven Hooks | Ilya, Tomasz Dolan, deckhand | forearm | 240 s | 85 | .10 | 3 |\\n| 2 | The Vanishing Act | Ilya, The Great Zamboni, magician | stomach | 300 s | 80 | .15 | 3 |\\n| 3 | Night Ferry | Ilya, three passengers | 3 tables | 360 s | 70/60/55 | .25 each | 5 |\\n| 4 | Sticks and Stones | Ilya, Ollie Brandt, 16 | forearm bone | 330 s | 75 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 5 | Introit | Ilya, Mr. Anselm, harbour pilot | liver | 360 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 6 | Cold Hands | **Sabine**, Pem's sister Ada | kidney bed | 360 s | 80 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 7 | Lacrimosa | Ilya, Ottilie Marr, hospice nurse | lung | 390 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 8 | Dies Irae | Ilya, Chief Bram | heart | 420 s | 75 | .35 | 5 |\\n260→| 9 | Libera Me | **both**, Nurse Reyes | whole chest | 540 s | 70 | .35 | 6 |\\n| 10 | Do No Harm | Ilya, Dr. Lindqvist | spine | 240 s | 60 | .05 | 2 |\\n\\n**Op 1, Eleven Hooks.** Tools: Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe.\\n\\n1. Move the tool onto a marker.\\n2. Drain two pools; hooks lie beneath.\\n3. Back out eleven hooks along their curved arrows (Reyes counts aloud).\\n4. Suture two lacerations.\\n5. Gel the rust-stained patch.\\n270→6. Dressing begins, then the gag: \\\"Twelve. I counted twelve.\\\" One last hook surfaces.\\n\\nTeach Syringe if vitals dip below 50, or at the latest in stage 5.\\n\\n**Op 2, The Vanishing Act.** Adds Scalpel, Scanner, Laser.\\n\\n1. Scalpel the midline guide.\\n2. Drain spot bleeders along the cut.\\n3. Scanner finds four swallowed props: key, coin, playing card, magnet pair.\\n4. Lance each (short scalpel stroke), then Forceps them out. The magnets obey a pull-speed limit.\\n280→5. The music changes. Scanner shows a tumour: \\\"That one isn't a prop.\\\"\\n6. Closed-path Scalpel around it, Forceps lift, Laser five satellite polyps, Drain, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 3, Night Ferry (triage).** Three separate fields, side by side, 24 units apart. Each has its own vitals, all ticking at once. D-pad, Tab or the on-screen table tabs whip-pan the camera between them.\\n\\n- Table A: leg gash (Suture, Drain).\\n- Table B: hull debris and burns (Forceps, Gel).\\n- Table C: chest wound (Scalpel, Drain, Suture, Laser).\\n\\nTasks arrive in small batches. At about 70% done, Table C crashes on a script: sound drops out, heartbeat, \\\"the room goes quiet\\\". **The Quiet awakens**: prompt the gift button, and it stays unlocked from here on. Losing any patient fails the op.\\n290→\\n**Op 4, Sticks and Stones (Bone Mend).** Sabine's cold commentary replaces some of Reyes's lines.\\n\\n1. Open, then Drain.\\n2. Bone Mend: grab six fragments (two under pools), rotate while held (right stick, mouse wheel or Q/E), and release onto the bone's silhouette. It snaps within ±15°; within ±5° is CLEAN.\\n3. Gel cement along the seams.\\n4. An artery pops: a sudden bleeder to Suture fast.\\n5. Scripted **Code Blue** teaches paddles.\\n6. Suture, Gel, Dressing. Sabine: \\\"Adequate.\\\"\\n\\n300→**Op 5, Introit** (section 6). Scanner reveals something moving, then the fight. Afterwards Laser six eggs, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 6, Cold Hands (transplant, as Sabine).** The player has The Second Look.\\n\\n1. Open.\\n2. Forceps place clamps on two vessels.\\n3. Short Scalpel strokes cut them.\\n4. Forceps lift out the failing kidney.\\n5. Fetch the donor kidney from the ice tray. A separate **cold-time bar** (120 s) starts.\\n6. Suture three anastomoses (artery, vein, ureter): precise, short.\\n310→7. Unclamp in the right order. The first time, a hidden clot bursts regardless; Sabine: \\\"Again.\\\" This forces a prompt to use the Second Look.\\n8. The kidney pinks up as blood returns, the game's most satisfying visual payoff. Tween its ramp from grey-plum to warm red.\\n9. A scan shows dormant Mercy in the removed-donor-tissue sample: story hook. Close.\\n\\n**Op 7, Lacrimosa** and **Op 8, Dies Irae** (section 6). Each has a short exploratory opening and a close.\\n\\n**Op 9, Libera Me** (section 6). The comm strip shows `NO SIGNAL`. There is no hint marker, no voice. A bot-driven partner hand shares the table.\\n\\n**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\\n\\n320→- Slow Scalpel, gentle Forceps. Each removal raises her vitals *and* her pain, and her voice lines change as feeling returns.\\n- Final Forceps extraction, then Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n- After all that action the slowness is the point. It should feel like an exhale.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. The strains (bosses)\\n\\nEach is a module in `src/sim/strains/` with a small state machine and a matching view in `src/view/strains/`. Each should be a 3D creature on the `actors` layer. Build them from the engine's animation tools: `SpringChain` for tendrils, `Squash`, `LegStepper` and `twoBoneIK` for crawling. Use a `rim` colour, an emissive hit flash, and a `dissolve: true` toon material for death. ✔ My Dies Irae mock (a glowing eye in a crown of seven red plates, `rim` lit, with `SpringChain` tendrils trailing onto the heart) read very well. **Place everything at `heightAt(x, z) + offset`** or the surface swallows it: ✔ my first version sat at a fixed height and vanished inside the dome, and it needed `y` of about 3 over the dome's top.\\n\\n330→**Introit, \\\"the Knock\\\" (liver, 3 HP).**\\n\\n- The core moves *under* the tissue on a spline at 1.6 units/s. Show it as a travelling bulge in the mesh and a faint blotch; the Scanner shows it crisply.\\n- Every 6 s it stops and \\\"knocks\\\": a puckered pore surfaces for 3 s.\\n  1. Lance the pore with a short Scalpel stroke.\\n  2. The core is exposed for 3.5 s. Grab it with Forceps and pull 2.5 units against its tether. Let go early and it snaps back and lacerates.\\n  3. The tether pops: −1 HP. It flees and leaves 2 lacerations to Suture. Speed +25%.\\n- A missed knock leaves a laceration and a pool. Dead: dissolves, then the eggs.\\n\\n**Lacrimosa, \\\"the Weeper\\\" (lung, 5 eyes, 3 HP each).** Eyes open in turns and weep droplets (use `BulletPool`) that roll toward the bottom of the screen at 1.5 units/s.\\n340→\\n- A droplet on bare tissue makes a nick and costs 1 vital.\\n- Drain sucks droplets within 0.7. Gel film lasts 10 s and kills droplets on contact.\\n- Laser an open eye for 1.2 s: it closes and takes 1 damage. An eye left open 8 s heals.\\n- **At half HP:** eyes crawl on stalks (`LegStepper`) and droplets drift toward your tip.\\n- **Last eye:** **the Sob**, three times. A dotted line crosses the lung; paint at least 80% of it with Gel in 6 s or a wave takes 25 vitals.\\n- Then Forceps pull the optic stalk on a tether.\\n\\n**Dies Irae, \\\"the Wrath\\\" (beating heart, 7 plates, 3 rounds).** Everything is on the beat. It starts at 72 BPM. The mesh thumps in **systole** (35% of the cycle); a tool used then is SLOPPY and nicks tissue. **Diastole** (65%) is safe. A ring around the tip and the EKG show the phase, and the music runs at the heart's tempo.\\n\\n350→- Round: cut a plate (short Scalpel stroke) within one diastole, lift it with Forceps in the next, then Laser the exposed eye, diastole only.\\n- Each plate: +6 BPM. A Syringe dose acts as a beta-blocker: −12 BPM.\\n- Wrath flares run along arteries as pools to Drain.\\n- At 120 BPM or more: **fibrillation**, a paddles shock on the beat.\\n- After round 3 the heart arrests: **Massage**, alternate L2/R2 (left/right click, J/K) on the beat 8 times, then the final cut.\\n\\n**Libera Me (whole chest, three stages).**\\n\\n1. **Sanctus, the False Clean.** The field looks healthy and the monitor reads a steady 99. It is lying; only the EKG jitters. Scanner shows which cysts are real. Laser eight real ones; a false one is a mistake. Clearing them drops the monitor to the true number (say 41), a horror beat.\\n2. **Reprise.** One Introit knock, two Lacrimosa eyes and a three-plate Dies Irae ring run at once. The bot partner handles the left half of the field and you handle the right.\\n360→3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\",\"content_concise\":\"245→\\n## 5. The ten operations\\n\\nEach op is a data file in `src/content/ops/` (section 11). Tools are introduced gradually; unused wheel slots dim. Numbers are starting points; tune with the balance report.\\n\\n250→| # | Op | Surgeon, patient | Arena | Time | Start vitals | Drain/s | Doses |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Eleven Hooks | Ilya, Tomasz Dolan, deckhand | forearm | 240 s | 85 | .10 | 3 |\\n| 2 | The Vanishing Act | Ilya, The Great Zamboni, magician | stomach | 300 s | 80 | .15 | 3 |\\n| 3 | Night Ferry | Ilya, three passengers | 3 tables | 360 s | 70/60/55 | .25 each | 5 |\\n| 4 | Sticks and Stones | Ilya, Ollie Brandt, 16 | forearm bone | 330 s | 75 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 5 | Introit | Ilya, Mr. Anselm, harbour pilot | liver | 360 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 6 | Cold Hands | **Sabine**, Pem's sister Ada | kidney bed | 360 s | 80 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 7 | Lacrimosa | Ilya, Ottilie Marr, hospice nurse | lung | 390 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 8 | Dies Irae | Ilya, Chief Bram | heart | 420 s | 75 | .35 | 5 |\\n260→| 9 | Libera Me | **both**, Nurse Reyes | whole chest | 540 s | 70 | .35 | 6 |\\n| 10 | Do No Harm | Ilya, Dr. Lindqvist | spine | 240 s | 60 | .05 | 2 |\\n\\n**Op 1, Eleven Hooks.** Tools: Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe.\\n\\n1. Move the tool onto a marker.\\n2. Drain two pools; hooks lie beneath.\\n3. Back out eleven hooks along their curved arrows (Reyes counts aloud).\\n4. Suture two lacerations.\\n5. Gel the rust-stained patch.\\n270→6. Dressing begins, then the gag: \\\"Twelve. I counted twelve.\\\" One last hook surfaces.\\n\\nTeach Syringe if vitals dip below 50, or at the latest in stage 5.\\n\\n**Op 2, The Vanishing Act.** Adds Scalpel, Scanner, Laser.\\n\\n1. Scalpel the midline guide.\\n2. Drain spot bleeders along the cut.\\n3. Scanner finds four swallowed props: key, coin, playing card, magnet pair.\\n4. Lance each (short scalpel stroke), then Forceps them out. The magnets obey a pull-speed limit.\\n280→5. The music changes. Scanner shows a tumour: \\\"That one isn't a prop.\\\"\\n6. Closed-path Scalpel around it, Forceps lift, Laser five satellite polyps, Drain, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 3, Night Ferry (triage).** Three separate fields, side by side, 24 units apart. Each has its own vitals, all ticking at once. D-pad, Tab or the on-screen table tabs whip-pan the camera between them.\\n\\n- Table A: leg gash (Suture, Drain).\\n- Table B: hull debris and burns (Forceps, Gel).\\n- Table C: chest wound (Scalpel, Drain, Suture, Laser).\\n\\nTasks arrive in small batches. At about 70% done, Table C crashes on a script: sound drops out, heartbeat, \\\"the room goes quiet\\\". **The Quiet awakens**: prompt the gift button, and it stays unlocked from here on. Losing any patient fails the op.\\n290→\\n**Op 4, Sticks and Stones (Bone Mend).** Sabine's cold commentary replaces some of Reyes's lines.\\n\\n1. Open, then Drain.\\n2. Bone Mend: grab six fragments (two under pools), rotate while held (right stick, mouse wheel or Q/E), and release onto the bone's silhouette. It snaps within ±15°; within ±5° is CLEAN.\\n3. Gel cement along the seams.\\n4. An artery pops: a sudden bleeder to Suture fast.\\n5. Scripted **Code Blue** teaches paddles.\\n6. Suture, Gel, Dressing. Sabine: \\\"Adequate.\\\"\\n\\n300→**Op 5, Introit** (section 6). Scanner reveals something moving, then the fight. Afterwards Laser six eggs, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 6, Cold Hands (transplant, as Sabine).** The player has The Second Look.\\n\\n1. Open.\\n2. Forceps place clamps on two vessels.\\n3. Short Scalpel strokes cut them.\\n4. Forceps lift out the failing kidney.\\n5. Fetch the donor kidney from the ice tray. A separate **cold-time bar** (120 s) starts.\\n6. Suture three anastomoses (artery, vein, ureter): precise, short.\\n310→7. Unclamp in the right order. The first time, a hidden clot bursts regardless; Sabine: \\\"Again.\\\" This forces a prompt to use the Second Look.\\n8. The kidney pinks up as blood returns, the game's most satisfying visual payoff. Tween its ramp from grey-plum to warm red.\\n9. A scan shows dormant Mercy in the removed-donor-tissue sample: story hook. Close.\\n\\n**Op 7, Lacrimosa** and **Op 8, Dies Irae** (section 6). Each has a short exploratory opening and a close.\\n\\n**Op 9, Libera Me** (section 6). The comm strip shows `NO SIGNAL`. There is no hint marker, no voice. A bot-driven partner hand shares the table.\\n\\n**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\\n\\n320→- Slow Scalpel, gentle Forceps. Each removal raises her vitals *and* her pain, and her voice lines change as feeling returns.\\n- Final Forceps extraction, then Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n- After all that action the slowness is the point. It should feel like an exhale.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. The strains (bosses)\\n\\nEach is a module in `src/sim/strains/` with a small state machine and a matching view in `src/view/strains/`. Each should be a 3D creature on the `actors` layer. Build them from the engine's animation tools: `SpringChain` for tendrils, `Squash`, `LegStepper` and `twoBoneIK` for crawling. Use a `rim` colour, an emissive hit flash, and a `dissolve: true` toon material for death. ✔ My Dies Irae mock (a glowing eye in a crown of seven red plates, `rim` lit, with `SpringChain` tendrils trailing onto the heart) read very well. **Place everything at `heightAt(x, z) + offset`** or the surface swallows it: ✔ my first version sat at a fixed height and vanished inside the dome, and it needed `y` of about 3 over the dome's top.\\n\\n330→**Introit, \\\"the Knock\\\" (liver, 3 HP).**\\n\\n- The core moves *under* the tissue on a spline at 1.6 units/s. Show it as a travelling bulge in the mesh and a faint blotch; the Scanner shows it crisply.\\n- Every 6 s it stops and \\\"knocks\\\": a puckered pore surfaces for 3 s.\\n  1. Lance the pore with a short Scalpel stroke.\\n  2. The core is exposed for 3.5 s. Grab it with Forceps and pull 2.5 units against its tether. Let go early and it snaps back and lacerates.\\n  3. The tether pops: −1 HP. It flees and leaves 2 lacerations to Suture. Speed +25%.\\n- A missed knock leaves a laceration and a pool. Dead: dissolves, then the eggs.\\n\\n**Lacrimosa, \\\"the Weeper\\\" (lung, 5 eyes, 3 HP each).** Eyes open in turns and weep droplets (use `BulletPool`) that roll toward the bottom of the screen at 1.5 units/s.\\n340→\\n- A droplet on bare tissue makes a nick and costs 1 vital.\\n- Drain sucks droplets within 0.7. Gel film lasts 10 s and kills droplets on contact.\\n- Laser an open eye for 1.2 s: it closes and takes 1 damage. An eye left open 8 s heals.\\n- **At half HP:** eyes crawl on stalks (`LegStepper`) and droplets drift toward your tip.\\n- **Last eye:** **the Sob**, three times. A dotted line crosses the lung; paint at least 80% of it with Gel in 6 s or a wave takes 25 vitals.\\n- Then Forceps pull the optic stalk on a tether.\\n\\n**Dies Irae, \\\"the Wrath\\\" (beating heart, 7 plates, 3 rounds).** Everything is on the beat. It starts at 72 BPM. The mesh thumps in **systole** (35% of the cycle); a tool used then is SLOPPY and nicks tissue. **Diastole** (65%) is safe. A ring around the tip and the EKG show the phase, and the music runs at the heart's tempo.\\n\\n350→- Round: cut a plate (short Scalpel stroke) within one diastole, lift it with Forceps in the next, then Laser the exposed eye, diastole only.\\n- Each plate: +6 BPM. A Syringe dose acts as a beta-blocker: −12 BPM.\\n- Wrath flares run along arteries as pools to Drain.\\n- At 120 BPM or more: **fibrillation**, a paddles shock on the beat.\\n- After round 3 the heart arrests: **Massage**, alternate L2/R2 (left/right click, J/K) on the beat 8 times, then the final cut.\\n\\n**Libera Me (whole chest, three stages).**\\n\\n1. **Sanctus, the False Clean.** The field looks healthy and the monitor reads a steady 99. It is lying; only the EKG jitters. Scanner shows which cysts are real. Laser eight real ones; a false one is a mistake. Clearing them drops the monitor to the true number (say 41), a horror beat.\\n2. **Reprise.** One Introit knock, two Lacrimosa eyes and a three-plate Dies Irae ring run at once. The bot partner handles the left half of the field and you handle the right.\\n360→3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":245,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"\\n## 5. The ten operations\\n\\nEach op is a data file in `src/content/ops/` (section 11). Tools are introduced gradually; unused wheel slots dim. Numbers are starting points; tune with the balance report.\\n\\n| # | Op | Surgeon, patient | Arena | Time | Start vitals | Drain/s | Doses |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Eleven Hooks | Ilya, Tomasz Dolan, deckhand | forearm | 240 s | 85 | .10 | 3 |\\n| 2 | The Vanishing Act | Ilya, The Great Zamboni, magician | stomach | 300 s | 80 | .15 | 3 |\\n| 3 | Night Ferry | Ilya, three passengers | 3 tables | 360 s | 70/60/55 | .25 each | 5 |\\n| 4 | Sticks and Stones | Ilya, Ollie Brandt, 16 | forearm bone | 330 s | 75 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 5 | Introit | Ilya, Mr. Anselm, harbour pilot | liver | 360 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 6 | Cold Hands | **Sabine**, Pem's sister Ada | kidney bed | 360 s | 80 | .20 | 3 |\\n| 7 | Lacrimosa | Ilya, Ottilie Marr, hospice nurse | lung | 390 s | 80 | .30 | 4 |\\n| 8 | Dies Irae | Ilya, Chief Bram | heart | 420 s | 75 | .35 | 5 |\\n| 9 | Libera Me | **both**, Nurse Reyes | whole chest | 540 s | 70 | .35 | 6 |\\n| 10 | Do No Harm | Ilya, Dr. Lindqvist | spine | 240 s | 60 | .05 | 2 |\\n\\n**Op 1, Eleven Hooks.** Tools: Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe.\\n\\n1. Move the tool onto a marker.\\n2. Drain two pools; hooks lie beneath.\\n3. Back out eleven hooks along their curved arrows (Reyes counts aloud).\\n4. Suture two lacerations.\\n5. Gel the rust-stained patch.\\n6. Dressing begins, then the gag: \\\"Twelve. I counted twelve.\\\" One last hook surfaces.\\n\\nTeach Syringe if vitals dip below 50, or at the latest in stage 5.\\n\\n**Op 2, The Vanishing Act.** Adds Scalpel, Scanner, Laser.\\n\\n1. Scalpel the midline guide.\\n2. Drain spot bleeders along the cut.\\n3. Scanner finds four swallowed props: key, coin, playing card, magnet pair.\\n4. Lance each (short scalpel stroke), then Forceps them out. The magnets obey a pull-speed limit.\\n5. The music changes. Scanner shows a tumour: \\\"That one isn't a prop.\\\"\\n6. Closed-path Scalpel around it, Forceps lift, Laser five satellite polyps, Drain, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 3, Night Ferry (triage).** Three separate fields, side by side, 24 units apart. Each has its own vitals, all ticking at once. D-pad, Tab or the on-screen table tabs whip-pan the camera between them.\\n\\n- Table A: leg gash (Suture, Drain).\\n- Table B: hull debris and burns (Forceps, Gel).\\n- Table C: chest wound (Scalpel, Drain, Suture, Laser).\\n\\nTasks arrive in small batches. At about 70% done, Table C crashes on a script: sound drops out, heartbeat, \\\"the room goes quiet\\\". **The Quiet awakens**: prompt the gift button, and it stays unlocked from here on. Losing any patient fails the op.\\n\\n**Op 4, Sticks and Stones (Bone Mend).** Sabine's cold commentary replaces some of Reyes's lines.\\n\\n1. Open, then Drain.\\n2. Bone Mend: grab six fragments (two under pools), rotate while held (right stick, mouse wheel or Q/E), and release onto the bone's silhouette. It snaps within ±15°; within ±5° is CLEAN.\\n3. Gel cement along the seams.\\n4. An artery pops: a sudden bleeder to Suture fast.\\n5. Scripted **Code Blue** teaches paddles.\\n6. Suture, Gel, Dressing. Sabine: \\\"Adequate.\\\"\\n\\n**Op 5, Introit** (section 6). Scanner reveals something moving, then the fight. Afterwards Laser six eggs, Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n\\n**Op 6, Cold Hands (transplant, as Sabine).** The player has The Second Look.\\n\\n1. Open.\\n2. Forceps place clamps on two vessels.\\n3. Short Scalpel strokes cut them.\\n4. Forceps lift out the failing kidney.\\n5. Fetch the donor kidney from the ice tray. A separate **cold-time bar** (120 s) starts.\\n6. Suture three anastomoses (artery, vein, ureter): precise, short.\\n7. Unclamp in the right order. The first time, a hidden clot bursts regardless; Sabine: \\\"Again.\\\" This forces a prompt to use the Second Look.\\n8. The kidney pinks up as blood returns, the game's most satisfying visual payoff. Tween its ramp from grey-plum to warm red.\\n9. A scan shows dormant Mercy in the removed-donor-tissue sample: story hook. Close.\\n\\n**Op 7, Lacrimosa** and **Op 8, Dies Irae** (section 6). Each has a short exploratory opening and a close.\\n\\n**Op 9, Libera Me** (section 6). The comm strip shows `NO SIGNAL`. There is no hint marker, no voice. A bot-driven partner hand shares the table.\\n\\n**Op 10, Do No Harm.** No time pressure in spirit: generous clock, soft music, no attacks. A pale strain lies curled along her spine and does not fight.\\n\\n- Slow Scalpel, gentle Forceps. Each removal raises her vitals *and* her pain, and her voice lines change as feeling returns.\\n- Final Forceps extraction, then Suture, Gel, Dressing.\\n- After all that action the slowness is the point. It should feel like an exhale.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. The strains (bosses)\\n\\nEach is a module in `src/sim/strains/` with a small state machine and a matching view in `src/view/strains/`. Each should be a 3D creature on the `actors` layer. Build them from the engine's animation tools: `SpringChain` for tendrils, `Squash`, `LegStepper` and `twoBoneIK` for crawling. Use a `rim` colour, an emissive hit flash, and a `dissolve: true` toon material for death. ✔ My Dies Irae mock (a glowing eye in a crown of seven red plates, `rim` lit, with `SpringChain` tendrils trailing onto the heart) read very well. **Place everything at `heightAt(x, z) + offset`** or the surface swallows it: ✔ my first version sat at a fixed height and vanished inside the dome, and it needed `y` of about 3 over the dome's top.\\n\\n**Introit, \\\"the Knock\\\" (liver, 3 HP).**\\n\\n- The core moves *under* the tissue on a spline at 1.6 units/s. Show it as a travelling bulge in the mesh and a faint blotch; the Scanner shows it crisply.\\n- Every 6 s it stops and \\\"knocks\\\": a puckered pore surfaces for 3 s.\\n  1. Lance the pore with a short Scalpel stroke.\\n  2. The core is exposed for 3.5 s. Grab it with Forceps and pull 2.5 units against its tether. Let go early and it snaps back and lacerates.\\n  3. The tether pops: −1 HP. It flees and leaves 2 lacerations to Suture. Speed +25%.\\n- A missed knock leaves a laceration and a pool. Dead: dissolves, then the eggs.\\n\\n**Lacrimosa, \\\"the Weeper\\\" (lung, 5 eyes, 3 HP each).** Eyes open in turns and weep droplets (use `BulletPool`) that roll toward the bottom of the screen at 1.5 units/s.\\n\\n- A droplet on bare tissue makes a nick and costs 1 vital.\\n- Drain sucks droplets within 0.7. Gel film lasts 10 s and kills droplets on contact.\\n- Laser an open eye for 1.2 s: it closes and takes 1 damage. An eye left open 8 s heals.\\n- **At half HP:** eyes crawl on stalks (`LegStepper`) and droplets drift toward your tip.\\n- **Last eye:** **the Sob**, three times. A dotted line crosses the lung; paint at least 80% of it with Gel in 6 s or a wave takes 25 vitals.\\n- Then Forceps pull the optic stalk on a tether.\\n\\n**Dies Irae, \\\"the Wrath\\\" (beating heart, 7 plates, 3 rounds).** Everything is on the beat. It starts at 72 BPM. The mesh thumps in **systole** (35% of the cycle); a tool used then is SLOPPY and nicks tissue. **Diastole** (65%) is safe. A ring around the tip and the EKG show the phase, and the music runs at the heart's tempo.\\n\\n- Round: cut a plate (short Scalpel stroke) within one diastole, lift it with Forceps in the next, then Laser the exposed eye, diastole only.\\n- Each plate: +6 BPM. A Syringe dose acts as a beta-blocker: −12 BPM.\\n- Wrath flares run along arteries as pools to Drain.\\n- At 120 BPM or more: **fibrillation**, a paddles shock on the beat.\\n- After round 3 the heart arrests: **Massage**, alternate L2/R2 (left/right click, J/K) on the beat 8 times, then the final cut.\\n\\n**Libera Me (whole chest, three stages).**\\n\\n1. **Sanctus, the False Clean.** The field looks healthy and the monitor reads a steady 99. It is lying; only the EKG jitters. Scanner shows which cysts are real. Laser eight real ones; a false one is a mistake. Clearing them drops the monitor to the true number (say 41), a horror beat.\\n2. **Reprise.** One Introit knock, two Lacrimosa eyes and a three-plate Dies Irae ring run at once. The bot partner handles the left half of the field and you handle the right.\\n3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"360→3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\\n450→- The font auto-uppercases and has `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >` ✔. Anything else, em dashes and ellipsis characters included, draws as a gap: type `-` and `...`.\\n\\n**Flow**\\n\\nTitle → Main → Story scene → Briefing → Operation → Results → next. Save after every op.\\n\\n- **Title:** dim OR-7, swinging lamp, title drawn big with an EKG line through it. \\\"Press ✕\\\" or \\\"Press Enter/Click\\\", following the last input. Theme music. Any input leads to Main.\\n- **Main menu** (over the dim theatre, the camera drifting):\\n  - **ON CALL:** Continue or New Shift, then pick a difficulty.\\n  - **OPERATING LOG:** replay cleared ops, showing best rank and a patient line. One chart at a time, flip with ←/→.\\n460→  - **CONSULT**\\n  - **SETTINGS**\\n  - **ABOUT**\\n- **Story scene:** set plus busts. ✕/Enter/click advances; hold △/Esc to skip. Typewriter text with gibberish voice, the speaker leaning in and the other dimmed. Occasional wide shots use full-body figures and the engine's `Timeline`.\\n- **Briefing:** a clipboard chart: patient name, age, job, hook, the op's title stamped, and the one-line objective. Not a stats page. Then the camera dives from the OR-7 wide shot down onto the field (fly the three.js camera directly) with an iris transition.\\n- **Operation HUD** (art pixels at 270 height):\\n  - **Top strip, 20 tall:** VITALS number at scale 2 and a live EKG on the left, clock at centre, Composure at right.\\n  - **Bottom strip, 32 tall:** speaker name and up to two lines of comm text.\\n  - **Bottom-right:** the tool wheel (about 48 square), with the current tool in the centre, clickable.\\n  - **Dose count** by the wheel. **Rating pop-ups** at scale 2 near the tip.\\n470→  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\\n- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\\n- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\\n- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\\n  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\\n  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\\n  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\\n- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \\\"all art and audio written in code\\\".\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\",\"content_concise\":\"360→3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\\n450→- The font auto-uppercases and has `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >` ✔. Anything else, em dashes and ellipsis characters included, draws as a gap: type `-` and `...`.\\n\\n**Flow**\\n\\nTitle → Main → Story scene → Briefing → Operation → Results → next. Save after every op.\\n\\n- **Title:** dim OR-7, swinging lamp, title drawn big with an EKG line through it. \\\"Press ✕\\\" or \\\"Press Enter/Click\\\", following the last input. Theme music. Any input leads to Main.\\n- **Main menu** (over the dim theatre, the camera drifting):\\n  - **ON CALL:** Continue or New Shift, then pick a difficulty.\\n  - **OPERATING LOG:** replay cleared ops, showing best rank and a patient line. One chart at a time, flip with ←/→.\\n460→  - **CONSULT**\\n  - **SETTINGS**\\n  - **ABOUT**\\n- **Story scene:** set plus busts. ✕/Enter/click advances; hold △/Esc to skip. Typewriter text with gibberish voice, the speaker leaning in and the other dimmed. Occasional wide shots use full-body figures and the engine's `Timeline`.\\n- **Briefing:** a clipboard chart: patient name, age, job, hook, the op's title stamped, and the one-line objective. Not a stats page. Then the camera dives from the OR-7 wide shot down onto the field (fly the three.js camera directly) with an iris transition.\\n- **Operation HUD** (art pixels at 270 height):\\n  - **Top strip, 20 tall:** VITALS number at scale 2 and a live EKG on the left, clock at centre, Composure at right.\\n  - **Bottom strip, 32 tall:** speaker name and up to two lines of comm text.\\n  - **Bottom-right:** the tool wheel (about 48 square), with the current tool in the centre, clickable.\\n  - **Dose count** by the wheel. **Rating pop-ups** at scale 2 near the tip.\\n470→  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\\n- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\\n- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\\n- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\\n  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\\n  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\\n  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\\n- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \\\"all art and audio written in code\\\".\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":360,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"3. **Miserere.** A pale, beautiful, gold-haloed core. It **copies you**: a ghost hand replays your last 3 s of tool motion and cuts where you cut, so you must keep moving differently. △/E tags between Ilya and Sabine (each with their gift); the other becomes the bot. Finish with a two-handed Forceps pull (you and the partner on one tether), then a forced Code Blue. On success, silence, then Reyes's line.\\n\\n**Consult op, Pile-Up (section 7).** A wave-based chest wound: hooks, pools, lacerations, polyps, surges, and a small Introit at T−40 s.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\\n- The font auto-uppercases and has `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >` ✔. Anything else, em dashes and ellipsis characters included, draws as a gap: type `-` and `...`.\\n\\n**Flow**\\n\\nTitle → Main → Story scene → Briefing → Operation → Results → next. Save after every op.\\n\\n- **Title:** dim OR-7, swinging lamp, title drawn big with an EKG line through it. \\\"Press ✕\\\" or \\\"Press Enter/Click\\\", following the last input. Theme music. Any input leads to Main.\\n- **Main menu** (over the dim theatre, the camera drifting):\\n  - **ON CALL:** Continue or New Shift, then pick a difficulty.\\n  - **OPERATING LOG:** replay cleared ops, showing best rank and a patient line. One chart at a time, flip with ←/→.\\n  - **CONSULT**\\n  - **SETTINGS**\\n  - **ABOUT**\\n- **Story scene:** set plus busts. ✕/Enter/click advances; hold △/Esc to skip. Typewriter text with gibberish voice, the speaker leaning in and the other dimmed. Occasional wide shots use full-body figures and the engine's `Timeline`.\\n- **Briefing:** a clipboard chart: patient name, age, job, hook, the op's title stamped, and the one-line objective. Not a stats page. Then the camera dives from the OR-7 wide shot down onto the field (fly the three.js camera directly) with an iris transition.\\n- **Operation HUD** (art pixels at 270 height):\\n  - **Top strip, 20 tall:** VITALS number at scale 2 and a live EKG on the left, clock at centre, Composure at right.\\n  - **Bottom strip, 32 tall:** speaker name and up to two lines of comm text.\\n  - **Bottom-right:** the tool wheel (about 48 square), with the current tool in the centre, clickable.\\n  - **Dose count** by the wheel. **Rating pop-ups** at scale 2 near the tip.\\n  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\\n- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\\n- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\\n- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\\n  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\\n  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\\n  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\\n- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \\\"all art and audio written in code\\\".\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f86dc2e8-d1ab-40f5-94ba-618526f5c6fb-24","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"730→\\n- ✔ `update()` does not run while `engine.paused` is true; it does run at `timeScale = 0`.\\n- `loadGame` clears HUD, music, loops, particles and lights; it keeps Input, volumes and look.\\n- `engine.settings.open()` is a mouse-driven DOM panel that pauses the engine: use it only on the touch-only path; build your own Settings.\\n- Start options: `aspect:'fill'`, `touch:false`, `settings:{ button:false, key: inSession ? false : '<slug>' }`, `background`, plus `withUrlOptions` for review flags.\\n- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\\n- Own URL flags outside a session, for tests: `?op= &stage= &diff= &seed= &bot= &god= &attract= &dev= &scene=`.\\n\\n---\\n740→\\n## 12. Balance\\n\\n**Dev Mode sliders (live, with Reset to Defaults).** All in `config.js`:\\n\\n- vitals drain ×, bleed drain, mistake penalty, max mistakes, time limit ×\\n- cursor speed, steady factor, aim assist, tool tolerance ×\\n- drain rate, laser burn time, syringe dose\\n- Composure gain per CLEAN, Quiet slow factor, Quiet drain, Second Look cost and seconds\\n- strain speed ×, strain HP ×, Dies Irae base BPM\\n750→- Code Blue zone width, co-op scale per seat\\n\\n**`node tests/balance.mjs`** runs each op on the bot at skills 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0 and prints time used, final vitals, mistakes and rank. Targets on Resident:\\n\\n| Bot skill | Should | |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 0 (idle, no input) | fail every op | |\\n| 0.4 | clear Ops 1 to 3, may lose bosses | a nervous beginner |\\n| 0.7 | clear all, mostly B or A, at least 20% clock left outside bosses | a decent player |\\n| 1.0 | S on all | sets `par` |\\n760→\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Testing\\n\\nOne command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and one count line. An optional filter (`sim`, `content`, `browser`, `hub`) lets you rerun only what you changed.\\n\\n**Node (fast, most tests):**\\n\\n- Each tool's rules, success and mistake paths.\\n770→- Every op: idle fails; bot 0.7 clears; determinism hash stable; retry-from-stage works.\\n- Code Blue paths, The Quiet's time scale, The Second Look's exact restore.\\n- Scoring and rank bounds.\\n- Slider apply and reset.\\n- Codec round trip and sizes at each op's peak.\\n- **Whole-game scripted playthrough:** `campaign.js` driven by the bot through every scene and op to credits, with save and unlock checks.\\n\\n**Content lint:**\\n\\n- Cast and sets referenced exist; every tool used; all text fits two wrapped lines at 342 art pixels wide; every character is in the font's set; glyph tokens valid.\\n780→- No `TODO` or placeholder strings; About has every field.\\n- No forbidden source names.\\n- `check.mjs --sheets` clean of problems.\\n\\n**Browser (Chromium, one or two at a time):** launch args ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`.\\n\\nSoftware WebGPU runs at 5 to 30 fps here; prefer the sim's state and `engine.step()` over waiting, and use a 960×540 viewport for logic. A pad stub:\\n```js\\nwindow.__pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', index:0, id:'stub', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0})), vibrationActuator:{ playEffect:()=>Promise.resolve('complete') } };\\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [window.__pad, null, null, null];   // add_init_script\\n790→```\\nCover:\\n\\n- The built page from `file://`: boots, no errors. Outside a session `AIHub.active` is false and `AIHub.seeded` is not true. Enter, Space, Enter, Space then still draws (the hub's own \\\"on its own\\\" check).\\n- Fresh profile: music slider 0.1.\\n- Menu navigation by pad stub, keys and mouse (hover moves focus).\\n- Prompts switch with the last device; the Xbox option swaps glyphs.\\n- A real drain and forceps action by mouse and by pad stub (the sim state changes at the aimed spot).\\n- Attract: idle 10 s starts it; key and pad each exit; save untouched.\\n- Touch-only with `p.devices['Pixel 7']`: the exact text, the ⚙, no joystick, attract runs.\\n800→- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes live config; reset restores it.\\n- Couch co-op with two stub pads: two independent tips.\\n- `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty throughout.\\n\\n**Sound:** render syllables and `SoundDef`s (`renderSound`) in Node: non-silent, finite. In the page, `audio.counts` rise while talking. An `AnalyserNode` level check on one voice line.\\n\\n**Hub:** copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` beside the built page in `dist/`. Serve **`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`**. ✔ The `-u` matters: when you read the port from a pipe without it, the line never arrives and your script hangs (this cost me about fifteen minutes). Stop that server by its PID. Run these with launch args plus `--no-sandbox`, a 1600×1000 viewport, and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`:\\n```\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\n810→harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2&scenario=server\\n```\\nAll must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\\n\\n**Kit tools** ✔ all work here after `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (about 1 to 3 s each): `node check.mjs` (serves on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port), `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys …`, `node check.mjs --sheets …`.\\n\\n**Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge**, at 1920×1080: each arena, each set, each bust, title, results, HUD readability. Look at them. Blank WebGPU canvases can happen; ✔ here `page.screenshot` captured every frame fine.\\n\\n820→---\\n\\n## 14. Build and packaging\\n\\n`tools/build.mjs` ✔ (this exact recipe gave a 6 MB page that booted from `file://` in about 1 s on software WebGPU):\\n\\n```js\\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['game.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=es2022','--outfile=dist/bundle.js']);\\nconst js = readFileSync('dist/bundle.js','utf8').replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script');\\nconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');           // verbatim: the hub compares it byte for byte\\n830→const pack = readFileSync('packs/kenney-furniture.json').toString('base64');\\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\\\n${session}\\\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\\n</head><body><div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-furniture.json':'data:application/json;base64,${pack}'};</script>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n${js}\\\\n</script></body></html>`;\\n```\\n\\n840→- The output name comes from your brief: one constant at the top of the script. Write `dist/game.html` for the tests and a copy where your brief wants the deliverable.\\n- Don't minify the HTML or touch the session client's text.\\n- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\\n- When you report research, say this plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; add anything you did yourself.\\n- For the exit-interview file your brief asks for, `aiHub.genre` is `Simulation`, `players` `1–4`, `series` `Trauma Center`. Good tags: `3d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Order of work\\n\\n850→Build in this order. Keep the game running and the tests green after each step.\\n\\n1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\\n2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\\n3. **All tools and the bot.** Scalpel, Laser, Scanner; Ops 2 and 3; Code Blue; The Quiet; bot and balance report; whole-op tests.\\n4. **The drama.** Busts, figures, sets, story stage, voices, sound effects, music director, results, saves. Eps 1 to 3 flow end to end.\\n5. **The shell.** Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch gate, About.\\n6. **Bosses and the rest.** Second Look, Bone Mend, transplant, Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me, Do No Harm, all scenes, campaign playthrough test.\\n7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\\n8. **Polish and balance.** Juice, feel, per-arena art, tune against the targets, full screenshot pass at 1080p, `docs/AUTHORING.md`.\\n860→9. **Finish.** Fill in About and your chat reply and exit-interview file as your brief says.\\n\\n**If you run short, cut whole content rather than leave anything half-made** (the brief forbids stubs). Cut in this order:\\n\\n1. The `RenderView` and `Mirror` touches.\\n2. Extra session fights (keep Pile-Up).\\n3. Op 3's third table.\\n4. Lacrimosa's crawling phase.\\n5. Op 6's cold-time bar.\\n\\n870→Never cut: Ops 1, 2, 5, 8, 9; both gifts; Code Blue; attract; Dev Mode; hub conformance; couch co-op.\\n\\n## 16. Done means\\n\\n| The brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\\n| Title by the brief's method | Yours, `src/core/meta.js` |\\n| One HTML, engine unmodified, session client verbatim | §14 |\\n| Native art plus new assets | §9 |\\n880→| Native animation plus new animations | §6, §9 (`HERO_CLIPS` on custom rigs, procedural tools) |\\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\\n| AI Hub integration and the game on its own | §7, §13 |\\n| Feature-complete demo showing every mechanic | §3, §5, §6 |\\n| World, characters, themes, tone, writing style | §2 |\\n| Infrastructure for more content with normal tools | §11, `docs/AUTHORING.md`, Dev Mode's Copy Op JSON |\\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | §8, §12 |\\n| Attract after 10 s, any input exits | §8 |\\n| Controller-first at 10 feet, native keyboard and mouse, prompts by last input, Xbox option | §4, §8 |\\n| No dense data screens | §8 |\",\"content_concise\":\"730→\\n- ✔ `update()` does not run while `engine.paused` is true; it does run at `timeScale = 0`.\\n- `loadGame` clears HUD, music, loops, particles and lights; it keeps Input, volumes and look.\\n- `engine.settings.open()` is a mouse-driven DOM panel that pauses the engine: use it only on the touch-only path; build your own Settings.\\n- Start options: `aspect:'fill'`, `touch:false`, `settings:{ button:false, key: inSession ? false : '<slug>' }`, `background`, plus `withUrlOptions` for review flags.\\n- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\\n- Own URL flags outside a session, for tests: `?op= &stage= &diff= &seed= &bot= &god= &attract= &dev= &scene=`.\\n\\n---\\n740→\\n## 12. Balance\\n\\n**Dev Mode sliders (live, with Reset to Defaults).** All in `config.js`:\\n\\n- vitals drain ×, bleed drain, mistake penalty, max mistakes, time limit ×\\n- cursor speed, steady factor, aim assist, tool tolerance ×\\n- drain rate, laser burn time, syringe dose\\n- Composure gain per CLEAN, Quiet slow factor, Quiet drain, Second Look cost and seconds\\n- strain speed ×, strain HP ×, Dies Irae base BPM\\n750→- Code Blue zone width, co-op scale per seat\\n\\n**`node tests/balance.mjs`** runs each op on the bot at skills 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0 and prints time used, final vitals, mistakes and rank. Targets on Resident:\\n\\n| Bot skill | Should | |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 0 (idle, no input) | fail every op | |\\n| 0.4 | clear Ops 1 to 3, may lose bosses | a nervous beginner |\\n| 0.7 | clear all, mostly B or A, at least 20% clock left outside bosses | a decent player |\\n| 1.0 | S on all | sets `par` |\\n760→\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Testing\\n\\nOne command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and one count line. An optional filter (`sim`, `content`, `browser`, `hub`) lets you rerun only what you changed.\\n\\n**Node (fast, most tests):**\\n\\n- Each tool's rules, success and mistake paths.\\n770→- Every op: idle fails; bot 0.7 clears; determinism hash stable; retry-from-stage works.\\n- Code Blue paths, The Quiet's time scale, The Second Look's exact restore.\\n- Scoring and rank bounds.\\n- Slider apply and reset.\\n- Codec round trip and sizes at each op's peak.\\n- **Whole-game scripted playthrough:** `campaign.js` driven by the bot through every scene and op to credits, with save and unlock checks.\\n\\n**Content lint:**\\n\\n- Cast and sets referenced exist; every tool used; all text fits two wrapped lines at 342 art pixels wide; every character is in the font's set; glyph tokens valid.\\n780→- No `TODO` or placeholder strings; About has every field.\\n- No forbidden source names.\\n- `check.mjs --sheets` clean of problems.\\n\\n**Browser (Chromium, one or two at a time):** launch args ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`.\\n\\nSoftware WebGPU runs at 5 to 30 fps here; prefer the sim's state and `engine.step()` over waiting, and use a 960×540 viewport for logic. A pad stub:\\n```js\\nwindow.__pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', index:0, id:'stub', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0})), vibrationActuator:{ playEffect:()=>Promise.resolve('complete') } };\\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [window.__pad, null, null, null];   // add_init_script\\n790→```\\nCover:\\n\\n- The built page from `file://`: boots, no errors. Outside a session `AIHub.active` is false and `AIHub.seeded` is not true. Enter, Space, Enter, Space then still draws (the hub's own \\\"on its own\\\" check).\\n- Fresh profile: music slider 0.1.\\n- Menu navigation by pad stub, keys and mouse (hover moves focus).\\n- Prompts switch with the last device; the Xbox option swaps glyphs.\\n- A real drain and forceps action by mouse and by pad stub (the sim state changes at the aimed spot).\\n- Attract: idle 10 s starts it; key and pad each exit; save untouched.\\n- Touch-only with `p.devices['Pixel 7']`: the exact text, the ⚙, no joystick, attract runs.\\n800→- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes live config; reset restores it.\\n- Couch co-op with two stub pads: two independent tips.\\n- `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty throughout.\\n\\n**Sound:** render syllables and `SoundDef`s (`renderSound`) in Node: non-silent, finite. In the page, `audio.counts` rise while talking. An `AnalyserNode` level check on one voice line.\\n\\n**Hub:** copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` beside the built page in `dist/`. Serve **`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`**. ✔ The `-u` matters: when you read the port from a pipe without it, the line never arrives and your script hangs (this cost me about fifteen minutes). Stop that server by its PID. Run these with launch args plus `--no-sandbox`, a 1600×1000 viewport, and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`:\\n```\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\n810→harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2&scenario=server\\n```\\nAll must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\\n\\n**Kit tools** ✔ all work here after `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (about 1 to 3 s each): `node check.mjs` (serves on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port), `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys …`, `node check.mjs --sheets …`.\\n\\n**Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge**, at 1920×1080: each arena, each set, each bust, title, results, HUD readability. Look at them. Blank WebGPU canvases can happen; ✔ here `page.screenshot` captured every frame fine.\\n\\n820→---\\n\\n## 14. Build and packaging\\n\\n`tools/build.mjs` ✔ (this exact recipe gave a 6 MB page that booted from `file://` in about 1 s on software WebGPU):\\n\\n```js\\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['game.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=es2022','--outfile=dist/bundle.js']);\\nconst js = readFileSync('dist/bundle.js','utf8').replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script');\\nconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');           // verbatim: the hub compares it byte for byte\\n830→const pack = readFileSync('packs/kenney-furniture.json').toString('base64');\\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\\\n${session}\\\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\\n</head><body><div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-furniture.json':'data:application/json;base64,${pack}'};</script>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n${js}\\\\n</script></body></html>`;\\n```\\n\\n840→- The output name comes from your brief: one constant at the top of the script. Write `dist/game.html` for the tests and a copy where your brief wants the deliverable.\\n- Don't minify the HTML or touch the session client's text.\\n- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\\n- When you report research, say this plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; add anything you did yourself.\\n- For the exit-interview file your brief asks for, `aiHub.genre` is `Simulation`, `players` `1–4`, `series` `Trauma Center`. Good tags: `3d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Order of work\\n\\n850→Build in this order. Keep the game running and the tests green after each step.\\n\\n1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\\n2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\\n3. **All tools and the bot.** Scalpel, Laser, Scanner; Ops 2 and 3; Code Blue; The Quiet; bot and balance report; whole-op tests.\\n4. **The drama.** Busts, figures, sets, story stage, voices, sound effects, music director, results, saves. Eps 1 to 3 flow end to end.\\n5. **The shell.** Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch gate, About.\\n6. **Bosses and the rest.** Second Look, Bone Mend, transplant, Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me, Do No Harm, all scenes, campaign playthrough test.\\n7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\\n8. **Polish and balance.** Juice, feel, per-arena art, tune against the targets, full screenshot pass at 1080p, `docs/AUTHORING.md`.\\n860→9. **Finish.** Fill in About and your chat reply and exit-interview file as your brief says.\\n\\n**If you run short, cut whole content rather than leave anything half-made** (the brief forbids stubs). Cut in this order:\\n\\n1. The `RenderView` and `Mirror` touches.\\n2. Extra session fights (keep Pile-Up).\\n3. Op 3's third table.\\n4. Lacrimosa's crawling phase.\\n5. Op 6's cold-time bar.\\n\\n870→Never cut: Ops 1, 2, 5, 8, 9; both gifts; Code Blue; attract; Dev Mode; hub conformance; couch co-op.\\n\\n## 16. Done means\\n\\n| The brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\\n| Title by the brief's method | Yours, `src/core/meta.js` |\\n| One HTML, engine unmodified, session client verbatim | §14 |\\n| Native art plus new assets | §9 |\\n880→| Native animation plus new animations | §6, §9 (`HERO_CLIPS` on custom rigs, procedural tools) |\\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\\n| AI Hub integration and the game on its own | §7, §13 |\\n| Feature-complete demo showing every mechanic | §3, §5, §6 |\\n| World, characters, themes, tone, writing style | §2 |\\n| Infrastructure for more content with normal tools | §11, `docs/AUTHORING.md`, Dev Mode's Copy Op JSON |\\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | §8, §12 |\\n| Attract after 10 s, any input exits | §8 |\\n| Controller-first at 10 feet, native keyboard and mouse, prompts by last input, Xbox option | §4, §8 |\\n| No dense data screens | §8 |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":730,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"\\n- ✔ `update()` does not run while `engine.paused` is true; it does run at `timeScale = 0`.\\n- `loadGame` clears HUD, music, loops, particles and lights; it keeps Input, volumes and look.\\n- `engine.settings.open()` is a mouse-driven DOM panel that pauses the engine: use it only on the touch-only path; build your own Settings.\\n- Start options: `aspect:'fill'`, `touch:false`, `settings:{ button:false, key: inSession ? false : '<slug>' }`, `background`, plus `withUrlOptions` for review flags.\\n- Saves: guarded `localStorage` under a versioned key. In a session the client hands you an empty store.\\n- `game.js` must import cleanly in Node for `check.mjs --headless`: guard `document`, `navigator.getGamepads` and `localStorage`.\\n- Own URL flags outside a session, for tests: `?op= &stage= &diff= &seed= &bot= &god= &attract= &dev= &scene=`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Balance\\n\\n**Dev Mode sliders (live, with Reset to Defaults).** All in `config.js`:\\n\\n- vitals drain ×, bleed drain, mistake penalty, max mistakes, time limit ×\\n- cursor speed, steady factor, aim assist, tool tolerance ×\\n- drain rate, laser burn time, syringe dose\\n- Composure gain per CLEAN, Quiet slow factor, Quiet drain, Second Look cost and seconds\\n- strain speed ×, strain HP ×, Dies Irae base BPM\\n- Code Blue zone width, co-op scale per seat\\n\\n**`node tests/balance.mjs`** runs each op on the bot at skills 0.4, 0.7 and 1.0 and prints time used, final vitals, mistakes and rank. Targets on Resident:\\n\\n| Bot skill | Should | |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 0 (idle, no input) | fail every op | |\\n| 0.4 | clear Ops 1 to 3, may lose bosses | a nervous beginner |\\n| 0.7 | clear all, mostly B or A, at least 20% clock left outside bosses | a decent player |\\n| 1.0 | S on all | sets `par` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Testing\\n\\nOne command: `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and one count line. An optional filter (`sim`, `content`, `browser`, `hub`) lets you rerun only what you changed.\\n\\n**Node (fast, most tests):**\\n\\n- Each tool's rules, success and mistake paths.\\n- Every op: idle fails; bot 0.7 clears; determinism hash stable; retry-from-stage works.\\n- Code Blue paths, The Quiet's time scale, The Second Look's exact restore.\\n- Scoring and rank bounds.\\n- Slider apply and reset.\\n- Codec round trip and sizes at each op's peak.\\n- **Whole-game scripted playthrough:** `campaign.js` driven by the bot through every scene and op to credits, with save and unlock checks.\\n\\n**Content lint:**\\n\\n- Cast and sets referenced exist; every tool used; all text fits two wrapped lines at 342 art pixels wide; every character is in the font's set; glyph tokens valid.\\n- No `TODO` or placeholder strings; About has every field.\\n- No forbidden source names.\\n- `check.mjs --sheets` clean of problems.\\n\\n**Browser (Chromium, one or two at a time):** launch args ✔ `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`.\\n\\nSoftware WebGPU runs at 5 to 30 fps here; prefer the sim's state and `engine.step()` over waiting, and use a 960×540 viewport for logic. A pad stub:\\n```js\\nwindow.__pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', index:0, id:'stub', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0})), vibrationActuator:{ playEffect:()=>Promise.resolve('complete') } };\\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [window.__pad, null, null, null];   // add_init_script\\n```\\nCover:\\n\\n- The built page from `file://`: boots, no errors. Outside a session `AIHub.active` is false and `AIHub.seeded` is not true. Enter, Space, Enter, Space then still draws (the hub's own \\\"on its own\\\" check).\\n- Fresh profile: music slider 0.1.\\n- Menu navigation by pad stub, keys and mouse (hover moves focus).\\n- Prompts switch with the last device; the Xbox option swaps glyphs.\\n- A real drain and forceps action by mouse and by pad stub (the sim state changes at the aimed spot).\\n- Attract: idle 10 s starts it; key and pad each exit; save untouched.\\n- Touch-only with `p.devices['Pixel 7']`: the exact text, the ⚙, no joystick, attract runs.\\n- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes live config; reset restores it.\\n- Couch co-op with two stub pads: two independent tips.\\n- `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty throughout.\\n\\n**Sound:** render syllables and `SoundDef`s (`renderSound`) in Node: non-silent, finite. In the page, `audio.counts` rise while talking. An `AnalyserNode` level check on one voice line.\\n\\n**Hub:** copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` beside the built page in `dist/`. Serve **`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`**. ✔ The `-u` matters: when you read the port from a pipe without it, the line never arrives and your script hangs (this cost me about fifteen minutes). Stop that server by its PID. Run these with launch args plus `--no-sandbox`, a 1600×1000 viewport, and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`:\\n```\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\\nharness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2&scenario=server\\n```\\nAll must give `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`.\\n\\n**Kit tools** ✔ all work here after `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder (about 1 to 3 s each): `node check.mjs` (serves on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port), `node check.mjs --headless game.js --keys …`, `node check.mjs --sheets …`.\\n\\n**Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge**, at 1920×1080: each arena, each set, each bust, title, results, HUD readability. Look at them. Blank WebGPU canvases can happen; ✔ here `page.screenshot` captured every frame fine.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Build and packaging\\n\\n`tools/build.mjs` ✔ (this exact recipe gave a 6 MB page that booted from `file://` in about 1 s on software WebGPU):\\n\\n```js\\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['game.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=es2022','--outfile=dist/bundle.js']);\\nconst js = readFileSync('dist/bundle.js','utf8').replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script');\\nconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');           // verbatim: the hub compares it byte for byte\\nconst pack = readFileSync('packs/kenney-furniture.json').toString('base64');\\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>\\\\n${session}\\\\n</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>${TITLE} — ${TAGLINE}</title> …description, theme-color, data-URL icon, hub:* tags…\\n</head><body><div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-furniture.json':'data:application/json;base64,${pack}'};</script>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\">\\\\n${js}\\\\n</script></body></html>`;\\n```\\n\\n- The output name comes from your brief: one constant at the top of the script. Write `dist/game.html` for the tests and a copy where your brief wants the deliverable.\\n- Don't minify the HTML or touch the session client's text.\\n- Also add `hub:type` Game, `hub:source` for the source, and an emblem icon as a data URL.\\n- When you report research, say this plan's planner read the source's Wikipedia page, the hub's protocol and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; add anything you did yourself.\\n- For the exit-interview file your brief asks for, `aiHub.genre` is `Simulation`, `players` `1–4`, `series` `Trauma Center`. Good tags: `3d`, `pixel art`, `story`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `comedy`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Order of work\\n\\nBuild in this order. Keep the game running and the tests green after each step.\\n\\n1. **Skeleton.** Unzip the kit and move the contents of its `pixel-engine/` folder to the dev folder root. `npm install playwright@1.63.0` there. Then: build script, test runner, an empty stage booting from `file://`, music default, input devices with pad stub test.\\n2. **One great op.** Sim core, tissue canvas, hand and tools, HUD, Drain, Forceps, Suture, Gel, Syringe, Op 1 playable on pad, mouse and keys. Make this feel wonderful before moving on.\\n3. **All tools and the bot.** Scalpel, Laser, Scanner; Ops 2 and 3; Code Blue; The Quiet; bot and balance report; whole-op tests.\\n4. **The drama.** Busts, figures, sets, story stage, voices, sound effects, music director, results, saves. Eps 1 to 3 flow end to end.\\n5. **The shell.** Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch gate, About.\\n6. **Bosses and the rest.** Second Look, Bone Mend, transplant, Introit, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae, Libera Me, Do No Harm, all scenes, campaign playthrough test.\\n7. **Consult.** Couch first (it proves the seats), then session, card, net, harness passes.\\n8. **Polish and balance.** Juice, feel, per-arena art, tune against the targets, full screenshot pass at 1080p, `docs/AUTHORING.md`.\\n9. **Finish.** Fill in About and your chat reply and exit-interview file as your brief says.\\n\\n**If you run short, cut whole content rather than leave anything half-made** (the brief forbids stubs). Cut in this order:\\n\\n1. The `RenderView` and `Mirror` touches.\\n2. Extra session fights (keep Pile-Up).\\n3. Op 3's third table.\\n4. Lacrimosa's crawling phase.\\n5. Op 6's cold-time bar.\\n\\nNever cut: Ops 1, 2, 5, 8, 9; both gifts; Code Blue; attract; Dev Mode; hub conformance; couch co-op.\\n\\n## 16. Done means\\n\\n| The brief asks for | Where |\\n|---|---|\\n| Genre and perspective chosen | §1 |\\n| Title by the brief's method | Yours, `src/core/meta.js` |\\n| One HTML, engine unmodified, session client verbatim | §14 |\\n| Native art plus new assets | §9 |\\n| Native animation plus new animations | §6, §9 (`HERO_CLIPS` on custom rigs, procedural tools) |\\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | §10 |\\n| AI Hub integration and the game on its own | §7, §13 |\\n| Feature-complete demo showing every mechanic | §3, §5, §6 |\\n| World, characters, themes, tone, writing style | §2 |\\n| Infrastructure for more content with normal tools | §11, `docs/AUTHORING.md`, Dev Mode's Copy Op JSON |\\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | §8, §12 |\\n| Attract after 10 s, any input exits | §8 |\\n| Controller-first at 10 feet, native keyboard and mouse, prompts by last input, Xbox option | §4, §8 |\\n| No dense data screens | §8 |\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"26acdfab-1cd6-43f9-8c83-7d36a91cb9f0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_46","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The implementation is very large.\n\nPlanning the bot's input strategy. Code blue requires charging when the needle is outside the zone and releasing when inside, with skill 0.5 or higher to avoid missing. Massage phase requires pressing sideL or sideR based on the desired action.\n\nGift holding logic: hold look when rewinding and composure covers the cost, or hold quiet when vitals drop below 35 and composure exceeds 25. The bot will target the nearest actionable entity on the active table, switching tables if necessary. Target priority is code and massage first, then droplets, open eyes, sob, living pores and cores, plates, bleeders, and pools.\n\nAdditional targets include clamps, fragments, incisions, tumors, wounds, gels, and hooks. Hidden entities require a scanner first. Rings are used when vitals fall below 50 and doses remain.\n\nThe suture algorithm positions the tool along the wound at slot.at offset by normal * ±0.45. It oscillates using a 0.45-second sine wave based on simulation time. The bot applies suture while moving.\n\nSuture detection triggers when the signed distance crosses zero, the amplitude is at least 0.25, and the tool is near the slot. Teleporting with place:true can skip a frame, but the step function checks only the current position, so alternating sides near the slot still registers as a crossing.\n\nSuture ties should be spaced roughly 0.4 seconds apart to avoid sloppy rhythm.\n\nScalpel pathing must not skip frames with place jumps, which would spike deviation. The bot should step along the path each frame at small intervals so maxAlong advances smoothly and deviation stays near zero. For circular paths, it will walk the polyline.\n\nForceps will grab by proximity and walk the path with place or seek, keeping mean deviation near zero. It auto-finishes at the end.\n\nMagnet movement is capped to speedLimit times 0.7 to prevent large jumps.\n\nFor fragments, the bot places on the fragment, uses to grab it, sets the angle to targetAng, then releases when use becomes false.\n\nGel painting requires visiting every cell center with use, since step 0.4 may leave neighbors unpainted.\n\nDrain targets the pool center and uses until finished.\n\nLaser targets an eye and uses until heat is depleted or the eye's health drops.\n\nThe bot must not hold use while traveling to avoid stray punishment. Scanner targets hidden entities by placing nearby and using once. Syringe targets rings by placing inside, using for 0.5 seconds, then releasing. Dressing walks its path like the scalpel. Diastole is skipped if the entity window is diastole and the phase is inactive. Plate sequence cuts with the scalpel, lifts with forceps, and burns with laser at the plate position; toolFor switches between steps. In introit, the pore appears at the strain position and takes priority over the core.\n\nWounds spawned after the strain dies are not in stage.spawned, so they persist into later stages. A suture stage with until kinds wound will clear them.\n\nUnsutured wounds are harmless bleeders and do not block strain death. Lacrimosa droplets should be drained when the laser is idle, since stray laser hits cause far more damage than minor vitals loss. A gel film can optionally catch droplets.\n\nThe bot will drain nearby droplets between each 1.2-second laser burn to reduce damage, since stray hits do not accumulate while the tool is idle. For Operation 6 \"Second Look,\" the planned sequence is: three clean composure actions to reach 60, an open incision, two clamps, two short cuts, and a kidney lift with forceps.\n\nThe Operation 6 plan now includes a donor fetch with forceps, three short sutures, and an unclamp step that triggers a clot. The bot holds the gift during this risky phase. A look action restores state from four seconds ago, but it does not restore the needRewind flag because that flag lives in persist. After rewinding, the unclamp succeeds on the next attempt.\n\nThe look action restores score, time, vitals, and entities. The -12 vitals loss from the clot is undone. A risk remains: if the snapshot predates the clamps being done, rewinding would lose progress and loop. The four-second history window may still contain the unclamp stage with clamps already finished if the bot acts quickly.\n\nA four-second history window risks restoring the bot to a mid-suture state, which would undo completed sutures. To prevent this, a pause stage could precede unclamp, or the bot could wait 4.5 seconds before attempting unclamp so the snapshot falls safely inside that stage.\n\nThe bot will wait until the current stage has advanced at least 4.5 seconds before attempting the first-clot unclamp. A `lookWouldStay` helper checks the history buffer for a snapshot from that point whose stage index matches the current one, ensuring the rewind target is inside the same stage and won't undo completed work.\n\nOperation 9 Sanctus begins with scanner and laser on eight real cysts. Fake cysts count as mistakes if hit. The stage ends when no real cysts remain and the sanctus dies. Lie status clears and vitals reset to 41.\n\nCysts spawn from the strain entity rather than the stage, so the stage until strain condition works correctly. The bot must scan first because laser skips hidden unmarked cysts. Seat 0 prefers right side and seat 1 prefers left side.\n\nFor Reprise, the plan uses both an explicit reprise strain and stage until strain. The reprise spawns a pore with life 4, an eye with 1 health and burn 1.0, and one plate. notePlate does not spawn additional plates; only die does. The plan requires three plates total.\n\nReprise will spawn three plates upfront instead of one at a time. The die condition fires when all plates are done, the pore is finished, and no living eyes remain.\n\nThe reprise eye has only one health point, so a single laser burn should kill it. However, `noteEyeLaser` appears to return early unless the strain name is \"lacrimosa\", which would prevent the eye from dying during Reprise.\n\nThe `noteEyeLaser` function returns early for non-lacrimosa strains, so Reprise eyes never get marked done. I will update it to decrement health and mark the eye finished when its health reaches zero.\n\nOperation 10 Miserere requires three incisions, then tethering hands two, then a code blue. The ghost punishes scalpel use on healthy tissue.\n\nThe bot will cut along the incision path so ghost replay stays near the target. A 4-second safe window after each cut prevents punishment if the ghost applies 3 seconds later. The bot remains within 0.85 of the incision to stay safe.\n\nAfter the three incisions, the tether spawns hands:2. Both seats must grab with forceps within 0.7 distance for 0.5 seconds. The test driver assigns seat 1 as a partner bot, so both bots seek the tether together.\n\nThe codeblue stage follows next. A dressing stage may also be included.\n\nOperation 10 uses the spine arena for slow extractions with vital and pain feedback, no attacks. The bot switches tables via input.table to match the active entity. Six fragments spawn, two hidden under pools until drained. Code blue tests drive the needle for success or stay idle for twelve seconds. Quiet tests compare time and vitals with and without the gift.\n\nThe Second Look test will verify that a look action restores state from four seconds ago, but the cursor stays at its current position because the restore step does not overwrite x or z. Determinism is guaranteed by identical seeds and inputs producing identical hashes. A compact snapshot codec will be designed for encoding and decoding. Rank bounds will be validated through rankFor tests. Slider controls will use applySlider and resetConfig.\n\nPar values will be calibrated by running skill 1.0 first and setting par to the resulting score. Tests will assert that this measured par equals the operation definition's par. Idle failures will be tested by advancing time with a small delta until the operation runs out of its time limit.\n\nOperation 3 drains vitals at 0.25 per second, so a skill of 0.7 leaves roughly 220 seconds before death. The resident already has one code blue left, so the operation fails either by vitals or by code blue timeout; God must not be set.\n\nSkill 0.7 is required when time remaining is at least 20 percent on non-boss operations. Bosses are excluded from this rule.\n\nThe campaign will consist of scenes, operations, a save log, and credits.\n\nStory text will use a specific font charset including letters, digits, punctuation marks, and spaces.\n\nStory text must stay within the font charset. Em dashes, unicode ellipses, and curly quotes are forbidden. Asterisk highlighting is allowed.\n\nLines will be kept at most 56 characters. A 57-character line wraps at 341 pixels, exceeding the 342-pixel limit.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6f0f77a-151d-4d6b-b29b-9902c41c06b7-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/game.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6f0f77a-151d-4d6b-b29b-9902c41c06b7-26","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function createGame|function start\\(|setVolume|renderSound|playMusic|frameView|hud\\.text|wasPressed","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/GUIDE.md","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6f0f77a-151d-4d6b-b29b-9902c41c06b7-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/index.html","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10193,"output_tokens":4369,"cache_read_input_tokens":73600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"b92cdc5c-1d19-4557-b799-e3becf6c245c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6f0f77a-151d-4d6b-b29b-9902c41c06b7-25","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n50→    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n60→    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n70→    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n80→    ctx.hud.clear();\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n50→    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n60→    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n70→    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n80→    ctx.hud.clear();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/game.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n    ctx.hud.clear();\\n\",\"total_lines\":103}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b6f0f77a-151d-4d6b-b29b-9902c41c06b7-26","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,