{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_54","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that hud.sprite exists for glyphs.\n\nStarting implementation across large files: sim fixes, bot, ops, codec, and tests. Also fixing reprise and noteEyeLaser. Reviewed stepScalpel for plates and confirmed no double-process bug.\n\nConfirmed plate liftPath pull length is correct. Forceps grab and pull after cut works properly. spawnPlate creates paths via makeEntity for plates with no existing path. Window nicks during systole while bot waits. Introit core life 3.5 and pull 2.5 are within acceptable timing.\n\nMissed introit knocks add bleed pools and faster vitals drop. The bot must hit all three cores to finish before time expires. Pore position updates only on spawn.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a42bf88d-549d-4f91-8c9b-22fa6bd980b7-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":88,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1398,"output_tokens":673,"cache_read_input_tokens":119296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"70d05509-1d3a-4f1e-8579-cfb1ab2026ff"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a42bf88d-549d-4f91-8c9b-22fa6bd980b7-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"88→### Tone rules\\n\\n90→- Short, breathless lines. Real-sounding jargon, delivered with total conviction.\\n- Tragedy and bathos sit side by side: a stage magician's comedy op turns into a cancer diagnosis in one line.\\n- In crisis, everyone shouts. Afterwards someone deflates it.\\n- Each beat is at most 2 lines of at most 60 characters. Display is uppercase (the engine's font). Allow `*word*` markup for a highlight colour.\\n\\nMore sample lines to set the voice:\\n\\n- Reyes, on a fall in vitals: \\\"He's losing blood faster than this hospital loses money. *Drain it.*\\\"\\n- Reyes, after a streak: \\\"...Adequate. Don't let it go to your head. It's not attached to anything useful.\\\"\\n- Ilya: \\\"It moved. Nurse Reyes, the liver moved.\\\" Reyes: \\\"Livers do not move, Doctor.\\\" Ilya: \\\"This one *knocked*.\\\"\\n100→- Sabine, over the intercom: \\\"Don't answer it until you're ready.\\\"\\n- Pem: \\\"Vitals are in the basement. I'd take the stairs, Doctor.\\\"\\n- Hesper: \\\"No one should hurt, Doctor. Not even you.\\\"\\n\\n### Story beats\\n\\nWrite each scene from its beat, 8 to 16 lines each.\\n\\n| Ep | Scene (set) | Beats | Then |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n110→| 1 | Night shift (OR-7) | Storm. Chief unreachable. \\\"You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.\\\" Deckhand Tomasz Dolan, eleven hooks. \\\"How do you get eleven fishhooks in one arm?\\\" \\\"It was a long net.\\\" | Op 1 |\\n| 2 | Morning rounds (ward) | Ilya fumbles rounds. Pem jokes. \\\"The Great Zamboni\\\", a stage magician, swallowed something during his act and won't say what. | Op 2. Mid-op the comedy dies: \\\"...That one isn't a prop.\\\" |\\n| 3 | Mass casualty (corridor) | A ferry collision. Three tables, one doctor. Bram's hand shakes as he hands Ilya the charts. | Op 3. The Quiet awakens |\\n| 4 | Aftermath (Chief's office) | Bram: \\\"How long did the room go quiet?\\\" He knows. The Foundation has complained to the board, so a consultant arrives: Dr. Achterberg. She audits Ilya on teen ferry survivor Ollie Brandt. | Op 4, with her on the gallery intercom |\\n| 5 | The smiling ward (ward) | Harbour pilot Mr. Anselm has an abdomen like a bag of knives and feels nothing. \\\"Isn't it wonderful?\\\" | Op 5. Something knocks. Sabine goes silent, then: \\\"Get it out.\\\" |\\n| 6 | The file (scrub room) | Sabine has seen this: the relief camp where she was blamed. MERC-Y named at last. She takes the next case herself. **Player becomes Sabine.** | Op 6. A dormant strain in a donor kidney from the Foundation's own bank |\\n| 7 | The visit (atrium, then ward) | Hesper arrives with flowers and a funding offer. Soft threat. Then Reyes's oldest friend, hospice nurse Ottilie Marr, is admitted, smiling. | Op 7. Ottilie feels pain again and thanks them for it. Reyes cries once, alone |\\n| 8 | The confession (Chief's office) | Bram confesses he co-wrote the paper. Hesper's plan: aerosol Mercy on the harbour ferries at dawn. Bram collapses; his tremor was Mercy all along, feeding his Quiet. | Op 8, on his beating heart. \\\"Don't you dare be gentle.\\\" He gives Ilya his old scalpel |\\n| 9 | The roof (helipad, rain) | Ilya and Sabine stop the release. Hesper, unarmed: \\\"You can't cure me of being right.\\\" The canister breaches. Reyes shields a patient and takes the full dose. She tells them to start without her, and falls. | Op 9. **No voice in your ear.** After the save, the comm strip finally speaks: \\\"...Your sutures are crooked, Doctor.\\\" |\\n| 10 | The stretcher (OR-7) | Hesper arrives dying. She took Mercy first, eleven years ago, so she'd never ask anything of others she wouldn't take herself. Everyone looks at Ilya. \\\"Scrub in.\\\" | Op 10. She feels pain for the first time in eleven years. \\\"Why?\\\" \\\"Because it's my shift.\\\" |\\n120→| End | Morning (roof) | The rain stops. Reyes, in a wheelchair: \\\"You've got a seven a.m.\\\" Shift Report (all ranks), credits | Back to title. Log unlocked |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Operating: the core game\\n\\n### The field and the cursor\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"88→### Tone rules\\n\\n90→- Short, breathless lines. Real-sounding jargon, delivered with total conviction.\\n- Tragedy and bathos sit side by side: a stage magician's comedy op turns into a cancer diagnosis in one line.\\n- In crisis, everyone shouts. Afterwards someone deflates it.\\n- Each beat is at most 2 lines of at most 60 characters. Display is uppercase (the engine's font). Allow `*word*` markup for a highlight colour.\\n\\nMore sample lines to set the voice:\\n\\n- Reyes, on a fall in vitals: \\\"He's losing blood faster than this hospital loses money. *Drain it.*\\\"\\n- Reyes, after a streak: \\\"...Adequate. Don't let it go to your head. It's not attached to anything useful.\\\"\\n- Ilya: \\\"It moved. Nurse Reyes, the liver moved.\\\" Reyes: \\\"Livers do not move, Doctor.\\\" Ilya: \\\"This one *knocked*.\\\"\\n100→- Sabine, over the intercom: \\\"Don't answer it until you're ready.\\\"\\n- Pem: \\\"Vitals are in the basement. I'd take the stairs, Doctor.\\\"\\n- Hesper: \\\"No one should hurt, Doctor. Not even you.\\\"\\n\\n### Story beats\\n\\nWrite each scene from its beat, 8 to 16 lines each.\\n\\n| Ep | Scene (set) | Beats | Then |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n110→| 1 | Night shift (OR-7) | Storm. Chief unreachable. \\\"You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.\\\" Deckhand Tomasz Dolan, eleven hooks. \\\"How do you get eleven fishhooks in one arm?\\\" \\\"It was a long net.\\\" | Op 1 |\\n| 2 | Morning rounds (ward) | Ilya fumbles rounds. Pem jokes. \\\"The Great Zamboni\\\", a stage magician, swallowed something during his act and won't say what. | Op 2. Mid-op the comedy dies: \\\"...That one isn't a prop.\\\" |\\n| 3 | Mass casualty (corridor) | A ferry collision. Three tables, one doctor. Bram's hand shakes as he hands Ilya the charts. | Op 3. The Quiet awakens |\\n| 4 | Aftermath (Chief's office) | Bram: \\\"How long did the room go quiet?\\\" He knows. The Foundation has complained to the board, so a consultant arrives: Dr. Achterberg. She audits Ilya on teen ferry survivor Ollie Brandt. | Op 4, with her on the gallery intercom |\\n| 5 | The smiling ward (ward) | Harbour pilot Mr. Anselm has an abdomen like a bag of knives and feels nothing. \\\"Isn't it wonderful?\\\" | Op 5. Something knocks. Sabine goes silent, then: \\\"Get it out.\\\" |\\n| 6 | The file (scrub room) | Sabine has seen this: the relief camp where she was blamed. MERC-Y named at last. She takes the next case herself. **Player becomes Sabine.** | Op 6. A dormant strain in a donor kidney from the Foundation's own bank |\\n| 7 | The visit (atrium, then ward) | Hesper arrives with flowers and a funding offer. Soft threat. Then Reyes's oldest friend, hospice nurse Ottilie Marr, is admitted, smiling. | Op 7. Ottilie feels pain again and thanks them for it. Reyes cries once, alone |\\n| 8 | The confession (Chief's office) | Bram confesses he co-wrote the paper. Hesper's plan: aerosol Mercy on the harbour ferries at dawn. Bram collapses; his tremor was Mercy all along, feeding his Quiet. | Op 8, on his beating heart. \\\"Don't you dare be gentle.\\\" He gives Ilya his old scalpel |\\n| 9 | The roof (helipad, rain) | Ilya and Sabine stop the release. Hesper, unarmed: \\\"You can't cure me of being right.\\\" The canister breaches. Reyes shields a patient and takes the full dose. She tells them to start without her, and falls. | Op 9. **No voice in your ear.** After the save, the comm strip finally speaks: \\\"...Your sutures are crooked, Doctor.\\\" |\\n| 10 | The stretcher (OR-7) | Hesper arrives dying. She took Mercy first, eleven years ago, so she'd never ask anything of others she wouldn't take herself. Everyone looks at Ilya. \\\"Scrub in.\\\" | Op 10. She feels pain for the first time in eleven years. \\\"Why?\\\" \\\"Because it's my shift.\\\" |\\n120→| End | Morning (roof) | The rain stops. Reyes, in a wheelchair: \\\"You've got a seven a.m.\\\" Shift Report (all ranks), credits | Back to title. Log unlocked |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Operating: the core game\\n\\n### The field and the cursor\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":88,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"### Tone rules\\n\\n- Short, breathless lines. Real-sounding jargon, delivered with total conviction.\\n- Tragedy and bathos sit side by side: a stage magician's comedy op turns into a cancer diagnosis in one line.\\n- In crisis, everyone shouts. Afterwards someone deflates it.\\n- Each beat is at most 2 lines of at most 60 characters. Display is uppercase (the engine's font). Allow `*word*` markup for a highlight colour.\\n\\nMore sample lines to set the voice:\\n\\n- Reyes, on a fall in vitals: \\\"He's losing blood faster than this hospital loses money. *Drain it.*\\\"\\n- Reyes, after a streak: \\\"...Adequate. Don't let it go to your head. It's not attached to anything useful.\\\"\\n- Ilya: \\\"It moved. Nurse Reyes, the liver moved.\\\" Reyes: \\\"Livers do not move, Doctor.\\\" Ilya: \\\"This one *knocked*.\\\"\\n- Sabine, over the intercom: \\\"Don't answer it until you're ready.\\\"\\n- Pem: \\\"Vitals are in the basement. I'd take the stairs, Doctor.\\\"\\n- Hesper: \\\"No one should hurt, Doctor. Not even you.\\\"\\n\\n### Story beats\\n\\nWrite each scene from its beat, 8 to 16 lines each.\\n\\n| Ep | Scene (set) | Beats | Then |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | Night shift (OR-7) | Storm. Chief unreachable. \\\"You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.\\\" Deckhand Tomasz Dolan, eleven hooks. \\\"How do you get eleven fishhooks in one arm?\\\" \\\"It was a long net.\\\" | Op 1 |\\n| 2 | Morning rounds (ward) | Ilya fumbles rounds. Pem jokes. \\\"The Great Zamboni\\\", a stage magician, swallowed something during his act and won't say what. | Op 2. Mid-op the comedy dies: \\\"...That one isn't a prop.\\\" |\\n| 3 | Mass casualty (corridor) | A ferry collision. Three tables, one doctor. Bram's hand shakes as he hands Ilya the charts. | Op 3. The Quiet awakens |\\n| 4 | Aftermath (Chief's office) | Bram: \\\"How long did the room go quiet?\\\" He knows. The Foundation has complained to the board, so a consultant arrives: Dr. Achterberg. She audits Ilya on teen ferry survivor Ollie Brandt. | Op 4, with her on the gallery intercom |\\n| 5 | The smiling ward (ward) | Harbour pilot Mr. Anselm has an abdomen like a bag of knives and feels nothing. \\\"Isn't it wonderful?\\\" | Op 5. Something knocks. Sabine goes silent, then: \\\"Get it out.\\\" |\\n| 6 | The file (scrub room) | Sabine has seen this: the relief camp where she was blamed. MERC-Y named at last. She takes the next case herself. **Player becomes Sabine.** | Op 6. A dormant strain in a donor kidney from the Foundation's own bank |\\n| 7 | The visit (atrium, then ward) | Hesper arrives with flowers and a funding offer. Soft threat. Then Reyes's oldest friend, hospice nurse Ottilie Marr, is admitted, smiling. | Op 7. Ottilie feels pain again and thanks them for it. Reyes cries once, alone |\\n| 8 | The confession (Chief's office) | Bram confesses he co-wrote the paper. Hesper's plan: aerosol Mercy on the harbour ferries at dawn. Bram collapses; his tremor was Mercy all along, feeding his Quiet. | Op 8, on his beating heart. \\\"Don't you dare be gentle.\\\" He gives Ilya his old scalpel |\\n| 9 | The roof (helipad, rain) | Ilya and Sabine stop the release. Hesper, unarmed: \\\"You can't cure me of being right.\\\" The canister breaches. Reyes shields a patient and takes the full dose. She tells them to start without her, and falls. | Op 9. **No voice in your ear.** After the save, the comm strip finally speaks: \\\"...Your sutures are crooked, Doctor.\\\" |\\n| 10 | The stretcher (OR-7) | Hesper arrives dying. She took Mercy first, eleven years ago, so she'd never ask anything of others she wouldn't take herself. Everyone looks at Ilya. \\\"Scrub in.\\\" | Op 10. She feels pain for the first time in eleven years. \\\"Why?\\\" \\\"Because it's my shift.\\\" |\\n| End | Morning (roof) | The rain stops. Reyes, in a wheelchair: \\\"You've got a seven a.m.\\\" Shift Report (all ranks), credits | Back to title. Log unlocked |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Operating: the core game\\n\\n### The field and the cursor\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"339e78ca-45a3-44e1-ada4-7ee5597d2fe6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_55","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The story will be written with 8 to 12 short lines per scene.\n\nThe suture system requires at least two frames per stitch. A 0.4-second interval equals 24 frames. A 1.2-unit wound needs three slots.\n\nShort wounds of 0.6 units need only two stitches. Anastomoses and the Bleeder are suture-like wounds. The gel paint logic checks coverage correctly after painting. Sob checks coverage even when unpainted this frame. Film entities act as radius catchers without creating cells.\n\nThe bot will skip film entities entirely since they lack cells. Droplet loss is acceptable.\n\nLacrimosa stalk spawns immediately after the third sob when no living remain. It pulls in subsequent frames and dies once its stage ends.\n\nThe first sob triggers a second sob immediately in the same tick because the eye is still alive and the phase has not yet shifted to sob. The third sob then spawns the Lacrimosa stalk.\n\nThe bot will paint each sob for about one second, keeping eye health at six. Eye health resets are safe without continuous laser. Reprise eye and three plates need fixes. The reprise pore expires in four frames and blocks wounds if it does. The bot will split seats zero and one by side: right for the pore, left for the eye.\n\nPlates will be spawned with alternating sides so each seat can safely target one. Seat zero will claim even-numbered entities and seat one odd-numbered ones, plus a side filter to prevent overlap.\n\nA `claim` helper prevents seat overlap by checking side preferences. The pore and two plates go to seat zero. Seat one handles the eye and the remaining plate. Dies plates have no side and can be claimed by either seat. Sanctus cysts are split by side, so both seats scan hidden cysts while laser targets their own side.\n\nFake cysts are marked with real=false and are skipped by the bot regardless of side. The scanner will prioritize hidden entities that belong to the bot's claim once the scanner is unlocked. Introit does not require scanning to complete. A clotReady helper is being added to select the best historical entry within the look window.\n\nThe `clotReady` helper checks that a historical sample matches the current stage index and that composure covers the look cost. If the unclamp is firstClot but the sample is missing or composure is too low, the bot skips that entity or idles. Waiting four seconds from stage start may not guarantee a valid sample if the history was recorded before the stage began.\n\nWaiting 4.5 seconds from stage start guarantees a valid historical sample exists within the look window. Vitals drain during idle, which is acceptable. The look latch stays active after a look until the gift is released; needRewind clears immediately after the look, so the gift is returned and the latch resets on the next frame. Restore may revert to a sample four seconds ago within the same stage, but unclamp remains incomplete.\n\nThe bot will not quiet during the look wait because composure stays high from prior cleans. Sabine seats all have look, but only seat zero is human, so the bot drives seat zero for gift look. In Op 9, seat zero remains quiet while seat one looks; forced rewind belongs to Op 6, and code blue is scripted.\n\nTag doctors will swap which seat is human. The couch player controls seat zero, and the tag input routes control to the other seat as bot. Tests explicitly drive both seats with botInput, so the tag does not affect balance.\n\nTag will toggle `focusSeat` so the other seat becomes bot-driven. In game, human seats receive device input while non-human seats are driven by bot; Op 9 sets seat one as non-human. Consult mode makes all seats human and reads pads, with couch tests using two browser pads. The coop scale formula applies only when consult is true.\n\nPile-up will be tested solo for the balance table, since consult mode raises drain and the skill 0.7 test already covers it. Consult tests will only verify two seats exist and gifts alternate. Session is excluded from the balance table. Par values are stored on each operation definition.\n\nHash stability will be verified by running 120 frames twice and confirming identical hashes.\n\nThe codec must stay under 1100 unreliable bytes during skill 0.7 play. It will drop finished entities, cap the list at 24 entries, and prefer unfinished ones. A 24-entity estimate yields roughly 720 bytes plus header.\n\nKeyframe JSON is capped at 16KB to prevent oversized gel cells and long path arrays.\n\nIf a keyframe exceeds the 16KB limit, its paths will be stripped and only gameplay-critical fields retained. A compact round-trip format will use string IDs and a `full` flag to preserve x, z, done, r, pulled, vitals, time, score, and stage. The codec will expose `encodeState`, `decodeState`, and `bytesOf` for validation. Peak memory during play will be measured by stepping the operation and checking the encoded size.\n\nA 32-bit coarse bitset will represent gel masks in snapshots, letting the view draw generic shapes without storing full paths. Entity indices will be used as stable identifiers for decoding. A bug was found where stepScalpel processes every started incision each frame even when the scalpel tool is active on one. The noteEyeLaser logic and reprise plate spawning also need fixing.\n\nThe bot must finish each started incision before starting another. Leaving a cut unfinished causes the cursor to drift too far, triggering a MISTAKE and pool. The scalpel tool does not require continuous use to keep an incision active, so the bot completes one path in one go.\n\nThe simulation will track only the closest scalpel target. Passing near a second incision start would accidentally begin a second cut, so limiting to one active target prevents this.\n\nThe scalpel step will now scan all eligible incisions but only act on the nearest one within a 0.55 tolerance range, or on any already started cut still under 0.8 deviation. This prevents accidental starts when passing near multiple targets.\n\nThe scalpel logic now processes only the single best target each frame. If the cursor wanders too far from a started cut, it may begin a second one while the first remains stuck in an unfinished state.\n\nThe bot will keep the started scalpel cut as its goal until it is finished, preventing the stage from stalling. The suture tool will also be limited to the nearest wound within a 1.5 tolerance range, and overlapping wounds will be spaced apart.\n\nGel targets will be spaced to prevent simultaneous completion. The `maxAlong` field will initialize to zero inside `makeEntity`. A helper for operation definitions is being drafted to reduce verbosity. Code will be written in parallel batches.\n\nA `hook` helper is being added to generate hook entities with default physics values. Par values will be exposed as a mutable export and set via a `setPar(id, n)` function so tests can read `op.par`. The test suite will run calibration first. Total simulation steps across all operations and skills are estimated at roughly 600k to 237k, which is acceptable for the available runtime.\n\nOperation durations are being estimated to fit within the 360-second time limit. Op 7 eyes take roughly 30 seconds, Op 8 around 40 seconds, and Op 5 introit about 40 seconds including its 18-second wait between knocks. Op 6 needs only 288 seconds because it is not a boss. The idle test will run for 240 seconds at 0.25-second timesteps, totaling 960 steps.\n\nThe idle test will run 10,000 steps total. Some operations fail earlier on vitals code blue after 12 seconds. Bot play must use a 1/60 second timestep because scalpel placement and suture intervals depend on sim.t advancing by exactly one frame each call. The code blue countdown uses real dt in stepCode, while the clock uses simDt.\n\nA timing mismatch was found in the suture logic. The bot uses real dt for its interval check, but quiet mode advances sim.t by only 0.1 seconds per call while the bot assumes 0.4 seconds passed. This causes sloppy stitches during quiet. The fix is to base the suture wait on sim.t instead of real dt.\n\nThe first suture stitch can fire immediately after the amp builds, then waits 0.42 seconds between crosses. Laser burn slows fourfold during quiet but still completes. Quiet mode also slows pore timers and scalpel placement, which helps the player by extending the introit window.\n\nQuiet mode will be disabled for the bot during suture, sob, and plate operations so ratings stay CLEAN. The bot will only use quiet in a manual unit test. Vitals must survive without quiet, so drain and speed are being tuned to keep them above 20. Op 3 table C loses about five vitals over roughly twenty seconds. Op 9 starts at forty-one vitals; sixty seconds of rest would drain twenty-one, leaving twenty, though mistakes could still kill the patient.\n\nThe bot will inject whenever vitals drop below forty-five and a ring exists with doses remaining. Op 9 needs a persistent ring spawned at stage one, since stepSyringe never marks it done and the stage would otherwise stall on an unfinished entity.\n\nStage clear logic will treat optional entities as finished, so rings can remain in the spawn list without blocking completion. Non-optional entities such as dressing must still be done. Ongoing pools must also be resolved before the stage can clear.\n\nDroplets are excluded from the spawned check because they are not in the spawn list, so they do not block strain. Nicks are optional and do not block stage clear. The firstClot pool is spawned by tryUnclamp and is absent from the stage list, so it disappears after rewind. Unclamps must be handled in order zero through two; the bot will pick the lowest unfinished unclamp first. Closing clamps can be done in any order.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-619b866a-12db-4713-9fb0-5bc668eb2a35-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"createGame|headless","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/check.mjs","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1823,"output_tokens":5269,"cache_read_input_tokens":120576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"1d43fde7-39a1-4410-bfe0-bfd22e4e3b88"}
