{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_67","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot gets stuck holding h11 at the end of the path. The pulled value stays zero.\n\nThe log shows h1 pulled zero, not h11. The bot is stuck at the same position from frame 60 to 160. The along metric may not match because the entity is not on the path. Hook pull length is 0.71. A deviance greater than one could tear and release the hook.\n\nThe hook did not release, so the deviance stayed within one. The pulled value is not increasing because the along metric is not advancing. The arcPath function may be looping near itself, causing the bot to think it is at the start of the path while visually at the end.\n\nThe arcPath function is being inspected to verify its endpoint logic. The bot may be failing the holding check in pathAim because it targets a different entity than the one currently held. I will log h11's pulled value, deviance, free status, path length, seat._along, and the input position relative to the path end.\n\nThe bot switched from holding h6 to h11 without finishing the previous hook. The pulled progress should have persisted, so it is unclear why h6 never completed.\n\nThe bot's `_along` value resets whenever `_pathId` changes. This causes the progress to restart on the new hook and prevents the previous one from finishing. The `pickEntity` function also favors nearby hooks, which triggers these switches before the current pull completes.\n\nThe `>= 0` check on `seat.holding` fails because the value is a string ID, so the bot never locks onto a held hook. I will replace it with a proper null or -1 guard. The bot should also prioritize the currently held entity in `pickEntity`, and remain committed to a scalpel once started, or to a suture wound while stitching.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab24f096-26e3-4270-b0c5-82e322025968-71","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev