{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_80","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tool runs once at the start position. Movement occurs on later frames without tool execution.\n\nOnly one tool trace appears. stepForceps likely returns early because held.path is missing, so the trace never records.\n\nreleaseHold does not return early when using is false. The string 'h1' coerces to NaN, so the check seat.holding < 0 fails. The function proceeds to clear holding.\n\nThe log shows holding stays h1, so using is true. The tool is forceps, so stepForceps should execute. I am re-examining applyTools to find why it does not run.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. Because `seat.holding` is the string `'h1'`, the expression `'h1' >= 0` evaluates to false. This makes `held` null even though the seat still holds the item. The code then skips the trace and returns early, so stepForceps never executes again.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-478ea0fe-4c48-4241-8710-b62dcf8e4952-86","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"holding","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":529,"output_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":194688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"4c450b62-eefb-4637-9694-3209915b3645"}
