"    id: 'op5',\"},{\"line_number\":263,\"content\":\"      { say: 'It knocked.', strain: 'introit', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":563,\"content\":\"  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op5'), 0.34),\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"aec2ec5c-5522-41f9-9591-934a9a1f2eb6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_94","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The pathT rate calculation equals zero.\n\nOver six seconds the pathT index advances by 2.4 segments. The loop points are spaced roughly 2.5 units apart, so the bot would need to hold the strain for the full duration to land consecutive knocks. The bot instead acts quickly: it cuts the pore immediately and pulls the core, which changes the timing.\n\nThe bot likely finishes each pore-and-core pair in about one second. That leaves six seconds between knocks, so the strain moves 2.4 segments and the knocks should be well spaced. The six wounds are actually three pairs of two close hits within each knock, not overlaps between separate knocks.\n\nThe two wounds per knock are too close together. Their midpoints are only about 0.4 units apart, which causes the suture to zigzag across the second wound. The fix is to space them at least 1.6 units apart.\n\nThe new wound positions are chosen to place their midpoints about 2.46 units apart. One will be a horizontal cut at (s.x - 1.6, s.z - 0.2) and the other a vertical cut at (s.x + 1.3, s.z - 0.8). Miss wounds should also be spaced when multiple occur near the same spot.\n\nMiss wounds at the knock site are acceptable because the next knock is six seconds away. Only one wound per miss occurs, so stacking is not a concern. Pools drain rather than being sutured.\n\nWounds do not set a `started` flag, so the bot's lock key depends only on cursor distance. At 2.4 units between the two wounds, the distance penalty is just 0.048, which is negligible compared to the rank difference of 24. The closer wound therefore wins the pick, though the cursor may briefly snap to the farther one while moving between them.\n\nLocking the suture target prevents the cursor from switching mid-stitch. The nearest-wound logic still selects the correct target because the two wounds are far enough apart. Other operations will be checked for similar spacing issues. Locking will also be added to pickEntity.\n\nThe `_su.id` lock is assigned in `sutureAim`, which runs after `pickEntity`, so the lock takes effect on the next frame. It only applies when the wound is on the active table; otherwise it is ignored. This prevents the cursor from switching to a different table, but it also means pools and other high-rank entities will be skipped while a suture is locked.\n\nThe suture lock should only apply to wounds. If a pool or other high-priority entity appears during suturing, it must take precedence. The revised logic checks for higher-rank targets inside the pick loop and only falls back to the locked wound when no better option exists.\n\nThe suture lock breaks automatically when a higher-priority entity appears, and the bot returns to the unfinished wound on its next pass. No reset is needed.\n\nThere is also a concern that `sutureAim` may misalign the cursor with the slot position because it normalizes the wound direction by its length before adding the 0.48-unit amplitude offset.\n\nThe suture cursor placement aligns correctly with the slot position. The flip logic works: it starts at side 1, crosses to -1 after 0.45 seconds, and holds there. This succeeded for one slot on s3 but stalled when oscillating with a neighbor. I will apply the spacing and lock fixes and re-run op5.\n\nMiss wound spacing is unnecessary at full skill. The stage has 360 seconds, so suturing six wounds should take about five seconds plus travel time. I also need to check whether any pools remain, since the stage only clears once both wounds and pools are handled.\n\nThe initial `_su.id` of 0 is harmless because it is overwritten after the first suture. Op 1 and op 9 wounds will be left unchanged if skill 1 already cleared them. The next step is to apply the fixes and run op5. After that, all skills must be tested across every operation, which will take considerable time.\n\nOp5 stalls at the 360-second limit, which explains its slowness. Once fixed, each operation should finish in about ten to thirty simulation seconds, or roughly six hundred to eighteen hundred frames, so the full sweep remains fast enough.\n\nThe remaining work is large but mechanical: writing tests and run.mjs, calibrating parameters, and building out the story, audio, view, game shell, hub, build pipeline, and evidence files. I will read the relevant PLAN sections first to ensure correct implementation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5ec6b97d-f747-430a-b3c6-35d318722b8f-14","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/strains.js","old_string":"      s.hp -= 1;\n      sim.flags.knocked = true;\n      add(sim, { kind: 'wound', x: s.x - 0.4, z: s.z, len: 0.9, dx: 1, dz: 0 });\n      add(sim, { kind: 'wound', x: s.x + 0.3, z: s.z - 0.2, len: 0.8, dx: 0.2, dz: 1 });","new_string":"      s.hp -= 1;\n      sim.flags.knocked = true;\n      // Pair stays far enough apart that a suture zigzag cannot change which wound is nearest.\n      add(sim, { kind: 'wound', x: s.x - 1.7, z: s.z - 0.15, len: 0.9, dx: 1, dz: 0 });\n      add(sim, { kind: 'wound', x: s.x + 1.35, z: s.z - 0.9, len: 0.8, dx: 0, dz: 1 });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5ec6b97d-f747-430a-b3c6-35d318722b8f-15","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"function pickEntity(sim, seat) {\n  if (seat.holding != null && seat.holding !== -1) {\n    const held = sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === seat.holding && !e.done);\n    if (held) return held;\n  }\n  let best = null;\n  let bestKey = 1e9;\n  for (const e of sim.entities) {","new_string":"function sutureLock(sim, seat) {\n  const id = seat._su && seat._su.id;\n  if (!id) return null;\n  const locked = sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === id && !e.done && (e.kind === 'wound' || e.kind === 'bleeder'));\n  if (!locked || (locked.table || 0) !== (sim.active || 0)) return null;\n  return locked;\n}\n\nfunction pickEntity(sim, seat) {\n  if (seat.holding != null && seat.holding !== -1) {\n    const held = sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === seat.holding && !e.done);\n    if (held) return held;\n  }\n  let best = null;\n  let bestKey = 1e9;\n  for (const e of sim.entities) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5ec6b97d-f747-430a-b3c6-35d318722b8f-16","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/bot.js","old_string":"    if (key < bestKey) {\n      bestKey = key;\n      best = e;\n    }\n  }\n  return best;\n}","new_string":"    if (key < bestKey) {\n      bestKey = key;\n      best = e;\n    }\n  }\n  const locked = sutureLock(sim, seat);\n  if (locked && (!best || (RANK[best.kind] ?? 30) >= RANK.wound)) return locked;\n  return best;\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42955,"output_tokens":3648,"cache_read_input_tokens":10112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"53933a15-7c47-49a5-869b-40057db91e97"}
