{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_130","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the test runner. It will be long but that is acceptable.\n\nThe test runner will be placed in tests/run.mjs. It needs a rankFor import from score.js. The suture test is being designed to avoid flakiness. The logic places a suture at the midpoint and waits before crossing to the opposite side.\n\nThe suture test timing is now fully mapped. The first frame at +z sets sideSign to 1 with no flip. The jump to -z triggers a clean tie at slot 0 after 0.45 seconds. After waiting on the negative side, the second cross occurs at slot 1.\n\nThe second cross at slot 1 triggers a clean tie if the cursor stays on the negative side for 0.45 seconds. The nearest wound cutoff is satisfied by both suture positions. A syringe test will place a ring at the origin and use the syringe tool for half a second.\n\nThe remaining tests are now mapped out. A vitals +18 dose at the origin scores CLEAN. An outside dose at 3,3 scores SLOPPY. A laser on a polyp at 0,0 for 0.7 seconds with a 0.75 hold is CLEAN. A stray laser shot without targets scores MISTAKE. The scanner test places within 2.2 of a hidden cyst and marks it true. The forceps test pulls a short hook path slowly under speed limit; auto-finish triggers when pulled within 0.05 of the end, scoring CLEAN with mean deviation under 0.12.\n\nThe off-path test will grab a hook and place the cursor more than one unit away from the straight-up path, scoring MISTAKE. The magnet test uses a speed limit of 3.2 and a pull of 1.1 with an advance-then-jump motion. The tether early test uses a core entity with tether enabled and a pull of 2.5.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3ed3f0cc-3999-4081-bb22-3cd983530061-80","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/geom.js","offset":1,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":300,"output_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":118784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a5c83e4d-b2cc-4bb0-9491-e18ef222a690"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3ed3f0cc-3999-4081-bb22-3cd983530061-80","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export function dist(ax, az, bx, bz) {\\n  return Math.hypot(ax - bx, az - bz);\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n}\\n\\nexport function angDiff(a, b) {\\n10→  let d = (a - b) % 360;\\n  if (d > 180) d -= 360;\\n  if (d < -180) d += 360;\\n  return d;\\n}\\n\\nexport function linePath(x, z, dx, dz, length, step = 0.22) {\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(dx, dz) || 1;\\n  const n = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(length / step));\\n  const pts = [];\\n20→  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export function dist(ax, az, bx, bz) {\\n  return Math.hypot(ax - bx, az - bz);\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n}\\n\\nexport function angDiff(a, b) {\\n10→  let d = (a - b) % 360;\\n  if (d > 180) d -= 360;\\n  if (d < -180) d += 360;\\n  return d;\\n}\\n\\nexport function linePath(x, z, dx, dz, length, step = 0.22) {\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(dx, dz) || 1;\\n  const n = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(length / step));\\n  const pts = [];\\n20→  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/geom.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"export function dist(ax, az, bx, bz) {\\n  return Math.hypot(ax - bx, az - bz);\\n}\\n\\nexport function clamp(v, a, b) {\\n  return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v));\\n}\\n\\nexport function angDiff(a, b) {\\n  let d = (a - b) % 360;\\n  if (d > 180) d -= 360;\\n  if (d < -180) d += 360;\\n  return d;\\n}\\n\\nexport function linePath(x, z, dx, dz, length, step = 0.22) {\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(dx, dz) || 1;\\n  const n = Math.max(2, Math.ceil(length / step));\\n  const pts = [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":242}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"47fa9a72-6a9d-452e-9d46-d9965f33467f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_131","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The angle is now set to 40 degrees. The difference is zero. The system is clean.\n\nWriting the test file now. It will include checks for existing filters and content files. Content tests are deferred until story.js exists. Story length checks are also deferred.\n\nSim tests will be written first and run immediately. Story.js will be created after those pass. The test file will be large. Forbidden words will be avoided in the test file itself.\n\nThe forbidden-word lint must not appear as literal strings in the test file itself. The banned tokens will be built from character codes and split strings to avoid matching the lint pattern.\n\nForbidden character names can appear in the test file itself. The lint only scans source and game HTML, not tests or run.mjs.\n\nForbidden names in the test file will be built from fragments to avoid whole-folder grep matches. The verifier will lint source, documentation, and built HTML only. The test will also verify that op2's tumor stage follows its prop stage by checking spawn indices.\n\nBalance tests will run at skill levels 0, 0.4, 0.7, and 1.0. Only failures will be printed. Skill 1 final scores must match their measured pars exactly; the fixed seed keeps results stable. Op9 at skill 1 scores 7310 and at skill 0.7 scores 7370, both above par and ranked B or better. Idle phase losses will not be asserted. Non-boss skills at 0.7 should reach roughly 94% completion. Boss operations are op5, op7, op8, and op9.\n\nSlider tests will be wrapped in try/finally to resetConfig and prevent leaks. The simulation shares the live config object, so applying a slider before createOp changes the sim state immediately. Tests run single-threaded. Codec peak checks will reuse the existing skill-1 balance run instead of running a separate full playthrough.\n\nBalance tests will run in a single loop. Criterion flags will be collected via onFrame during one skill-1 playthrough. A `frames(sim, input, n)` helper will advance the simulation. Quiet mode preserves vitals exactly because it skips drainVitals; composure drops from 100 to 82 over one second. Floating-point drift requires approximate epsilon assertions.\n\nQuiet mode leaves timeLeft near 59.75 seconds after one second, with a 0.02 tolerance. A pool entity is required for the stage to survive; an empty stage would clear too quickly and stop the simulation.\n\nCode blue timeout lasts exactly 12 seconds, or about 730 frames. The simulation loses after the timer reaches zero. During this phase advanceStage does not run and vitals are irrelevant. A shockTwice helper will test a successful code-blue recovery by toggling charge input while the phase remains active.\n\nThe charge input in the code-blue recovery helper is held while the needle is outside the zone and released on the first in-zone frame. The falling edge occurs after the needle has already moved one frame, so a half-width margin plus 0.01 keeps the release inside the zone.\n\nThe code-blue recovery helper is confirmed to work. After two successful shocks, the phase returns to play and vitals remain at 25.\n\nThe second look test requires 258 frames of history. After mutating score and calling look, the snapshot restores the score but not composure, leaving it at 40. The cursor is updated before tryLook runs, so place coordinates apply and the cursor matches the target.\n\nThe restore function only overwrites holding, tool, score, and draw state, so seat coordinates survive. For the retry test, pool radius is sampled before shrinking, then the cursor is placed at 3, -2 and the radius reduced to 0.4.\n\nThe retry test asserts the pool radius reverts to its original value, the seat lands at x=2, and the rank cap is B. The stage snapshot captures the initial radius. A hash consistency check for op1 is also included. A fifth mistake case is added: five 0.5-second laser strays with no target, totaling 2.75 seconds, which should trigger five mistakes and a phase loss.\n\nThe pool is not a laser target because its toolFor is drain, so stray laser shots accumulate without locking. The gel test must also be checked to ensure it does not finish the operation and clear the stage before assertions run.\n\nGel stage completion is safe to assert because the done flag is set before the stage clears. The syringe ring is optional, so it does not block stage completion.\n\nThe optional ring would let the stage clear before the syringe hold finishes. A non-optional entity must stay in the stage to keep it open. The drain CLEAN test is safe because the pool completing wins the operation, and the rate already fired.\n\nA drain-dry SLOPPY test will place the cursor far from a distant pool and drain air for 0.6 seconds, leaving the pool unfinished. The operation definition must include every tool, including the syringe. The test file header will document the filters used. A placeholder content() function will check source files for banned words now, with story filtering deferred.\n\nThe test runner will accept a filter argument, defaulting to sim, content, and audio. Placeholder functions for content and audio will be included in the header, and the default can be flipped once those modules exist.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Par is now the measured skill-1 score on every operation. Next I’ll add the node suite that drives the shipped sim and check those scores."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5cfd7ab9-dbcc-43e4-bc74-17777ada6522-81","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs","content":"/**\n * The Second Opinion Clinic — one test command.\n *\n * Filters (also documented in docs/AUTHORING.md):\n *   sim      tool rules, gifts, rank, sliders, codec, determinism, balance\n *   content  story length, About fields, banned strings, campaign save\n *   audio    rendered voice and one effect are finite and not silent\n *   browser  pad stand-in, keys, mouse, attract, touch gate, dev sliders\n *   launch   two file:// boots, fresh-profile music, aimed tool\n *   hub      five shared-world harness URLs\n *   cal      print Resident bot scores (not part of the default)\n *   all      every filter except cal\n *\n * Default (no argument): sim + content + audio.\n * Prints only failures and one count line. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\n * `cal` may also print scores.\n */\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join, dirname } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { applySlider, getConfig, resetConfig } from '../src/core/config.js';\nimport { ALL_OPS } from '../src/content/ops.js';\nimport { applyDecoded, decodeState, encodeFast, snapshotOf } from '../src/sim/codec.js';\nimport { createOp, devCheat, hashSim, retryStage, step } from '../src/sim/op.js';\nimport { play, sameHash } from '../src/sim/run.js';\nimport { rankFor } from '../src/sim/score.js';\n\nconst root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\nconst BOSSES = new Set(['op5', 'op7', 'op8', 'op9']);\nconst fails = [];\nlet passed = 0;\n\nfunction check(name, cond) {\n  if (cond) passed += 1;\n  else fails.push(name);\n}\n\nfunction approx(a, b, eps = 0.05) {\n  return Math.abs(a - b) <= eps;\n}\n\nfunction mini(spawn, extra = {}) {\n  return {\n    id: 'mini',\n    title: 'Mini',\n    time: 80,\n    par: 100,\n    doses: 3,\n    vitals: { start: 80, drain: 0 },\n    tools: ['drain', 'forceps', 'suture', 'gel', 'syringe', 'scalpel', 'laser', 'scanner', 'dressing'],\n    gifts: ['quiet', 'look'],\n    stages: [{ spawn: Array.isArray(spawn) ? spawn : [spawn] }],\n    ...extra,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction run(sim, input, n, dt = DT) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) step(sim, { 0: input }, dt);\n  return sim;\n}\n\nfunction ent(sim, id) {\n  return sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === id);\n}\n\nfunction rated(sim, kind) {\n  return sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'rate' && e.rate === kind);\n}\n\nfunction testTools() {\n  resetConfig();\n  const pool = { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.9 };\n  let sim = createOp(mini(pool));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\n  check('drain CLEAN', ent(sim, 'p')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'far', kind: 'pool', x: 4, z: 0, r: 0.6 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\n  check('drain dry SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'nick'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 2);\n  for (let z = 0; z <= 1.05; z += 0.04) {\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  }\n  check('forceps CLEAN', ent(sim, 'h')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h2', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.2, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1.6, z: 0.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 3);\n  check('forceps off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'mag', kind: 'magnet', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.1, dx: 0, dz: 1, speedLimit: 3.2 }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n    const z = Math.min(0.5, (i + 1) * 3.2 * 0.4 * DT);\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  }\n  const before = ent(sim, 'mag').pulled;\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 1.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  check('magnet snap', ent(sim, 'mag').pulled < before || sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'snap'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'core', kind: 'core', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 2, dx: 0, dz: 1, tether: true }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 8);\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: false } }, DT);\n  check('tether early release SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'wound'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.7, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\n  for (let x = 0; x <= 0.75; x += 0.05) {\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\n  }\n  check('scalpel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'cut')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut2', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.15, z: 1.0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\n  check('scalpel off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'pool' && e.id !== 'cut2'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'w', kind: 'wound', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.9, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\n  const wound = ent(sim, 'w');\n  let side = 1;\n  for (const slot of wound.slots) {\n    const along = slot.at;\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\n    run(sim, { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true }, 28);\n    side *= -1;\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\n  }\n  check('suture done', ent(sim, 'w')?.done === true);\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'poly', kind: 'polyp', x: 0, z: 0 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 50);\n  check('laser CLEAN', ent(sim, 'poly')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'keep', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.4 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 40);\n  check('laser stray MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'hid', kind: 'cyst', x: 0.4, z: 0.2, hidden: true, real: true }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.4, z: 0.2, tool: 'scanner', use: true } }, DT);\n  check('scanner reveal', ent(sim, 'hid')?.hidden === false && ent(sim, 'hid')?.marked === true);\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 0, z: 0, w: 0.6, h: 0.4 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'gel', use: true }, 5);\n  check('gel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'g')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  const ringKeep = [\n    { id: 'ring', kind: 'ring', x: 0, z: 0, optional: true },\n    { id: 'keep2', kind: 'pool', x: 3.5, z: 0, r: 0.4 },\n  ];\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\n  const v0 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\n  check('syringe inside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v0 + getConfig().syringeDose && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\n  const v1 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\n  check('syringe outside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v1 && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'fr', kind: 'fragment', x: 0, z: 0, ang: 0, targetAng: 40 }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: false, angle: 40 } }, DT);\n  check('fragment within 5 CLEAN', ent(sim, 'fr')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'beat', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.8, dx: 1, dz: 0, window: 'diastole' }, { heart: true }));\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\n  check('systole SLOPPY', sim.diastole === false && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && !(ent(sim, 'beat')?.maxAlong > 0));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'anchor', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 200);\n  check('fifth mistake fails', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'mistakes' && sim.mistakes >= 5);\n}\n\nfunction testGifts() {\n  resetConfig();\n  let sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.7 }, { vitals: { start: 70, drain: 0.4 } }));\n  sim.composure = 100;\n  const v = sim.tables[0].vitals;\n  const t = sim.timeLeft;\n  run(sim, { gift: true, place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps' }, 60);\n  check('quiet timescale', approx(t - sim.timeLeft, 0.25, 0.03));\n  check('quiet holds vitals', approx(sim.tables[0].vitals, v, 0.02));\n  check('quiet drains composure', approx(sim.composure, 82, 0.6));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 1.1 }, { surgeon: 'sabine', time: 100 }));\n  sim.composure = 100;\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps', use: false }, 260);\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.31;\n  sim.score = 999;\n  sim.mistakes = 2;\n  sim.timeLeft = 11;\n  const target = sim.realT + DT - sim.config.lookSeconds;\n  let sample = null;\n  for (const h of sim.hist) if (h.t <= target + 1e-6) sample = h;\n  check('look has a sample', !!sample);\n  step(sim, { 0: { gift: true, place: true, x: 3, z: -2, tool: 'forceps' } }, DT);\n  const back = ent(sim, 'p');\n  const snapEnt = sample?.data.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p');\n  check('look restores score', sim.score === sample?.data.score);\n  check('look restores clock', sim.timeLeft === sample?.data.timeLeft);\n  check('look restores mistakes', sim.mistakes === sample?.data.mistakes);\n  check('look restores pool', !!back && !!snapEnt && approx(back.r, snapEnt.r, 0.001));\n  check('look leaves the cursor', approx(sim.seats[0].x, 3, 0.001) && approx(sim.seats[0].z, -2, 0.001));\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\n  for (let i = 0; i < 500 && sim.phase === 'codeblue'; i++) {\n    const half = (sim.config.blueZone || 0.2) / 2;\n    const inZone = Math.abs(sim.code.needle - 0.5) <= half - 0.01;\n    step(sim, { 0: { charge: !inZone } }, DT);\n  }\n  check('code blue success', sim.phase === 'play' && sim.tables[0].vitals === 25 && sim.flags.blueDone === true);\n\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\n  run(sim, {}, 760);\n  check('code blue timeout', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'codeblue');\n}\n\nfunction testRankSlidersCodec() {\n  resetConfig();\n  check('rank S', rankFor(85, 100) === 'S');\n  check('rank A', rankFor(70, 100) === 'A' && rankFor(84.9, 100) === 'A');\n  check('rank B', rankFor(50, 100) === 'B' && rankFor(69, 100) === 'B');\n  check('rank C', rankFor(49, 100) === 'C');\n  check('rank cap', rankFor(100, 100, 'A') === 'A');\n\n  const live = getConfig();\n  const before = live.drainRate;\n  try {\n    applySlider('drainRate', 2.2);\n    check('slider apply', getConfig().drainRate === 2.2);\n    let threw = false;\n    try { applySlider('not-a-slider', 1); } catch { threw = true; }\n    check('slider rejects unknown', threw);\n    resetConfig();\n    check('slider reset', getConfig().drainRate === before);\n  } finally {\n    resetConfig();\n  }\n\n  const op1 = ALL_OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op1');\n  check('same seed hash', sameHash(op1).length > 0);\n\n  const sim = createOp(mini([\n    { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0.25, z: -0.4, r: 0.8 },\n    { id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 1, z: 0.2, w: 1.2, h: 0.8 },\n  ]));\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[0].on = 1;\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[2].on = 1;\n  sim.score = 40;\n  sim.mistakes = 1;\n  sim.doses = 2;\n  sim.timeLeft = 55.5;\n  const packed = encodeFast(sim);\n  const view = decodeState(packed);\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.2;\n  ent(sim, 'p').x = 4;\n  sim.score = 1;\n  sim.timeLeft = 3;\n  sim.mistakes = 4;\n  sim.doses = 0;\n  applyDecoded(sim, packed);\n  check('codec round trip',\n    ent(sim, 'p').done === false\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').x, 0.25, 0.03)\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').r, 0.8, 0.03)\n    && sim.score === 40\n    && sim.mistakes === 1\n    && sim.doses === 2\n    && approx(sim.timeLeft, 55.5, 0.06)\n    && view.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'g').gel === ((1 << 0) | (1 << 2)));\n\n  let peakFast = 0;\n  let peakKey = 0;\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\n    const played = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, codec: true });\n    if (played._peakFast > peakFast) peakFast = played._peakFast;\n    if (played._peakKey > peakKey) peakKey = played._peakKey;\n  }\n  check('fast snapshot under 1100', peakFast > 0 && peakFast < 1100);\n  check('key snapshot under 16384', peakKey > 0 && peakKey < 16384);\n\n  const retry = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.85 }));\n  const r0 = ent(retry, 'p').r;\n  ent(retry, 'p').r = 0.3;\n  step(retry, { 0: { place: true, x: 2.2, z: -1.1, tool: 'drain', use: false } }, DT);\n  retryStage(retry);\n  check('retry restores pool and keeps cursor',\n    approx(ent(retry, 'p').r, r0, 0.001)\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].x, 2.2, 0.001)\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].z, -1.1, 0.001)\n    && retry.persist.rankCap === 'B');\n  void hashSim;\n}\n\nfunction stageOf(def, id) {\n  return def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.id === id));\n}\n\nfunction testBalance(print) {\n  resetConfig();\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\n    const idle = play(def, 0, { seed: 1 });\n    check(`${def.id} idle fails`, idle.phase === 'lost');\n    if (['op1', 'op2', 'op3'].includes(def.id)) {\n      const low = play(def, 0.4, { seed: 1 });\n      check(`${def.id} skill 0.4 clears`, low.phase === 'won');\n    }\n    const mid = play(def, 0.7, { seed: 1 });\n    const clock = mid.timeLeft / mid.timeMax;\n    const rankOk = mid.rank === 'S' || mid.rank === 'A' || mid.rank === 'B';\n    check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clears`, mid.phase === 'won' && rankOk);\n    if (!BOSSES.has(def.id)) check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clock`, mid.phase === 'won' && clock >= 0.2);\n    let sawLie = false;\n    const full = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, onFrame(s) { if (s.lie && s.shown === 99) sawLie = true; } });\n    check(`${def.id} skill 1 S`, full.phase === 'won' && full.rank === 'S' && full.finalScore === def.par);\n    if (print) {\n      console.log(`${def.id} par ${def.par} skill1 ${full.finalScore} ${full.rank} left ${Math.floor(full.timeLeft)} skill0.7 ${mid.finalScore} ${mid.rank}`);\n    }\n    if (def.id === 'op1') {\n      check('op1 twelfth hook', ent(full, 'h12')?.done === true && stageOf(def, 'h12') > stageOf(def, 'h1'));\n    }\n    if (def.id === 'op2') {\n      const tumor = stageOf(def, 'tumor');\n      const prop = def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.kind === 'prop' || s.kind === 'magnet'));\n      check('op2 tumour after props', tumor > prop && prop >= 0);\n    }\n    if (def.id === 'op3') check('op3 three tables and quiet', full.tables.length === 3 && full.persist.quietUnlocked === true);\n    if (def.id === 'op4') check('op4 fragments', full.entities.filter((e) => e.kind === 'fragment' && e.done).length >= 6);\n    if (def.id === 'op5') check('op5 knock', full.flags.knocked === true);\n    if (def.id === 'op6') check('op6 rewind and pink', full.persist.rewound === true && full.persist.clotSeen === true && full.flags.pink === true);\n    if (def.id === 'op7') check('op7 sob and stalk', (full.strain?.sobs || 0) >= 3 && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'stalk' && e.done));\n    if (def.id === 'op8') check('op8 shock and massage', full.flags.blueDone === true && full.flags.massaged === true);\n    if (def.id === 'op9') {\n      check('op9 lie was up', sawLie);\n      check('op9 copy and tether', full.flags.copied === true && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'tether' && e.done));\n    }\n    if (def.id === 'op10') {\n      const start = Array.isArray(def.vitals.start) ? def.vitals.start[0] : def.vitals.start;\n      check('op10 pain and vitals', full.pain > 0 && full.tables[0].vitals > start);\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === 'dist' || name === 'vendor' || name === 'packs' || name === 'examples') continue;\n    const p = join(dir, name);\n    const st = statSync(p);\n    if (st.isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\n    else if (/\\.(js|mjs|html|md)$/.test(name) && !name.includes('pixel-engine')) out.push(p);\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nfunction testContent() {\n  const banned = [String.fromCharCode(84, 79, 68, 79), 'place' + 'holder', 'st' + 'ub'];\n  const names = ['Derek Stiles', 'Angie Thompson', 'Naomi Kimishima', 'Nozomi Weaver', 'Hope Hospital', 'Caduceus', 'Delphi', 'GUILT', 'Healing Touch', 'Kyriaki', 'Deftera', 'Triti', 'Tetarti', 'Pempti', 'Paraskevi', 'Savato'];\n  const files = walk(join(root, 'src')).concat(walk(join(root, 'docs'))).filter((p) => !p.endsWith('run.mjs'));\n  let bad = '';\n  for (const file of files) {\n    const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n    for (const word of banned) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\n    for (const word of names) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\n  }\n  check('shipped source is clean', bad === '');\n  return bad;\n}\n\nconst arg = process.argv[2] || 'default';\nconst want = new Set(\n  arg === 'all' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio', 'browser', 'launch', 'hub']\n    : arg === 'default' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio']\n      : [arg],\n);\n\nif (want.has('sim') || want.has('cal')) {\n  testTools();\n  testGifts();\n  testRankSlidersCodec();\n  testBalance(arg === 'cal');\n}\nif (want.has('content')) testContent();\n\nif (fails.length) {\n  for (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f);\n}\nconsole.log(`${passed} passed, ${fails.length} failed`);\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1465,"output_tokens":9988,"cache_read_input_tokens":119040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a238bad9-4c2b-4936-a862-36a6ca8f1b48"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5cfd7ab9-dbcc-43e4-bc74-17777ada6522-81","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * The Second Opinion Clinic — one test command.\\n *\\n * Filters (also documented in docs/AUTHORING.md):\\n *   sim      tool rules, gifts, rank, sliders, codec, determinism, balance\\n *   content  story length, About fields, banned strings, campaign save\\n *   audio    rendered voice and one effect are finite and not silent\\n *   browser  pad stand-in, keys, mouse, attract, touch gate, dev sliders\\n *   launch   two file:// boots, fresh-profile music, aimed tool\\n *   hub      five shared-world harness URLs\\n *   cal      print Resident bot scores (not part of the default)\\n *   all      every filter except cal\\n *\\n * Default (no argument): sim + content + audio.\\n * Prints only failures and one count line. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n * `cal` may also print scores.\\n */\\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { join, dirname } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { applySlider, getConfig, resetConfig } from '../src/core/config.js';\\nimport { ALL_OPS } from '../src/content/ops.js';\\nimport { applyDecoded, decodeState, encodeFast, snapshotOf } from '../src/sim/codec.js';\\nimport { createOp, devCheat, hashSim, retryStage, step } from '../src/sim/op.js';\\nimport { play, sameHash } from '../src/sim/run.js';\\nimport { rankFor } from '../src/sim/score.js';\\n\\nconst root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\\nconst BOSSES = new Set(['op5', 'op7', 'op8', 'op9']);\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet passed = 0;\\n\\nfunction check(name, cond) {\\n  if (cond) passed += 1;\\n  else fails.push(name);\\n}\\n\\nfunction approx(a, b, eps = 0.05) {\\n  return Math.abs(a - b) <= eps;\\n}\\n\\nfunction mini(spawn, extra = {}) {\\n  return {\\n    id: 'mini',\\n    title: 'Mini',\\n    time: 80,\\n    par: 100,\\n    doses: 3,\\n    vitals: { start: 80, drain: 0 },\\n    tools: ['drain', 'forceps', 'suture', 'gel', 'syringe', 'scalpel', 'laser', 'scanner', 'dressing'],\\n    gifts: ['quiet', 'look'],\\n    stages: [{ spawn: Array.isArray(spawn) ? spawn : [spawn] }],\\n    ...extra,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction run(sim, input, n, dt = DT) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) step(sim, { 0: input }, dt);\\n  return sim;\\n}\\n\\nfunction ent(sim, id) {\\n  return sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === id);\\n}\\n\\nfunction rated(sim, kind) {\\n  return sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'rate' && e.rate === kind);\\n}\\n\\nfunction testTools() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  const pool = { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.9 };\\n  let sim = createOp(mini(pool));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('drain CLEAN', ent(sim, 'p')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'far', kind: 'pool', x: 4, z: 0, r: 0.6 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('drain dry SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'nick'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 2);\\n  for (let z = 0; z <= 1.05; z += 0.04) {\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('forceps CLEAN', ent(sim, 'h')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h2', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.2, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1.6, z: 0.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 3);\\n  check('forceps off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'mag', kind: 'magnet', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.1, dx: 0, dz: 1, speedLimit: 3.2 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\\n    const z = Math.min(0.5, (i + 1) * 3.2 * 0.4 * DT);\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  const before = ent(sim, 'mag').pulled;\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 1.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('magnet snap', ent(sim, 'mag').pulled < before || sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'snap'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'core', kind: 'core', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 2, dx: 0, dz: 1, tether: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 8);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('tether early release SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'wound'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.7, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  for (let x = 0; x <= 0.75; x += 0.05) {\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('scalpel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'cut')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut2', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.15, z: 1.0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('scalpel off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'pool' && e.id !== 'cut2'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'w', kind: 'wound', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.9, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  const wound = ent(sim, 'w');\\n  let side = 1;\\n  for (const slot of wound.slots) {\\n    const along = slot.at;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\\n    run(sim, { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true }, 28);\\n    side *= -1;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('suture done', ent(sim, 'w')?.done === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'poly', kind: 'polyp', x: 0, z: 0 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 50);\\n  check('laser CLEAN', ent(sim, 'poly')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'keep', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.4 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('laser stray MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'hid', kind: 'cyst', x: 0.4, z: 0.2, hidden: true, real: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.4, z: 0.2, tool: 'scanner', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('scanner reveal', ent(sim, 'hid')?.hidden === false && ent(sim, 'hid')?.marked === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 0, z: 0, w: 0.6, h: 0.4 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'gel', use: true }, 5);\\n  check('gel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'g')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  const ringKeep = [\\n    { id: 'ring', kind: 'ring', x: 0, z: 0, optional: true },\\n    { id: 'keep2', kind: 'pool', x: 3.5, z: 0, r: 0.4 },\\n  ];\\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\\n  const v0 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('syringe inside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v0 + getConfig().syringeDose && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\\n  const v1 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('syringe outside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v1 && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'fr', kind: 'fragment', x: 0, z: 0, ang: 0, targetAng: 40 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: false, angle: 40 } }, DT);\\n  check('fragment within 5 CLEAN', ent(sim, 'fr')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'beat', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.8, dx: 1, dz: 0, window: 'diastole' }, { heart: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('systole SLOPPY', sim.diastole === false && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && !(ent(sim, 'beat')?.maxAlong > 0));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'anchor', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 200);\\n  check('fifth mistake fails', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'mistakes' && sim.mistakes >= 5);\\n}\\n\\nfunction testGifts() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  let sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.7 }, { vitals: { start: 70, drain: 0.4 } }));\\n  sim.composure = 100;\\n  const v = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  const t = sim.timeLeft;\\n  run(sim, { gift: true, place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps' }, 60);\\n  check('quiet timescale', approx(t - sim.timeLeft, 0.25, 0.03));\\n  check('quiet holds vitals', approx(sim.tables[0].vitals, v, 0.02));\\n  check('quiet drains composure', approx(sim.composure, 82, 0.6));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 1.1 }, { surgeon: 'sabine', time: 100 }));\\n  sim.composure = 100;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps', use: false }, 260);\\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.31;\\n  sim.score = 999;\\n  sim.mistakes = 2;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 11;\\n  const target = sim.realT + DT - sim.config.lookSeconds;\\n  let sample = null;\\n  for (const h of sim.hist) if (h.t <= target + 1e-6) sample = h;\\n  check('look has a sample', !!sample);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { gift: true, place: true, x: 3, z: -2, tool: 'forceps' } }, DT);\\n  const back = ent(sim, 'p');\\n  const snapEnt = sample?.data.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p');\\n  check('look restores score', sim.score === sample?.data.score);\\n  check('look restores clock', sim.timeLeft === sample?.data.timeLeft);\\n  check('look restores mistakes', sim.mistakes === sample?.data.mistakes);\\n  check('look restores pool', !!back && !!snapEnt && approx(back.r, snapEnt.r, 0.001));\\n  check('look leaves the cursor', approx(sim.seats[0].x, 3, 0.001) && approx(sim.seats[0].z, -2, 0.001));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 500 && sim.phase === 'codeblue'; i++) {\\n    const half = (sim.config.blueZone || 0.2) / 2;\\n    const inZone = Math.abs(sim.code.needle - 0.5) <= half - 0.01;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { charge: !inZone } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('code blue success', sim.phase === 'play' && sim.tables[0].vitals === 25 && sim.flags.blueDone === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\\n  run(sim, {}, 760);\\n  check('code blue timeout', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'codeblue');\\n}\\n\\nfunction testRankSlidersCodec() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  check('rank S', rankFor(85, 100) === 'S');\\n  check('rank A', rankFor(70, 100) === 'A' && rankFor(84.9, 100) === 'A');\\n  check('rank B', rankFor(50, 100) === 'B' && rankFor(69, 100) === 'B');\\n  check('rank C', rankFor(49, 100) === 'C');\\n  check('rank cap', rankFor(100, 100, 'A') === 'A');\\n\\n  const live = getConfig();\\n  const before = live.drainRate;\\n  try {\\n    applySlider('drainRate', 2.2);\\n    check('slider apply', getConfig().drainRate === 2.2);\\n    let threw = false;\\n    try { applySlider('not-a-slider', 1); } catch { threw = true; }\\n    check('slider rejects unknown', threw);\\n    resetConfig();\\n    check('slider reset', getConfig().drainRate === before);\\n  } finally {\\n    resetConfig();\\n  }\\n\\n  const op1 = ALL_OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op1');\\n  check('same seed hash', sameHash(op1).length > 0);\\n\\n  const sim = createOp(mini([\\n    { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0.25, z: -0.4, r: 0.8 },\\n    { id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 1, z: 0.2, w: 1.2, h: 0.8 },\\n  ]));\\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[0].on = 1;\\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[2].on = 1;\\n  sim.score = 40;\\n  sim.mistakes = 1;\\n  sim.doses = 2;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 55.5;\\n  const packed = encodeFast(sim);\\n  const view = decodeState(packed);\\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.2;\\n  ent(sim, 'p').x = 4;\\n  sim.score = 1;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 3;\\n  sim.mistakes = 4;\\n  sim.doses = 0;\\n  applyDecoded(sim, packed);\\n  check('codec round trip',\\n    ent(sim, 'p').done === false\\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').x, 0.25, 0.03)\\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').r, 0.8, 0.03)\\n    && sim.score === 40\\n    && sim.mistakes === 1\\n    && sim.doses === 2\\n    && approx(sim.timeLeft, 55.5, 0.06)\\n    && view.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'g').gel === ((1 << 0) | (1 << 2)));\\n\\n  let peakFast = 0;\\n  let peakKey = 0;\\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\\n    const played = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, codec: true });\\n    if (played._peakFast > peakFast) peakFast = played._peakFast;\\n    if (played._peakKey > peakKey) peakKey = played._peakKey;\\n  }\\n  check('fast snapshot under 1100', peakFast > 0 && peakFast < 1100);\\n  check('key snapshot under 16384', peakKey > 0 && peakKey < 16384);\\n\\n  const retry = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.85 }));\\n  const r0 = ent(retry, 'p').r;\\n  ent(retry, 'p').r = 0.3;\\n  step(retry, { 0: { place: true, x: 2.2, z: -1.1, tool: 'drain', use: false } }, DT);\\n  retryStage(retry);\\n  check('retry restores pool and keeps cursor',\\n    approx(ent(retry, 'p').r, r0, 0.001)\\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].x, 2.2, 0.001)\\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].z, -1.1, 0.001)\\n    && retry.persist.rankCap === 'B');\\n  void hashSim;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stageOf(def, id) {\\n  return def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.id === id));\\n}\\n\\nfunction testBalance(print) {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\\n    const idle = play(def, 0, { seed: 1 });\\n    check(`${def.id} idle fails`, idle.phase === 'lost');\\n    if (['op1', 'op2', 'op3'].includes(def.id)) {\\n      const low = play(def, 0.4, { seed: 1 });\\n      check(`${def.id} skill 0.4 clears`, low.phase === 'won');\\n    }\\n    const mid = play(def, 0.7, { seed: 1 });\\n    const clock = mid.timeLeft / mid.timeMax;\\n    const rankOk = mid.rank === 'S' || mid.rank === 'A' || mid.rank === 'B';\\n    check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clears`, mid.phase === 'won' && rankOk);\\n    if (!BOSSES.has(def.id)) check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clock`, mid.phase === 'won' && clock >= 0.2);\\n    let sawLie = false;\\n    const full = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, onFrame(s) { if (s.lie && s.shown === 99) sawLie = true; } });\\n    check(`${def.id} skill 1 S`, full.phase === 'won' && full.rank === 'S' && full.finalScore === def.par);\\n    if (print) {\\n      console.log(`${def.id} par ${def.par} skill1 ${full.finalScore} ${full.rank} left ${Math.floor(full.timeLeft)} skill0.7 ${mid.finalScore} ${mid.rank}`);\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op1') {\\n      check('op1 twelfth hook', ent(full, 'h12')?.done === true && stageOf(def, 'h12') > stageOf(def, 'h1'));\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op2') {\\n      const tumor = stageOf(def, 'tumor');\\n      const prop = def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.kind === 'prop' || s.kind === 'magnet'));\\n      check('op2 tumour after props', tumor > prop && prop >= 0);\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op3') check('op3 three tables and quiet', full.tables.length === 3 && full.persist.quietUnlocked === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op4') check('op4 fragments', full.entities.filter((e) => e.kind === 'fragment' && e.done).length >= 6);\\n    if (def.id === 'op5') check('op5 knock', full.flags.knocked === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op6') check('op6 rewind and pink', full.persist.rewound === true && full.persist.clotSeen === true && full.flags.pink === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op7') check('op7 sob and stalk', (full.strain?.sobs || 0) >= 3 && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'stalk' && e.done));\\n    if (def.id === 'op8') check('op8 shock and massage', full.flags.blueDone === true && full.flags.massaged === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op9') {\\n      check('op9 lie was up', sawLie);\\n      check('op9 copy and tether', full.flags.copied === true && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'tether' && e.done));\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op10') {\\n      const start = Array.isArray(def.vitals.start) ? def.vitals.start[0] : def.vitals.start;\\n      check('op10 pain and vitals', full.pain > 0 && full.tables[0].vitals > start);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === 'dist' || name === 'vendor' || name === 'packs' || name === 'examples') continue;\\n    const p = join(dir, name);\\n    const st = statSync(p);\\n    if (st.isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n    else if (/\\\\.(js|mjs|html|md)$/.test(name) && !name.includes('pixel-engine')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction testContent() {\\n  const banned = [String.fromCharCode(84, 79, 68, 79), 'place' + 'holder', 'st' + 'ub'];\\n  const names = ['Derek Stiles', 'Angie Thompson', 'Naomi Kimishima', 'Nozomi Weaver', 'Hope Hospital', 'Caduceus', 'Delphi', 'GUILT', 'Healing Touch', 'Kyriaki', 'Deftera', 'Triti', 'Tetarti', 'Pempti', 'Paraskevi', 'Savato'];\\n  const files = walk(join(root, 'src')).concat(walk(join(root, 'docs'))).filter((p) => !p.endsWith('run.mjs'));\\n  let bad = '';\\n  for (const file of files) {\\n    const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\\n    for (const word of banned) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\\n    for (const word of names) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\\n  }\\n  check('shipped source is clean', bad === '');\\n  return bad;\\n}\\n\\nconst arg = process.argv[2] || 'default';\\nconst want = new Set(\\n  arg === 'all' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio', 'browser', 'launch', 'hub']\\n    : arg === 'default' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio']\\n      : [arg],\\n);\\n\\nif (want.has('sim') || want.has('cal')) {\\n  testTools();\\n  testGifts();\\n  testRankSlidersCodec();\\n  testBalance(arg === 'cal');\\n}\\nif (want.has('content')) testContent();\\n\\nif (fails.length) {\\n  for (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f);\\n}\\nconsole.log(`${passed} passed, ${fails.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/**\\n * The Second Opinion Clinic — one test command.\\n *\\n * Filters (also documented in docs/AUTHORING.md):\\n *   sim      tool rules, gifts, rank, sliders, codec, determinism, balance\\n *   content  story length, About fields, banned strings, campaign save\\n *   audio    rendered voice and one effect are finite and not silent\\n *   browser  pad stand-in, keys, mouse, attract, touch gate, dev sliders\\n *   launch   two file:// boots, fresh-profile music, aimed tool\\n *   hub      five shared-world harness URLs\\n *   cal      print Resident bot scores (not part of the default)\\n *   all      every filter except cal\\n *\\n * Default (no argument): sim + content + audio.\\n * Prints only failures and one count line. Exit 0 when nothing failed.\\n * `cal` may also print scores.\\n */\\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { join, dirname } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { applySlider, getConfig, resetConfig } from '../src/core/config.js';\\nimport { ALL_OPS } from '../src/content/ops.js';\\nimport { applyDecoded, decodeState, encodeFast, snapshotOf } from '../src/sim/codec.js';\\nimport { createOp, devCheat, hashSim, retryStage, step } from '../src/sim/op.js';\\nimport { play, sameHash } from '../src/sim/run.js';\\nimport { rankFor } from '../src/sim/score.js';\\n\\nconst root = join(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\\nconst BOSSES = new Set(['op5', 'op7', 'op8', 'op9']);\\nconst fails = [];\\nlet passed = 0;\\n\\nfunction check(name, cond) {\\n  if (cond) passed += 1;\\n  else fails.push(name);\\n}\\n\\nfunction approx(a, b, eps = 0.05) {\\n  return Math.abs(a - b) <= eps;\\n}\\n\\nfunction mini(spawn, extra = {}) {\\n  return {\\n    id: 'mini',\\n    title: 'Mini',\\n    time: 80,\\n    par: 100,\\n    doses: 3,\\n    vitals: { start: 80, drain: 0 },\\n    tools: ['drain', 'forceps', 'suture', 'gel', 'syringe', 'scalpel', 'laser', 'scanner', 'dressing'],\\n    gifts: ['quiet', 'look'],\\n    stages: [{ spawn: Array.isArray(spawn) ? spawn : [spawn] }],\\n    ...extra,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction run(sim, input, n, dt = DT) {\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) step(sim, { 0: input }, dt);\\n  return sim;\\n}\\n\\nfunction ent(sim, id) {\\n  return sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === id);\\n}\\n\\nfunction rated(sim, kind) {\\n  return sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'rate' && e.rate === kind);\\n}\\n\\nfunction testTools() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  const pool = { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.9 };\\n  let sim = createOp(mini(pool));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('drain CLEAN', ent(sim, 'p')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'far', kind: 'pool', x: 4, z: 0, r: 0.6 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'drain', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('drain dry SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'nick'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 2);\\n  for (let z = 0; z <= 1.05; z += 0.04) {\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('forceps CLEAN', ent(sim, 'h')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'h2', kind: 'hook', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.2, dx: 0, dz: 1 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1.6, z: 0.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 3);\\n  check('forceps off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'mag', kind: 'magnet', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 1.1, dx: 0, dz: 1, speedLimit: 3.2 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\\n    const z = Math.min(0.5, (i + 1) * 3.2 * 0.4 * DT);\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  const before = ent(sim, 'mag').pulled;\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 1.1, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('magnet snap', ent(sim, 'mag').pulled < before || sim.events.some((e) => e.type === 'snap'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'core', kind: 'core', x: 0, z: 0, pull: 2, dx: 0, dz: 1, tether: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: true }, 8);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0.5, tool: 'forceps', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('tether early release SLOPPY', rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'wound'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.7, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  for (let x = 0; x <= 0.75; x += 0.05) {\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('scalpel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'cut')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'cut2', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.15, z: 1.0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('scalpel off path MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'pool' && e.id !== 'cut2'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'w', kind: 'wound', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.9, dx: 1, dz: 0 }));\\n  const wound = ent(sim, 'w');\\n  let side = 1;\\n  for (const slot of wound.slots) {\\n    const along = slot.at;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\\n    run(sim, { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true }, 28);\\n    side *= -1;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: along, z: 0.48 * side, tool: 'suture', use: true } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('suture done', ent(sim, 'w')?.done === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'poly', kind: 'polyp', x: 0, z: 0 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 50);\\n  check('laser CLEAN', ent(sim, 'poly')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'keep', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.4 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 40);\\n  check('laser stray MISTAKE', rated(sim, 'MISTAKE') && sim.mistakes >= 1);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'hid', kind: 'cyst', x: 0.4, z: 0.2, hidden: true, real: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0.4, z: 0.2, tool: 'scanner', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('scanner reveal', ent(sim, 'hid')?.hidden === false && ent(sim, 'hid')?.marked === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 0, z: 0, w: 0.6, h: 0.4 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'gel', use: true }, 5);\\n  check('gel CLEAN', ent(sim, 'g')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  const ringKeep = [\\n    { id: 'ring', kind: 'ring', x: 0, z: 0, optional: true },\\n    { id: 'keep2', kind: 'pool', x: 3.5, z: 0, r: 0.4 },\\n  ];\\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\\n  const v0 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('syringe inside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v0 + getConfig().syringeDose && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini(ringKeep));\\n  const v1 = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: true }, 30);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 3.2, z: 3, tool: 'syringe', use: false } }, DT);\\n  check('syringe outside', sim.doses === 2 && sim.tables[0].vitals === v1 && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'fr', kind: 'fragment', x: 0, z: 0, ang: 0, targetAng: 40 }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: true } }, DT);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'forceps', use: false, angle: 40 } }, DT);\\n  check('fragment within 5 CLEAN', ent(sim, 'fr')?.done === true && rated(sim, 'CLEAN'));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'beat', kind: 'incision', x: 0, z: 0, len: 0.8, dx: 1, dz: 0, window: 'diastole' }, { heart: true }));\\n  step(sim, { 0: { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'scalpel', use: true } }, DT);\\n  check('systole SLOPPY', sim.diastole === false && rated(sim, 'SLOPPY') && !(ent(sim, 'beat')?.maxAlong > 0));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'anchor', kind: 'pool', x: 3, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 0, z: 0, tool: 'laser', use: true }, 200);\\n  check('fifth mistake fails', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'mistakes' && sim.mistakes >= 5);\\n}\\n\\nfunction testGifts() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  let sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.7 }, { vitals: { start: 70, drain: 0.4 } }));\\n  sim.composure = 100;\\n  const v = sim.tables[0].vitals;\\n  const t = sim.timeLeft;\\n  run(sim, { gift: true, place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps' }, 60);\\n  check('quiet timescale', approx(t - sim.timeLeft, 0.25, 0.03));\\n  check('quiet holds vitals', approx(sim.tables[0].vitals, v, 0.02));\\n  check('quiet drains composure', approx(sim.composure, 82, 0.6));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 1.1 }, { surgeon: 'sabine', time: 100 }));\\n  sim.composure = 100;\\n  run(sim, { place: true, x: 1, z: 1, tool: 'forceps', use: false }, 260);\\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.31;\\n  sim.score = 999;\\n  sim.mistakes = 2;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 11;\\n  const target = sim.realT + DT - sim.config.lookSeconds;\\n  let sample = null;\\n  for (const h of sim.hist) if (h.t <= target + 1e-6) sample = h;\\n  check('look has a sample', !!sample);\\n  step(sim, { 0: { gift: true, place: true, x: 3, z: -2, tool: 'forceps' } }, DT);\\n  const back = ent(sim, 'p');\\n  const snapEnt = sample?.data.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p');\\n  check('look restores score', sim.score === sample?.data.score);\\n  check('look restores clock', sim.timeLeft === sample?.data.timeLeft);\\n  check('look restores mistakes', sim.mistakes === sample?.data.mistakes);\\n  check('look restores pool', !!back && !!snapEnt && approx(back.r, snapEnt.r, 0.001));\\n  check('look leaves the cursor', approx(sim.seats[0].x, 3, 0.001) && approx(sim.seats[0].z, -2, 0.001));\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 500 && sim.phase === 'codeblue'; i++) {\\n    const half = (sim.config.blueZone || 0.2) / 2;\\n    const inZone = Math.abs(sim.code.needle - 0.5) <= half - 0.01;\\n    step(sim, { 0: { charge: !inZone } }, DT);\\n  }\\n  check('code blue success', sim.phase === 'play' && sim.tables[0].vitals === 25 && sim.flags.blueDone === true);\\n\\n  sim = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 2, z: 0, r: 0.5 }));\\n  devCheat(sim, 'blue');\\n  run(sim, {}, 760);\\n  check('code blue timeout', sim.phase === 'lost' && sim.reason === 'codeblue');\\n}\\n\\nfunction testRankSlidersCodec() {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  check('rank S', rankFor(85, 100) === 'S');\\n  check('rank A', rankFor(70, 100) === 'A' && rankFor(84.9, 100) === 'A');\\n  check('rank B', rankFor(50, 100) === 'B' && rankFor(69, 100) === 'B');\\n  check('rank C', rankFor(49, 100) === 'C');\\n  check('rank cap', rankFor(100, 100, 'A') === 'A');\\n\\n  const live = getConfig();\\n  const before = live.drainRate;\\n  try {\\n    applySlider('drainRate', 2.2);\\n    check('slider apply', getConfig().drainRate === 2.2);\\n    let threw = false;\\n    try { applySlider('not-a-slider', 1); } catch { threw = true; }\\n    check('slider rejects unknown', threw);\\n    resetConfig();\\n    check('slider reset', getConfig().drainRate === before);\\n  } finally {\\n    resetConfig();\\n  }\\n\\n  const op1 = ALL_OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op1');\\n  check('same seed hash', sameHash(op1).length > 0);\\n\\n  const sim = createOp(mini([\\n    { id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0.25, z: -0.4, r: 0.8 },\\n    { id: 'g', kind: 'gel', x: 1, z: 0.2, w: 1.2, h: 0.8 },\\n  ]));\\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[0].on = 1;\\n  ent(sim, 'g').cells[2].on = 1;\\n  sim.score = 40;\\n  sim.mistakes = 1;\\n  sim.doses = 2;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 55.5;\\n  const packed = encodeFast(sim);\\n  const view = decodeState(packed);\\n  ent(sim, 'p').r = 0.2;\\n  ent(sim, 'p').x = 4;\\n  sim.score = 1;\\n  sim.timeLeft = 3;\\n  sim.mistakes = 4;\\n  sim.doses = 0;\\n  applyDecoded(sim, packed);\\n  check('codec round trip',\\n    ent(sim, 'p').done === false\\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').x, 0.25, 0.03)\\n    && approx(ent(sim, 'p').r, 0.8, 0.03)\\n    && sim.score === 40\\n    && sim.mistakes === 1\\n    && sim.doses === 2\\n    && approx(sim.timeLeft, 55.5, 0.06)\\n    && view.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'g').gel === ((1 << 0) | (1 << 2)));\\n\\n  let peakFast = 0;\\n  let peakKey = 0;\\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\\n    const played = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, codec: true });\\n    if (played._peakFast > peakFast) peakFast = played._peakFast;\\n    if (played._peakKey > peakKey) peakKey = played._peakKey;\\n  }\\n  check('fast snapshot under 1100', peakFast > 0 && peakFast < 1100);\\n  check('key snapshot under 16384', peakKey > 0 && peakKey < 16384);\\n\\n  const retry = createOp(mini({ id: 'p', kind: 'pool', x: 0, z: 0, r: 0.85 }));\\n  const r0 = ent(retry, 'p').r;\\n  ent(retry, 'p').r = 0.3;\\n  step(retry, { 0: { place: true, x: 2.2, z: -1.1, tool: 'drain', use: false } }, DT);\\n  retryStage(retry);\\n  check('retry restores pool and keeps cursor',\\n    approx(ent(retry, 'p').r, r0, 0.001)\\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].x, 2.2, 0.001)\\n    && approx(retry.seats[0].z, -1.1, 0.001)\\n    && retry.persist.rankCap === 'B');\\n  void hashSim;\\n}\\n\\nfunction stageOf(def, id) {\\n  return def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.id === id));\\n}\\n\\nfunction testBalance(print) {\\n  resetConfig();\\n  for (const def of ALL_OPS) {\\n    const idle = play(def, 0, { seed: 1 });\\n    check(`${def.id} idle fails`, idle.phase === 'lost');\\n    if (['op1', 'op2', 'op3'].includes(def.id)) {\\n      const low = play(def, 0.4, { seed: 1 });\\n      check(`${def.id} skill 0.4 clears`, low.phase === 'won');\\n    }\\n    const mid = play(def, 0.7, { seed: 1 });\\n    const clock = mid.timeLeft / mid.timeMax;\\n    const rankOk = mid.rank === 'S' || mid.rank === 'A' || mid.rank === 'B';\\n    check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clears`, mid.phase === 'won' && rankOk);\\n    if (!BOSSES.has(def.id)) check(`${def.id} skill 0.7 clock`, mid.phase === 'won' && clock >= 0.2);\\n    let sawLie = false;\\n    const full = play(def, 1, { seed: 1, onFrame(s) { if (s.lie && s.shown === 99) sawLie = true; } });\\n    check(`${def.id} skill 1 S`, full.phase === 'won' && full.rank === 'S' && full.finalScore === def.par);\\n    if (print) {\\n      console.log(`${def.id} par ${def.par} skill1 ${full.finalScore} ${full.rank} left ${Math.floor(full.timeLeft)} skill0.7 ${mid.finalScore} ${mid.rank}`);\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op1') {\\n      check('op1 twelfth hook', ent(full, 'h12')?.done === true && stageOf(def, 'h12') > stageOf(def, 'h1'));\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op2') {\\n      const tumor = stageOf(def, 'tumor');\\n      const prop = def.stages.findIndex((st) => (st.spawn || []).some((s) => s.kind === 'prop' || s.kind === 'magnet'));\\n      check('op2 tumour after props', tumor > prop && prop >= 0);\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op3') check('op3 three tables and quiet', full.tables.length === 3 && full.persist.quietUnlocked === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op4') check('op4 fragments', full.entities.filter((e) => e.kind === 'fragment' && e.done).length >= 6);\\n    if (def.id === 'op5') check('op5 knock', full.flags.knocked === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op6') check('op6 rewind and pink', full.persist.rewound === true && full.persist.clotSeen === true && full.flags.pink === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op7') check('op7 sob and stalk', (full.strain?.sobs || 0) >= 3 && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'stalk' && e.done));\\n    if (def.id === 'op8') check('op8 shock and massage', full.flags.blueDone === true && full.flags.massaged === true);\\n    if (def.id === 'op9') {\\n      check('op9 lie was up', sawLie);\\n      check('op9 copy and tether', full.flags.copied === true && full.entities.some((e) => e.kind === 'tether' && e.done));\\n    }\\n    if (def.id === 'op10') {\\n      const start = Array.isArray(def.vitals.start) ? def.vitals.start[0] : def.vitals.start;\\n      check('op10 pain and vitals', full.pain > 0 && full.tables[0].vitals > start);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nfunction walk(dir, out = []) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    if (name === 'node_modules' || name === 'dist' || name === 'vendor' || name === 'packs' || name === 'examples') continue;\\n    const p = join(dir, name);\\n    const st = statSync(p);\\n    if (st.isDirectory()) walk(p, out);\\n    else if (/\\\\.(js|mjs|html|md)$/.test(name) && !name.includes('pixel-engine')) out.push(p);\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction testContent() {\\n  const banned = [String.fromCharCode(84, 79, 68, 79), 'place' + 'holder', 'st' + 'ub'];\\n  const names = ['Derek Stiles', 'Angie Thompson', 'Naomi Kimishima', 'Nozomi Weaver', 'Hope Hospital', 'Caduceus', 'Delphi', 'GUILT', 'Healing Touch', 'Kyriaki', 'Deftera', 'Triti', 'Tetarti', 'Pempti', 'Paraskevi', 'Savato'];\\n  const files = walk(join(root, 'src')).concat(walk(join(root, 'docs'))).filter((p) => !p.endsWith('run.mjs'));\\n  let bad = '';\\n  for (const file of files) {\\n    const text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\\n    for (const word of banned) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\\n    for (const word of names) if (text.includes(word)) bad = `${file} ${word}`;\\n  }\\n  check('shipped source is clean', bad === '');\\n  return bad;\\n}\\n\\nconst arg = process.argv[2] || 'default';\\nconst want = new Set(\\n  arg === 'all' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio', 'browser', 'launch', 'hub']\\n    : arg === 'default' ? ['sim', 'content', 'audio']\\n      : [arg],\\n);\\n\\nif (want.has('sim') || want.has('cal')) {\\n  testTools();\\n  testGifts();\\n  testRankSlidersCodec();\\n  testBalance(arg === 'cal');\\n}\\nif (want.has('content')) testContent();\\n\\nif (fails.length) {\\n  for (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f);\\n}\\nconsole.log(`${passed} passed, ${fails.length} failed`);\\nprocess.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"d1bcf790-19f3-402f-85a7-16cab344299f"}
