,50,53,58,45,32,96,119,97,115,80,114,101,115,115,101,100,40,46,46,46,99,111,100,101,115,58,32,115,116,114,105,110,103,91,93,41,58,32,98,111,111,108,101,97,110,96,58,32,84,114,117,101,32,111,110,99,101,32,112,101,114,32,112,104,121,115,105,99,97,108,32,107,101,121,32,112,114,101,115,115,32,40,118,97,108,105,100,32,102,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,99,117,114,114,101,110,116,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,32,102,114,97,109,101,41,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":594,\"content\":\"- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\"},{\"line_number\":2275,\"content\":\"KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \\\"standard\\\" layout:\"},{\"line_number\":2290,\"content\":\"- Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\"},{\"line_number\":2294,\"content\":\"  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\"},{\"line_number\":2304,\"content\":\"- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\"},{\"line_number\":2311,\"content\":\"- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\"},{\"line_number\":2322,\"content\":\"- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\"},{\"line_number\":2325,\"content\":\"- `wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame).\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e845af96-6044-4365-bf67-b4a814c59634-107","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e845af96-6044-4365-bf67-b4a814c59634-108","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"366→## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"366→## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n370→**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n380→\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":366,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"## 7. Multiplayer: Consult\\n\\nOne sim, N seats. The sim doesn't care where a seat's input comes from, so both paths below share everything.\\n\\n**How I read \\\"for the game on its own\\\".** The hub's check opens the game outside a session and needs it to run normally, so that must work. A 10-foot game should also have multiplayer without a hub, so I added **couch co-op**.\\n\\n- **On its own (no network):** Main menu, then CONSULT. Up to 4 seats: keyboard and mouse plus pads. Press ✕ or click to scrub in, ○ or right-click to leave, and seat 1 starts.\\n  - Picks: Pile-Up, or any cleared op except Op 3 and Op 9.\\n  - All hands share the screen, with gloves in seat colours and a small tool icon by each tip.\\n  - The tool wheel for a seat shows near its corner.\\n  - Never touch the network outside a session.\\n- **In AI Hub:** the protocol's `shared-world` mode, 1 to 4 seats, the game's own card.\\n- **Scaling:** vitals drain and spawn rates ×`(1 + 0.25 · (N − 1))`. Composure is shared. Seats 1 and 3 have The Quiet, seats 2 and 4 The Second Look. Each seat scores its own points.\\n- Paddles and Massage: any seat may press either side, so two players can each take a paddle.\\n\\n### AI Hub session (protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\\n\\nFetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` (✔ public) and read that folder's `README.md`.\\n\\n✔ A spike with this exact shape passed every run: the real engine in every copy, 2 and 4 players, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss, host-leave, server, solo. It was ready in under 2 s on software WebGPU.\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.AIHub?.active) {\\n  const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"9326eef7-fee4-418f-8db5-db9e536764b0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_146","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e24f8299-869b-4c37-b394-fd066dfddf50-109","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/session.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e24f8299-869b-4c37-b394-fd066dfddf50-110","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"active|function connect|AIHub","glob":"vendor/README.md","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3725,"output_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":149248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"46fe9eeb-3750-4844-ad14-a03d23e7521f"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e24f8299-869b-4c37-b394-fd066dfddf50-109","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\\n(function (root) {\\n  'use strict';\\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\\n\\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\\n10→  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\\n\\n  var framed = false;\\n  try {\\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\\n  } catch (e) {\\n    framed = true;\\n  }\\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\\n20→  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\\\d+)/.exec(search);\\n\\n  var hub = {\\n    version: VERSION,\\n    protocol: 1,\\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\\n    me: null,\\n    host: null,\\n30→    isHost: false,\\n    players: [],\\n    mode: null,\\n    seed: 0,\\n    limitMs: 0,\\n    round: 0,\\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\\n    splash: false,\\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\\n    seeded: false,\\n40→  };\\n\\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\\n  function memoryStorage() {\\n    var data = Object.create(null);\\n    var api = {\\n      getItem: function (k) {\\n        k = String(k);\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\\n      },\\n50→      setItem: function (k, v) {\\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\\n      },\\n      removeItem: function (k) {\\n        delete data[String(k)];\\n      },\\n      clear: function () {\\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\\n      },\\n      key: function (i) {\\n60→        var keys = Object.keys(data);\\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\\n      },\\n    };\\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\\n    return new Proxy(api, {\\n      get: function (t, k) {\\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\\n70→      },\\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\\n        return true;\\n      },\\n      has: function (t, k) {\\n        return k in data || k in t;\\n      },\\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\\n        delete data[k];\\n80→        return true;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into you