{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e677787e-db7f-4109-854b-7756111b8a36-136","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2295→- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n  the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n  finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n  a frame is not lost.\\n2300→- Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game…\\n\\n- `new Input(target: Window | null = window)`\\n- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\\n- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n- `wheel: number`: Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out).\\n- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\\n- `readonly analog: { x: number; y: number; }`: Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active.\\n- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\\n- `gamepadConnected: boolean`: True while any gamepad is connected.\\n2310→- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\\n- `gamepadDeadzone: number`: Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1).\\n- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\\n- `now: number`: Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`.\\n- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n- `pressWindow: number`: Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped.\\n- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas).\\n- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\\n2320→- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\\n- `beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void`: Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\\n- `isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean`\\n- `anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code).\\n- `wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame).\\n- `consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a pause, a l…\\n- `consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array.\\n- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\\n- `setState(s: InputState, now: number): void`: Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go.\\n2330→- `get queuedPresses: string[]`: Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests).\\n- `clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void`: Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input).\\n- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n- `endFrame(): void`: Call at the end of each rendered frame.\\n- `setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void`: Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false).\\n- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\\n- `setButtons(bits: number): void`: Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would.\\n- `get mouseButtons: number`: Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`.\\n- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\\n- `send(command: unknown): void`: Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked, a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keep…\\n2340→- `get commands: readonly unknown[]`: This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\\n- `deliver(): void`: Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`.\\n- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\\n- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\\n- `playBefore(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\",\"content_concise\":\"2295→- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n  the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n  finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n  a frame is not lost.\\n2300→- Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game…\\n\\n- `new Input(target: Window | null = window)`\\n- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\\n- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n- `wheel: number`: Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out).\\n- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\\n- `readonly analog: { x: number; y: number; }`: Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active.\\n- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\\n- `gamepadConnected: boolean`: True while any gamepad is connected.\\n2310→- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\\n- `gamepadDeadzone: number`: Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1).\\n- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\\n- `now: number`: Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`.\\n- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n- `pressWindow: number`: Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped.\\n- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas).\\n- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\\n2320→- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\\n- `beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void`: Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\\n- `isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean`\\n- `anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code).\\n- `wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame).\\n- `consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a pause, a l…\\n- `consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array.\\n- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\\n- `setState(s: InputState, now: number): void`: Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go.\\n2330→- `get queuedPresses: string[]`: Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests).\\n- `clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void`: Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input).\\n- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n- `endFrame(): void`: Call at the end of each rendered frame.\\n- `setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void`: Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false).\\n- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\\n- `setButtons(bits: number): void`: Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would.\\n- `get mouseButtons: number`: Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`.\\n- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\\n- `send(command: unknown): void`: Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked, a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keep…\\n2340→- `get commands: readonly unknown[]`: This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\\n- `deliver(): void`: Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`.\\n- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\\n- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\\n- `playBefore(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"offset\":2295,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n  the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n  finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n  a frame is not lost.\\n- Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game…\\n\\n- `new Input(target: Window | null = window)`\\n- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\\n- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n- `wheel: number`: Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out).\\n- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\\n- `readonly analog: { x: number; y: number; }`: Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active.\\n- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\\n- `gamepadConnected: boolean`: True while any gamepad is connected.\\n- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\\n- `gamepadDeadzone: number`: Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1).\\n- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\\n- `now: number`: Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`.\\n- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n- `pressWindow: number`: Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped.\\n- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas).\\n- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\\n- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\\n- `beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void`: Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\\n- `isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean`\\n- `anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code).\\n- `wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame).\\n- `consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a pause, a l…\\n- `consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array.\\n- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\\n- `setState(s: InputState, now: number): void`: Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go.\\n- `get queuedPresses: string[]`: Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests).\\n- `clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void`: Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input).\\n- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n- `endFrame(): void`: Call at the end of each rendered frame.\\n- `setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void`: Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false).\\n- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\\n- `setButtons(bits: number): void`: Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would.\\n- `get mouseButtons: number`: Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`.\\n- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\\n- `send(command: unknown): void`: Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked, a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keep…\\n- `get commands: readonly unknown[]`: This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\\n- `deliver(): void`: Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`.\\n- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\\n- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\\n- `playBefore(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"2aa0fcbc-46ac-42c9-9be6-bba67e73ffaf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_163","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"wasPressed applies to the current render frame, not fixedUpdate.\n\nMenu input will be read in update() using wasPressed and consumePress. Gamepad buttons will be polled manually since the button map is empty. Edge detection requires storing previous button states. Right stick axes 2 and 3 control tools when magnitude exceeds 0.6. R2 triggers tool 7 at analog value above 0.4. L2 triggers gift tool 6. moveAxis may include d-pad and WASD even without gamepad button mappings.\n\nKeyboard and d-pad input will use isDown to avoid double-counting with the gamepad sticks.\n\nMouse input will use pointer movement as the last device key. Wheel events will be read from ctx.input.wheel in update(). Tab will be added to preventKeys, and a contextmenu listener will be attached to the canvas during setup. Pointer lock will be disabled. The camera position and lookAt target will be set at the end of each update, though the rig may overwrite them afterward.\n\nZoom limits will be set to 1 so the wheel controls tools instead of zooming. The rig may consume wheel events, so I will check for wheel input in fixedUpdate at the start and again in update.\n\nWheel input will be sampled in both fixed and update cycles and latched. The results stamp will display a large letter rank. A dev mode panel will list sliders and offer L1/R1 or Q/E tabs for toggling between sliders, cheats, jump, and view modes; the user can navigate with clicks or the D-pad. Slider changes will apply live via applySlider because the simulation holds a reference to the config object. Resetting will call resetConfig(). Cheat buttons will invoke devCheat directly, and the jump option will let the user select a stage to load.\n\nThe UI will avoid the word \"stub\". An authoring document and a build script will be added. The bundled HTML will use inline assets to minimize extra requests. Head tags will include a data-URL SVG favicon, description, theme-color, and meta hub tags.\n\nThe title will be \"The Second Opinion Clinic — The truth, stat.\" The build script can import the title from src/core/meta.js because the project uses ES modules. It will copy harness.html and the root HTML into dist/ without minifying. Script tags will be escaped and session data prepended verbatim. The Kenney pixel asset placeholder will be included even if unused.\n\nThe Kenney pixel asset will be embedded as base64 to match the build recipe, adding roughly 675 KB. The bundle should remain around 7 MB total. Setup will guard against a fake document in headless environments. Directional and ambient lights will be added to the scene, and a point light will be requested at [0, 5.2, 0.4] with intensity 5 and radius 15.\n\nThe engine background will be set to 0x141018. Tissue will receive shadows. Menu hover coordinates will be converted from NDC to art pixels.\n\nMenu items will be checked against known rectangles. The pointer index becomes the active focus when the cursor is inside an item. A click on MouseLeft confirms the selection. The last pointer position is stored to detect movement and set the input device key. The default controller glyph set is PS, but it can be overridden to Xbox in settings.\n\nThe confirmation button label will be ENTER for keyboard input, A for Xbox glyphs, and CROSS otherwise. An idle timer will return the user to the title screen after ten seconds of inactivity on the title and menu screens; it resets on any input. The attract mode will run an op1 simulation with god mode and bots enabled, display a banner on the HUD, and destroy the simulation without saving.\n\nA touch gate will block the game until the user presses a key or connects a gamepad. The gate element uses the exact text and sits beside the engine settings gear. A touch-only detector checks for fine pointers, touch points, and connected gamepads.\n\nThe touch gate will be a full-screen overlay with pointer-events none so it does not block the engine settings button. It shows the required controller or keyboard prompt. The detection logic returns true only for touch-only devices with no fine pointer and no connected gamepad.\n\nThe overlay z-index will be 5 so the engine settings gear remains clickable. The gate text must match exactly for test detection. No extra settings controls or joysticks will be added. Tests for content and audio will be included in run.mjs.\n\nBrowser tests will be written in the same run.mjs file and launched by Playwright. They will be excluded from the default filter so they do not run automatically. Screenshots will be saved to the scratch directory, and the test runner will accept a SCRATCH environment variable or fall back to a hardcoded path. The verifier audits both committed tests and saved evidence.\n\nEvidence files must be written to scratch during the goal so the verifier can audit them. The committed tests remain in the dev folder, while scratch holds the live proof.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim suite is green (96 passed). Par matches the skill-1 scores. Next I’ll add the story, audio, and the playable shell."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-137","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"2","content":"Pure sim + Op 1 tools and tests","status":"completed"},{"id":"3","content":"Scalpel, laser, scanner, ops 2-3, Code Blue, Quiet, bot balance","status":"completed"},{"id":"6","content":"Remaining ops, Second Look, strains, campaign playthrough","status":"completed"},{"id":"4","content":"Story, voices, music, results, saves for episodes 1-3","status":"in_progress"},{"id":"5","content":"Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch, About","status":"pending"},{"id":"7","content":"Couch Consult + AI Hub session, card, net, five harnesses","status":"pending"},{"id":"8","content":"Balance, authoring note, exit interview, root HTML, launch + test evidence","status":"pending"}],"merge":true}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-138","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/story.js","content":"/** Story scenes. Each line is one HUD row: at most 57 characters, font charset only. */\n\nexport const CAST = {\n  ilya: { name: 'Ilya Marsh', role: 'Resident', timbre: 0, pitch: 1.18, speed: 1.25, color: '#3aa0a8' },\n  reyes: { name: 'Odalys Reyes', role: 'Scrub nurse', timbre: 1, pitch: 0.86, speed: 1.15, color: '#1e3a5f' },\n  sabine: { name: 'Sabine Achterberg', role: 'Consultant', timbre: 2, pitch: 0.78, speed: 0.82, color: '#6b3a55' },\n  bram: { name: 'Cornelius Bram', role: 'Chief of Surgery', timbre: 1, pitch: 0.62, speed: 0.75, color: '#d8d2c8' },\n  pem: { name: 'Pemberton Okoye', role: 'Anaesthetist', timbre: 0, pitch: 0.8, speed: 0.9, color: '#e07a2f' },\n  hesper: { name: 'Hesper Lindqvist', role: 'Foundation', timbre: 2, pitch: 0.96, speed: 0.7, color: '#f4f1ea' },\n  patient: { name: 'Patient', role: 'Chart', timbre: 0, pitch: 1, speed: 0.95, color: '#c4a484' },\n};\n\nconst line = (who, say) => ({ who, say });\n\nexport const SCENES = [\n  {\n    id: 'night',\n    set: 'or7',\n    title: 'Night shift',\n    op: 'op1',\n    lines: [\n      line('reyes', 'Storm on the glass. The chief is not picking up.'),\n      line('reyes', 'You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.'),\n      line('ilya', 'I can do this. Nurse Reyes, can I do this?'),\n      line('reyes', 'Deckhand Tomasz Dolan. Eleven hooks in one arm.'),\n      line('patient', 'It was a long net. Please do not ask again.'),\n      line('reyes', 'His daughter is married on Saturday. Hands in.'),\n      line('ilya', 'OR-7. The truth, stat. I will not freeze.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Drain first. Then the hooks. Then you count.'),\n      line('pem', 'He is under. Sleeping like a costly baby.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Scalpel later. The sharp end faces the patient.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'rounds',\n    set: 'ward',\n    title: 'Morning rounds',\n    op: 'op2',\n    lines: [\n      line('ilya', 'Rounds. I have the charts. I think I do.'),\n      line('pem', 'You have the charts. You also have coffee on them.'),\n      line('reyes', 'The Great Zamboni swallowed half his act.'),\n      line('patient', 'A magician never reveals the method, Doctor.'),\n      line('pem', 'He will reveal it on the table. That is the method.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Key, coin, card, magnet. He smiled the whole time.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Find every prop. Then find what is not a prop.'),\n      line('ilya', 'If the stomach is a stage, I hate the encore.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Less poetry. More scanner. He is waiting.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'ferry',\n    set: 'corridor',\n    title: 'Mass casualty',\n    op: 'op3',\n    lines: [\n      line('reyes', 'Ferry collision. Three tables. One of you.'),\n      line('bram', 'Charts. Take them. My hand is... it is fine.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Chief, your hand is shaking.'),\n      line('bram', 'Old hands shake. Young hands work. Go.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Table one is bleeding. Table two is glass.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Table three has a polyp and no time.'),\n      line('ilya', 'I cannot be in three places.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Then be fast. And do not let the room go quiet.'),\n      line('pem', 'Vitals are in the basement. Take the stairs.'),\n      line('ilya', 'I can hear my own pulse. That is new.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'office',\n    set: 'office',\n    title: 'Aftermath',\n    op: 'op4',\n    lines: [\n      line('bram', 'How long did the room go quiet?'),\n      line('ilya', 'I do not know. The monitors slowed down.'),\n      line('bram', 'I know that quiet. I used to live inside it.'),\n      line('reyes', 'The Foundation complained to the board.'),\n      line('bram', 'So they sent a consultant. Be polite. Be exact.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Dr. Achterberg. I audit the work, not the legend.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Teen ferry survivor. Ollie Brandt. Bone is a puzzle.'),\n      line('ilya', 'You have two opinions already?'),\n      line('sabine', 'You have two options. The second is also wrong.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Gallery intercom is live. She can hear you panic.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'smile',\n    set: 'ward',\n    title: 'The smiling ward',\n    op: 'op5',\n    lines: [\n      line('reyes', 'Harbour pilot Anselm. Abdomen like a bag of knives.'),\n      line('patient', 'Is it not wonderful? I cannot feel a thing.'),\n      line('ilya', 'That is not wonderful. That is a warning.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Do not answer it until you are ready.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Answer what?'),\n      line('patient', 'It knocks when the room is kind to me.'),\n      line('ilya', 'It moved. Nurse Reyes, the liver moved.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Livers do not move, Doctor.'),\n      line('ilya', 'This one knocked.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Get it out. I will be quiet now. You should not.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'file',\n    set: 'scrub',\n    title: 'The file',\n    op: 'op6',\n    lines: [\n      line('sabine', 'I have seen this. A relief camp. I was blamed.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Blamed for what?'),\n      line('sabine', 'For a comfort that eats. They named it MERC-Y.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Metabolic endo-receptor cytoform, type Y.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Spoken as Mercy. It kills pain. Then it feeds.'),\n      line('ilya', 'The Foundation banked a donor kidney.'),\n      line('sabine', 'I will take this one. You assist. Watch the clock.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Dr. Achterberg operates. Ilya, second look is hers.'),\n      line('sabine', 'If the colour is wrong, rewind. Do not argue.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Ada Okoye is twenty-nine. She teaches children.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'visit',\n    set: 'atrium',\n    title: 'The visit',\n    op: 'op7',\n    lines: [\n      line('hesper', 'Flowers for the ward. And a funding offer.'),\n      line('hesper', 'No one should hurt, Doctor. Not even you.'),\n      line('ilya', 'People should get to say where they hurt.'),\n      line('hesper', 'Pain is only the body begging. I taught it to stop.'),\n      line('reyes', 'My oldest friend was admitted this hour.'),\n      line('patient', 'Ottilie Marr. Hospice nurse. I am smiling. See?'),\n      line('reyes', 'She never smiles like that. Cut the smile off.'),\n      line('ilya', 'If she feels it again, we did the right thing.'),\n      line('sabine', 'The eyes open in turn. Do not let them weep out.'),\n      line('reyes', 'I will cry later. Alone. Do the work.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'confess',\n    set: 'office',\n    title: 'The confession',\n    op: 'op8',\n    lines: [\n      line('bram', 'I co-wrote the paper. I was proud of it.'),\n      line('ilya', 'You made Mercy?'),\n      line('bram', 'I made a quiet room. She made a product.'),\n      line('hesper', 'Dawn ferries. A fine mist. No one should hurt.'),\n      line('bram', 'My tremor was never age. It was feeding.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Chief!'),\n      line('bram', 'On the heart. Diastole only. Do not be gentle.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Do not you dare be gentle.'),\n      line('bram', 'The old scalpel is yours. Show up tomorrow.'),\n      line('pem', 'I am here. The boat can wait. So can retirement.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'roof',\n    set: 'helipad',\n    title: 'The roof',\n    op: 'op9',\n    lines: [\n      line('ilya', 'The canister is on the helipad. Rain, of course.'),\n      line('sabine', 'We stop the release. Then we deal with her.'),\n      line('hesper', 'You cannot cure me of being right.'),\n      line('ilya', 'We are not here to cure you. We are here to stop you.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Seal is failing. Get the patient off this roof.'),\n      line('hesper', 'It is only comfort.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Start without me.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Reyes!'),\n      line('sabine', 'No voice in your ear. Both of us. Now.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Table is open. I will not wait for permission.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'stretcher',\n    set: 'or7',\n    title: 'The stretcher',\n    op: 'op10',\n    lines: [\n      line('hesper', 'I took the first dose. Eleven years ago.'),\n      line('hesper', 'I would not ask of anyone what I would not take.'),\n      line('sabine', 'She is dying of her own kindness.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Everyone is looking at you, Doctor.'),\n      line('ilya', 'Scrub in.'),\n      line('pem', 'She will feel this. That is the point, I think.'),\n      line('ilya', 'A pale strain along the spine. It does not fight.'),\n      line('hesper', 'Why does it hurt?'),\n      line('ilya', 'Because it is my shift.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Slow. Pain means she is still here.'),\n    ],\n  },\n  {\n    id: 'morning',\n    set: 'roof',\n    title: 'Morning',\n    op: null,\n    lines: [\n      line('ilya', 'The rain stopped. I do not trust it.'),\n      line('reyes', 'You have a seven a.m. Do not be late.'),\n      line('ilya', 'You are in a wheelchair.'),\n      line('reyes', 'And you are still holding coffee. We persist.'),\n      line('sabine', 'Shift report is on the desk. Read every rank.'),\n      line('pem', 'I did not retire. The boat took it personally.'),\n      line('bram', 'Medicine is not miracles. It is tomorrow.'),\n      line('ilya', 'The truth, stat.'),\n      line('reyes', 'Adequate. Do not let it go to your head.'),\n    ],\n  },\n];\n\nexport function sceneById(id) {\n  return SCENES.find((s) => s.id === id) || null;\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-139","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/about.js","content":"/** About / Credits copy. The exit interview uses these same strings. */\n\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:40:40',\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\n  genre: 'Simulation',\n  perspective: 'Fixed overhead surgical view',\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.28.2',\n  artDirection: 'Engine pixel-toon look, original OR sets, primitive busts, canvas tissue',\n  animation: 'Engine clock plus sim-driven tool motion, heart pulse, and code-blue needle',\n  audio: 'Original chiptune songs, SoundDef effects, and formant gibberish voices. No audio files.',\n  online: 'Couch consult on one machine, and AI Hub shared-world for 1 to 4 players. No other network.',\n  testing: 'Node sim suite, Playwright on software WebGPU, hub harness on 127.0.0.1. No physical pad, no second person, no iOS Safari, no TV.',\n  research: 'The planner read the source Wikipedia page, the hub protocol, and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes. This build followed PLAN.md and the engine docs on this machine.',\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\n  usage: 'added on import',\n};\n\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  'Testing caught 7 issues: a string id compared as a number, a magnet pull that snapped, overlapping suture targets, a missing clot flag, a copy-hand that ended before it landed, and 2 syringe asserts that used the wrong keeper.',\n  '4 would be game-breaking: hooks never left the field, the magnet could not be extracted, Op 5 never closed, and the transplant skipped its forced rewind.',\n  'The most helpful test was the skill-1 bot play of every operation, which failed in the live sim and named the stuck entity.',\n  'The least helpful test was a screenshot of a menu with no input behind it. Appearance did not show whether focus moved.',\n];\n\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\n  'The pure renderSound and Song data made every effect and track testable in Node, and the HUD art-pixel grid matched the fill-mode canvas.',\n  'I guessed wrong once: a held entity id is a string, so a numeric comparison never saw the grab. The fixed camera and the audio storage key behaved as the guide describes.',\n  'The operation sim, the eight tools, the strains, couch seats, and the shared-world host loop. The engine does not ship a surgery model.',\n  'Keeping pad buttons from also pressing keyboard keys, while still reading analog triggers, took the longest to get straight.',\n  'none',\n  'A way to mark a gamepad button as \"read it yourself\" without clearing the whole map by hand.',\n];\n\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  'The plan named the beats, the tools, and the pass lines, so the game could be built against checks instead of a vibe.',\n  'Two documents both said how to boot, and they disagreed about whether screens swap by loading a new game. Pause had to stay inside one game or the music died.',\n  'Making one bot clear every operation at the top rank, including the rewind and the two-handed pull, without lowering par.',\n  'Ask for the exit-interview counts after the suite has run, and name one file as the only source of the balance numbers.',\n];\n\nexport const AI_HUB = {\n  name: 'The Second Opinion Clinic',\n  tagline: 'The truth, stat.',\n  description: 'A rainy harbour hospital where telling the truth is the first cut. Keep the patient alive, close the strain, and top the team score.',\n  type: 'Game',\n  genre: 'Simulation',\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\n  series: 'Trauma Center',\n  players: '1\\u20134',\n  controls: 'Stick or mouse moves the tool. R2 or click uses it. Right stick or keys 1-8 pick a tool.',\n  tags: ['3d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\n};\n\nexport const ABOUT_FIELDS = [\n  ['Date', SOURCE_INFORMATION.date],\n  ['Source', SOURCE_INFORMATION.source],\n  ['Plan', SOURCE_INFORMATION.plan],\n  ['Genre and Perspective', `${SOURCE_INFORMATION.genre}; ${SOURCE_INFORMATION.perspective}`],\n  ['Tech', SOURCE_INFORMATION.tech],\n  ['Art Direction', SOURCE_INFORMATION.artDirection],\n  ['Animation', SOURCE_INFORMATION.animation],\n  ['Audio', SOURCE_INFORMATION.audio],\n  ['Online', SOURCE_INFORMATION.online],\n  ['Testing', SOURCE_INFORMATION.testing],\n  ['Research', SOURCE_INFORMATION.research],\n  ['Environment', SOURCE_INFORMATION.environment],\n  ['Model', SOURCE_INFORMATION.model],\n  ['Usage', SOURCE_INFORMATION.usage],\n];\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-140","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/campaign.js","content":"import { STORY_OPS } from './ops.js';\nimport { SCENES } from './story.js';\nimport { clearSave, emptySave, writeSave } from '../core/save.js';\nimport { play } from '../sim/run.js';\n\n/** Bot play from the first scene through the last operation and into the credits. */\nexport function playCampaign(opts = {}) {\n  clearSave();\n  const save = emptySave();\n  const skill = opts.skill ?? 1;\n  const results = [];\n  for (const scene of SCENES) {\n    save.scenes.push(scene.id);\n    if (!scene.op) continue;\n    const def = STORY_OPS.find((op) => op.id === scene.op);\n    const sim = play(def, skill, { seed: opts.seed ?? 1 });\n    save.ops[def.id] = { rank: sim.rank, score: sim.finalScore, won: sim.phase === 'won' };\n    if (def.id === 'op3' && sim.phase === 'won') save.quiet = true;\n    results.push(sim);\n    writeSave(save);\n  }\n  save.log = true;\n  save.credits = true;\n  writeSave(save);\n  return { save, results };\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1878,"output_tokens":7395,"cache_read_input_tokens":181760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"f1246a32-03dd-49d3-a623-3a2e86aa026e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-137","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [in_progress] 1: RNG title, download kit + hub, boot empty scene from file://\\n- [completed] 2: Pure sim + Op 1 tools and tests\\n- [completed] 3: Scalpel, laser, scanner, ops 2-3, Code Blue, Quiet, bot balance\\n- [in_progress] 4: Story, voices, music, results, saves for episodes 1-3\\n- [pending] 5: Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch, About\\n- [completed] 6: Remaining ops, Second Look, strains, campaign playthrough\\n- [pending] 7: Couch Consult + AI Hub session, card, net, five harnesses\\n- [pending] 8: Balance, authoring note, exit interview, root HTML, launch + test evidence\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"RNG title, download kit + hub, boot empty scene from file://\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Pure sim + Op 1 tools and tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Scalpel, laser, scanner, ops 2-3, Code Blue, Quiet, bot balance\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Story, voices, music, results, saves for episodes 1-3\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch, About\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Remaining ops, Second Look, strains, campaign playthrough\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Couch Consult + AI Hub session, card, net, five harnesses\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Balance, authoring note, exit interview, root HTML, launch + test evidence\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"1\":{\"content\":\"RNG title, download kit + hub, boot empty scene from file://\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},\"2\":{\"content\":\"Pure sim + Op 1 tools and tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"3\":{\"content\":\"Scalpel, laser, scanner, ops 2-3, Code Blue, Quiet, bot balance\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"4\":{\"content\":\"Story, voices, music, results, saves for episodes 1-3\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},\"5\":{\"content\":\"Title, menus, prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode, attract, touch, About\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"6\":{\"content\":\"Remaining ops, Second Look, strains, campaign playthrough\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"7\":{\"content\":\"Couch Consult + AI Hub session, card, net, five harnesses\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"},\"8\":{\"content\":\"Balance, authoring note, exit interview, root HTML, launch + test evidence\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a01ba828-40dc-454d-9c60-3e978ab0e839-138","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** Story scenes. Each line is one HUD row: at most 57 characters, font charset only. */\\n\\nexport const CAST = {\\n  ilya: { name: 'Ilya Marsh', role: 'Resident', timbre: 0, pitch: 1.18, speed: 1.25, color: '#3aa0a8' },\\n  reyes: { name: 'Odalys Reyes', role: 'Scrub nurse', timbre: 1, pitch: 0.86, speed: 1.15, color: '#1e3a5f' },\\n  sabine: { name: 'Sabine Achterberg', role: 'Consultant', timbre: 2, pitch: 0.78, speed: 0.82, color: '#6b3a55' },\\n  bram: { name: 'Cornelius Bram', role: 'Chief of Surgery', timbre: 1, pitch: 0.62, speed: 0.75, color: '#d8d2c8' },\\n  pem: { name: 'Pemberton Okoye', role: 'Anaesthetist', timbre: 0, pitch: 0.8, speed: 0.9, color: '#e07a2f' },\\n  hesper: { name: 'Hesper Lindqvist', role: 'Foundation', timbre: 2, pitch: 0.96, speed: 0.7, color: '#f4f1ea' },\\n  patient: { name: 'Patient', role: 'Chart', timbre: 0, pitch: 1, speed: 0.95, color: '#c4a484' },\\n};\\n\\nconst line = (who, say) => ({ who, say });\\n\\nexport const SCENES = [\\n  {\\n    id: 'night',\\n    set: 'or7',\\n    title: 'Night shift',\\n    op: 'op1',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('reyes', 'Storm on the glass. The chief is not picking up.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'You. Yes, you. The one holding the coffee.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'I can do this. Nurse Reyes, can I do this?'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Deckhand Tomasz Dolan. Eleven hooks in one arm.'),\\n      line('patient', 'It was a long net. Please do not ask again.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'His daughter is married on Saturday. Hands in.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'OR-7. The truth, stat. I will not freeze.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Drain first. Then the hooks. Then you count.'),\\n      line('pem', 'He is under. Sleeping like a costly baby.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Scalpel later. The sharp end faces the patient.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'rounds',\\n    set: 'ward',\\n    title: 'Morning rounds',\\n    op: 'op2',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('ilya', 'Rounds. I have the charts. I think I do.'),\\n      line('pem', 'You have the charts. You also have coffee on them.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'The Great Zamboni swallowed half his act.'),\\n      line('patient', 'A magician never reveals the method, Doctor.'),\\n      line('pem', 'He will reveal it on the table. That is the method.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Key, coin, card, magnet. He smiled the whole time.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Find every prop. Then find what is not a prop.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'If the stomach is a stage, I hate the encore.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Less poetry. More scanner. He is waiting.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'ferry',\\n    set: 'corridor',\\n    title: 'Mass casualty',\\n    op: 'op3',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('reyes', 'Ferry collision. Three tables. One of you.'),\\n      line('bram', 'Charts. Take them. My hand is... it is fine.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Chief, your hand is shaking.'),\\n      line('bram', 'Old hands shake. Young hands work. Go.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Table one is bleeding. Table two is glass.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Table three has a polyp and no time.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'I cannot be in three places.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Then be fast. And do not let the room go quiet.'),\\n      line('pem', 'Vitals are in the basement. Take the stairs.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'I can hear my own pulse. That is new.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'office',\\n    set: 'office',\\n    title: 'Aftermath',\\n    op: 'op4',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('bram', 'How long did the room go quiet?'),\\n      line('ilya', 'I do not know. The monitors slowed down.'),\\n      line('bram', 'I know that quiet. I used to live inside it.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'The Foundation complained to the board.'),\\n      line('bram', 'So they sent a consultant. Be polite. Be exact.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Dr. Achterberg. I audit the work, not the legend.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Teen ferry survivor. Ollie Brandt. Bone is a puzzle.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'You have two opinions already?'),\\n      line('sabine', 'You have two options. The second is also wrong.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Gallery intercom is live. She can hear you panic.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'smile',\\n    set: 'ward',\\n    title: 'The smiling ward',\\n    op: 'op5',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('reyes', 'Harbour pilot Anselm. Abdomen like a bag of knives.'),\\n      line('patient', 'Is it not wonderful? I cannot feel a thing.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'That is not wonderful. That is a warning.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Do not answer it until you are ready.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Answer what?'),\\n      line('patient', 'It knocks when the room is kind to me.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'It moved. Nurse Reyes, the liver moved.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Livers do not move, Doctor.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'This one knocked.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Get it out. I will be quiet now. You should not.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'file',\\n    set: 'scrub',\\n    title: 'The file',\\n    op: 'op6',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('sabine', 'I have seen this. A relief camp. I was blamed.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Blamed for what?'),\\n      line('sabine', 'For a comfort that eats. They named it MERC-Y.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Metabolic endo-receptor cytoform, type Y.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Spoken as Mercy. It kills pain. Then it feeds.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'The Foundation banked a donor kidney.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'I will take this one. You assist. Watch the clock.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Dr. Achterberg operates. Ilya, second look is hers.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'If the colour is wrong, rewind. Do not argue.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Ada Okoye is twenty-nine. She teaches children.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'visit',\\n    set: 'atrium',\\n    title: 'The visit',\\n    op: 'op7',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('hesper', 'Flowers for the ward. And a funding offer.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'No one should hurt, Doctor. Not even you.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'People should get to say where they hurt.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'Pain is only the body begging. I taught it to stop.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'My oldest friend was admitted this hour.'),\\n      line('patient', 'Ottilie Marr. Hospice nurse. I am smiling. See?'),\\n      line('reyes', 'She never smiles like that. Cut the smile off.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'If she feels it again, we did the right thing.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'The eyes open in turn. Do not let them weep out.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'I will cry later. Alone. Do the work.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'confess',\\n    set: 'office',\\n    title: 'The confession',\\n    op: 'op8',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('bram', 'I co-wrote the paper. I was proud of it.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'You made Mercy?'),\\n      line('bram', 'I made a quiet room. She made a product.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'Dawn ferries. A fine mist. No one should hurt.'),\\n      line('bram', 'My tremor was never age. It was feeding.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Chief!'),\\n      line('bram', 'On the heart. Diastole only. Do not be gentle.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Do not you dare be gentle.'),\\n      line('bram', 'The old scalpel is yours. Show up tomorrow.'),\\n      line('pem', 'I am here. The boat can wait. So can retirement.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'roof',\\n    set: 'helipad',\\n    title: 'The roof',\\n    op: 'op9',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('ilya', 'The canister is on the helipad. Rain, of course.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'We stop the release. Then we deal with her.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'You cannot cure me of being right.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'We are not here to cure you. We are here to stop you.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Seal is failing. Get the patient off this roof.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'It is only comfort.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Start without me.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Reyes!'),\\n      line('sabine', 'No voice in your ear. Both of us. Now.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Table is open. I will not wait for permission.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'stretcher',\\n    set: 'or7',\\n    title: 'The stretcher',\\n    op: 'op10',\\n    lines: [\\n      line('hesper', 'I took the first dose. Eleven years ago.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'I would not ask of anyone what I would not take.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'She is dying of her own kindness.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Everyone is looking at you, Doctor.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Scrub in.'),\\n      line('pem', 'She will feel this. That is the point, I think.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'A pale strain along the spine. It does not fight.'),\\n      line('hesper', 'Why does it hurt?'),\\n      line('ilya', 'Because it is my shift.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Slow. Pain means she is still here.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'morning',\\n    set: 'roof',\\n    title: 'Morning',\\n    op: null,\\n    lines: [\\n      line('ilya', 'The rain stopped. I do not trust it.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'You have a seven a.m. Do not be late.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'You are in a wheelchair.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'And you are still holding coffee. We persist.'),\\n      line('sabine', 'Shift report is on the desk. Read every rank.'),\\n      line('pem', 'I did not retire. The boat took it personally.'),\\n      line('bram', 'Medicine is not miracles. It is tomorrow.'),\\n      line('ilya', 'The truth, stat.'),\\n      line('reyes', 'Adequate. Do not let it go to your head.'),\\n    ],\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function sceneById(id) {\\n  return SCENES.find((s) => s.id === id) || null;\\n}\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/story.js has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/story.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/story.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** Story scenes. Each line is one HUD row: at most 57 characters, font charset only. */\\n\\nexport const CAST = {\\n  ilya: { name: 'Ilya Marsh', role: 'Resident', timbre: 0, pitch: 1.18, speed: 1.25, color: '#3aa0a8' },\\n  reyes: { name: 'Odalys Reyes', role: 'Scrub nurse', timbre: 1, pitch: 0.86, speed: 1.15, color: '#1e3a5f' },\\n  sabine: { name: 'Sabine Achterberg', role: 'Consultant', timbre: 2, pitch: 0.78, speed: 0.82, color: '#6b3a55' },\\n  bram: { name: 'Cornelius Bram', role: 'Chief of 