{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_165","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Story lines are valid. Next: audio, then the big game files.\n\nWriting a compact voice renderer and songs in voice.js. Then devices, view, session, app, and game.js. Song patterns will keep the same step count per track.\n\nThe title song is 16 steps per track. I will write several songs for different game states. The music director will pick the right one based on vitals and op id. Voice.js will use a finite buffer and renderSound to avoid silence.\n\nVoice.js is being implemented with a glottal impulse train filtered by two one-pole formants. The renderSyllable function generates 110 ms of audio at 22050 Hz using pitch and vowel parameters.\n\nThe voice renderer is now complete. A pulse train of sine formants will not be silent.\n\nvoiceLine concatenates syllables for letters. voicePcm maps each character to a vowel and assigns a pitch to every character. It uses a cast table with different pitch values for each character.\n\nThe voice renderer now handles spaces and exclamation marks. It concatenates syllable chunks into a single Float32Array. A CLICK sound effect is defined for UI feedback.\n\nTests will verify voicePcm and effectBuffer. The main app is next, written in parts if needed.\n\nPlanned game flow:\n- Title screen accepts any button press to enter the menu.\n- Menu options include Start, Continue, Consult, Log, Settings, and About.\n- Start begins scene 0 for new games or resumes from the next unplayed scene.\n- fixedUpdate runs at 60 fps.\n- Winning a phase advances to results.\n- Story text appears before the operation briefing.\n\nStory text advances on confirm. After the last line it goes to the operation briefing or credits. The briefing shows the patient chart and starts the operation on confirm.\n\nThe results screen shows a rank stamp and a follow-up line. The player confirms to continue the story.\n\nCredits appear after the morning scene. They return to the title screen.\n\nDuring an operation the player can pause with Esc. The pause menu offers Resume, Retry stage, Settings, Dev, and Quit. Consult mode lets the player join seats, pick an operation, and start. Settings controls difficulty, glyph layout, rumble, music volume, SFX, voices, and reset. About scrolls fields and shows feedback. Log lists completed operations and ranks if unlocked.\n\nAttract mode will appear after ten seconds on the title or menu screen. URL parameters can override the initial game mode after setup. If session info exists, the mode card is shown and the title screen is skipped.\n\ndevices.js defines eight tools and a readHuman function that returns input for a seat. Seat zero uses keyboard, mouse, and pad zero. Other seats use only their assigned pad. Device state such as last device, active tool, and previous buttons will be stored in the app.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ee743594-47ab-4d64-bb79-25fe43576e31-142","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"input\\.drop|input\\.steady|input\\.gift","glob":"**/op.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":545,"output_tokens":1743,"cache_read_input_tokens":191360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"3acf4ced-1856-4c66-b1fc-aa274d328a04"}
