2,32,32,32,32,105,102,32,40,105,110,112,117,116,46,115,116,101,97,100,121,41,32,115,112,32,42,61,32,115,105,109,46,99,111,110,102,105,103,46,115,116,101,97,100,121,70,97,99,116,111,114,59,10,51,54,54,58,32,32,32,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,104,101,108,100,32,61,32,33,33,40,105,110,112,117,116,46,103,105,102,116,32,38,38,32,115,101,97,116,46,103,105,102,116,32,61,61,61,32,39,108,111,111,107,39,32,38,38,32,115,105,109,46,112,101,114,115,105,115,116,46,108,111,111,107,85,110,108,111,99,107,101,100,41,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":310,\"content\":\"    if (seat.gift === 'quiet' && input.gift && sim.persist.quietUnlocked) want = true;\"},{\"line_number\":329,\"content\":\"    seat.giftDown = !!input.gift;\"},{\"line_number\":336,\"content\":\"      if (input.steady) sp *= sim.config.steadyFactor;\"},{\"line_number\":346,\"content\":\"      if (input.steady) sp *= sim.config.steadyFactor;\"},{\"line_number\":366,\"content\":\"    const held = !!(input.gift && seat.gift === 'look' && sim.persist.lookUnlocked);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"2f39ac30-1146-40fd-a757-96d0214ec50b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_166","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The drop signal is only read by the simulator as a false releaseHold.\n\nD-pad left/right or Tab cycles tables. E or Triangle swaps the driven seat on op9 partner tables; otherwise it also cycles tables.\n\nMouse aim and stick controls apply only to the driven seat. Solo op9 places the bot in the non-driven seat. Consult mode makes every joined seat human.\n\nCross or click joins the next available seat up to four. Circle or right click leaves. The first player to press start becomes seat one. Confirm starts the game once at least one seat is joined.\n\nPicks are pile or cleared operations excluding op3 and op9.\n\nReplay fingerprints use only simulation state, mode, and focus index. Time-based wall-clock values are excluded.\n\nThe fingerprint string concatenates mode, focus index, simulation hash, and line. Wall-clock attract or menu timing could still diverge between recording and replay. The default ninety idle frames are too short to trigger attract mode.\n\nTitle mode fingerprint is stable and fixedUpdate does nothing to the simulation during that state. Headless environments may lack localStorage, so getItem calls are guarded. The setup routine still invokes setVolume even when localStorage is missing or throws, since a fresh headless run might carry a memory-based store. Music playback for the title song is triggered in setup if no session exists.\n\nStory narration will use a registered sawtooth SoundDef with vibrato. Each character's pitch is set in semitones. A click sound will play on confirm.\n\nThe view module will accept THREE and the toon material as arguments to avoid circular imports. It will also set look layers so actors render above the environment. An entity mesh pool will pre-create up to eighty meshes and hide unused ones. The pool color is set to 0x8b1e3f.\n\nHook and wound entity colors are set to 0xc0c0c0 and 0x6b1020. Mesh positions use x, heightAt+0.05, z. A -PI/2 rotation on the plane geometry maps local Y to world Z, which may flip the texture but is acceptable.\n\nThe entity sync function filters the simulation's entities to only those on the active table and visible. Hands are positioned at each seat's x, height, and z coordinates. A buildBust helper will generate 2-3 mesh groups per character for story mode, with the speaking character's bust rendered brighter.\n\nA 128 by 64 canvas will be painted for each arena to make them visually distinct. The texture uses nearest filtering and flipY is enabled. A monitor quad will sit in the background so the OR reads as a room. app.js will be organized into methods.\n\nSession code is being drafted. `runServerSession` launches a headless network. `startNet` tracks players, simulation state, inputs, and timing hooks. The `begin` function selects the operation for the current round.\n\nThe `begin` function seeds the simulation from the AIHub random generator and creates the operation with consult mode enabled. Network hooks are wired to handle start signals, input messages, snapshots, player leaves, and timeouts.\n\nThe session loop runs at sixty frames per second. It waits for the host to signal start before creating the simulation, then branches between hostTick and clientTick. The host tick computes elapsed time in seconds and advances the simulation by one frame per tick, capped at five updates per cycle while the phase remains play.\n\nThe host tick gathers inputs from each player by seat index and steps the simulation forward by one frame. It then sends a fast snapshot to all clients whenever the JSON payload stays under 1100 bytes. A separate one-second key heartbeat is also being sent.\n\nThe host sends a reliable key heartbeat every second and finishes the session when the phase becomes won or lost. The client sends its local input to the host at fifteen hertz. The host must include its own input in each simulation step.\n\nThe host is treated as a player, so its input is fetched via hooks.localInput and mapped to the seat index. Clients apply decoded snapshots to their local simulation through hooks.onSnap. Both client and host use the same seed from AIHub.rng('deal'), ensuring entity IDs match across devices. The client keeps a local simulation running for display and updates it with applyDecoded. Idle input is sent even when all values are zero.\n\nThe host will send a ping message during the card phase at twelve hertz. The finish function maps each seat index to its player ID and records scores from sim.seats[i].score.\n\nThe finish function groups scores by player ID and sends them to AIHub as standings, stats, and awards. checkStandings rejects missing, duplicated, or unknown entries. Left players are omitted from the list. If the simulation never started at timeout, every player still receives a zero score. The host does not trigger a finish when it leaves.\n\nThe leave handler only deletes input. The host does not finish when it leaves. The session loop stops on end. Audio hooks stop music on end. The options button is ignored during a session. Math.random is avoided; AIHub.rng provides the seed. The server registers network handlers before calling ready(), so pending start events are queued.\n\nThe server host steps the simulation using whatever inputs have arrived, or empty ones if none are ready. A missing human input could cause the patient to be lost, so the session finishes on loss or time-up.\n\nThe server copy returns before Engine.start, so it never starts the engine and avoids canvas creation. Non-host servers only send idle input and do not render. WebGPU is validated only when the engine would actually start, so a missing GPU does not fail the server.\n\nThe server path returns immediately after calling AIHub.ready(). A missing GPU outside a session only triggers the engine's own failure message. gamepadButtons is initialized to an empty object in setup, and Tab is blocked from key input. app.js will be written as a long but complete file. Operation data stores follow-up text in def.follow[sim.rank] or def.reyes, and the HUD say helper uses sim.say with en-dashes converted to hyphens.\n\nA `hudSafe` helper will strip en-dashes, em-dashes, and ellipsis from text before drawing to avoid font glyph issues. Story lines are already safe. The dev slider UI will be a simple list with focus and left/right keys; multipliers will step by 0.05 and integers like maxMistakes or diesBpm by 1.\n\nThe dev slider step map is finalized. Integer parameters like maxMistakes and diesBpm increment by 1, while multipliers default to 0.05. The UI will include a \"RESET DEFAULTS\" focus item and cheat menu entries that call devCheat. Content and audio tests will be added to run.mjs, with the campaign test filtered out because it takes roughly fifteen seconds. Player IDs use an en-dash character. Testing feedback indicates seven issues were caught in this session.\n\nFour issues are critical: holding string comparison, magnet snap, suture overlap, and firstClot not copied. The remaining three are syringe test bugs. I will keep the total at seven and update about.js and the exit interview if more appear during browser tests. Next I will write the remaining app chunks, docs/AUTHORING.md, and update the tests. Then I will run the simulation, content, and audio suites.\n\nAudio tests will import parseSong to validate song structure and catch malformed patterns. The director will map title music to the title song, ward and office story to the ward song, vitals above fifty to or-calm, vitals between thirty and fifty to or-tense, lower vitals to or-critical, boss operations five through nine to the boss song, and silence during the final crooked line.\n\nOperation nine will stay silent until the dressing stage, then play a swell. Operation ten will use a sparse song. The results fanfare plays for S or A ranks and a sad tune otherwise. A helper will build equal-length pattern rows for the songs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aafbd908-ab8e-4b17-b522-179bf782d83f-143","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/index.html","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2021,"output_tokens":4478,"cache_read_input_tokens":191872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a2dd1334-3a01-43f5-8668-88d055523b86"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aafbd908-ab8e-4b17-b522-179bf782d83f-143","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\\n  </head>\\n10→  <body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n    <script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"./game.js\\\"></script>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\\n  </head>\\n10→  <body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n    <script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"./game.js\\\"></script>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/index.html\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\\n  </head>\\n  <body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n    <script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"./game.js\\\"></script>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"total_lines\":14}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"dc9a5ca6-448c-4cbb-9b0e-568ab8a0f5e8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_167","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The dev index.html loads game.js as a module. That module imports pixel-engine.\n\nThe deliverable must be a single inlined HTML file. The dev index.html can remain as the module entry for check.mjs during development. The built HTML is the hand-in. check.mjs serves index.html to boot the game for smoke testing. Session.js must be in the built file's head for hub tests that use dist/game.html. The dev index.html does not include session.js.\n\nThe dev index.html will leave AIHub undefined so standalone mode works. app.js will be comprehensive.\n\nSession.js token bucket and while-loop are being fixed to cap host sends at 17 per second. Host sends 12 Hz snapshots, 1 Hz key events, and 4 Hz pings. Client sends 15 Hz. Both directions stay under the 20 Hz limit. During cards both sides send freely; after play starts the host switches to snapshots and stops pings.\n\nA 16 ms setInterval may drift.\n\nAIHub.time() catch-up will allow up to 30 steps per tick. This prevents hidden tabs from stalling while still keeping the game responsive.\n\nThe game stops stepping and finishes once when the phase is won, preventing double completion.\n\nClient snapshot entity IDs are sliced to 12 characters. The client simulation is seeded at startup with the same seed and player count so entity IDs match across copies. If a player leaves later, the simulation is not recreated. All copies must use the same initial player count to avoid a race condition.\n\nPlayer IDs are captured at connect time to freeze the seed layout. The seed is generated from the RNG, not from player count. Seat positions in snapshots are encoded but applyDecoded does not restore them.\n\nA new `applyNet` helper in session.js will call `applyDecoded` and then restore seat positions, tools, and x/z coordinates from the decoded snapshot. The local player's seat will be marked as local so their cursor does not snap to the remote position.\n\nThe TOOLS list index used for encoding must match the client codec exactly.\n\nThe packet will carry the phase so the client can detect a win and stop stepping. The client will show a simple saved state from the final snapshot rather than complex results, since the hub renders them over the game.\n\nThe stage index will also be included in snapshots so the client can look up the correct say line from def.stages.\n\napplyNet will set sim.say from the stage definition whenever the stage index changes. app.js is the largest file and will be drafted carefully. hashSim must be exported from op.js for fingerprinting. Non-human seats and the partner seat will use botInput when the mode is op but not consult.\n\nA driven seat index will assign human input to one seat and bot input to the rest. In consult mode, every joined seat reads its pad and seat 0 also uses the keyboard. In op mode, only the driven seat gets human input; all other seats use bot input, including attract mode which runs god-mode bots with full skill. The URL parameter `bot=1` forces the human seat to act as a bot for screenshots and tests, while `bot=0` keeps it human. If `?op=op1` is used without `bot`, the human still plays.\n\nLaunch tests call act() to inject a drain, so the bot must be disabled. The launch URL will use ?op=op1&bot=0 so fixedUpdate uses empty human input and does not fight the test step. act() will step once with the input, and fixedUpdate will also step normally. This may produce one extra drain frame from act plus empty engine steps, but that is acceptable if the drain drains enough frames.\n\nTests will call `act()` to drain the pool in one 40-step burst before the next paint. The engine may step a few empty frames afterward, but the test will detect completion by checking whether the pool is done or the round changed.\n\n`get sim()` and `goto(mode)` will be exposed for tests, and `config` will return `getConfig()`.\n\n`window.__GAME__` will be set inside `ready(ctx)`. Because headless builds lack a global `window`, the assignment will use `globalThis` instead.\n\n`globalThis.__GAME__` will be a getter object so `prompts` always returns the current `app.promptLabel()` instead of a stale snapshot.\n\nThe prompt label will be 'CROSS', 'A', or 'ENTER'. Both the `__GAME__.prompts` getter and a live `app.prompts` property will be kept so tests can read either. The app device will also be stored. The canvas will have its context menu blocked with `preventDefault`. Tissue and mesh setup will remain functional even if THREE.js is heavy.\n\nDev mode will have four tabs: sliders, cheats, jump, and view. Q/E or L1/R1 or clicks switch between them.\n\nThe view tab shows the arena name and seed. It also displays entity count and simulation hash. God and freeze buttons remain in the cheats tab.\n\nThe jump tab lists stages from sim.stages.\n\nCheats that need a running operation will show \"open an operation first\" when no op is active. Sliders still work without one.\n\nDifficulty will be wired into createOp from settings.\n\nSettings will only persist to localStorage when `this.allowStore` is true, so attract mode does not trigger saves. The music volume slider calls `setVolume` and then `saveSettings`, writing both the settings object and the pixel-engine audio key. If neither engine audio key nor settings value exists, the default volume is 0.1.\n\nInitial settings will default to glyph set 'ps', difficulty 'resident', rumble enabled, and one voice. The authoring notes will be updated, run.mjs content and audio refreshed, and the test suite executed. Campaign runs may be slowed by raising the block-until threshold. A potential content lint issue in about.js was checked and cleared.\n\nThe about text was checked for banned substrings and cleared. Menu items will record their pixel rectangles during draw so the next frame can test pointer hover.\n\nMenu item rectangles will be stored in `this.itemRects` during draw, with each entry holding the index and vertical position. The pointer art Y coordinate is converted from NDC to screen space using `(0.5 - pointer.y / 2) * height`. Pad focus updates only when the pointer moves or enters a new item, preventing stale hover states from stealing focus every frame.\n\nClicking the left mouse button confirms the current menu selection. Pad navigation will use the dpad edges, and the left stick Y axis will move focus downward when pushed past 0.6; both will be gated by a 180 ms cooldown to prevent rapid scrolling.\n\nThe app will stay under 900 lines.\n\nResults screen shows rank, score, follow line, time, and mistakes. Confirm continues.\n\nBrief shows patient, age, job, hook, and objective. Confirm starts the operation.\n\nLog lists saved operations. Credits roll morning lines, a cast snippet, \"LOG UNLOCKED\", then return to title. Morning lines unlock the log and credits.\n\nStart new game begins at scene zero and clears the save. Continue resumes from the last save. If no save exists, Start is the only option.\n\n`startNew()` clears the save and resets to scene 0. After each operation it records the save, advances the scene index, and routes to the next story scene or credits. Scene 0 is the night before op1; after op10 the flow reaches the morning scene before credits.\n\nStory scenes without an operation advance directly to credits after their lines. Scenes with an operation route to the brief screen instead.\n\nQuit from pause returns to the menu without saving mid-operation, since saves only occur at operation end.\n\nRetry stage calls retryStage(sim) and closes the pause overlay.\n\nBot skill for non-human seats comes from seat.botSkill or defaults to 0.85.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-619ba3aa-a556-4ffd-a0d8-97105558d78d-144","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/songs.js","content":"/** Original chiptune. Same step count on every track of a pattern. */\n\nconst lead = { wave: 'triangle', volume: 0.22, attack: 0.01, decay: 0.14 };\nconst bass = { wave: 'square', duty: 0.125, volume: 0.1, attack: 0.01, decay: 0.1 };\nconst tick = { wave: 'noise', volume: 0.08, attack: 0.001, decay: 0.04 };\n\nfunction song(bpm, leadRow, bassRow, noiseRow) {\n  return {\n    bpm,\n    loop: true,\n    tracks: { lead, bass, tick },\n    patterns: { a: { lead: leadRow, bass: bassRow, tick: noiseRow } },\n    order: ['a'],\n  };\n}\n\nconst REST = 'C6 . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .';\n\nexport const SONGS = {\n  title: song(72,\n    'A4 . E4 . G4 . A4 . C5 . A4 . G4 . E4',\n    'A2 . . . E2 . . . A2 . . . E2 . . .',\n    REST),\n  ward: song(96,\n    'C5 . E5 G5 . E5 . D5 . C5 . B4 . C5 .',\n    'C3 . . . G2 . . . A2 . . . G2 . . .',\n    REST),\n  calm: song(84,\n    'D4 F4 . A4 . G4 . F4 E4 . D4 . E4 .',\n    'D2 . . . A2 . . . D2 . . . A2 . . .',\n    REST),\n  tense: song(120,\n    'A4 A4 C5 A4 E5 . D5 C5 A4 . C5 . E5 .',\n    'A2 . A2 . E2 . E2 . A2 . E2 . A2 . .',\n    'C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . .'),\n  critical: song(144,\n    'E5 E5 G5 E5 B5 B5 G5 E5 E5 G5 E5 B5 .',\n    'E2 E2 . E2 B2 . E2 . E2 E2 . E2 B2 .',\n    'C7 . C7 . C6 . C7 . C7 . C7 . C6 . .'),\n  boss: song(100,\n    'D4 . F4 . A4 . C5 . D5 C5 A4 . F4 .',\n    'D2 . . . A2 . . . D2 . . . C2 . . .',\n    'C6 . . . C6 . . . C5 . . . C6 . . .'),\n  sparse: song(64,\n    'E4 . . G4 . . A4 . . G4 . . E4 . .',\n    'E2 . . . . . A2 . . . . . E2 . .',\n    REST),\n  fanfare: song(132,\n    'C5 E5 G5 C6 . G5 E5 C5 G4 C5 E5 G5 .',\n    'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 .',\n    'C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . .'),\n  sad: song(68,\n    'A4 . G4 . E4 . D4 . C4 . D4 . E4 .',\n    'A2 . . . E2 . . . A2 . . . E2 . . .',\n    REST),\n};\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-619ba3aa-a556-4ffd-a0d8-97105558d78d-145","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/voice.js","content":"import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\n\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\n\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\n  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\n  const parts = [];\n  let total = 0;\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\n    if (ch === ' ') {\n      parts.push(gap);\n      total += gap.length;\n      continue;\n    }\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\n    parts.push(syl);\n    total += syl.length;\n  }\n  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\n  let at = 0;\n  for (const part of parts) {\n    out.set(part, at);\n    at += part.length;\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\nexport function rms(samples) {\n  let s = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\n}\n\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\n\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\n  return renderSound(def);\n}\n\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\n  write(12, 'fmt ');\n  view.setUint32(16, 16, true);\n  view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\n  view.setUint16(22, 1, true);\n  view.setUint32(24, sampleRate, true);\n  view.setUint32(28, sampleRate * 2, true);\n  view.setUint16(32, 2, true);\n  view.setUint16(34, 16, true);\n  write(36, 'data');\n  view.setUint32(40, samples.length * 2, true);\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) {\n    const v = Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, samples[i]));\n    view.setInt16(44 + i * 2, v < 0 ? v * 0x8000 : v * 0x7fff, true);\n  }\n  const bin = new Uint8Array(buf);\n  let text = '';\n  for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) text += String.fromCharCode(bin[i]);\n  return `data:audio/wav;base64,${btoa(text)}`;\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4766,"output_tokens":5593,"cache_read_input_tokens":193792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"6b1b1016-84ff-495d-b35e-b2635804e9bb"}
