ne_number\":376,\"content\":\"const arg = process.argv[2] || 'default';\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28ec69d4-6b13-46ae-9739-e6dfa05a3567-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** About / Credits copy. The exit interview uses these same strings. */\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:40:40',\\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n  perspective: 'Fixed overhead surgical view',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n10→  artDirection: 'Engine pixel-toon look, original OR sets, primitive busts, canvas tissue',\\n  animation: 'Engine clock plus sim-driven tool motion, heart pulse, and code-blue needle',\\n  audio: 'Original chiptune songs, SoundDef effects, and formant gibberish voices. No audio files.',\\n  online: 'Couch consult on one machine, and AI Hub shared-world for 1 to 4 players. No other network.',\\n  testing: 'Node sim suite, Playwright on software WebGPU, hub harness on 127.0.0.1. No physical pad, no second person, no iOS Safari, no TV.',\\n  research: 'The planner read the source Wikipedia page, the hub protocol, and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes. This build followed PLAN.md and the engine docs on this machine.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n20→\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Testing caught 7 issues: a string id compared as a number, a magnet pull that snapped, overlapping suture targets, a missing clot flag, a copy-hand that ended before it landed, and 2 syringe asserts that used the wrong keeper.',\\n  '4 would be game-breaking: hooks never left the field, the magnet could not be extracted, Op 5 never closed, and the transplant skipped its forced rewind.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the skill-1 bot play of every operation, which failed in the live sim and named the stuck entity.',\\n  'The least helpful test was a screenshot of a menu with no input behind it. Appearance did not show whether focus moved.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The pure renderSound and Song data made every effect and track testable in Node, and the HUD art-pixel grid matched the fill-mode canvas.',\\n30→  'I guessed wrong once: a held entity id is a string, so a numeric comparison never saw the grab. The fixed camera and the audio storage key behaved as the guide describes.',\\n  'The operation sim, the eight tools, the strains, couch seats, and the shared-world host loop. The engine does not ship a surgery model.',\\n  'Keeping pad buttons from also pressing keyboard keys, while still reading analog triggers, took the longest to get straight.',\\n  'none',\\n  'A way to mark a gamepad button as \\\"read it yourself\\\" without clearing the whole map by hand.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The plan named the beats, the tools, and the pass lines, so the game could be built against checks instead of a vibe.',\\n  'Two documents both said how to boot, and they disagreed about whether screens swap by loading a new game. Pause had to stay inside one game or the music died.',\\n40→  'Making one bot clear every operation at the top rank, including the rewind and the two-handed pull, without lowering par.',\\n  'Ask for the exit-interview counts after the suite has run, and name one file as the only source of the balance numbers.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'The Second Opinion Clinic',\\n  tagline: 'The truth, stat.',\\n  description: 'A rainy harbour hospital where telling the truth is the first cut. Keep the patient alive, close the strain, and top the team score.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n50→  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  series: 'Trauma Center',\\n  players: '1\\\\u20134',\\n  controls: 'Stick or mouse moves the tool. R2 or click uses it. Right stick or keys 1-8 pick a tool.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const ABOUT_FIELDS = [\\n  ['Date', SOURCE_INFORMATION.date],\\n  ['Source', SOURCE_INFORMATION.source],\\n60→  ['Plan', SOURCE_INFORMATION.plan],\\n  ['Genre and Perspective', `${SOURCE_INFORMATION.genre}; ${SOURCE_INFORMATION.perspective}`],\\n  ['Tech', SOURCE_INFORMATION.tech],\\n  ['Art Direction', SOURCE_INFORMATION.artDirection],\\n  ['Animation', SOURCE_INFORMATION.animation],\\n  ['Audio', SOURCE_INFORMATION.audio],\\n  ['Online', SOURCE_INFORMATION.online],\\n  ['Testing', SOURCE_INFORMATION.testing],\\n  ['Research', SOURCE_INFORMATION.research],\\n  ['Environment', SOURCE_INFORMATION.environment],\\n70→  ['Model', SOURCE_INFORMATION.model],\\n  ['Usage', SOURCE_INFORMATION.usage],\\n];\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** About / Credits copy. The exit interview uses these same strings. */\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:40:40',\\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n  perspective: 'Fixed overhead surgical view',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n10→  artDirection: 'Engine pixel-toon look, original OR sets, primitive busts, canvas tissue',\\n  animation: 'Engine clock plus sim-driven tool motion, heart pulse, and code-blue needle',\\n  audio: 'Original chiptune songs, SoundDef effects, and formant gibberish voices. No audio files.',\\n  online: 'Couch consult on one machine, and AI Hub shared-world for 1 to 4 players. No other network.',\\n  testing: 'Node sim suite, Playwright on software WebGPU, hub harness on 127.0.0.1. No physical pad, no second person, no iOS Safari, no TV.',\\n  research: 'The planner read the source Wikipedia page, the hub protocol, and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes. This build followed PLAN.md and the engine docs on this machine.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n20→\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Testing caught 7 issues: a string id compared as a number, a magnet pull that snapped, overlapping suture targets, a missing clot flag, a copy-hand that ended before it landed, and 2 syringe asserts that used the wrong keeper.',\\n  '4 would be game-breaking: hooks never left the field, the magnet could not be extracted, Op 5 never closed, and the transplant skipped its forced rewind.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the skill-1 bot play of every operation, which failed in the live sim and named the stuck entity.',\\n  'The least helpful test was a screenshot of a menu with no input behind it. Appearance did not show whether focus moved.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The pure renderSound and Song data made every effect and track testable in Node, and the HUD art-pixel grid matched the fill-mode canvas.',\\n30→  'I guessed wrong once: a held entity id is a string, so a numeric comparison never saw the grab. The fixed camera and the audio storage key behaved as the guide describes.',\\n  'The operation sim, the eight tools, the strains, couch seats, and the shared-world host loop. The engine does not ship a surgery model.',\\n  'Keeping pad buttons from also pressing keyboard keys, while still reading analog triggers, took the longest to get straight.',\\n  'none',\\n  'A way to mark a gamepad button as \\\"read it yourself\\\" without clearing the whole map by hand.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The plan named the beats, the tools, and the pass lines, so the game could be built against checks instead of a vibe.',\\n  'Two documents both said how to boot, and they disagreed about whether screens swap by loading a new game. Pause had to stay inside one game or the music died.',\\n40→  'Making one bot clear every operation at the top rank, including the rewind and the two-handed pull, without lowering par.',\\n  'Ask for the exit-interview counts after the suite has run, and name one file as the only source of the balance numbers.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'The Second Opinion Clinic',\\n  tagline: 'The truth, stat.',\\n  description: 'A rainy harbour hospital where telling the truth is the first cut. Keep the patient alive, close the strain, and top the team score.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n50→  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  series: 'Trauma Center',\\n  players: '1\\\\u20134',\\n  controls: 'Stick or mouse moves the tool. R2 or click uses it. Right stick or keys 1-8 pick a tool.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const ABOUT_FIELDS = [\\n  ['Date', SOURCE_INFORMATION.date],\\n  ['Source', SOURCE_INFORMATION.source],\\n60→  ['Plan', SOURCE_INFORMATION.plan],\\n  ['Genre and Perspective', `${SOURCE_INFORMATION.genre}; ${SOURCE_INFORMATION.perspective}`],\\n  ['Tech', SOURCE_INFORMATION.tech],\\n  ['Art Direction', SOURCE_INFORMATION.artDirection],\\n  ['Animation', SOURCE_INFORMATION.animation],\\n  ['Audio', SOURCE_INFORMATION.audio],\\n  ['Online', SOURCE_INFORMATION.online],\\n  ['Testing', SOURCE_INFORMATION.testing],\\n  ['Research', SOURCE_INFORMATION.research],\\n  ['Environment', SOURCE_INFORMATION.environment],\\n70→  ['Model', SOURCE_INFORMATION.model],\\n  ['Usage', SOURCE_INFORMATION.usage],\\n];\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/about.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/** About / Credits copy. The exit interview uses these same strings. */\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_INFORMATION = {\\n  date: '2026-11-04 22:40:40',\\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n  perspective: 'Fixed overhead surgical view',\\n  tech: 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.28.2',\\n  artDirection: 'Engine pixel-toon look, original OR sets, primitive busts, canvas tissue',\\n  animation: 'Engine clock plus sim-driven tool motion, heart pulse, and code-blue needle',\\n  audio: 'Original chiptune songs, SoundDef effects, and formant gibberish voices. No audio files.',\\n  online: 'Couch consult on one machine, and AI Hub shared-world for 1 to 4 players. No other network.',\\n  testing: 'Node sim suite, Playwright on software WebGPU, hub harness on 127.0.0.1. No physical pad, no second person, no iOS Safari, no TV.',\\n  research: 'The planner read the source Wikipedia page, the hub protocol, and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes. This build followed PLAN.md and the engine docs on this machine.',\\n  environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n  model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n  usage: 'added on import',\\n};\\n\\nexport const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'Testing caught 7 issues: a string id compared as a number, a magnet pull that snapped, overlapping suture targets, a missing clot flag, a copy-hand that ended before it landed, and 2 syringe asserts that used the wrong keeper.',\\n  '4 would be game-breaking: hooks never left the field, the magnet could not be extracted, Op 5 never closed, and the transplant skipped its forced rewind.',\\n  'The most helpful test was the skill-1 bot play of every operation, which failed in the live sim and named the stuck entity.',\\n  'The least helpful test was a screenshot of a menu with no input behind it. Appearance did not show whether focus moved.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The pure renderSound and Song data made every effect and track testable in Node, and the HUD art-pixel grid matched the fill-mode canvas.',\\n  'I guessed wrong once: a held entity id is a string, so a numeric comparison never saw the grab. The fixed camera and the audio storage key behaved as the guide describes.',\\n  'The operation sim, the eight tools, the strains, couch seats, and the shared-world host loop. The engine does not ship a surgery model.',\\n  'Keeping pad buttons from also pressing keyboard keys, while still reading analog triggers, took the longest to get straight.',\\n  'none',\\n  'A way to mark a gamepad button as \\\"read it yourself\\\" without clearing the whole map by hand.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  'The plan named the beats, the tools, and the pass lines, so the game could be built against checks instead of a vibe.',\\n  'Two documents both said how to boot, and they disagreed about whether screens swap by loading a new game. Pause had to stay inside one game or the music died.',\\n  'Making one bot clear every operation at the top rank, including the rewind and the two-handed pull, without lowering par.',\\n  'Ask for the exit-interview counts after the suite has run, and name one file as the only source of the balance numbers.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const AI_HUB = {\\n  name: 'The Second Opinion Clinic',\\n  tagline: 'The truth, stat.',\\n  description: 'A rainy harbour hospital where telling the truth is the first cut. Keep the patient alive, close the strain, and top the team score.',\\n  type: 'Game',\\n  genre: 'Simulation',\\n  source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n  series: 'Trauma Center',\\n  players: '1\\\\u20134',\\n  controls: 'Stick or mouse moves the tool. R2 or click uses it. Right stick or keys 1-8 pick a tool.',\\n  tags: ['3d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n};\\n\\nexport const ABOUT_FIELDS = [\\n  ['Date', SOURCE_INFORMATION.date],\\n  ['Source', SOURCE_INFORMATION.source],\\n  ['Plan', SOURCE_INFORMATION.plan],\\n  ['Genre and Perspective', `${SOURCE_INFORMATION.genre}; ${SOURCE_INFORMATION.perspective}`],\\n  ['Tech', SOURCE_INFORMATION.tech],\\n  ['Art Direction', SOURCE_INFORMATION.artDirection],\\n  ['Animation', SOURCE_INFORMATION.animation],\\n  ['Audio', SOURCE_INFORMATION.audio],\\n  ['Online', SOURCE_INFORMATION.online],\\n  ['Testing', SOURCE_INFORMATION.testing],\\n  ['Research', SOURCE_INFORMATION.research],\\n  ['Environment', SOURCE_INFORMATION.environment],\\n  ['Model', SOURCE_INFORMATION.model],\\n  ['Usage', SOURCE_INFORMATION.usage],\\n];\\n\",\"total_lines\":72}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28ec69d4-6b13-46ae-9739-e6dfa05a3567-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n10→  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n20→}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n30→      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n40→  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n50→  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n60→}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n70→  write(12, 'fmt ');\\n  view.setUint32(16, 16, true);\\n  view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint16(22, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint32(24, sampleRate, true);\\n  view.setUint32(28, sampleRate * 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(32, 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(34, 16, true);\\n  write(36, 'data');\\n  view.setUint32(40, samples.length * 2, true);\\n80→  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n10→  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n20→}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n30→      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n40→  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n50→  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n60→}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n70→  write(12, 'fmt ');\\n  view.setUint32(16, 16, true);\\n  view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint16(22, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint32(24, sampleRate, true);\\n  view.setUint32(28, sampleRate * 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(32, 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(34, 16, true);\\n  write(36, 'data');\\n  view.setUint32(40, samples.length * 2, true);\\n80→  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/voice.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n  write(12, 'fmt ');\\n  view.setUint32(16, 16, true);\\n  view.setUint16(20, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint16(22, 1, true);\\n  view.setUint32(24, sampleRate, true);\\n  view.setUint32(28, sampleRate * 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(32, 2, true);\\n  view.setUint16(34, 16, true);\\n  write(36, 'data');\\n  view.setUint32(40, samples.length * 2, true);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":88}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28ec69d4-6b13-46ae-9739-e6dfa05a3567-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/game.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n\",\"total_lines\":103}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28ec69d4-6b13-46ae-9739-e6dfa05a3567-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/core/meta.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"export const TITLE = 'The Second Opinion Clinic';\\nexport const TAGLINE = 'The truth, stat.';\\nexport const SLUG = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic';\\nexport const FILE_BASE = 'The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040';\\n\",\"total_lines\":4}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28ec69d4-6b13-46ae-9739-e6dfa05a3567-12","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→SOURCE: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\n\\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\\n\\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\\n\\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\\n\\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\\n10→\\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\\n\\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, the riftlight engine kit. Keep the engine (pixel-engine.js) as it ships, as its guide says, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\\n\\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\\n\\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\\n\\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\\n20→\\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\\n\\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n30→Effort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n40→  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\n50→No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n60→\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\n70→Scope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\n80→Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\n90→No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:40\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n100→- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n110→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n120→    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\n130→Testing Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n140→- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n150→- What was the hardest thing to do?\\n- What would you change in this prompt?\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→SOURCE: Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\n\\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\\n\\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\\n\\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\\n\\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\\n10→\\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\\n\\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, the riftlight engine kit. Keep the engine (pixel-engine.js) as it ships, as its guide says, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\\n\\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic p