{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_178","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The applyDecoded and decodeState exports are needed.\n\nI need to check the rest of the codec for applyDecoded. The host must handle inputs from both local pads and network players. I will store the latest input per player ID. Clients send input messages at 15Hz even when idle.\n\nHost snapshots run at 12Hz unreliable, 1Hz reliable keyframes, and 4Hz events. The host bot must finish the round to pass the harness. Skill 1 should clear session ops with reduced strain HP. If the bot does not win before time-up, the host must call finish().\n\nThe host bot must finish the operation quickly. I will accelerate the simulation by running many steps per tick, or use a catch-up loop, so the 200-second session ends in seconds rather than minutes.\n\nThe host bot must finish the operation before the 4-minute wall-clock limit. The pile skill 1 test completed in only 5 seconds of game time, so the bot can clear a 200-second session in roughly 5 seconds of wall clock. This confirms that realtime simulation is sufficient.\n\nSession operations should finish in 5 to 30 seconds of simulation time. Bosses may take 30 to 60 seconds. That is acceptable for the harnesses.\n\nThe host must drive the bot and step the simulation. It must call finish when the round ends.\n\nClients must send input during the card phase before the round starts. The host sends pings at roughly 4Hz during that window. AIHub.time() is -Infinity until the round begins.\n\nThe host interval will use wall-clock setInterval. During the card phase it will ping and send inputs. After the round starts it will catch up on simulation steps.\n\nThe host interval will compute the elapsed time since the last tick and step the simulation for that many frames, capped at thirty steps per cycle. It will send snapshots and call finish when the round ends. During the countdown phase it will not step the simulation yet still send input. When the timer reaches zero it will call finish(false). If the host leaves the room it will not call finish because the hub voids the round.\n\nThe finishRound function will collect present player IDs from AIHub.players, compute each seat score, and group players by score to determine standings.\n\nThe finishRound function sorts present players by score and groups ties into arrays. It then calls AIHub.finish with standings, scores, win state, stats, and awards. Stats must contain at most six entries per player with names and text under sixteen characters. Awards must contain at most three items with titles under twenty-four characters and details under forty. The operation seed is generated from AIHub.rng('deal') and passed to createOp; Math.random must not be used for gameplay.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55bd1515-a166-43d5-b828-e641d3f67046-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scenario|server|__hubCheck|complete","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/harness.html","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-55bd1515-a166-43d5-b828-e641d3f67046-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function check|pass|server|host-leave|finish|idle","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/round.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4566,"output_tokens":1774,"cache_read_input_tokens":84864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"6f48cca8-fd5f-44e6-ac21-8c498752a283"}
