{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_186","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking Engine.start options around lines 140-220 for camera and background settings.","signature":"uU0iDKUFxzZAGD0aJocBXqy61znyRDy7hP+72NvbdM6+0fxYioT7dqw/okb6ZXAf817OWR35DuCavrvWtAKURyMjtdfSJxA9cWsZSjtTafKVYXbLvI61diGSNRZzJgYyYpschuW+Xse1Q8H/yWA"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-59","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/Engine.d.ts","offset":120,"limit":100}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-60","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function toonMaterial","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/render/toon.d.ts"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-61","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/campaign.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1807,"output_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":108672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"2a5931e6-269f-46a3-9ebb-f43f580dfe33"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-59","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→     * physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset\\n     * (e.g. side-scroller lane lock, hiding the player model in first person).\\n     */\\n    onCameraChange?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Called when the game is unloaded (`engine.loadGame(other)` or `engine.dispose()`),\\n     * before the engine removes its scene objects, physics bodies, triggers, particles, HUD\\n     * and music. Free anything else the game owns: DOM, timers, listeners, HMR hooks.\\n     */\\n    dispose?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n130→}\\nexport interface EngineOptions {\\n    container?: HTMLElement;\\n    resolution?: Resolution;\\n    /**\\n     * `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width\\n     * follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly\\n     * `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport\\n     * at an integer scale, without black borders or stretched pixels.\\n     */\\n140→    aspect?: AspectMode;\\n    /**\\n     * Cap the render loop (simulation keeps its fixed 60 Hz physics step). Default 60, so\\n     * 120 Hz phones don't run the whole pipeline twice per game frame. 0 = display rate.\\n     */\\n    maxFps?: number;\\n    /** Shadow map quality, or `auto` (default: low on touch devices, else medium; lowered once on a slow start). */\\n    quality?: QualityOption;\\n    /** Pixel-styled loading indicator while the renderer, physics and assets load. Default true. */\\n    loadingScreen?: boolean;\\n150→    mode?: RenderMode;\\n    edges?: EdgeSettings;\\n    /** Camera preset + parameters. Pick one per game; not meant to change during play. */\\n    camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    /** Post filters (ids from FILTERS) applied in Pixel mode, in order. */\\n    filters?: readonly string[];\\n    /**\\n     * A full look: pixel art or clean rendering and filters per layer (characters & objects,\\n     * environment) plus whole-scene filters (render/look.ts). Wins over `filters` and `edges`.\\n     */\\n160→    look?: Look;\\n    /**\\n     * Seed for `ctx.random`: each level gets its own stream from this and the game's name, so\\n     * the same seed replays the same game. Default 1. `?seed=` in the URL.\\n     */\\n    seed?: number;\\n    /**\\n     * Frames of input the engine keeps for each level (`recording()`). Default `MAX_FRAMES`, an\\n     * hour at 60 fps (up to some 20 MB of JSON with the mouse moving all the time); 0 records nothing.\\n     */\\n170→    record?: number;\\n    /** Debug panel. Default: on in dev (`vite`) or with ?debug=1, off in production builds. */\\n    debugUI?: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer\\n     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\\n     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\\n     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\\n     */\\n    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\\n180→    /**\\n     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\\n     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\\n     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\\n     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\\n     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\\n     */\\n    settings?: {\\n        button?: TouchCorner | boolean;\\n        key?: string | false;\\n190→    };\\n    /** On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0. */\\n    touch?: boolean;\\n    /** On-screen action buttons. Default: the platformer's (DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS). */\\n    touchButtons?: readonly TouchButton[];\\n    /**\\n     * The touch top bar of the engine hotkeys (ⓘ debug panel, P, R, ◐ looks, ♪ mute), on a touch\\n     * screen while they are on (see `debugKeys`). Default true; false hides it even then, unless\\n     * the debug panel is on (`?debug=1`, dev builds).\\n     */\\n200→    touchBar?: boolean;\\n    background?: number;\\n}\\n/** `Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs. */\\nexport interface HeadlessOptions extends EngineOptions {\\n    /**\\n     * The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at\\n     * DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\\n     */\\n    viewport?: Viewport;\\n210→    /** How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`. */\\n    assets?: AssetReader;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Read engine options from the URL:\\n *   ?mode=raw  ?res=320  ?debug=1|0\\n *   ?aspect=fixed|adaptive  ?fps=30 (0 = uncapped)  ?quality=low|medium|high|auto\\n *   ?camera=iso|topdown|side|third|first|free|fixed  ?zoom=1.5\\n *   ?cam=<JSON CameraConfig>   (e.g. the config printed by the free camera)\\n *   ?filters=crt,lcd  or  ?look=handheld (a LOOK_PRESETS name, e.g. pixel_heroes)\",\"content_concise\":\"120→     * physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset\\n     * (e.g. side-scroller lane lock, hiding the player model in first person).\\n     */\\n    onCameraChange?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Called when the game is unloaded (`engine.loadGame(other)` or `engine.dispose()`),\\n     * before the engine removes its scene objects, physics bodies, triggers, particles, HUD\\n     * and music. Free anything else the game owns: DOM, timers, listeners, HMR hooks.\\n     */\\n    dispose?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n130→}\\nexport interface EngineOptions {\\n    container?: HTMLElement;\\n    resolution?: Resolution;\\n    /**\\n     * `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width\\n     * follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly\\n     * `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport\\n     * at an integer scale, without black borders or stretched pixels.\\n     */\\n140→    aspect?: AspectMode;\\n    /**\\n     * Cap the render loop (simulation keeps its fixed 60 Hz physics step). Default 60, so\\n     * 120 Hz phones don't run the whole pipeline twice per game frame. 0 = display rate.\\n     */\\n    maxFps?: number;\\n    /** Shadow map quality, or `auto` (default: low on touch devices, else medium; lowered once on a slow start). */\\n    quality?: QualityOption;\\n    /** Pixel-styled loading indicator while the renderer, physics and assets load. Default true. */\\n    loadingScreen?: boolean;\\n150→    mode?: RenderMode;\\n    edges?: EdgeSettings;\\n    /** Camera preset + parameters. Pick one per game; not meant to change during play. */\\n    camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    /** Post filters (ids from FILTERS) applied in Pixel mode, in order. */\\n    filters?: readonly string[];\\n    /**\\n     * A full look: pixel art or clean rendering and filters per layer (characters & objects,\\n     * environment) plus whole-scene filters (render/look.ts). Wins over `filters` and `edges`.\\n     */\\n160→    look?: Look;\\n    /**\\n     * Seed for `ctx.random`: each level gets its own stream from this and the game's name, so\\n     * the same seed replays the same game. Default 1. `?seed=` in the URL.\\n     */\\n    seed?: number;\\n    /**\\n     * Frames of input the engine keeps for each level (`recording()`). Default `MAX_FRAMES`, an\\n     * hour at 60 fps (up to some 20 MB of JSON with the mouse moving all the time); 0 records nothing.\\n     */\\n170→    record?: number;\\n    /** Debug panel. Default: on in dev (`vite`) or with ?debug=1, off in production builds. */\\n    debugUI?: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer\\n     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\\n     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\\n     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\\n     */\\n    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\\n180→    /**\\n     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\\n     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\\n     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\\n     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\\n     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\\n     */\\n    settings?: {\\n        button?: TouchCorner | boolean;\\n        key?: string | false;\\n190→    };\\n    /** On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0. */\\n    touch?: boolean;\\n    /** On-screen action buttons. Default: the platformer's (DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS). */\\n    touchButtons?: readonly TouchButton[];\\n    /**\\n     * The touch top bar of the engine hotkeys (ⓘ debug panel, P, R, ◐ looks, ♪ mute), on a touch\\n     * screen while they are on (see `debugKeys`). Default true; false hides it even then, unless\\n     * the debug panel is on (`?debug=1`, dev builds).\\n     */\\n200→    touchBar?: boolean;\\n    background?: number;\\n}\\n/** `Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs. */\\nexport interface HeadlessOptions extends EngineOptions {\\n    /**\\n     * The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at\\n     * DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\\n     */\\n    viewport?: Viewport;\\n210→    /** How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`. */\\n    assets?: AssetReader;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Read engine options from the URL:\\n *   ?mode=raw  ?res=320  ?debug=1|0\\n *   ?aspect=fixed|adaptive  ?fps=30 (0 = uncapped)  ?quality=low|medium|high|auto\\n *   ?camera=iso|topdown|side|third|first|free|fixed  ?zoom=1.5\\n *   ?cam=<JSON CameraConfig>   (e.g. the config printed by the free camera)\\n *   ?filters=crt,lcd  or  ?look=handheld (a LOOK_PRESETS name, e.g. pixel_heroes)\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":100,\"raw_output\":\"     * physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset\\n     * (e.g. side-scroller lane lock, hiding the player model in first person).\\n     */\\n    onCameraChange?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Called when the game is unloaded (`engine.loadGame(other)` or `engine.dispose()`),\\n     * before the engine removes its scene objects, physics bodies, triggers, particles, HUD\\n     * and music. Free anything else the game owns: DOM, timers, listeners, HMR hooks.\\n     */\\n    dispose?(ctx: GameContext): void;\\n}\\nexport interface EngineOptions {\\n    container?: HTMLElement;\\n    resolution?: Resolution;\\n    /**\\n     * `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width\\n     * follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly\\n     * `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport\\n     * at an integer scale, without black borders or stretched pixels.\\n     */\\n    aspect?: AspectMode;\\n    /**\\n     * Cap the render loop (simulation keeps its fixed 60 Hz physics step). Default 60, so\\n     * 120 Hz phones don't run the whole pipeline twice per game frame. 0 = display rate.\\n     */\\n    maxFps?: number;\\n    /** Shadow map quality, or `auto` (default: low on touch devices, else medium; lowered once on a slow start). */\\n    quality?: QualityOption;\\n    /** Pixel-styled loading indicator while the renderer, physics and assets load. Default true. */\\n    loadingScreen?: boolean;\\n    mode?: RenderMode;\\n    edges?: EdgeSettings;\\n    /** Camera preset + parameters. Pick one per game; not meant to change during play. */\\n    camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    /** Post filters (ids from FILTERS) applied in Pixel mode, in order. */\\n    filters?: readonly string[];\\n    /**\\n     * A full look: pixel art or clean rendering and filters per layer (characters & objects,\\n     * environment) plus whole-scene filters (render/look.ts). Wins over `filters` and `edges`.\\n     */\\n    look?: Look;\\n    /**\\n     * Seed for `ctx.random`: each level gets its own stream from this and the game's name, so\\n     * the same seed replays the same game. Default 1. `?seed=` in the URL.\\n     */\\n    seed?: number;\\n    /**\\n     * Frames of input the engine keeps for each level (`recording()`). Default `MAX_FRAMES`, an\\n     * hour at 60 fps (up to some 20 MB of JSON with the mouse moving all the time); 0 records nothing.\\n     */\\n    record?: number;\\n    /** Debug panel. Default: on in dev (`vite`) or with ?debug=1, off in production builds. */\\n    debugUI?: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer\\n     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\\n     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\\n     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\\n     */\\n    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\\n    /**\\n     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\\n     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\\n     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\\n     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\\n     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\\n     */\\n    settings?: {\\n        button?: TouchCorner | boolean;\\n        key?: string | false;\\n    };\\n    /** On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0. */\\n    touch?: boolean;\\n    /** On-screen action buttons. Default: the platformer's (DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS). */\\n    touchButtons?: readonly TouchButton[];\\n    /**\\n     * The touch top bar of the engine hotkeys (ⓘ debug panel, P, R, ◐ looks, ♪ mute), on a touch\\n     * screen while they are on (see `debugKeys`). Default true; false hides it even then, unless\\n     * the debug panel is on (`?debug=1`, dev builds).\\n     */\\n    touchBar?: boolean;\\n    background?: number;\\n}\\n/** `Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs. */\\nexport interface HeadlessOptions extends EngineOptions {\\n    /**\\n     * The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at\\n     * DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\\n     */\\n    viewport?: Viewport;\\n    /** How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`. */\\n    assets?: AssetReader;\\n}\\n/**\\n * Read engine options from the URL:\\n *   ?mode=raw  ?res=320  ?debug=1|0\\n *   ?aspect=fixed|adaptive  ?fps=30 (0 = uncapped)  ?quality=low|medium|high|auto\\n *   ?camera=iso|topdown|side|third|first|free|fixed  ?zoom=1.5\\n *   ?cam=<JSON CameraConfig>   (e.g. the config printed by the free camera)\\n *   ?filters=crt,lcd  or  ?look=handheld (a LOOK_PRESETS name, e.g. pixel_heroes)\\n\",\"total_lines\":613}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-60","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,67,108,105,110,105,99,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,47,116,121,112,101,115,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,114,101,110,100,101,114,47,116,111,111,110,46,100,46,116,115,10,53,56,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,100,101,99,108,97,114,101,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,116,111,111,110,77,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,40,99,111,108,111,114,58,32,67,111,108,111,114,82,101,112,114,101,115,101,110,116,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,111,112,116,105,111,110,115,63,58,32,84,111,111,110,77,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,79,112,116,105,111,110,115,41,58,32,77,101,115,104,84,111,111,110,78,111,100,101,77,97,116,101,114,105,97,108,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/render/toon.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":58,\"content\":\"export declare function toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options?: ToonMaterialOptions): MeshToonNodeMaterial;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cc92a3b0-5c90-4acf-b6ed-f25744f9fcbc-61","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { STORY_OPS } from './ops.js';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story.js';\\nimport { clearSave, emptySave, writeSave } from '../core/save.js';\\nimport { play } from '../sim/run.js';\\n\\n/** Bot play from the first scene through the last operation and into the credits. */\\nexport function playCampaign(opts = {}) {\\n  clearSave();\\n  const save = emptySave();\\n10→  const skill = opts.skill ?? 1;\\n  const results = [];\\n  for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n    save.scenes.push(scene.id);\\n    if (!scene.op) continue;\\n    const def = STORY_OPS.find((op) => op.id === scene.op);\\n    const sim = play(def, skill, { seed: opts.seed ?? 1 });\\n    save.ops[def.id] = { rank: sim.rank, score: sim.finalScore, won: sim.phase === 'won' };\\n    if (def.id === 'op3' && sim.phase === 'won') save.quiet = true;\\n    results.push(sim);\\n20→    writeSave(save);\\n  }\\n  save.log = true;\\n  save.credits = true;\\n  writeSave(save);\\n  return { save, results };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { STORY_OPS } from './ops.js';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story.js';\\nimport { clearSave, emptySave, writeSave } from '../core/save.js';\\nimport { play } from '../sim/run.js';\\n\\n/** Bot play from the first scene through the last operation and into the credits. */\\nexport function playCampaign(opts = {}) {\\n  clearSave();\\n  const save = emptySave();\\n10→  const skill = opts.skill ?? 1;\\n  const results = [];\\n  for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n    save.scenes.push(scene.id);\\n    if (!scene.op) continue;\\n    const def = STORY_OPS.find((op) => op.id === scene.op);\\n    const sim = play(def, skill, { seed: opts.seed ?? 1 });\\n    save.ops[def.id] = { rank: sim.rank, score: sim.finalScore, won: sim.phase === 'won' };\\n    if (def.id === 'op3' && sim.phase === 'won') save.quiet = true;\\n    results.push(sim);\\n20→    writeSave(save);\\n  }\\n  save.log = true;\\n  save.credits = true;\\n  writeSave(save);\\n  return { save, results };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/campaign.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"import { STORY_OPS } from './ops.js';\\nimport { SCENES } from './story.js';\\nimport { clearSave, emptySave, writeSave } from '../core/save.js';\\nimport { play } from '../sim/run.js';\\n\\n/** Bot play from the first scene through the last operation and into the credits. */\\nexport function playCampaign(opts = {}) {\\n  clearSave();\\n  const save = emptySave();\\n  const skill = opts.skill ?? 1;\\n  const results = [];\\n  for (const scene of SCENES) {\\n    save.scenes.push(scene.id);\\n    if (!scene.op) continue;\\n    const def = STORY_OPS.find((op) => op.id === scene.op);\\n    const sim = play(def, skill, { seed: opts.seed ?? 1 });\\n    save.ops[def.id] = { rank: sim.rank, score: sim.finalScore, won: sim.phase === 'won' };\\n    if (def.id === 'op3' && sim.phase === 'won') save.quiet = true;\\n    results.push(sim);\\n    writeSave(save);\\n  }\\n  save.log = true;\\n  save.credits = true;\\n  writeSave(save);\\n  return { save, results };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":26}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"3579a9ba-ac23-4f57-bfe3-48af8e725b87"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_187","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough information to write the game.\n\nI'll structure clinic.js carefully to avoid bugs. The launch URL will use flags like `op`, `stage`, and `seed`. Setting `op` starts the game directly in operation mode. I'm also planning an `act()` function for direct simulation stepping, which tests will call to verify entity changes.\n\n`window.__GAME__` will expose the clinic app, simulation state, mode switching, config, and `act()`. Prompts will be available as both a string label and an object with confirm text, device, and glyphs. Menu focus will use d-pad, arrow keys, and mouse hover to select items.\n\nThe main menu will have five items: ON CALL, OPERATING LOG, CONSULT, SETTINGS, and ABOUT. I'm deciding whether the title screen should also have a focusable element so tests can verify d-pad, keyboard, and mouse navigation before reaching the menu.\n\nThe title screen will require a confirm button to enter the menu. Other directions will not leave it. Tests can jump directly to the menu via `__GAME__.goto('menu')`. The verifier will audit these tests.\n\nBrowser tests will load the page, wait for `__GAME__`, and verify menu focus changes via d-pad, arrow keys, and mouse hover. The attract mode will idle for ten seconds on the title or menu screen, then exit to the title without writing a save file if any input is detected.\n\nExit from attract mode must not write to localStorage. I will snapshot the store before and after the idle period. The engine audio key may be written during boot, but attract itself must stay clean.\n\nDev mode will open from pause via Escape or goto('pause'). It will expose sliders for every DEFAULTS key. Changing a slider calls applySlider. Resetting restores the original values. Tests will verify that vitalsDrainMul can be set to 2 and then reset to 1.\n\nI will expose `app.devSet(key, value)` and `app.devReset()` so the dev UI can use them directly. The pause menu will include a Dev Mode option that opens the dev screen. That screen will let the user change slider values with left and right controls and reset all settings. Tests will interact with these real UI elements rather than calling internal functions directly.\n\nThe dev screen will use ArrowLeft and ArrowRight to adjust the focused slider. A browser test will load the game in operation mode, pause via Escape, open Dev Mode, nudge vitalsDrainMul to 2, and verify the config value.\n\nThe dev-mode test will also confirm the reset button restores the original slider values.\n\nKeyboard focus navigation must work for all menus.\n\nTwo-player mode will use independent gamepads. Each pad controls one seat via its left stick axes. Tests will mock navigator.getGamepads to return two pads, set their axes, step the engine, and verify that each seat moves independently.\n\nI need a way to trigger a frame from outside the engine loop. I will store the engine on window or use requestAnimationFrame.\n\nPlaywright will wait 100 milliseconds between steps, which is slower than the 60Hz fixedUpdate loop.\n\nThe engine polls getGamepads directly instead of relying on automatic moveAxis updates when gamepadButtons is empty.\n\nSettings will store a 'ps' or 'xbox' glyph preference in soc:settings. This changes the prompt label to 'A' or 'CROSS' for pad input, then 'ENTER'. The prompt logic runs after the key press.\n\nFor the Pixel 7 test device, the engine will detect touch-only mode before starting by checking fine-pointer support, maxTouchPoints, and gamepad presence.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-29288112-2115-42ba-81f2-dded7ffc5126-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"joystick|class=","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/TouchControls.d.ts"}},{"t