{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4226d822-58a9-4904-b13b-9228472bf356-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n180→    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n190→    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n200→    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\",\"content_concise\":\"110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n180→    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n190→    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n200→    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/input.d.ts\",\"offset\":110,\"limit\":110,\"raw_output\":\"    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n    constructor(target?: Window | null);\\n    /**\\n     * Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the\\n     * canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches\\n     * pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n     */\\n    attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void;\\n    /** Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas). */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    /** Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay. */\\n    release(): void;\\n    /** Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads). */\\n    reset(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired\\n     * queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\\n     */\\n    beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void;\\n    get pointerLocked(): boolean;\\n    isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code). */\\n    anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame). */\\n    wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than\\n     * `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or\\n     * several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a\\n     * pause, a loading screen or a long hitch) never fires late.\\n     */\\n    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n\",\"total_lines\":278}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"79dee98d-6e55-420b-aedd-dedd4d53cef0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_193","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"padAxis y maps to forward. Standard axis 1 is down-positive, but the engine may invert it.\n\nRaw gamepad axes will drive menu navigation. Stick down moves focus down. Button edge detection tracks previous states per pad. Keyboard controls use arrow keys, s/w, enter/space to confirm, and escape to back. Mouse hover maps pointer coordinates to art pixels and sets focus when the pointer moves over a known item.\n\nFocus will not switch from pad to mouse unless the mouse actually moves. Clicking confirms selection. A new `pollIntent` function in `devices.js` will return a clean intent object with sampled pads, button states, and mouse events to keep the clinic code small.\n\nThe default device is 'pad' with PS glyphs. It switches to 'key' on keyboard input, to 'mouse' on click or movement, and to 'pad' on controller input. Prompts show ENTER for key and mouse, A for Xbox pads, and CROSS otherwise. Tests will see both key and mouse as ENTER.\n\nPad 1 will not override the default pad device. Each pad maps its left stick to seat x and z, right stick to rotation, R2 or button 0 to use, button 6 to gift, and button 4 to steady.\n\nPad 0 owns seat 0 and pad 1 owns seat 1. Keyboard or mouse input only claims seat 0 when no pad is present.\n\nRight stick flicks select tools. The eight tools are scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, syringe, gel, laser, and scanner. Flicking triggers a tool change when the stick magnitude crosses 0.6.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7327bffa-497f-4ce1-b22d-5cac678cd8e6-72","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"input\\.(sx|sz|use|tool|place|seek)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1513,"output_tokens":993,"cache_read_input_tokens":125824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"80857f2a-72da-48e7-a3bf-0f7fa038a8f3"}
