{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_198","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that input.table sets the active table.\n\nI have a solid design and am ready to write all files. I'll fix songs first, then create devices.js, session.js, stage.js, hud.js, clinic.js, game.js, plus build, authoring, and test updates. I'll also update PROGRESS.md.\n\nI'll keep clinic input handling clean and test it with headless and a small node test. Session standings will be unit-tested via a pure `buildStandings` function exported from session.js, avoiding AIHub dependencies. I'll also prevent `openSession` from starting timers in tests.\n\nTime-up will finish the game immediately after the grace period. A finish before start is an error, so finishing is blocked until the playing phase begins. If the simulation is not created by time-up, it will finish with zero scores. The simulation is created on the start event, followed by a countdown and then the playing phase.\n\nThe start handler will be wrapped in try/catch to prevent unhandled protocol errors. Player names render via hud.text rather than innerHTML. AIHub assigns sequential numeric IDs from 0 to N-1, and the server uses ID N as its own identity with no local input. Clinic state is shared across the player host.\n\nLocal input updates each frame into `state.localInput` and `state.inputs[me]`. Client prediction will apply the snapshot first, then immediately reapply local seat positions so the player's own seat stays accurate even when snapshots overwrite it.\n\napplyDecoded returns the phase, so the client will set it directly from decodeState. The host remains authoritative for seat movement; the client will integrate a local cursor to keep its own seat position accurate until the next snapshot arrives.\n\nThe local cursor will be stored in `state.cursor[me]` and drawn directly, so any seat jump from snapshot updates is acceptable for the harness.\n\n`game.js` will export `createGame()` and only boot the full game when `document` exists. Headless tests can import it directly and call `createGame()` without triggering the document boot.\n\nThe boot catch block will log errors to prevent harness unhandled rejections. Engine.start is configured with a fixed camera preset, low quality, and touch-only controls.\n\nThe touch gate will be visible while the engine loads, and it will be removed if a pad connects later. Pixel 7 devices are correctly detected via maxTouchPoints. The settings button will be verified after the first browser run.\n\nI'll keep clinic.js under 900 lines by moving menu definitions and drawing code into hud.js, which will export `draw(ctx, app)`. stage.js will export `createStage(ctx)` and `sync(stage, app, pulse)`. Rain particles are skipped for time. The bust geometry uses a head sphere, shoulder box, and hair box with CAST colors. The title room needs a floor plane, wall, lamp cylinder, and monitor box; toonMaterial lacks emissive support so the monitor will use a different approach.\n\nThe EKG monitor will be a green box; the HUD will draw the line. `setLookLayer` is confirmed to export from `pixel-engine.js`. I will avoid throwing in `update` so the engine can capture errors cleanly. The dev cheat win path works correctly, and the results screen appears automatically when the phase switches to won.\n\nI confirmed that `win()` sets the rank, so the results screen will display it. I will assert that every story operation wins in the test campaign. The morning scene has no operation but still counts as a pushed scene with log and credits enabled. I also need to add a font test for the story lines shown on the HUD.\n\nI will scan ops.js and story.js for forbidden characters and bad strings before writing code. The hold flag in the game shell will be named `simHold`.\n\nInput edges will be tracked in a `padPrev` Map or array of button booleans. Keyboard tool keys 1–8 and mouse wheel will cycle tools for seat 0. A click inside the bottom-right 56px wheel box will also trigger a tool change. Rumble effects will use the vibration actuator when enabled, with a guard for missing hardware. I will write the files now, plus update docs/AUTHORING.md and extend run.mjs.\n\nA new `tests/browser.mjs` will export an async `runBrowser(root, scratch, filter)` function. The main `run.mjs` script will be converted from synchronous to async so it can await filter execution. The scratch path will be read from the `SCRATCH` environment variable rather than hardcoded inside the repository.\n\nThe test script will hardcode the scratch path as its default output directory. This ensures evidence is written automatically on reruns without requiring the SCRATCH environment variable.\n\nThe test script will default to the hardcoded scratch path when the `GOAL_SCRATCH` environment variable is absent. The launch harness will import Playwright from the project's local node_modules and launch Chromium with the `--enable-unsafe-webgpu` flag.\n\nThe browser launch flags include SwiftShader for WebGPU and Vulkan, no sandbox, and autoplay bypass. Headless mode is enabled with a 960x540 viewport for logic and 1920x1080 for screenshots. Each test run creates a fresh browser context to avoid profile state. The harness waits up to sixty seconds for `window.__GAME__.sim` to appear before proceeding.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-29407d22-c0ac-45a1-a859-bf7529902590-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"gpuErrors|errors:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4982,"output_tokens":2922,"cache_read_input_tokens":136192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"8169ee48-19cf-4d