matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/songs.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/songs.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"  boss: song(100,\\n    'D4 . F4 . A4 . C5 . D5 C5 A4 . F4 .',\\n    'D2 . . . A2 . . . D2 . . . C2 . . .',\\n    'C6 . . . C6 . . . C5 . . . C6 . . .'),\\n  sparse: song(64,\\n    'E4 . . G4 . . A4 . . G4 . . E4 . .',\\n    'E2 . . . . . A2 . . . . . E2 . .',\\n    REST),\\n  fanfare: song(132,\\n    'C5 E5 G5 C6 . G5 E5 C5 G4 C5 E5 G5 .',\\n    'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 .',\\n    'C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . .'),\",\"old_line\":40,\"new_string\":\"  boss: song(100,\\n    'D4 . F4 . A4 . C5 . D5 C5 A4 . F4 . D4',\\n    'D2 . . . A2 . . . D2 . . . C2 . . .',\\n    'C6 . . . C6 . . . C5 . . . C6 . . .'),\\n  sparse: song(64,\\n    'E4 . . G4 . . A4 . . G4 . . E4 . . .',\\n    'E2 . . . . . A2 . . . . . E2 . . .',\\n    REST),\\n  fanfare: song(132,\\n    'C5 E5 G5 C6 . G5 E5 C5 G4 C5 E5 G5 C6 . . .',\\n    'C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 . G2 . C3 . . .',\\n    'C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . C6 . . .'),\",\"new_line\":40,\"context_before\":\"    'E5 E5 G5 E5 B5 . B5 G5 E5 . G5 E5 B5 . E5 .',\\n    'E2 E2 . E2 B2 . E2 . E2 E2 . E2 B2 . E2 .',\\n    'C7 . C7 . C6 . C7 . C7 . C7 . C6 . C7 .'),\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  sad: song(68,\\n    'A4 . G4 . E4 . D4 . C4 . D4 . E4 .',\\n    'A2 . . . E2 . . . A2 . . . E2 . . .',\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"8981261a-94df-4b76-9458-8a7d7fd9e676"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_209","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No non-ASCII characters found in src. Now writing the game files.\n\nVerifying note counts for the fanfare, bass, tick, and sparse lead sequences. Each totals 16 notes.\n\nThe bass and calm lead sequences also total 16 notes each.\n\nThe director function will be added to songs.js. The remaining source files are devices, session, stage, hud, clinic, game, build, and authoring. Clinic will serve as the integration point.\n\nWriting stage.js now. It defines an ARENA color map for body parts and a SEAT palette, then begins the createView function.\n\nBuilding the stage room in stage.js. Adding a dark floor, a wall, and a lamp with a pole.\n\nAdding a monitor to the stage room. Creating an invisible tissue plane for body part visuals. Beginning the four hand groups.\n\nEach hand group now contains a palm and a tip. Both are hidden and assigned to the actors look layer. A pool of forty-eight invisible red spheres is also created for entities.\n\nAdding six invisible actor groups to the stage. Each group contains a colored head and body mesh, positioned in a row behind the monitor.\n\nAdding ambient and directional lights to the stage scene. A spotlight is also requested. The createView function returns the room, tissue plane, hands, entities, busts, and lamp. The syncView function begins by checking whether the current mode is operational or story.\n\nFinishing syncView. The room hides during operational modes and the tissue plane appears only when simulation data exists. Actor busts show during story, title, card, brief, or credits modes.\n\nNow calculating how to displace the tissue plane vertices using heightAt. The plane is rotated -90 degrees on the X axis, so local Y coordinates map to world Z.\n\nDeriving the rotation matrix for a -90 degree X rotation confirms that local Y maps to world negative Z. Local X stays unchanged.\n\nLocal Z becomes world Y after the rotation. Local Y becomes world negative Z. The tissue plane is 16 units wide and 9 units deep in local space. World height maps to local Z. World depth maps to negative local Y.\n\nThe tissue plane displacement code is now written. Local Z is set to heightAt using world X and negative local Y. Vertex normals are recomputed each frame. Entity mesh placement is next.\n\nEntity meshes are placed at world coordinates with a small height offset. Hands sit slightly higher above their seats. The title room will show busts of Ilya and Reyes for the required screenshot, and story mode will zoom in for a close-up. Camera position will be set based on the current mode. Tissue geometry updates will be skipped when the plane is hidden. The stage scene is complete. HUD drawing is large but straightforward.\n\nWriting the `drawHud` function. Adding a `clean` helper to sanitize text by replacing smart quotes and ellipses with ASCII equivalents. Prompts will use a small cross sprite for PS buttons and plain text for Xbox A.\n\nMenu text will use scale 2 for readability from ten feet away. Headers scale to 3. The prompt glyphs remain sprites rather than font characters.\n\nA bright rectangle behind the active menu item will serve as the focus marker. All mode-specific draw functions will be consolidated into a single file. The `trackFor` helper is being added to songs.js. Clinic's `act` method now steps the simulation forward by one frame using the input body and seat. A `devNudge` helper is being added for slider adjustments. The `promptState` getter is also being exposed.\n\nThe default device is pad and the default glyphs are PS. The prompt state returns the confirm glyph, device type, and glyphs setting. The test will document that pressing ArrowRight switches the device to key, which then requires a pad press to show A.\n\nThe test will press the pad after switching to key mode. The game must call getGamepads each update so the engine detects the edge. gamepadButtons will be reset in setup and ready to prevent stale input. All source files are now being written.\n\nA pre-suite parse check will be added to songs.js. The clinic consult flow will show a join screen with seat selection and a pick list excluding ops 3 and 9. Confirming joins seat zero or the pad index, and confirming again starts the operation with consult mode enabled.\n\nPad button 0 joins the pad's seat and button 1 leaves. The log screen will read saved data and list operations with left and right navigation. About pages cover source fields, testing, engine, prompt, and credits; L1 and R1 change pages. Credits text cites MIT, Three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0, and code-written art and audio. Saving will also happen after each operation in the live game.\n\nA `saveProgress` guard will block saves during attract mode and when `blockSave` is true. The save routine appends the scene ID, records the operation's rank, score, and win state, enables quiet mode if op3 won, then writes the file. A new shift clears the save entirely. Settings are written to localStorage only when the user changes them, not on boot.\n\nAttract mode will not call writeSettings or setVolume. The idle clock uses performance.now, which is available in Node.js for headless runs. Even if headless steps take real time, ninety frames should stay under ten seconds, and the fingerprint does not include idle time.\n\nA wall-clock attract timer would break headless replay. The first run might enter attract mode while the replay skips it, causing a fingerprint mismatch. The idle check must not rely on real time.\n\nFrame counting would fail for low-fps browsers, so wall clock is required. Headless runs finish in under two seconds, so the ten-second idle threshold will not trigger attract mode during replay.\n\nThe attract timer will be gated by `typeof document !== 'undefined'`. Headless runs lack a document object, so attract mode never starts there and the replay fingerprint stays stable. The browser still uses wall-clock idle detection.\n\nA Node unit test for `buildStandings` will be added to session.js content tests so session logic can be verified without a browser. A separate test will confirm that `openSession` is not required.\n\nThe `buildStandings` function sorts players by score and groups ties into arrays. A content test will verify that a missing player is excluded and duplicates are not added. Each player receives two stats, which stays within the six-per-player limit.\n\nAwards will be limited to one per player, capped at three total. Scores must be finite numbers. The finish logic will skip completion when all players have left. A new `director.js` audio file will be added to keep the clinic module small.\n\nThe `trackFor` helper will be appended to songs.js using StrReplace. Clinic will cache two THREE.Vector3 instances for mouse raycasting and import THREE directly. Context menu and tab key events will be blocked during setup.\n\nThe clinic module will import hashSim, step, createOp, devCheat, retryStage, botInput, aim, ops, story, save, config, songs, devices, and session state. Total file sizes are estimated at roughly four hundred lines for the HUD, seven hundred for the clinic, two hundred for the stage, two hundred fifty for session logic, and two hundred for devices. The devices.js file will be drafted in a single write call. A tool flicking helper is being added to detect directional input from analog stick magnitude.\n\nThe devices module will map analog stick angles to eight tool sectors and only fire on rising edge, tracking previous magnitude per pad. Keyboard 1 through 8 will also select tools. The build script will write the output HTML to a path one directory above the dev folder.\n\nThe build script will import meta.js to read FILE_BASE. Session.js will be copied verbatim without trimming, preserving any trailing newline. Script close tags will only be escaped in the bundled output. Harness files will be copied to the work root as well. The inlined HTML is large but acceptable to write. The esbuild command targets ES2022 and outputs an ESM bundle.\n\npixel-engine.js will be bundled directly rather than externalized. AIHub is global and needs no import. The clinic menu's confirm action routes to call or log mode.\n\nThe clinic menu now routes to consult, settings, and about modes. The call screen offers difficulty selection, a new shift button, and a continue button that requires an existing save. Story progression advances lines and transitions to the brief or credits screen when finished. The brief screen confirms by beginning the operation. Results confirm saves progress and moves to the next scene or title. The pause menu provides resume, retry, restart, settings, dev, and quit options.\n\nA `sceneIndex` property will be added to the app. The new-shift action clears the save, resets the scene index and story line, and re-enables saving. The call screen will display the stored difficulty from settings. Files will be written in two or three batches. When an operation phase ends, the game switches to results during normal updates rather than inside the attract loop; attract mode will advance to the next reel instead.\n\nA reel clock will advance each attract-mode operation after eight seconds or when the phase ends. The pile-up operation will use four seats and consult mode, while all other attract operations use one seat. Every seat in the attract loop will be a bot. Banner text will match exactly.\n\nExit attract mode returns to the title screen, resets the idle timer, and swallows input without saving. The save guard stays active during the attract loop and is released on exit, but no save occurs then. Settings are not modified while attract mode runs. Dev mode will expose five tabs: balance, cheats, jump, actions, and view, switched with Q/E or L1/R1.\n\nDev mode tabs will handle balance, cheats, jump, actions, and view. Balance lists default settings with a reset button; arrow keys nudge values and Enter resets the config. Cheats toggles devCheat on Enter. Jump loads an operation from the list. Actions triggers immediate outcomes like win or fail. View controls hitboxes, bot visibility, and speed via left-right arrows. Simulation speed is a 0.1 to 3 slider stored on the app object. A frame-step toggle pauses the simulation and advances it one frame on confirm. Hitboxes render entity IDs when enabled. Bot play is controlled by app.botOn and app.botSkill.\n\nThe URL parameter `bot=1` will enable bot play for seat 0. Pause will no longer use `engine.paused`. Escape toggles between operation and pause modes, returns from settings or dev mode to pause, exits menu sub-menus to the main menu, and skips story text to the brief or credits screen. During an active session, Escape is ignored. The HUD will draw a session card when the mode is `card`. A session begins when time reaches zero while a simulation exists.\n\nSession mode will be entered when the session simulation exists and the client time is non-negative; otherwise it falls back to the card mode. The local seat data is sampled from the devices module for the current player. Fixed update will skip stepping during sessions because the interval handles simulation advancement. On the client, the local seat will still move in the main update loop since the interval does not step there.\n\nThe host will copy the local seat input into the shared inputs array every frame so the simulation interval can read it immediately. The client will also update its local seat position each frame using the sampled device input.\n\nThe server will not use the clinic module, so `state.local` is unused there and inputs arrive only through messages. The card screen will display the exact goal and how-to text. Player names from `AIHub.players` will be cleaned for the HUD font and rendered as plain text without HTML. A heartbeat animation will be added to the title screen using HUD rectangles. The files are now being written, and the clinic module may be split if it grows too large.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The sim is in place. Next I’ll correct the song patterns and add the game shell, session loop, and tests that drive them."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcd7a7f0-c3f9-49d5-90ba-9da08bb77b17-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/songs.js","old_string":"  sad: song(68,\n    'A4 . G4 . E4 . D4 . C4 . D4 . E4 .',\n    'A2 . . . E2 . . . A2 . . . E2 . . .',\n    REST),\n};","new_string":"  sad: song(68,\n    'A4 . G4 . E4 . D4 . C4 . D4 . E4 .',\n    'A2 . . . E2 . . . A2 . . . E2 . . .',\n    REST),\n};\n\nconst BOSSES = new Set(['op5', 'op7', 'op8', 'op9', 'sop5', 'sop7', 'sop8']);\n\n/** Which song fits this screen. Null means silence. */\nexport function trackFor(mode, sim) {\n  if (mode === 'results') {\n    const rank = sim?.rank;\n    return rank === 'S' || rank === 'A' ? 'fanfare' : 'sad';\n  }\n  if (mode === 'story' || mode === 'brief' || mode === 'credits') return 'ward';\n  if (mode === 'op' || mode === 'pause' || mode === 'dev' || mode === 'attract' || mode === 'session') {\n    const id = sim?.id || '';\n    if (id === 'op10') return 'sparse';\n    if (id === 'op9' || id === 'sop9') return (sim?.stageIndex || 0) >= 2 ? 'boss' : null;\n    if (BOSSES.has(id)) return 'boss';\n    const v = sim?.tables?.[0]?.vitals ?? 80;\n    if (v > 50) return 'calm';\n    if (v > 30) return 'tense';\n    return 'critical';\n  }\n  return 'title';\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fcd7a7f0-c3f9-49d5-90ba-9da08bb77b17-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/input/devices.js","new_string":"/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\n\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\n\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\n\nexport function readPads() {\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\n  let list = [];\n  try {\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\n  } catch {\n    return [];\n  }\n  const out = [];\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\n  return out;\n}\n\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\n}\n\nfunction button(pad, i) {\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\n  if (!b) return 0;\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\n  return b.value || 0;\n}\n\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\n  const was = !!prev[i];\n  prev[i] = down;\n  return down && !was;\n}\n\n/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\n  let tool = null;\n  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\n  }\n  prev.flick = mag;\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\n  return {\n    index: pad.index || 0,\n    sx,\n    sz: sy,\n    rx,\n    ry,\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\n    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\n    tool,\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || pad.buttons?.some((b) => b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)),\n  };\n  // sy stored after return would be skipped; store before by writing prev below via wrapper\n}\n\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\n  const pads = readPads();\n  const sampled = [];\n  let any = false;\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\n    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\n    slot.sy = sy;\n    if (row.any) any = true;\n    sampled.push(row);\n  });\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\n}\n\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\n  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\n}\n\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4542,"output_tokens":9410,"cache_read_input_tokens":152064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"c3f17626-202a-40fa-a935-bf7bc67275d6"}
