{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb050097-db0e-4d8e-94cb-1fcced871a81-28","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,67,108,105,110,105,99,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,47,116,121,112,101,115,47,101,110,103,105,110,101,47,69,110,103,105,110,101,46,100,46,116,115,10,49,51,49,58,101,120,112,111,114,116,32,105,110,116,101,114,102,97,99,101,32,69,110,103,105,110,101,79,112,116,105,111,110,115,32,123,10,49,52,48,58,32,32,32,32,97,115,112,101,99,116,63,58,32,65,115,112,101,99,116,77,111,100,101,59,10,49,55,50,58,32,32,32,32,100,101,98,117,103,85,73,63,58,32,98,111,111,108,101,97,110,59,10,49,56,55,58,32,32,32,32,115,101,116,116,105,110,103,115,63,58,32,123,10,49,57,50,58,32,32,32,32,116,111,117,99,104,63,58,32,98,111,111,108,101,97,110,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"export interface EngineOptions {\"},{\"line_number\":140,\"content\":\"    aspect?: AspectMode;\"},{\"line_number\":172,\"content\":\"    debugUI?: boolean;\"},{\"line_number\":187,\"content\":\"    settings?: {\"},{\"line_number\":192,\"content\":\"    touch?: boolean;\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb050097-db0e-4d8e-94cb-1fcced871a81-29","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\",\"content_concise\":\"400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n430→\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n440→---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n\\n**Head tags** (session client first, unmodified, see section 14):\\n- `hub:session` 1\\n- `hub:session-players` 1-4\\n- `hub:session-mode` shared-world\\n- `hub:session-minutes` 4\\n- `hub:webgpu` required\\n- `hub:session-goal` \\\"Keep the patient alive and top the team score\\\" (≤ 60 chars)\\n- `hub:session-howto` \\\"Stick/mouse: move tool. R2/click: use. Right stick/1-8: pick tool.\\\" (≤ 80 chars)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Screens and flow\\n\\n**10-foot rules** for every screen:\\n\\n- One idea per screen; at most about 8 rows at once.\\n- Text never below the engine font at scale 1 (at 1080p that is 28-pixel caps, ✔ reads well). Headers at scale 2+.\\n- A big focused item with a bright marker. Clipboard, chart and rubber-stamp motifs, never tables of data.\\n- Everything lives on the HUD canvas (`ctx.hud`), anchored to `hud.width`/`hud.height`, which vary (section 9). `hud.text` doesn't wrap and clips at the edge ✔, so write a `wrap(text, width)` helper using `hud.measure`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb050097-db0e-4d8e-94cb-1fcced871a81-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n10→  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n20→}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n30→      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n40→  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n50→  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n60→}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n70→  write(12, 'fmt ');\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n10→  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n20→}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n30→      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n40→  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n50→  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n60→}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n70→  write(12, 'fmt ');\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/audio/voice.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"import { renderSound } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\n\\nconst VOWEL = { a: [700, 1200], e: [450, 1900], i: [320, 2200], o: [520, 900], u: [340, 780], y: [320, 2200] };\\n\\n/** One glottal syllable. Pure PCM so Node can hear it with no audio device. */\\nexport function renderSyllable(pitch = 1, vowel = 'a', ms = 110, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.floor((sampleRate * ms) / 1000));\\n  const out = new Float32Array(n);\\n  const pair = VOWEL[vowel] || VOWEL.a;\\n  const f0 = 120 * pitch;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n    const t = i / sampleRate;\\n    const env = Math.sin((Math.PI * i) / n);\\n    const pulse = (t * f0) % 1 < 0.12 ? 1 : 0.15;\\n    const tone = Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[0] * t) * 0.55 + Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * pair[1] * t) * 0.35;\\n    out[i] = pulse * env * tone * 0.6;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function voicePcm(who, text, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const pitch = CAST[who]?.pitch || 1;\\n  const parts = [];\\n  let total = 0;\\n  const gap = new Float32Array(Math.floor(sampleRate * 0.035));\\n  for (const raw of String(text || '')) {\\n    const ch = raw.toLowerCase();\\n    if (ch === ' ') {\\n      parts.push(gap);\\n      total += gap.length;\\n      continue;\\n    }\\n    const vowel = VOWEL[ch] ? ch : 'a';\\n    const ms = ch === '!' ? 80 : ch === '?' ? 140 : 100;\\n    const syl = renderSyllable(pitch, vowel, ms, sampleRate);\\n    parts.push(syl);\\n    total += syl.length;\\n  }\\n  const out = new Float32Array(Math.max(1, total));\\n  let at = 0;\\n  for (const part of parts) {\\n    out.set(part, at);\\n    at += part.length;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nexport function rms(samples) {\\n  let s = 0;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < samples.length; i++) s += samples[i] * samples[i];\\n  return Math.sqrt(s / Math.max(1, samples.length));\\n}\\n\\nexport const CLICK = { wave: 'square', freq: 740, freqEnd: 180, decay: 0.07, volume: 0.4, duty: 0.25 };\\nexport const ALARM = { wave: 'square', freq: 440, freqEnd: 880, decay: 0.28, volume: 0.35, duty: 0.5 };\\n\\nexport function effectBuffer(def = CLICK) {\\n  return renderSound(def);\\n}\\n\\nexport function wavDataUrl(samples, sampleRate = 22050) {\\n  const bytes = 44 + samples.length * 2;\\n  const buf = new ArrayBuffer(bytes);\\n  const view = new DataView(buf);\\n  const write = (off, str) => { for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++) view.setUint8(off + i, str.charCodeAt(i)); };\\n  write(0, 'RIFF');\\n  view.setUint32(4, bytes - 8, true);\\n  write(8, 'WAVE');\\n  write(12, 'fmt ');\\n\",\"total_lines\":88}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fb050097-db0e-4d8e-94cb-1fcced871a81-31","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"063f7114-3754-43f6-bc70-ac9186a92e81"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_228","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-494de02c-6782-4b45-9d2a-0113b0070f39-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/Engine.d.ts","offset":131,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-494de02c-6782-4b45-9d2a-0113b0070f39-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export function parseSong|function parseSong","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/pixel-engine.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-494de02c-6782-4b45-9d2a-0113b0070f39-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/aim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2771,"output_tokens":312,"cache_read_input_tokens":86656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"0281e4a7-6c15-4f52-8b3d-f4443532fbbf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-494de02c-6782-4b45-9d2a-0113b0070f39-32","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"131→export interface EngineOptions {\\n    container?: HTMLElement;\\n    resolution?: Resolution;\\n    /**\\n     * `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width\\n     * follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly\\n     * `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport\\n     * at an integer scale, without black borders or stretched pixels.\\n     */\\n140→    aspect?: AspectMode;\\n    /**\\n     * Cap the render loop (simulation keeps its fixed 60 Hz physics step). Default 60, so\\n     * 120 Hz phones don't run the whole pipeline twice per game frame. 0 = display rate.\\n     */\\n    maxFps?: number;\\n    /** Shadow map quality, or `auto` (default: low on touch devices, else medium; lowered once on a slow start). */\\n    quality?: QualityOption;\\n    /** Pixel-styled loading indicator while the renderer, physics and assets load. Default true. */\\n    loadingScreen?: boolean;\\n150→    mode?: RenderMode;\\n    edges?: EdgeSettings;\\n    /** Camera preset + parameters. Pick one per game; not meant to change during play. */\\n    camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    /** Post filters (ids from FILTERS) applied in Pixel mode, in order. */\\n    filters?: readonly string[];\\n    /**\\n     * A full look: pixel art or clean rendering and filters per layer (characters & objects,\\n     * environment) plus whole-scene filters (render/look.ts). Wins over `filters` and `edges`.\\n     */\\n160→    look?: Look;\\n    /**\\n     * Seed for `ctx.random`: each level gets its own stream from this and the game's name, so\\n     * the same seed replays the same game. Default 1. `?seed=` in the URL.\\n     */\\n    seed?: number;\\n    /**\\n     * Frames of input the engine keeps for each level (`recording()`). Default `MAX_FRAMES`, an\\n     * hour at 60 fps (up to some 20 MB of JSON with the mouse moving all the time); 0 records nothing.\\n     */\\n170→    record?: number;\\n    /** Debug panel. Default: on in dev (`vite`) or with ?debug=1, off in production builds. */\\n    debugUI?: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer\\n     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\\n     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\\n     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\\n     */\\n    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\\n180→    /**\\n     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\\n     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\\n     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\\n     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\\n     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\\n     */\\n    settings?: {\\n        button?: TouchCorner | boolean;\\n        key?: string | false;\\n190→    };\\n    /** On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0. */\\n    touch?: boolean;\\n    /** On-screen action buttons. Default: the platformer's (DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS). */\\n    touchButtons?: readonly TouchButton[];\\n    /**\\n     * The touch top bar of the engine hotkeys (ⓘ debug panel, P, R, ◐ looks, ♪ mute), on a touch\\n     * screen while they are on (see `debugKeys`). Default true; false hides it even then, unless\\n     * the debug panel is on (`?debug=1`, dev builds).\\n     */\\n200→    touchBar?: boolean;\\n    background?: number;\\n}\\n/** `Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs. */\\nexport interface HeadlessOptions extends EngineOptions {\\n    /**\\n     * The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at\\n     * DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\\n     */\\n    viewport?: Viewport;\\n210→    /** How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`. */\",\"content_concise\":\"131→export interface EngineOptions {\\n    container?: HTMLElement;\\n    resolution?: Resolution;\\n    /**\\n     * `adaptive` (default): the art height stays `resolution.height` and the art width\\n     * follows the screen's aspect (portrait phones fill the screen). `fixed`: always exactly\\n     * `resolution`, letterboxed. `fill`: adjusts both art dimensions to cover the viewport\\n     * at an integer scale, without black borders or stretched pixels.\\n     */\\n140→    aspect?: AspectMode;\\n    /**\\n     * Cap the render loop (simulation keeps its fixed 60 Hz physics step). Default 60, so\\n     * 120 Hz phones don't run the whole pipeline twice per game frame. 0 = display rate.\\n     */\\n    maxFps?: number;\\n    /** Shadow map quality, or `auto` (default: low on touch devices, else medium; lowered once on a slow start). */\\n    quality?: QualityOption;\\n    /** Pixel-styled loading indicator while the renderer, physics and assets load. Default true. */\\n    loadingScreen?: boolean;\\n150→    mode?: RenderMode;\\n    edges?: EdgeSettings;\\n    /** Camera preset + parameters. Pick one per game; not meant to change during play. */\\n    camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    /** Post filters (ids from FILTERS) applied in Pixel mode, in order. */\\n    filters?: readonly string[];\\n    /**\\n     * A full look: pixel art or clean rendering and filters per layer (characters & objects,\\n     * environment) plus whole-scene filters (render/look.ts). Wins over `filters` and `edges`.\\n     */\\n160→    look?: Look;\\n    /**\\n     * Seed for `ctx.random`: each level gets its own stream from this and the game's name, so\\n     * the same seed replays the same game. Default 1. `?seed=` in the URL.\\n     */\\n    seed?: number;\\n    /**\\n     * Frames of input the engine keeps for each level (`recording()`). Default `MAX_FRAMES`, an\\n     * hour at 60 fps (up to some 20 MB of JSON with the mouse moving all the time); 0 records nothing.\\n     */\\n170→    record?: number;\\n    /** Debug panel. Default: on in dev (`vite`) or with ?debug=1, off in production builds. */\\n    debugUI?: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer\\n     * tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players\\n     * have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an object rebinds\\n     * or disables (null) single actions, and they still come with the debug panel.\\n     */\\n    debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption;\\n180→    /**\\n     * The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate,\\n     * sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true:\\n     * 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for none: open the\\n     * panel from your own menu (`engine.settings.open()`). `key`: where they are saved\\n     * (localStorage `pixel-engine:settings:<key>`; default the first game's name), false: nowhere.\\n     */\\n    settings?: {\\n        button?: TouchCorner | boolean;\\n        key?: string | false;\\n190→    };\\n    /** On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0. */\\n    touch?: boolean;\\n    /** On-screen action buttons. Default: the platformer's (DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS). */\\n    touchButtons?: readonly TouchButton[];\\n    /**