a-a=\\\"${e}\\\"]`).addEventListener(`click`,t);c(`close`,()=>o.close()),c(`done`,()=>o.close()),c(`reset`,()=>{o.reset(),e.audio.resetVolumes(),this.sync()}),this.root.addEv [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"64699c7b-095a-4c58-96ca-3871d4f6af50"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_230","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"pixel-engine.js is a single long line.\n\nI'll validate songs by importing parseSong in Node. I'll check music.d.ts for step count errors. Then I'll write game.js, AUTHORING, and test extensions, then run validation.\n\nWriting a touch-only gate for game.js. It detects fine-pointer devices, touchscreens, and connected gamepads to block unsupported input.\n\nThe touch gate is styled as a full-screen overlay. `createGame` returns a new Clinic instance. Default start options disable touch, set a dark background, low quality, and a fixed camera preset.\n\nThe boot function checks for the AIHub global. It shows the touch gate on unsupported devices and hides the start button there. Otherwise it uses a top-right button. If the hub is active it attempts to connect as a shared-world session with seats 1 through 4. It opens the network session and marks the hub ready when a server is found.\n\nThe boot function now checks for WebGPU support and fails if it is unavailable. It passes the session and touch-only flag into `createGame`, then starts the engine with the app container and merged options. If no hub info exists, it falls back to standalone mode.\n\ncheck.mjs imports the module and calls createGame() in a headless Node environment. The boot function is skipped there because it requires document. Clinic must not touch document. The constructor uses THREE.Vector3 which is safe. loadSettings checks localStorage first. Clinic.setup runs createView with THREE and toonMaterial. This must not throw in headless mode. playMusic parses songs. Bad song data will crash the headless engine.\n\nTitle mode fingerprint is stable. Headless location may be undefined, so applyUrl stays off and the mode remains title. Attract mode is document-gated. gamepadButtons initializes as an empty object. setLookLayer on a Group could crash headless; toonMaterial().clone() might fail if cloning is unsupported; lights.request is guarded by try/catch; canvas textures are skipped without document. The enterScene attract bug is not critical.\n\nHeadless mode includes a HUD, so drawHud calls in Clinic.update could throw if the API differs. I need to verify the sprite method signature in Hud.d.ts because GLYPH uses x and o mapped through INK. Story text like \"My hand is... it is fine.\" uses ASCII dots rather than ellipsis characters. I will check all story lines for length and charset compliance.\n\nCampaign mode will test all eleven operations at skill 1. This adds roughly 200,000 simulation steps, but it should finish in about ten to thirty seconds in Node. The existing balance tests already cover skills 0, 0.4, 0.7, and 1.0 for every operation, so this extra pass is acceptable. I am also writing an audio test that imports parseSong and the SONGS constant from pixel-engine.js.\n\nThe audio test iterates every song in SONGS and catches parseSong errors. It also generates a voice sample and an effect buffer, then asserts both are finite and have RMS above 0.01.\n\nVoice generation is fast because the buffer is short. Content tests will enforce story line limits, scene lengths between 8 and 16 lines, required about fields, and campaign save data. The current scanner skips game.js because it only walks src/ and docs/, but that file must be included since it is shipped. The built HTML is large and may contain forbidden strings like TODO.\n\nThe bundled root HTML is outside the dev folder, so the source scanner will not see it. However, the shipped HTML embeds the engine source, which could contain forbidden words like TODO or placeholder. The verifier might scan that HTML directly.\n\nThe engine must remain unmodified. If pixel-engine.js contains TODO or placeholder strings, the bundled HTML will include them too. The content test excludes that file, so the verifier may still flag those words in the shipped output.\n\nI will scan pixel-engine.js and session.js for forbidden strings like TODO or placeholder. The test runner must become async to support browser tests, Playwright, and the hub.\n\nThe test runner is now async. It runs simulation, content, and audio checks synchronously, but defers browser, launch, and hub tests until after the main function returns. Browser tests are disabled by default. Evidence files will be written to the SCRATCH directory.\n\nTests must not hardcode the scratch path. The verifier audits committed tests and evidence, so any hardcoded reference would break when scratch is deleted.\n\nTests will resolve the scratch path from an environment variable or a relative fallback. The verifier re-runs the same tests, so evidence files must remain available in that directory.\n\nThe scratch path is `../../tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/implementer` relative to the dev folder. The verifier audits committed tests and evidence before the goal ends, so the directory will still exist during verification.\n\nThe scratch path will be computed relative to the work root rather than hardcoded. The tmp directory is a sibling of the work folder, so the path can be derived from the test file's location.\n\nThe absolute scratch path is preferred over a relative one because it matches the plan and is clearer. Browser tests will target the built page so they exercise shipped code. They must run after the build step. Node tests will run first, then the build, then browser, launch, and hub tests.\n\nThe launch test will use Playwright to load the built root HTML via file://. It targets Chromium with WebGPU flags and a fresh context without storage. The test asserts that music equals 0.1, the framing offset is zero, and the canvas covers the viewport. It verifies that act drains on player one, that hashSim matches, and that page errors are absent. Screenshots are saved as launch-1.png and launch-2.png. A launch.txt summary is written to the scratch directory. The test runs after the build step.\n\nThe built root HTML is located one level up from the dev folder. Browser tests will load it via file:// and drive the title screen with Playwright keyboard input. The hub's own \"on its own\" check—pressing Enter, Space, Enter, Space and verifying still draws—will be performed in either the launch or browser test.\n\nA Playwright init script will inject a fake gamepad into `window.__pads` so the engine can read `navigator.getGamepads` during browser tests.\n\nThe engine input maps pads to keys unless gamepadButtons is empty. Clinic sets that object to {} in setup and every update.\n\nMenu focus starts on the title screen. Pressing Enter opens the menu. ArrowDown moves focus. The test will verify __GAME__.app.focus.\n\nHover tests use Playwright mouse movement. The engine converts pointer.y from NDC to art pixels using hud.height. At 960x540 fill mode the art size depends on pixel scale.\n\nThe test will compute the HUD height from `__GAME__.art.h` to map art coordinates to CSS pixels for mouse movement. Framing offset zero means the canvas covers the viewport with a linear pixel mapping. The settings test will open the menu, change the glyph set, and verify that `promptState().confirm` becomes 'A'. The glyphs row is row zero, and ArrowRight nudges the selection.\n\nThe settings test will open the menu, select the SETTINGS row, press Enter, and then ArrowRight to change the glyph set. The attract test will wait ten seconds with no input so the engine naturally enters attract mode; it will then verify that pressing a key exits attract without writing to localStorage. The browser test will target a Pixel 7 device.\n\nThe browser test will use Playwright's exact Pixel 7 device profile. It targets the settings button by its Unicode gear symbol and skips any element with a data-t=\"stick\" attribute.\n\nDev mode testing will start the operation via URL parameters, pause with Escape, open Dev mode by pressing Enter on row four, and verify that the first slider raises vitalsDrainMul to 1.1. The test will then press End to reach the RESET row, confirm it, and check that the value resets to 1.\n\nA two-pad test will load the URL with seats=2 and consult flags so both players begin as humans.\n\nThe two-pad test will omit the hold flag so fixedUpdate steps normally. Each pad will be assigned a different horizontal axis value, and the engine will run a few frames to verify that both seats move independently.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"human:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-38","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/audio/music.d.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-39","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/ops.js","offset":540,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1269,"output_tokens":4736,"cache_read_input_tokens":91392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a7b021a9-bf4f-4006-ab97-795fdcd2aa83"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-37","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,47,84,104,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,67,108,105,110,105,99,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,47,115,114,99,47,115,105,109,47,111,112,46,106,115,10,51,51,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,104,117,109,97,110,58,32,99,111,110,115,117,108,116,32,63,32,116,114,117,101,32,58,32,105,32,61,61,61,32,48,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"      human: consult ? true : i === 0,\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-38","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { type SoundDef } from './synth';\\n/** A track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those). */\\nexport type Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>;\\n/**\\n * A chiptune song as data. Each pattern holds one string per track: space-separated steps,\\n * where a step is a note ('C4', 'F#5', 'Bb2'), '.' (rest) or '-' (hold the previous note).\\n * Every track of a pattern must have the same number of steps. For `noise` tracks the\\n * note's pitch is the noise rate: C6 is a snare-ish hiss, C8 a hi-hat tick.\\n */\\n10→export interface Song {\\n    bpm: number;\\n    /** Steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Default 4. */\\n    stepsPerBeat?: number;\\n    tracks: Record<string, Instrument>;\\n    patterns: Record<string, Record<string, string>>;\\n    /** Pattern names in play order. */\\n    order: readonly string[];\\n    /** Loop forever (default true). */\\n    loop?: boolean;\\n20→}\\nexport interface SongNote {\\n    track: string;\\n    /** Step index from the start of the song. */\\n    step: number;\\n    /** Length in steps (1 + following holds). */\\n    steps: number;\\n    freq: number;\\n}\\nexport interface ParsedSong {\\n30→    /** Seconds per step. */\\n    stepTime: number;\\n    /** Total steps in one pass of `order`. */\\n    length: number;\\n    notes: SongNote[];\\n}\\n/** Flatten a song into timed notes. Throws on malformed patterns, so tests catch typos. */\\nexport declare function parseSong(song: Song): ParsedSong;\\n/** The playable SoundDef for one note of a track. */\\nexport declare function noteSound(instrument: Instrument, freq: number, seconds: number): SoundDef;\\n40→/** The playground's short looping track: C major, bouncy, 2 × 16 steps. */\\nexport declare const PLAYGROUND_SONG: Song;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { type SoundDef } from './synth';\\n/** A track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those). */\\nexport type Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>;\\n/**\\n * A chiptune song as data. Each pattern holds one string per track: space-separated steps,\\n * where a step is a note ('C4', 'F#5', 'Bb2'), '.' (rest) or '-' (hold the previous note).\\n * Every track of a pattern must have the same number of steps. For `noise` tracks the\\n * note's pitch is the noise rate: C6 is a snare-ish hiss, C8 a hi-hat tick.\\n */\\n10→export interface Song {\\n    bpm: number;\\n    /** Steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Default 4. */\\n    stepsPerBeat?: number;\\n    tracks: Record<string, Instrument>;\\n    patterns: Record<string, Record<string, string>>;\\n    /** Pattern names in play order. */\\n    order: readonly string[];\\n    /** Loop forever (default true). */\\n    loop?: boolean;\\n20→}\\nexport interface SongNote {\\n    track: string;\\n    /** Step index from the start of the song. */\\n    step: number;\\n    /** Length in steps (1 + following holds). */\\n    steps: number;\\n    freq: number;\\n}\\nexport interface ParsedSong {\\n30→    /** Seconds per step. */\\n    stepTime: number;\\n    /** Total steps in one pass of `order`. */\\n    length: number;\\n    notes: SongNote[];\\n}\\n/** Flatten a song into timed notes. Throws on malformed patterns, so tests catch typos. */\\nexport declare function parseSong(song: Song): ParsedSong;\\n/** The playable SoundDef for one note of a track. */\\nexport declare function noteSound(instrument: Instrument, freq: number, seconds: number): SoundDef;\\n40→/** The playground's short looping track: C major, bouncy, 2 × 16 steps. */\\nexport declare const PLAYGROUND_SONG: Song;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/audio/music.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"import { type SoundDef } from './synth';\\n/** A track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those). */\\nexport type Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>;\\n/**\\n * A chiptune song as data. Each pattern holds one string per track: space-separated steps,\\n * where a step is a note ('C4', 'F#5', 'Bb2'), '.' (rest) or '-' (hold the previous note).\\n * Every track of a pattern must have the same number of steps. For `noise` tracks the\\n * note's pitch is the noise rate: C6 is a snare-ish hiss, C8 a hi-hat tick.\\n */\\nexport interface Song {\\n    bpm: number;\\n    /** Steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Default 4. */\\n    stepsPerBeat?: number;\\n    tracks: Record<string, Instrument>;\\n    patterns: Record<string, Record<string, string>>;\\n    /** Pattern names in play order. */\\n    order: readonly string[];\\n    /** Loop forever (default true). */\\n    loop?: boolean;\\n}\\nexport interface SongNote {\\n    track: string;\\n    /** Step index from the start of the song. */\\n    step: number;\\n    /** Length in steps (1 + following holds). */\\n    steps: number;\\n    freq: number;\\n}\\nexport interface ParsedSong {\\n    /** Seconds per step. */\\n    stepTime: number;\\n    /** Total steps in one pass of `order`. */\\n    length: number;\\n    notes: SongNote[];\\n}\\n/** Flatten a song into timed notes. Throws on malformed patterns, so tests catch typos. */\\nexport declare function parseSong(song: Song): ParsedSong;\\n/** The playable SoundDef for one note of a track. */\\nexport declare function noteSound(instrument: Instrument, freq: number, seconds: number): SoundDef;\\n/** The playground's short looping track: C major, bouncy, 2 × 16 steps. */\\nexport declare const PLAYGROUND_SONG: Song;\\n\",\"total_lines\":41}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-324df24d-aa9e-4f8a-9afb-49628d7975ef-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"540→        spawn: [\\n          line('ip', 'pore', 0.4, 0.2, { len: 0.5, dx: 1, dz: 0.1 }),\\n          line('ic', 'core', 0.5, -0.4, { pull: 1.6, dx: 0.2, dz: 1, tether: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Dress it.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('pg', 'gel', 0, -1.3, { w: 1.5, h: 0.6 }),\\n          line('pd', 'dressing', 0, 1.4, { len: 1.3, dx: 1, dz: 0 }),\\n550→          line('ringp', 'ring', 2.3, 0.2, { optional: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    ],\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function sessionOp(base, mul) {\\n  return { ...base, id: `s${base.id}`, session: true, time: 200, strainHp: mul, par: base.par };\\n}\\n560→\\nexport const SESSION_OPS = [\\n  OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'pile'),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op5'), 0.34),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op7'), 0.4),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op8'), 1 / 7),\\n];\\n\\nexport const STORY_OPS = OPS.filter((o) => o.n <= 10);\\nexport const ALL_OPS = OPS;\\n570→\\nexport function opById(id) {\\n  return OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || SESSION_OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || null;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"540→        spawn: [\\n          line('ip', 'pore', 0.4, 0.2, { len: 0.5, dx: 1, dz: 0.1 }),\\n          line('ic', 'core', 0.5, -0.4, { pull: 1.6, dx: 0.2, dz: 1, tether: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Dress it.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('pg', 'gel', 0, -1.3, { w: 1.5, h: 0.6 }),\\n          line('pd', 'dressing', 0, 1.4, { len: 1.3, dx: 1, dz: 0 }),\\n550→          line('ringp', 'ring', 2.3, 0.2, { optional: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    ],\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function sessionOp(base, mul) {\\n  return { ...base, id: `s${base.id}`, session: true, time: 200, strainHp: mul, par: base.par };\\n}\\n560→\\nexport const SESSION_OPS = [\\n  OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'pile'),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op5'), 0.34),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op7'), 0.4),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op8'), 1 / 7),\\n];\\n\\nexport const STORY_OPS = OPS.filter((o) => o.n <= 10);\\nexport const ALL_OPS = OPS;\\n570→\\nexport function opById(id) {\\n  return OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || SESSION_OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || null;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/ops.js\",\"offset\":540,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"        spawn: [\\n          line('ip', 'pore', 0.4, 0.2, { len: 0.5, dx: 1, dz: 0.1 }),\\n          line('ic', 'core', 0.5, -0.4, { pull: 1.6, dx: 0.2, dz: 1, tether: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Dress it.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('pg', 'gel', 0, -1.3, { w: 1.5, h: 0.6 }),\\n          line('pd', 'dressing', 0, 1.4, { len: 1.3, dx: 1, dz: 0 }),\\n          line('ringp', 'ring', 2.3, 0.2, { optional: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n    ],\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function sessionOp(base, mul) {\\n  return { ...base, id: `s${base.id}`, session: true, time: 200, strainHp: mul, par: base.par };\\n}\\n\\nexport const SESSION_OPS = [\\n  OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'pile'),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op5'), 0.34),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op7'), 0.4),\\n  sessionOp(OPS.find((o) => o.id === 'op8'), 1 / 7),\\n];\\n\\nexport const STORY_OPS = OPS.filter((o) => o.n <= 10);\\nexport const ALL_OPS = OPS;\\n\\nexport function opById(id) {\\n  return OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || SESSION_OPS.find((o) => o.id === id) || null;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":573}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"3c82d1a7-224a-4c42-8a99-6956b4901e63"}
