{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_233","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"hub.ready() returns early under certain conditions.\n\nClinic.ready() calls AIHub.ready() after Engine.start. The harness needs ready() before the card check, but Engine.start can take several seconds. This fits within the 20-second budget if the engine starts quickly. The host must not finish the operation in the first ~1.5 seconds. Once loaded, ready() is called without a keypress.\n\nThe server copy calls ready() immediately without Engine.start. Players connect before Engine.start and then call ready() inside game.ready. A bug was found: hub.ready() returns early if the welcome message has not arrived yet, so it never retries.\n\nA polling loop could retry ready() if the welcome message hasn't arrived yet. The sentReady flag is internal, so detecting a no-op without it is difficult.\n\nA retry loop will be added in Clinic.ready. It calls ready() immediately and then polls every 200 milliseconds for 15 seconds, since the welcome message may arrive after the first frame. Once sentReady is set, repeated calls are harmless. The harness pokes Enter to answer cards, and Clinic listens for both window keydown and engine wasPressed.\n\nThe host sends a ping before the engine starts. Clients send input during card reads. The host only finishes on win, loss, or time-up. It does not finish on idle or host-leave.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a3f2d16c-f921-44c0-abaa-b87c524e07e9-45","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/net/session.js","offset":96}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a3f2d16c-f921-44c0-abaa-b87c524e07e9-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/harness.html","offset":400,"limit":150}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1528,"output_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":100736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"affa3347-c485-450b-9bc2-4b37cbd97e84"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a3f2d16c-f921-44c0-abaa-b87c524e07e9-45","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"96→ */\\nexport function openSession(hub) {\\n  const state = {\\n    sim: null,\\n100→    inputs: {},\\n    local: { x: 0, z: 1.2, tool: 'forceps', use: false, gift: false, steady: false, sx: 0, sz: 0 },\\n    card: null,\\n    started: false,\\n    ended: false,\\n    finished: false,\\n    lastT: null,\\n    tokens: 16,\\n    refill: nowMs(),\\n    acc: { input: 0, snap: 0, key: 0, ping: 0 },\\n110→    me: hub.me,\\n    timer: 0,\\n    silence: null,\\n    onSim: null,\\n  };\\n\\n  const send = (data, reliable) => {\\n    if (state.ended || state.finished) return;\\n    if (!allow(state)) return;\\n    hub.send(data, { reliable: !!reliable });\\n120→  };\\n\\n  hub.on('card', (card) => {\\n    state.card = card;\\n  });\\n  hub.on('start', () => {\\n    state.started = true;\\n    state.me = hub.me;\\n    if (state.sim) return;\\n    try {\\n130→      beginOp(hub, state);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err?.message || err));\\n    }\\n  });\\n  hub.on('message', (data) => {\\n    if (!data || data.t === 'p') return;\\n    if (data.t === 'i' && Number.isInteger(data.n)) {\\n      state.inputs[data.n] = {\\n        x: data.x, z: data.z, sx: data.sx, sz: data.sz, tool: data.tool,\\n140→        use: !!data.use, gift: !!data.gift, steady: !!data.steady,\\n      };\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if ((data.t === 's' || data.t === 'k') && !hub.isHost) applySnap(state, data.snap);\\n  });\\n  hub.on('leave', () => {\\n    /* The hub voids a host leave. This copy does not finish. */\\n  });\\n  hub.on('time-up', () => finishRound(hub, state, false));\\n150→  hub.on('end', () => {\\n    state.ended = true;\\n    clearInterval(state.timer);\\n    state.silence?.();\\n  });\\n\\n  hub.probe?.(() => ({\\n    scene: state.sim ? 'op' : 'card',\\n    menu: '',\\n    world: state.sim?.id || 'card',\\n160→    input: 'pad',\\n  }));\\n\\n  state.timer = setInterval(() => {\\n    try {\\n    if (state.ended) return;\\n    const t = hub.time();\\n    const wall = nowMs();\\n    if (!hub.isHost && state.me != null) {\\n      state.acc.input += wall - (state.acc.inputAt || wall);\\n170→      state.acc.inputAt = wall;\\n      if (state.acc.input >= 66) {\\n        state.acc.input = 0;\\n        const loc = state.local || {};\\n        send({\\n          t: 'i', n: state.me, x: loc.x || 0, z: loc.z || 0, sx: loc.sx || 0, sz: loc.sz || 0,\\n          tool: loc.tool || 'forceps', use: !!loc.use, gift: !!loc.gift, steady: !!loc.steady,\\n        }, false);\\n      }\\n    } else if (hub.isHost) {\\n180→      state.acc.ping += wall - (state.acc.pingAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.pingAt = wall;\\n      if (!state.started || t < 0) {\\n        if (state.acc.ping >= 250) {\\n          state.acc.ping = 0;\\n          send({ t: 'p' }, false);\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (state.sim && !state.finished) {\\n190→        if (state.lastT == null) state.lastT = t;\\n        let steps = Math.round((t - state.lastT) / (DT * 1000));\\n        if (steps > 4) steps = 4;\\n        if (steps < 0) steps = 0;\\n        state.lastT += steps * DT * 1000;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) step(state.sim, hostInputs(state), DT);\\n        if (state.sim.phase === 'won' || state.sim.phase === 'lost') finishRound(hub, state, state.sim.phase === 'won');\\n      }\\n      state.acc.snap += wall - (state.acc.snapAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.snapAt = wall;\\n200→      if (state.sim && state.acc.snap >= 84) {\\n        state.acc.snap = 0;\\n        send({ t: 's', snap: encodeFast(state.sim) }, false);\\n      }\\n      state.acc.key += wall - (state.acc.keyAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.keyAt = wall;\\n      if (state.sim && state.acc.key >= 1000) {\\n        state.acc.key = 0;\\n        send({ t: 'k', snap: encodeKey(state.sim) }, true);\\n      }\\n210→    }\\n    } catch {\\n      /* A bad tick must not take the round down. */\\n    }\\n  }, 34);\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stopSession(state) {\\n220→  if (!state) return;\\n  state.ended = true;\\n  clearInterval(state.timer);\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"96→ */\\nexport function openSession(hub) {\\n  const state = {\\n    sim: null,\\n100→    inputs: {},\\n    local: { x: 0, z: 1.2, tool: 'forceps', use: false, gift: false, steady: false, sx: 0, sz: 0 },\\n    card: null,\\n    started: false,\\n    ended: false,\\n    finished: false,\\n    lastT: null,\\n    tokens: 16,\\n    refill: nowMs(),\\n    acc: { input: 0, snap: 0, key: 0, ping: 0 },\\n110→    me: hub.me,\\n    timer: 0,\\n    silence: null,\\n    onSim: null,\\n  };\\n\\n  const send = (data, reliable) => {\\n    if (state.ended || state.finished) return;\\n    if (!allow(state)) return;\\n    hub.send(data, { reliable: !!reliable });\\n120→  };\\n\\n  hub.on('card', (card) => {\\n    state.card = card;\\n  });\\n  hub.on('start', () => {\\n    state.started = true;\\n    state.me = hub.me;\\n    if (state.sim) return;\\n    try {\\n130→      beginOp(hub, state);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err?.message || err));\\n    }\\n  });\\n  hub.on('message', (data) => {\\n    if (!data || data.t === 'p') return;\\n    if (data.t === 'i' && Number.isInteger(data.n)) {\\n      state.inputs[data.n] = {\\n        x: data.x, z: data.z, sx: data.sx, sz: data.sz, tool: data.tool,\\n140→        use: !!data.use, gift: !!data.gift, steady: !!data.steady,\\n      };\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if ((data.t === 's' || data.t === 'k') && !hub.isHost) applySnap(state, data.snap);\\n  });\\n  hub.on('leave', () => {\\n    /* The hub voids a host leave. This copy does not finish. */\\n  });\\n  hub.on('time-up', () => finishRound(hub, state, false));\\n150→  hub.on('end', () => {\\n    state.ended = true;\\n    clearInterval(state.timer);\\n    state.silence?.();\\n  });\\n\\n  hub.probe?.(() => ({\\n    scene: state.sim ? 'op' : 'card',\\n    menu: '',\\n    world: state.sim?.id || 'card',\\n160→    input: 'pad',\\n  }));\\n\\n  state.timer = setInterval(() => {\\n    try {\\n    if (state.ended) return;\\n    const t = hub.time();\\n    const wall = nowMs();\\n    if (!hub.isHost && state.me != null) {\\n      state.acc.input += wall - (state.acc.inputAt || wall);\\n170→      state.acc.inputAt = wall;\\n      if (state.acc.input >= 66) {\\n        state.acc.input = 0;\\n        const loc = state.local || {};\\n        send({\\n          t: 'i', n: state.me, x: loc.x || 0, z: loc.z || 0, sx: loc.sx || 0, sz: loc.sz || 0,\\n          tool: loc.tool || 'forceps', use: !!loc.use, gift: !!loc.gift, steady: !!loc.steady,\\n        }, false);\\n      }\\n    } else if (hub.isHost) {\\n180→      state.acc.ping += wall - (state.acc.pingAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.pingAt = wall;\\n      if (!state.started || t < 0) {\\n        if (state.acc.ping >= 250) {\\n          state.acc.ping = 0;\\n          send({ t: 'p' }, false);\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (state.sim && !state.finished) {\\n190→        if (state.lastT == null) state.lastT = t;\\n        let steps = Math.round((t - state.lastT) / (DT * 1000));\\n        if (steps > 4) steps = 4;\\n        if (steps < 0) steps = 0;\\n        state.lastT += steps * DT * 1000;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) step(state.sim, hostInputs(state), DT);\\n        if (state.sim.phase === 'won' || state.sim.phase === 'lost') finishRound(hub, state, state.sim.phase === 'won');\\n      }\\n      state.acc.snap += wall - (state.acc.snapAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.snapAt = wall;\\n200→      if (state.sim && state.acc.snap >= 84) {\\n        state.acc.snap = 0;\\n        send({ t: 's', snap: encodeFast(state.sim) }, false);\\n      }\\n      state.acc.key += wall - (state.acc.keyAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.keyAt = wall;\\n      if (state.sim && state.acc.key >= 1000) {\\n        state.acc.key = 0;\\n        send({ t: 'k', snap: encodeKey(state.sim) }, true);\\n      }\\n210→    }\\n    } catch {\\n      /* A bad tick must not take the round down. */\\n    }\\n  }, 34);\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stopSession(state) {\\n220→  if (!state) return;\\n  state.ended = true;\\n  clearInterval(state.timer);\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/net/session.js\",\"offset\":96,\"raw_output\":\" */\\nexport function openSession(hub) {\\n  const state = {\\n    sim: null,\\n    inputs: {},\\n    local: { x: 0, z: 1.2, tool: 'forceps', use: false, gift: false, steady: false, sx: 0, sz: 0 },\\n    card: null,\\n    started: false,\\n    ended: false,\\n    finished: false,\\n    lastT: null,\\n    tokens: 16,\\n    refill: nowMs(),\\n    acc: { input: 0, snap: 0, key: 0, ping: 0 },\\n    me: hub.me,\\n    timer: 0,\\n    silence: null,\\n    onSim: null,\\n  };\\n\\n  const send = (data, reliable) => {\\n    if (state.ended || state.finished) return;\\n    if (!allow(state)) return;\\n    hub.send(data, { reliable: !!reliable });\\n  };\\n\\n  hub.on('card', (card) => {\\n    state.card = card;\\n  });\\n  hub.on('start', () => {\\n    state.started = true;\\n    state.me = hub.me;\\n    if (state.sim) return;\\n    try {\\n      beginOp(hub, state);\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err?.message || err));\\n    }\\n  });\\n  hub.on('message', (data) => {\\n    if (!data || data.t === 'p') return;\\n    if (data.t === 'i' && Number.isInteger(data.n)) {\\n      state.inputs[data.n] = {\\n        x: data.x, z: data.z, sx: data.sx, sz: data.sz, tool: data.tool,\\n        use: !!data.use, gift: !!data.gift, steady: !!data.steady,\\n      };\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if ((data.t === 's' || data.t === 'k') && !hub.isHost) applySnap(state, data.snap);\\n  });\\n  hub.on('leave', () => {\\n    /* The hub voids a host leave. This copy does not finish. */\\n  });\\n  hub.on('time-up', () => finishRound(hub, state, false));\\n  hub.on('end', () => {\\n    state.ended = true;\\n    clearInterval(state.timer);\\n    state.silence?.();\\n  });\\n\\n  hub.probe?.(() => ({\\n    scene: state.sim ? 'op' : 'card',\\n    menu: '',\\n    world: state.sim?.id || 'card',\\n    input: 'pad',\\n  }));\\n\\n  state.timer = setInterval(() => {\\n    try {\\n    if (state.ended) return;\\n    const t = hub.time();\\n    const wall = nowMs();\\n    if (!hub.isHost && state.me != null) {\\n      state.acc.input += wall - (state.acc.inputAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.inputAt = wall;\\n      if (state.acc.input >= 66) {\\n        state.acc.input = 0;\\n        const loc = state.local || {};\\n        send({\\n          t: 'i', n: state.me, x: loc.x || 0, z: loc.z || 0, sx: loc.sx || 0, sz: loc.sz || 0,\\n          tool: loc.tool || 'forceps', use: !!loc.use, gift: !!loc.gift, steady: !!loc.steady,\\n        }, false);\\n      }\\n    } else if (hub.isHost) {\\n      state.acc.ping += wall - (state.acc.pingAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.pingAt = wall;\\n      if (!state.started || t < 0) {\\n        if (state.acc.ping >= 250) {\\n          state.acc.ping = 0;\\n          send({ t: 'p' }, false);\\n        }\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (state.sim && !state.finished) {\\n        if (state.lastT == null) state.lastT = t;\\n        let steps = Math.round((t - state.lastT) / (DT * 1000));\\n        if (steps > 4) steps = 4;\\n        if (steps < 0) steps = 0;\\n        state.lastT += steps * DT * 1000;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) step(state.sim, hostInputs(state), DT);\\n        if (state.sim.phase === 'won' || state.sim.phase === 'lost') finishRound(hub, state, state.sim.phase === 'won');\\n      }\\n      state.acc.snap += wall - (state.acc.snapAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.snapAt = wall;\\n      if (state.sim && state.acc.snap >= 84) {\\n        state.acc.snap = 0;\\n        send({ t: 's', snap: encodeFast(state.sim) }, false);\\n      }\\n      state.acc.key += wall - (state.acc.keyAt || wall);\\n      state.acc.keyAt = wall;\\n      if (state.sim && state.acc.key >= 1000) {\\n        state.acc.key = 0;\\n        send({ t: 'k', snap: encodeKey(state.sim) }, true);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    } catch {\\n      /* A bad tick must not take the round down. */\\n    }\\n  }, 34);\\n\\n  return state;\\n}\\n\\nexport function stopSession(state) {\\n  if (!state) return;\\n  state.ended = true;\\n  clearInterval(state.timer);\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":223}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a3f2d16c-f921-44c0-abaa-b87c524e07e9-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '') => {\\n    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\\n    renderChecks(checks);\\n    return !!pass;\\n410→  };\\n  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\\n  window.__hubCheck = report;\\n  try {\\n    const state = await newRound();\\n    if (!state) {\\n      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const n = state.n;\\n420→    const m = state.metas;\\n    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\\n    const seats = String(m?.players ?? '').match(/\\\\d+/g)?.map(Number) ?? [];\\n    const [least, most = least] = seats;\\n    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\\n    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\\n\\n    // Every copy: the players, and in a server round the server's copy.\\n    const copies = () => [...(state.status?.players ?? []), ...(state.status?.server ? [state.status.server] : [])];\\n    const helloed = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.hello), TIMINGS.helloMs + 1000);\\n430→    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    if (!helloed) return;\\n    const caps = state.coordinator.seats().map((s) => s.caps);\\n    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\\n    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\\n    if (state.cells.some((c) => !c.frame.contentDocument)) {\\n      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n440→    // The card collects ready: every game readies up by itself once loaded, with no prompt and no key.\\n    const loaded = await until(() => copies().every((p) => p.ready), 20_000);\\n    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\\n    // A game that shows its own card takes the players' answers on it: Enter is Ready.\\n    if (caps.some((c) => c?.card)) {\\n      const players = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.server);\\n      const sent = await until(() => players.every((c) => c.cardSent), 2000);\\n      for (const cell of players) poke(cell, 'Enter');\\n      const answered = await until(() => players.every((c) => state.answers.ready.has(c.key)), 3000);\\n      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\\n450→    }\\n    releaseRound(state);\\n    const started = await until(() => state.status?.phase !== 'loading', 15_000);\\n    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\\n    if (!started || state.record) return;\\n\\n    await until(() => state.status.phase === 'playing' || state.record, TIMINGS.countdownMs + 2000);\\n    const arrows = ['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'a', 'd', 'w', 's'];\\n    const randomly = async (ms) => {\\n      const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n460→      while (performance.now() < end && !state.record) {\\n        for (const cell of state.cells) if (!cell.gone && !cell.server) poke(cell, arrows[Math.floor(Math.random() * arrows.length)]);\\n        await sleep(150);\\n      }\\n    };\\n    await randomly(Math.min(1500, playMs / 4));\\n\\n    const mode = state.coordinator.mode;\\n    // Parallel and ghost: every copy runs its own world from the same seeded start. A game\\n    // still tagged race was built to race's contract: no seeded start, and no progress asked.\\n470→    const own = SELF_REPORTED.includes(mode);\\n    const legacyRace = own && !seedsRandom(m?.mode);\\n    if (own && !legacyRace) {\\n      const seeded = state.cells.every((c) => c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded === true);\\n      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\\n    }\\n\\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave') removeCell(state.cells[0]);\\n    else if (n >= 3) removeCell(state.cells[n - 1]);\\n    await randomly(playMs / 2);\\n480→    const remaining = state.cells.filter((c) => !c.gone);\\n    if (own) {\\n      if (mode === 'parallel') {\\n        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\\n          state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\\n      } else {\\n        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\\n          remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent}`).join(' '));\\n      }\\n      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\\n490→        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key}: ${c.progress.length} report${c.progress.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`).join(', '));\\n    } else {\\n      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\\n        remaining.map((c) => `${c.key} ↑${c.bridge.stats.sent} ↓${c.bridge.stats.received}`).join(' '));\\n    }\\n\\n    if (!state.record) state.coordinator.timeUp();\\n    const ended = await until(() => state.record, TIMINGS.graceMs + 2000);\\n    const record = state.record;\\n    if (serverMode) {\\n500→      // The world ran on the server: the players heard it, and only the host may finish a shared world.\\n      const serverCell = state.cells.find((c) => c.server);\\n      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\\n        record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason}), host ${record.hostId}, server sent ${serverCell.bridge.stats.sent}` : 'no end');\\n    }\\n    if (scenario === 'host-leave' && !SELF_REPORTED.includes(state.coordinator.mode)) {\\n      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\\n    } else {\\n      check('the round ends with a valid result', ended && record.status === 'played', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end within the grace period');\\n    }\\n510→    await sleep(300);\\n    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\\n    const issues = [...(state.status?.issues ?? []), ...state.cells.flatMap((c) => c.bridge.issues)];\\n    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\\n    const violations = state.cells.flatMap((c) => {\\n      let extra = [];\\n      try {\\n        extra = c.frame.contentWindow?.__hubViolations ?? [];\\n      } catch {}\\n      return [...c.violations, ...extra].map((v) => `${c.key}: ${v}`);\\n520→    });\\n    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\\n  } finally {\\n    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\\n    report.done = true;\\n    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\\n    log(`conformance: ${report.pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL'}`);\\n  }\\n530→}\\n\\nfunction renderChecks(checks) {\\n  $('checklist').replaceChildren(\\n    ...checks.map((c) => {\\n      const li = document.createElement('li');\\n      li.className = c.pass ? 'ok' : 'bad';\\n      li.textContent = c.name + (c.detail && !c.pass ? ` — ${c.detail}` : '');\\n      li.title = c.detail;\\n      return li;\\n540→    }),\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nif (auto) conformance();\\nelse if ($('game').value) newRound();\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n  const checks = [];\\n  const check = (name, pass, detail = '