{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_254","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine contains placeholder, stub, or TODO markers.\n\nThe bundled engine cannot be stripped, so TODOs may appear in the shipped HTML. The source lint and tests only scan src and docs, not the bundle. I will check the exact grep matches if needed.\n\nI will keep the source clean and avoid stubbed features. I am preemptively updating mint and rose to lime and red in hud.js to prevent color lookup errors. Title scale 2 text may be wide but will not throw. I am now writing files and fixing Clinic.ready.\n\nClinic.ready now polls AIHub readiness every 250 ms with a 18-second timeout. dispose clears that timer and silences the session. The server path never constructs Clinic, so it avoids the timer entirely.\n\nThe dev index.html loads game.js as a module without session.js, so AIHub is undefined there. The boot function guards against this by checking globalThis.AIHub and falling back to standalone Engine.start when the hub is inactive or missing.\n\nThe boot function requests a shared-world session with seats 1 and 4 and card mode. It fails and returns if the hub rejects the connection. On success it opens the session, marks the hub ready, and returns for server paths. For client paths it checks for WebGPU support and fails with a note if unavailable. Otherwise it opens the session.\n\nThe boot function starts the engine with the session and options. It adds a standalone WebGPU check that shows a friendly note if GPU is missing.\n\nThe WebGPU fallback note uses a light gray font and 16px sans-serif styling. file:// URLs report navigator.gpu with flags, so launch tests pass without extra checks. check.mjs headless mode skips boot entirely. Desktop mouse users bypass the gate because any-pointer fine is true. Pixel 7 devices trigger the gate since they lack a fine pointer and have touch points.\n\nI will verify in the test whether Playwright Pixel 7 mobile emulation reports a fine pointer. The settings button selector will target the gear icon or aria label. I will inspect the engine markup after the first browser run. The attract screen sits behind the gate with pointer-events none so the engine button remains clickable.\n\nThe gate text will be exactly \"Controller or keyboard required\". game.js will remove the #touch-gate element on keydown and gamepadconnected events.\n\nClinic also removes the gate during setup, so duplicating that logic in game.js is harmless. The test should not press keys before checking the gate text on Pixel 7. The dev index.html does not need a title update because game.js boots Clinic directly. withUrlOptions may override the camera from URL parameters, which is acceptable. Setting record to zero prevents storing an hour of input; headless check.mjs uses its own recording instead.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ad034c3d-d6bd-48a3-8f78-dd2226eeeacc-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"type HudAnchor","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/hud/Hud.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1810,"output_tokens":1615,"cache_read_input_tokens":127360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"6b63938d-1d51-484d-bd2e-01fe9300a679"}
