e/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/types/engine/hud/Hud.d.ts\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":4,\"content\":\"export type HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right';\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"b5fff58f-46c5-4465-a49d-243da778c436"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_255","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Proceeding to write all the code.\n\nPlanning the browser test module for live.mjs. It will export functions to handle browser, launch, hub, and package evidence. Screenshots at 1920x1080 will capture the title, arenas, busts, HUD, and results stamp. These may be combined with logic tests at 960x540 or handled separately.\n\nMapping the ten arenas to their operation URLs with god mode enabled. Screenshots will wait for the game to paint before capturing. Blank frames will be detected using ImageMagick mean brightness rather than direct canvas sampling.\n\nDrafting the `bootOnce` helper to launch a headless browser at 960x540, navigate to the first operation with a fixed seed and god mode enabled, and collect page errors. The blank-frame check will run ImageMagick on the screenshot and fail if mean brightness is near zero. Two launches must produce matching hashes after the same action.\n\nThe bootOnce helper now waits for the game engine to initialize, then executes a drain action at a fixed position and repeats it thirty times to change the pool state.\n\nThe `bootOnce` helper will return the music state, pool data, framing, canvas and viewport dimensions, page errors, GPU errors, and AI hub flags. A small clinic change is needed: add a `hash` getter to the game API that returns `hashSim(this.sim)`, since `hashSim` is not currently exposed on `__GAME__`.\n\nThe fingerprint string will be `op|focus|line|hash`, so the hash sits at the end. Two runs must match this final segment. After the drain action, the pool radius should drop from 0.7 or reach done; a failure there is honest. `hold=1` keeps fixed updates paused while `act()` still runs. Music volume should read 0.1 because the fresh context lacks localStorage audio data and `clinic.setup` initializes it. The exact framing field names are still needed.\n\nFraming fields are artWidth, artHeight, scale, offsetX, offsetY, cssWidth, and cssHeight. Fill mode offsets are zero and the canvas covers the viewport.\n\nA title-page browser check will load the page without a query string, press Enter, Space, Enter, Space, then verify the canvas exists, no errors occur, AIHub is inactive, and seeded is not true.\n\nScreenshots at 1920x1080 will use a separate context. The title page loads without query parameters. Each arena screenshot uses ?op=&god=1&hold=1.\n\nBust screenshots will use the night scene query. HUD screenshots will use op1. For the results screenshot, loading with dev mode enabled and triggering a win via devCheat would leave the game stuck in dev mode because the results transition only runs when mode is op. This path is blocked.\n\nThe mode transition logic will be updated so that winning an operation switches the game from dev mode into results mode. This allows the test to reach the results stamp without leaving the user stuck in the dev overlay.\n\nThe mode transition condition is being expanded to include dev and pause alongside op. This lets the test reach results after winning from dev mode or after pausing from op mode. God mode prevents death during screenshots.\n\nThe results screenshot will show the rank stamp at scale 6. Arena screenshots will keep the god and hold view, revealing tissue through syncView. The bust screenshot targets the night scene story mode.\n\nThe hub test will start a Python server, then drive five URLs sequentially with one browser per URL to save memory. It waits for dataset.complete, checks __hubCheck.pass, writes hub.txt, and kills the server by PID.\n\nFour WebGPU players may cause out-of-memory errors. Quality low helps. Each URL may need up to 120 seconds.\n\nEach URL will get a 90-second timeout. The Python server binds to 127.0.0.1 from the dist folder. The harness game path is relative to that directory. The harness, bridge, and round files will be copied into dist.\n\nPackage.txt will record the pixel-engine.js hash, whether the session is embedded or fetched, and the exit-interview JSON. A shell script at the end of the run will compute these hashes and write the file. The node test runner will not include this check by default.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-da53dc91-32a7-4c50-9fd4-85775b49d147-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^## Task checklist|^- \\[ \\]","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1831,"output_tokens":2193,"cache_read_input_tokens":129152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"c4474275-f942-48ca-a1d5-3725a63dafcb"}
