{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5d5580aa-669d-47e4-8472-53926d1a198e-131","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→alone {\\\"active\\\":false,\\\"seeded\\\":false,\\\"mode\\\":\\\"title\\\"}\\nafter keys {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"call\\\",\\\"focus\\\":0,\\\"canvas\\\":true}\\nhover {\\\"focus\\\":1,\\\"device\\\":\\\"key\\\",\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"ENTER\\\"} point 384,252\\nxbox {\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"CROSS\\\",\\\"device\\\":\\\"pad\\\",\\\"glyphs\\\":\\\"ps\\\"}\\nattract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"attract\\\",\\\"save\\\":null,\\\"settings\\\":null}\\npad attract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"menu\\\",\\\"save\\\":null}\\nslider 1 reset 1\\nseats -1.2,-0.6121271354118106 -> 0.9666666666666665,-2.778793802078477\\nmouse drain 0.7 -> {\\\"r\\\":0.18666666666666698,\\\"done\\\":true}\\n10→touch {\\\"text\\\":\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\",\\\"stick\\\":false,\\\"buttons\\\":[\\\"✕\\\",\\\"Reset\\\",\\\"Done\\\",\\\"⚙\\\"]} mode attract\\nresults mode pause\\npage errors \\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→alone {\\\"active\\\":false,\\\"seeded\\\":false,\\\"mode\\\":\\\"title\\\"}\\nafter keys {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"call\\\",\\\"focus\\\":0,\\\"canvas\\\":true}\\nhover {\\\"focus\\\":1,\\\"device\\\":\\\"key\\\",\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"ENTER\\\"} point 384,252\\nxbox {\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"CROSS\\\",\\\"device\\\":\\\"pad\\\",\\\"glyphs\\\":\\\"ps\\\"}\\nattract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"attract\\\",\\\"save\\\":null,\\\"settings\\\":null}\\npad attract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"menu\\\",\\\"save\\\":null}\\nslider 1 reset 1\\nseats -1.2,-0.6121271354118106 -> 0.9666666666666665,-2.778793802078477\\nmouse drain 0.7 -> {\\\"r\\\":0.18666666666666698,\\\"done\\\":true}\\n10→touch {\\\"text\\\":\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\",\\\"stick\\\":false,\\\"buttons\\\":[\\\"✕\\\",\\\"Reset\\\",\\\"Done\\\",\\\"⚙\\\"]} mode attract\\nresults mode pause\\npage errors \\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/implementer/browser.txt\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"alone {\\\"active\\\":false,\\\"seeded\\\":false,\\\"mode\\\":\\\"title\\\"}\\nafter keys {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"call\\\",\\\"focus\\\":0,\\\"canvas\\\":true}\\nhover {\\\"focus\\\":1,\\\"device\\\":\\\"key\\\",\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"ENTER\\\"} point 384,252\\nxbox {\\\"confirm\\\":\\\"CROSS\\\",\\\"device\\\":\\\"pad\\\",\\\"glyphs\\\":\\\"ps\\\"}\\nattract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"attract\\\",\\\"save\\\":null,\\\"settings\\\":null}\\npad attract {\\\"mode\\\":\\\"menu\\\",\\\"save\\\":null}\\nslider 1 reset 1\\nseats -1.2,-0.6121271354118106 -> 0.9666666666666665,-2.778793802078477\\nmouse drain 0.7 -> {\\\"r\\\":0.18666666666666698,\\\"done\\\":true}\\ntouch {\\\"text\\\":\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\",\\\"stick\\\":false,\\\"buttons\\\":[\\\"✕\\\",\\\"Reset\\\",\\\"Done\\\",\\\"⚙\\\"]} mode attract\\nresults mode pause\\npage errors \\n\",\"total_lines\":12}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"e3326ce5-5d31-48f9-bd8e-997d9b5b59f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_284","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Keyboard focus movement is failing.\n\nArrowDown failed to move focus from 0 to 1 on the call screen. Space and Enter may have left the game in a state that swallowed the key.\n\nEnter and Space worked, so keys are generally functional. The ArrowDown press may be too brief for the engine to register between frames.\n\nThe engine queues fixed-step presses. wasPressed only checks the current render frame. A key pressed after the frame starts should be seen next frame.\n\nThe test reads focus immediately after pressing ArrowDown. The engine may process the key on the next animation frame, so the read happens before the change registers. Enter and Space worked because multiple sequential presses were enough to trigger the menu confirm before the check.\n\nThe fix is to wait for the focus value to change rather than reading it immediately after pressing ArrowDown. Software WebGPU rendering may be too slow, causing quick key presses to be missed between engine polls.\n\nThe engine uses event-driven input rather than polling, so wasPressed should register on the next frame even for brief key presses. The focus read happens before that frame processes the queued key. A 200ms wait after each action should fix this. The hover test also needs review because focus remained at 0 after the failed ArrowDown.\n\nThe second ArrowDown in the hover section successfully moved focus to 1. The mouse move did not change the device key or shift focus to 2.\n\nThe mouse move likely failed for the same reason as the ArrowDown: the engine frame had not yet processed the input before the test evaluated state. The device remained set to key, and focus stayed at 1 from that earlier press. The hover y-coordinate calculation may also be incorrect, so focus would not reach row 2 even if the move were registered.\n\nThe hover y-coordinate math is correct. The target point at 252 pixels maps to row 2, so the focus failure was not caused by a calculation error.\n\nThe xbox test confirmed the pad device was set correctly, but the glyph toggle failed because the test was not on the settings screen. The hover section left focus on the menu, so the pad press did not reach the settings screen where ArrowDown and Enter were meant to open it.\n\nThe first Enter and Space presses confirmed the menu selection, leaving the game in call mode. ArrowDown and Enter then triggered pickCall instead of opening settings. The test sequence must be fixed so that on the menu page, only ArrowDown is used to move focus without confirming into a call.\n\nThe test sequence is being split into two pages. The first page will verify the canvas still draws after repeated Enter and Space presses without asserting focus. The second page will enter the menu, move focus with ArrowDown, hover to row 2, open settings, toggle glyphs with ArrowRight, press pad and key buttons, and wait for confirmations.\n\nA new issue was discovered: pressing the pad button exits attract mode but sets the mode to \"menu\" instead of \"title\". The exitAttract function appears to be setting the wrong mode.\n\nThe pad button press is held during the title frame, so pads.any remains true. The title screen's button handler sees this held state and immediately returns to menu mode. This explains why exitAttract sets the mode to title, but the pad button still triggers a return to menu.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. exitAttract sets swallowed to true, but the pad button remains held across frames. On the next frame, the title screen sees the still-down button and immediately returns to menu mode.\n\nTwo fixes are being considered for the pad button held-state bug. One approach changes the title screen to require an input edge rather than a held button, so the exit-attract press does not trigger an immediate return to menu. The other introduces a latch flag that ignores all pad input for one frame after attract exits.\n\nThe held-pad fix is confirmed: the title screen will ignore a button that remains pressed across frames, so exitAttract no longer triggers an immediate return to menu. The attract start is also protected from accidental re-entry.\n\nThe dev slider test failed because ArrowRight did not change the value. This likely means focus never reached the Dev mode, or Escape paused the game and the subsequent arrow presses were missed. If the game was paused, Enter on Resume returns to op mode, leaving ArrowRight with nothing to nudge.\n\nThe two-pad test passed. Opposite seats moved in opposite directions. The mouse drain test passed. Ray aim works correctly. The touch gate test passed for both the settings gear and attract mode. The attract-after-idle test also passed.\n\nThe results-mode pause check failed. The key sequence did not reach the Win screen. It ended on pause instead. I will add waits and log the mode at each step. I will use waitForFunction to wait for the correct state.\n\nThe Escape key exit from attract mode passed. The pad exit bug is fixed with the ate latch, so exiting attract now correctly returns to title instead of menu. The keyboard focus failure was caused by a race condition and by testing on the call screen rather than the menu, so the test sequence will be restructured. The xbox glyphs test failed because the settings screen was never opened.\n\nThe holdOff latch will be set inside exitAttract so the title screen ignores the held pad button. The test will wait 300ms after the pad press to confirm the mode is title.\n\nA `tap` helper is being drafted to press a key and wait for a predicate via `waitForFunction`. The predicate must be a string because the function gets serialized. This is more reliable than fixed 200ms waits for the dev slider.\n\nA new `until` helper is being drafted to press a key and wait for a predicate via `waitForFunction`. If the key is missed and the predicate times out, it retries up to six times. The helper will return false instead of throwing, so `check()` can record the failure rather than aborting.\n\nThe hover test will wait for the device to switch to mouse after the move. The settings path will navigate from menu focus 0 down to 3, enter, wait for the settings mode, then press right and wait for the glyphs toggle. Retries will be added for missed ArrowDown presses. The title screen will use Space to open the menu, and another Space to confirm the first item into a call. The canvas-draw test will be split into its own page. The dev mode sequence will start by pressing Escape and waiting for pause mode.\n\nThe dev slider test will press ArrowDown four times to reach the fourth option, then Enter to open dev mode, and ArrowRight to nudge the drain multiplier. If any ArrowDown fails to change focus, the wait will throw; that error will be caught so check() can record a clean failure instead of aborting.\n\nThe results path will use the 'e' key for tabs. The title screen test will be split so Enter opens the menu and Space confirms the first item, instead of pressing both keys together. The xbox test will start fresh from the menu page after hover to avoid stale state. The holdOff latch will be inserted in readInput immediately after computing button and moved, before the attract check. The browser() function will be rewritten to fix flaky behavior.\n\nThe holdOff latch will block both held buttons and mouse movement, so the title screen ignores the pad press across frames. The results tab will use the lowercase 'e' key via until(), and devTab must be exposed on app for verification. I also need to check whether Arrow keys on the menu are intercepted by the engine camera.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab07d3c9-72f8-4606-9546-3c0709fded33-132","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js","old_string":"    const button = key || click || right || pads.any;\n    if (this.mode === 'attract' && (button || moved)) {\n      this.exitAttract();\n      return;\n    }","new_string":"    const button = key || click || right || pads.any;\n    if (this.holdOff) {\n      if (button || moved) return;\n      this.holdOff = false;\n    }\n    if (this.mode === 'attract' && (button || moved)) {\n      this.exitAttract();\n      this.holdOff = true;\n      return;\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab07d3c9-72f8-4606-9546-3c0709fded33-133","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/live.mjs","old_string":"async function openPage(context, url) {","new_string":"async function poke(page, key, ready, timeout = 800) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n    await page.keyboard.press(key);\n    if (!ready) {\n      await page.waitForTimeout(150);\n      return true;\n    }\n    try {\n      await page.waitForFunction(ready, { timeout });\n      return true;\n    } catch {\n      /* the frame may have missed a short press */\n    }\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n\nasync function openPage(context, url) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ab07d3c9-72f8-4606-9546-3c0709fded33-134","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/live.mjs","old_string":"    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n    await page.keyboard.press('Space');\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n    await page.keyboard.press('Space');\n    await page.waitForTimeout(200);\n    const afterKeys = await page.evaluate(() => ({\n      mode: window.__GAME__.app.mode,\n      focus: window.__GAME__.app.focus,\n      canvas: !!document.querySelector('canvas'),\n    }));\n    check('keys still draw', afterKeys.canvas && afterKeys.mode !== 'title');\n    note(`after keys ${JSON.stringify(afterKeys)}`);\n\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\n    const focusKey = await page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.focus);\n    check('keyboard moves focus', focusKey === 1);\n    const point = await page.evaluate(() => {\n      const art = window.__GAME__.art;\n      const box = document.querySelector('canvas').getBoundingClientRect();\n      const artY = 74 + 2 * 26;\n      return { x: box.left + box.width * 0.4, y: box.top + (artY / art.h) * box.height };\n    });\n    await page.mouse.move(point.x, point.y);\n    await page.waitForTimeout(150);\n    const hovered = await page.evaluate(() => ({\n      focus: window.__GAME__.app.focus,\n      device: window.__GAME__.prompts.device,\n      confirm: window.__GAME__.prompts.confirm,\n    }));\n    check('hover moves focus', hovered.focus === 2 && hovered.device === 'mouse' && hovered.confirm === 'ENTER');\n    note(`hover ${JSON.stringify(hovered)} point ${point.x},${point.y}`);\n\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowDown');\n    await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowRight');\n    await page.waitForTimeout(100);\n    await pressPad(page, 0, 0, true);\n    await page.waitForTimeout(200);\n    const xbox = await page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.prompts);\n    check('xbox glyphs', xbox.glyphs === 'xbox' && xbox.device === 'pad' && xbox.confirm === 'A');\n    note(`xbox ${JSON.stringify(xbox)}`);\n    await page.keyboard.press('ArrowLeft');\n    await page.waitForTimeout(100);\n    const keyed = await page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.prompts);\n    check('key prompt', keyed.device === 'key' && keyed.confirm === 'ENTER');\n    await context.close();","new_string":"    await poke(page, 'Enter');\n    await poke(page, 'Space');\n    await poke(page, 'Enter');\n    await poke(page, 'Space');\n    const afterKeys = await page.evaluate(() => ({\n      mode: window.__GAME__.app.mode,\n      focus: window.__GAME__.app.focus,\n      canvas: !!document.querySelector('canvas'),\n    }));\n    check('keys still draw', afterKeys.canvas && afterKeys.mode !== 'title');\n    note(`after keys ${JSON.stringify(afterKeys)}`);\n    await context.close();\n\n    const menuCtx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\n    await installPads(menuCtx, 1);\n    const menu = await openPage(menuCtx, fileUrl(root));\n    await poke(menu.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'menu');\n    await poke(menu.page, 'ArrowDown', () => window.__GAME__.app.focus === 1);\n    const focusKey = await menu.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.focus);\n    check('keyboard moves focus', focusKey === 1);\n    const point = await menu.page.evaluate(() => {\n      const art = window.__GAME__.art;\n      const box = document.querySelector('canvas').getBoundingClientRect();\n      const artY = 74 + 2 * 26;\n      return { x: box.left + box.width * 0.4, y: box.top + (artY / art.h) * box.height };\n    });\n    await menu.page.mouse.move(point.x, point.y);\n    let hovered = { focus: focusKey, device: 'key', confirm: 'ENTER' };\n    try {\n      await menu.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__.app.focus === 2 && window.__GAME__.prompts.device === 'mouse', { timeout: 2000 });\n      hovered = await menu.page.evaluate(() => ({\n        focus: window.__GAME__.app.focus,\n        device: window.__GAME__.prompts.device,\n        confirm: window.__GAME__.prompts.confirm,\n      }));\n    } catch {\n      hovered = await menu.page.evaluate(() => ({\n        focus: window.__GAME__.app.focus,\n        device: window.__GAME__.prompts.device,\n        confirm: window.__GAME__.prompts.confirm,\n        pointer: window.__GAME__.app.ctx.input.pointer,\n      }));\n    }\n    check('hover moves focus', hovered.focus === 2 && hovered.device === 'mouse' && hovered.confirm === 'ENTER');\n    note(`hover ${JSON.stringify(hovered)} point ${point.x},${point.y}`);\n\n    await poke(menu.page, 'ArrowDown', () => window.__GAME__.app.focus === 3);\n    await poke(menu.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'settings');\n    await poke(menu.page, 'ArrowRight', () => window.__GAME__.app.settings.glyphs === 'xbox');\n    await pressPad(menu.page, 0, 0, true);\n    try {\n      await menu.page.waitForFunction(() => {\n        const p = window.__GAME__.prompts;\n        return p.glyphs === 'xbox' && p.device === 'pad' && p.confirm === 'A';\n      }, { timeout: 2000 });\n    } catch { /* recorded below */ }\n    const xbox = await menu.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.prompts);\n    check('xbox glyphs', xbox.glyphs === 'xbox' && xbox.device === 'pad' && xbox.confirm === 'A');\n    note(`xbox ${JSON.stringify(xbox)}`);\n    await pressPad(menu.page, 0, 0, false);\n    await poke(menu.page, 'ArrowLeft', () => window.__GAME__.prompts.device === 'key' && window.__GAME__.prompts.confirm === 'ENTER');\n    const keyed = await menu.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.prompts);\n    check('key prompt', keyed.device === 'key' && keyed.confirm === 'ENTER');\n    await menuCtx.close();"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":489,"output_tokens":5681,"cache_read_input_tokens":183552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a56b1713-d45e-4aad-8750-58fa9b4c69f5"}
