mera directly) with an iris transition.\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"- **VIEW:** hitbox overlay (entity circles and ids), Bot Plays (with skill slider), Sim Speed 0.1× to 3×, Frame Step, FPS and sim stats.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"5d4d770f-f8b1-4145-a47c-726adf48abcc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_316","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f27bda67-2577-41af-9f8f-65b573bebde9-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md","offset":390,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f27bda67-2577-41af-9f8f-65b573bebde9-37","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"content tests|standings|buildStandings","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1484,"output_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":83584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"4f435959-193c-4df3-861b-83aa1f33fe95"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f27bda67-2577-41af-9f8f-65b573bebde9-36","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\",\"content_concise\":\"390→  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n400→  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n410→  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n420→  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":390,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  if (info) return runSession(info);       // null: no hub after all, fall through to the normal game\\n}\\nrunStandalone();\\n\\nfunction runSession(info) {\\n  AIHub.on('card', updateCard);            // { left, paused, starting, ready, asked, ... }\\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);       // play begins when AIHub.time() >= 0\\n  AIHub.on('message', onMessage);\\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => retireSeat(id));\\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (AIHub.isHost) finishRound(false); });\\n  AIHub.on('end', stopInputAndSound);      // playMusic(null), stopLoops(), nothing more sent\\n  startHostLoopIfHost();                   // on a timer from AIHub.time(), never from the renderer\\n  if (info.server) { AIHub.ready(); return; }   // ✔ a server copy never starts the engine\\n  startEngineThen(() => AIHub.ready());    // no key press\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **No WebGPU in a session:** `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`. Check `navigator.gpu` before `Engine.start` and show a friendly message outside a session.\\n- **Session rules:** no title, menus, pause, saves, attract or dev mode. Options does nothing. No alert/confirm/prompt, no new tabs, no sockets, no chat. Names come only from `info.players` and are drawn with `hud.text`. Don't use `Math.random` for gameplay; seed the sim with `AIHub.rng('deal')`.\\n- **The card (CardStage):** OR-7 wide shot with one masked figure per player in their seat colour, title, players with READY marks, how to win, controls for this player's device, time left. Answers:\\n  - Enter, ✕ or a tap on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\\n  - △, M or a tap on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`.\\n  - ✔ `ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter')` catches the harness's synthetic key.\\n- **Round choice:** `info.round` cycles the session list: Pile-Up, then trimmed Introit, Lacrimosa and Dies Irae fights (`session: true` stages, ≤ 4 minutes). All tools unlocked, hints on, Reyes's lines on.\\n- **Finish:** when the patient is saved or lost, or at `time-up`:\\n  ```js\\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: groupsByPoints, scores, won: patientSaved, stats, awards });\\n  ```\\n  - Every present player must appear once in `standings`.\\n  - Limits: 6 stats per player (name and text ≤ 16 chars), 3 awards per player (title ≤ 24, detail ≤ 40).\\n  - Awards: STEADIEST HAND, MOST STITCHES, SAVED THE DAY, SLOPPIEST (kindly).\\n\\n### Networking\\n\\n- **Authority:** the host's copy runs the sim on a timer (`setInterval`, catch-up from `AIHub.time()`). A hidden tab must not stall it, and a server copy has no renderer.\\n- **Clients to host:** 15 Hz `AIHub.send({t:'i', n, x, z, tool, use, gift, steady}, { to: AIHub.host, reliable: false })`, always sent, even idle (the harness requires traffic both ways).\\n- **Host to all:** 12 Hz unreliable snapshot, plus 1 Hz reliable keyframe, plus up to 4 Hz reliable event batches (ratings, comm lines, stage changes, sounds).\\n  - That totals at most 17 messages/s against the limit of 20/s (burst 40). Add your own token bucket; the client drops over-limit sends.\\n- **Sizes:** keep unreliable snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (above about 1,200 they fragment and are lost whole). Use fixed-point ints in positional arrays: `[id, kind, x, z, a, b]`. Gel masks are a coarse bitset. Keyframes ≤ 16 KB. Test both at each op's peak.\\n- **Feel:** a client moves its own tip locally at once using the same integrator and corrects gently if it drifts over 1 unit. It plays tool loops, sparks and rumble locally. Everything else renders from interpolated snapshots about 120 ms behind. The view reads a plain state object, whether from a local sim or the network.\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f27bda67-2577-41af-9f8f-65b573bebde9-37","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,