{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_320","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Host leaves void immediately via settle().\n\nThe hostGone flag handles time-up. The 1.5-second window before host leave is too short for a skill-1 bot to win, so the session uses human inputs only. In server mode, the server itself acts as the host.\n\nClients send messages to hub.host. The server sends snaps to all remaining copies. Each copy tracks sent and received counts. The allow() guard returns from the interval entirely when denied. Both client and host paths call allow() before hub.send, so there is no double-charge.\n\nThe message handler receives both data and from, but only data is used. Traffic exists before play starts because the host sends pings early. The sent and received check applies after play begins and after a player is removed. Only remaining copies matter. The server receives client inputs.\n\nThe server counts received messages through stats.received, and clients receive host snaps. The host sends pings every 250 milliseconds before play starts, so dropped packets are unlikely. The host copy uses the host branch of the interval and does not send idle messages.\n\nencodeFast snapshots might exceed the 16384-byte limit and be dropped by the hub or client. That would prevent sent and received counts from incrementing. Pre-start pings are small enough to avoid this, so they should still register.\n\nWebGPU initialization is unlikely to fail because the browser test already passed with identical GPU flags. The real risk is a 20-second ready timeout when five WebGPU contexts start simultaneously under low quality and earlyoom pressure.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-87abe85a-e9cd-4946-bd43-ba4bfafd741a-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/harness.html","offset":360,"limit":45}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1172,"output_tokens":1083,"cache_read_input_tokens":88320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"033cb757-fe9b-42b1-97d1-28ee619f8f23"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-87abe85a-e9cd-4946-bd43-ba4bfafd741a-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"360→$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n370→  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\\n380→ * turns \\\"true\\\".\\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\\n\\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\\nasync function until(test, ms) {\\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\\n    if (test()) return true;\\n    await sleep(50);\\n  }\\n390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\",\"content_concise\":\"360→$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n370→  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\\n380→ * turns \\\"true\\\".\\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\\n\\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\\nasync function until(test, ms) {\\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\\n    if (test()) return true;\\n    await sleep(50);\\n  }\\n390→  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n400→  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/harness.html\",\"offset\":360,\"limit\":45,\"raw_output\":\"$('restart').onclick = () => newRound();\\n$('release').onclick = () => releaseRound();\\n$('timeup').onclick = () => current?.coordinator.timeUp();\\n$('remove').onclick = () => {\\n  const cell = current?.cells.find((c) => c.key === $('who').value);\\n  if (cell) removeCell(cell);\\n};\\n$('hide').onclick = () => {\\n  if (!current) return;\\n  current.hidden = !current.hidden;\\n  $('hide').setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(current.hidden));\\n  (current.cells.find((c) => c.server) ?? current.cells[0])?.bridge.visibility(current.hidden);\\n  log(`host tab ${current.hidden ? 'hidden' : 'shown'}`);\\n};\\nfor (const id of ['latency', 'jitter', 'loss']) $(id).onchange = applyNet;\\n\\n/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n * ?auto=1 — the conformance run. It presses keys inside each frame with\\n * synthetic events while the round plays (the frames must be served from this\\n * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\\n * turns \\\"true\\\".\\n * ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */\\n\\nconst sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));\\nasync function until(test, ms) {\\n  const end = performance.now() + ms;\\n  while (performance.now() < end) {\\n    if (test()) return true;\\n    await sleep(50);\\n  }\\n  return test();\\n}\\n\\nfunction poke(cell, key) {\\n  const doc = cell.frame.contentDocument;\\n  const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\\n  if (!doc || !win) return false;\\n  const target = doc.activeElement && doc.activeElement !== doc.documentElement ? doc.activeElement : doc.body || doc.documentElement;\\n  const init = { key, code: key === ' ' ? 'Space' : key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: win };\\n  target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keydown', init));\\n  setTimeout(() => target.dispatchEvent(new win.KeyboardEvent('keyup', init)), 120);\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nasync function conformance() {\\n\",\"total_lines\":548}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"1f8c73f8-5a17-43e2-b394-2a47a0a40863"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_321","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The keydown event is dispatched on the iframe body and bubbles up.\n\nThe window listener should catch the Enter key. Mode is card because setup runs before ready. A race condition is possible if the engine calls ready before setup.\n\nThe harness sends Enter exactly once after waiting for cardSent. If the game misses that single keypress, the test fails.\n\nThe engine might intercept Enter during the capture phase and stop propagation. Our bubble listener on window should still fire because capture listeners run before the bubble phase.\n\nIf the engine stops propagation during capture on window, the event never reaches the target or bubble phase. Our window listener would not fire.\n\nThe engine's `readCard` method also checks `input.wasPressed('Enter')`. It runs before menu handling when a session exists, so it should answer even if the window listener misses the key.\n\nThe engine's input system should detect the synthetic keydown if it listens on window or document. The PLAN confirms that `wasPressed` catches the harness key, so both the window listener and the engine's `readCard` provide coverage.\n\n`wasPressed` is edge-triggered per frame. The synthetic keydown is recorded immediately, and `readInput` will see it during the next `update()` call. It latches until consumed, so it should register correctly if the update loop runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9b8f475e-b5fa-4eb9-9f36-c116067ab61c-42","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["d585c28e-81f5-4709-834b-79f5bd44ef7b"],"timeout_ms":180000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1605,"output_tokens":1007,"cache_read_input_tokens":89472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"377918f9-9d95-4c83-9bb9-2500ad638dfe"}
