DE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":171,\"content\":\"    if (this.won) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'YOU WIN!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"ctx.hud.text(6, 6, 'LIVES 3', { anchor: 'top-right' });              // anchors: top-left (default), top,\"},{\"line_number\":434,\"content\":\"ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });        //   top-right, left, center, right, bottom-*\"},{\"line_number\":670,\"content\":\"    if (this.clearedAt !== null) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'LEVEL CLEAR!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\"},{\"line_number\":951,\"content\":\"    ctx.hud.text(6, 6, '1-6 LOOKS  T CHUNKY', { anchor: 'bottom-left' });\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":2775,\"content\":\"  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\"},{\"line_number\":3440,\"content\":\"function textureDef(def: T): T\"},{\"line_number\":3473,\"content\":\"function textureMap(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, opts: TextureOptions = {}): DataTexture\"},{\"line_number\":3484,\"content\":\"function textureSheet(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, opts: TextureSheetOptions = {}): TextureSheet\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"f1c1ec86-e8aa-4d34-b7e9-598307897e37"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_332","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `anchor` property on `hud.text` sets screen corner offsets, not text alignment within a box.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-aad2e35a-f6f4-4e3c-8e37-544c1f6b8f76-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md","offset":2770,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1918,"output_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":115968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"fcf74569-6883-4c7b-89ea-49df4f181420"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-aad2e35a-f6f4-4e3c-8e37-544c1f6b8f76-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2770→(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\\n- `visible: boolean`\\n2780→- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\\n- `get height: number`\\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n2790→### type HudAnchor\\n\\n```ts\\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\\n```\\n\\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\\n\\n### type HudColor\\n\\n2800→```ts\\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\\n```\\n\\n### interface HudOptions\\n\\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\\n2810→\\n### hudPlace()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\\n```\\n\\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\\n\\n2820→## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\\n\\n### addModelColliders()\\n\\n```ts\",\"content_concise\":\"2770→(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\\n- `visible: boolean`\\n2780→- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\\n- `get height: number`\\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\\n- `dispose(): void`\\n\\n2790→### type HudAnchor\\n\\n```ts\\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\\n```\\n\\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\\n\\n### type HudColor\\n\\n2800→```ts\\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\\n```\\n\\n### interface HudOptions\\n\\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\\n2810→\\n### hudPlace()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\\n```\\n\\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\\n\\n2820→## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\\n\\n### addModelColliders()\\n\\n```ts\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/API.md\",\"offset\":2770,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\\n\\n  ctx.hud.clear();\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\\n\\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\\n- 