{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_335","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f7c8f28a-930f-4464-b197-ca317a85bf0a-69","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/ui/hud.js","offset":1,"limit":37}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":412,"output_tokens":100,"cache_read_input_tokens":120448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"0ba9204a-8358-4967-9485-f248b9bc5b17"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f7c8f28a-930f-4464-b197-ca317a85bf0a-69","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** HUD drawing. The engine font uppercases; keep every glyph in its set. */\\n\\nimport { ABOUT_FIELDS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK } from '../content/about.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\nimport { TOOLS } from '../input/devices.js';\\nimport { DEFAULTS } from '../core/config.js';\\n\\nexport const ROW = 26;\\n\\n10→const INK = {\\n  x: 'white',\\n  o: 'sand',\\n};\\n\\nconst GLYPH = {\\n  CROSS: ['..x..', '..x..', 'xxxxx', '..x..', '..x..'],\\n  A: ['.xxx.', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x...x', 'x...x'],\\n  ENTER: ['xxxxx', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x....', 'x....'],\\n};\\n20→\\nexport function clean(value) {\\n  return String(value ?? '')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2014', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2013', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2026', '...')\\n    .replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9 .,;:!?\\\\-+%/()[\\\\]'\\\"#&*=<>]/g, '');\\n}\\n\\nexport function rowTop(index) {\\n30→  return 74 + index * ROW;\\n}\\n\\nfunction glyphBox(hud, x, y, name) {\\n  const rows = GLYPH[name] || GLYPH.ENTER;\\n  hud.sprite(x, y, rows, INK, { scale: 2 });\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** HUD drawing. The engine font uppercases; keep every glyph in its set. */\\n\\nimport { ABOUT_FIELDS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK } from '../content/about.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\nimport { TOOLS } from '../input/devices.js';\\nimport { DEFAULTS } from '../core/config.js';\\n\\nexport const ROW = 26;\\n\\n10→const INK = {\\n  x: 'white',\\n  o: 'sand',\\n};\\n\\nconst GLYPH = {\\n  CROSS: ['..x..', '..x..', 'xxxxx', '..x..', '..x..'],\\n  A: ['.xxx.', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x...x', 'x...x'],\\n  ENTER: ['xxxxx', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x....', 'x....'],\\n};\\n20→\\nexport function clean(value) {\\n  return String(value ?? '')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2014', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2013', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2026', '...')\\n    .replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9 .,;:!?\\\\-+%/()[\\\\]'\\\"#&*=<>]/g, '');\\n}\\n\\nexport function rowTop(index) {\\n30→  return 74 + index * ROW;\\n}\\n\\nfunction glyphBox(hud, x, y, name) {\\n  const rows = GLYPH[name] || GLYPH.ENTER;\\n  hud.sprite(x, y, rows, INK, { scale: 2 });\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/ui/hud.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":37,\"raw_output\":\"/** HUD drawing. The engine font uppercases; keep every glyph in its set. */\\n\\nimport { ABOUT_FIELDS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFORMATION, TESTING_FEEDBACK } from '../content/about.js';\\nimport { CAST } from '../content/story.js';\\nimport { TOOLS } from '../input/devices.js';\\nimport { DEFAULTS } from '../core/config.js';\\n\\nexport const ROW = 26;\\n\\nconst INK = {\\n  x: 'white',\\n  o: 'sand',\\n};\\n\\nconst GLYPH = {\\n  CROSS: ['..x..', '..x..', 'xxxxx', '..x..', '..x..'],\\n  A: ['.xxx.', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x...x', 'x...x'],\\n  ENTER: ['xxxxx', 'x...x', 'xxxxx', 'x....', 'x....'],\\n};\\n\\nexport function clean(value) {\\n  return String(value ?? '')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2014', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2013', '-')\\n    .replaceAll('\\\\u2026', '...')\\n    .replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9 .,;:!?\\\\-+%/()[\\\\]'\\\"#&*=<>]/g, '');\\n}\\n\\nexport function rowTop(index) {\\n  return 74 + index * ROW;\\n}\\n\\nfunction glyphBox(hud, x, y, name) {\\n  const rows = GLYPH[name] || GLYPH.ENTER;\\n  hud.sprite(x, y, rows, INK, { scale: 2 });\\n}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":240}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"7adfa4f5-3be3-41fe-b0da-ede59451ff01"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_336","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fixing anchor offsets for the title screen. The art is 480x270, so its center point is 240, 135.\n\nWorking out the exact y offset for the title screen. The text should sit near y=48, so the offset is -87 from the center point. Checking whether hudPlace uses top-left corner placement or centers the element on the anchor.\n\nCenter anchor places the element's center at screen center plus offset. The function returns top-left coordinates. Text is centered on the anchor point. drawTitle currently only receives width, so height must be passed to compute the offset. The title will scale to 2 and sit at visual y ~ 36 from the top.\n\nTagline offset is -57. Glyph and PRESS offset is -11. EKG uses absolute top-left coordinates, so it stays at y=170. The PRESS text will sit slightly right of the glyph.\n\nSwitching to top-left placement for the title screen. The glyph will sit at absolute x=204, y=116. Text will be centered manually using measure() instead of relying on center or top-right anchors with absolute coordinates.\n\nTitle text is centered at x=91. Tagline sits at y=72. Glyph box and PRESS text are placed at x=204 and y=112. EKG renders at y=168. The clock text is being prepared.\n\nThe clock text is centered at the top of the screen. The Composure indicator will anchor to the top-right corner. The exact direction of positive x and y offsets from that corner is being determined.\n\nThe top-right anchor places the text's right edge 8 pixels from the right screen edge and 4 pixels from the top. Positive x moves inward from the right, while positive y moves downward from the top. The composure indicator will be placed at (8, 4) with scale 1. Vitals text sits at x=8, scale 2.\n\nThe card title is centered at y=16. The card line fits at x=20. The results rank at x=410 is within bounds.\n\nThe wheel HUD uses absolute top-left coordinates and looks correct. The EKG line at y=170 sits in the lower-middle of the screen, so it may cross through characters behind the title. That is acceptable if the title remains fixed above them.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a3089f4-56d6-436d-82a8-38f4a797224f-70","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/live.mjs","offset":280,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":493,"output_tokens":2379,"cache_read_input_tokens":120832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"20e68dc8-e2f9-461f-8178-45282e7f3cd3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9a3089f4-56d6-436d-82a8-38f4a797224f-70","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"280→    const phone = devices['Pixel 7'];\\n    const touch = await browser.newContext({ ...phone });\\n    const touchPage = await openPage(touch, fileUrl(root));\\n    await touchPage.page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n    const gate = await touchPage.page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      text: document.getElementById('touch-gate')?.textContent || '',\\n      stick: !!document.querySelector('[data-t=\\\"stick\\\"]'),\\n      buttons: [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].map((b) => b.textContent),\\n    }));\\n    await touchPage.page.waitForTimeout(11000);\\n290→    const phoneMode = await touchPage.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.mode);\\n    check('touch gate', gate.text === 'Controller or keyboard required' && gate.stick === false && phoneMode === 'attract');\\n    check('touch settings', gate.buttons.some((t) => t && t.includes('\\\\u2699')));\\n    note(`touch ${JSON.stringify(gate)} mode ${phoneMode}`);\\n    await touch.close();\\n\\n    const shot = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n    const shotPage = await openPage(shot, fileUrl(root));\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(600);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'title.png') });\\n300→    await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'scene=night'), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'story');\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'bust.png') });\\n    for (const [op, arena] of ARENAS) {\\n      await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, `op=${op}&seed=1&god=1&hold=1&bot=0`), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n      await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim);\\n      await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, `arena-${arena}.png`) });\\n    }\\n310→    await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'op=op1&seed=1&bot=0&hold=1'), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim);\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'hud.png') });\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Escape', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'pause');\\n    for (let i = 1; i <= 4; i++) await poke(shotPage.page, 'ArrowDown', (n) => window.__GAME__.app.focus === n, i);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'dev');\\n    for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) await poke(shotPage.page, 'e', (n) => window.__GAME__.app.devTab === n, i);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'ArrowDown', () => window.__GAME__.app.focus === 1);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'results');\\n320→    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n    const rankMode = await shotPage.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.mode);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'results.png') });\\n    check('results stamp screen', rankMode === 'results');\\n    note(`results mode ${rankMode}`);\\n    note(`page errors ${errors.join(' | ')}`);\\n    check('browser page errors', errors.length === 0);\\n    await shot.close();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n330→    writeFileSync(join(SCRATCH, 'browser.txt'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function launch(root, check) {\\n  mkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\n  const browser = await browserApp();\\n  const runs = [];\\n  try {\\n    for (let n = 1; n <= 2; n++) {\\n340→      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n      const page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err)));\\n      await page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'op=op1&seed=1&bot=0&hold=1'), { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 60000 });\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim, { timeout: 45000 });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(600);\\n      const state = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const g = window.__GAME__;\\n        const eng = g.engine;\\n350→        const framing = eng.renderer ? eng.renderer.framing : null;\\n        const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n        const before = g.sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p1');\\n        const r0 = before ? before.r : null;\\n        const done0 = before ? !!before.done : null;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < 45; i++) g.act({ tool: 'drain', place: true, x: -3.1, z: -1.1, use: true, seat: 0 });\\n        const after = g.sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p1');\\n        return {\\n          music: g.music,\\n360→          fingerprint: g.app.fingerprint(),\\n          r0,\\n          r1: after ? after.r : null,\\n          done0,\\n          done: after ? after.done : null,\\n          framing,\\n          canvas: { w: rect.width, h: rect.height },\\n          view: { w: window.innerWidth, h: window.innerHeight },\\n          errors: (eng.errors || []).slice(0, 6),\\n          gpu: eng.renderer && eng.renderer.gpuErrors ? eng.renderer.gpuErrors.slice(0, 6) : [],\\n370→          active: window.AIHub ? window.AIHub.active : null,\\n          seeded: window.AIHub ? window.AIHub.seeded : null,\\n        };\\n      });\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, `launch-${n}.png`) });\\n      const mean = execFileSync('magick', [join(SCRATCH, `launch-${n}.png`), '-format', '%[fx:mean]', 'info:'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim();\\n      state.mean = Number(mean);\\n      state.pageErrors = errors;\\n      runs.push(state);\\n      await context.close();\\n380→    }\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n  const lines = runs.map((run, i) => `run ${i + 1}\\\\n${JSON.stringify(run, null, 2)}`).join('\\\\n');\\n  writeFileSync(join(SCRATCH, 'launch.txt'), lines + '\\\\n');\\n  const a = runs[0];\\n  const b = runs[1];\\n  const cover = (run) => run.canvas.w >= run.view.w - 2 && run.canvas.h >= run.view.h - 2;\\n  const ox = (run) => {\\n390→    const f = run.framing || {};\\n    return (f.offsetX || 0) === 0 && (f.offsetY || 0) === 0;\\n  };\\n  check('launch no page errors', runs.every((run) => run.pageErrors.length === 0 && run.errors.length === 0 && run.gpu.length === 0));\\n  check('launch music 0.1', runs.every((run) => Math.abs(run.music - 0.1) < 0.001));\\n  check('launch fill', runs.every((run) => cover(run) && ox(run)));\\n  check('launch painted', runs.every((run) => run.mean > 0.02));\\n  check('launch drain', runs.every((run) => run.done0 === false && (run.done === true || (run.r1 != null && run.r1 < run.r0 - 0.05))));\\n  check('launch agree', a.fingerprint === b.fingerprint && a.r1 === b.r1);\\n  check('launch alone', runs.every((run) => run.active === false && run.seeded !== true));\",\"content_concise\":\"280→    const phone = devices['Pixel 7'];\\n    const touch = await browser.newContext({ ...phone });\\n    const touchPage = await openPage(touch, fileUrl(root));\\n    await touchPage.page.waitForTimeout(500);\\n    const gate = await touchPage.page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      text: document.getElementById('touch-gate')?.textContent || '',\\n      stick: !!document.querySelector('[data-t=\\\"stick\\\"]'),\\n      buttons: [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].map((b) => b.textContent),\\n    }));\\n    await touchPage.page.waitForTimeout(11000);\\n290→    const phoneMode = await touchPage.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.mode);\\n    check('touch gate', gate.text === 'Controller or keyboard required' && gate.stick === false && phoneMode === 'attract');\\n    check('touch settings', gate.buttons.some((t) => t && t.includes('\\\\u2699')));\\n    note(`touch ${JSON.stringify(gate)} mode ${phoneMode}`);\\n    await touch.close();\\n\\n    const shot = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n    const shotPage = await openPage(shot, fileUrl(root));\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(600);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'title.png') });\\n300→    await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'scene=night'), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'story');\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'bust.png') });\\n    for (const [op, arena] of ARENAS) {\\n      await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, `op=${op}&seed=1&god=1&hold=1&bot=0`), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n      await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim);\\n      await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(400);\\n      await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, `arena-${arena}.png`) });\\n    }\\n310→    await shotPage.page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'op=op1&seed=1&bot=0&hold=1'), { waitUntil: 'load' });\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim);\\n    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'hud.png') });\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Escape', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'pause');\\n    for (let i = 1; i <= 4; i++) await poke(shotPage.page, 'ArrowDown', (n) => window.__GAME__.app.focus === n, i);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'dev');\\n    for (let i = 1; i <= 3; i++) await poke(shotPage.page, 'e', (n) => window.__GAME__.app.devTab === n, i);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'ArrowDown', () => window.__GAME__.app.focus === 1);\\n    await poke(shotPage.page, 'Enter', () => window.__GAME__.app.mode === 'results');\\n320→    await shotPage.page.waitForTimeout(300);\\n    const rankMode = await shotPage.page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.app.mode);\\n    await shotPage.page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, 'results.png') });\\n    check('results stamp screen', rankMode === 'results');\\n    note(`results mode ${rankMode}`);\\n    note(`page errors ${errors.join(' | ')}`);\\n    check('browser page errors', errors.length === 0);\\n    await shot.close();\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n330→    writeFileSync(join(SCRATCH, 'browser.txt'), log.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport async function launch(root, check) {\\n  mkdirSync(SCRATCH, { recursive: true });\\n  const browser = await browserApp();\\n  const runs = [];\\n  try {\\n    for (let n = 1; n <= 2; n++) {\\n340→      const context = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 960, height: 540 } });\\n      const page = await context.newPage();\\n      const errors = [];\\n      page.on('pageerror', (err) => errors.push(String(err)));\\n      await page.goto(fileUrl(root, 'op=op1&seed=1&bot=0&hold=1'), { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 60000 });\\n      await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.sim, { timeout: 45000 });\\n      await page.waitForTimeout(600);\\n      const state = await page.evaluate(() => {\\n        const g = window.__GAME__;\\n        const eng = g.engine;\\n350→        const framing = eng.renderer ? eng.renderer.framing : null;\\n        const canvas = document.querySelector('canvas');\\n        const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n        const before = g.sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p1');\\n        const r0 = before ? before.r : null;\\n        const done0 = before ? !!before.done : null;\\n        for (let i = 0; i < 45; i++) g.act({ tool: 'drain', place: true, x: -3.1, z: -1.1, use: true, seat: 0 });\\n        const after = g.sim.entities.find((e) => e.id === 'p1');\\n        return {\\n          music: g.music,\\n360→          fingerprint: g.app.fingerprint(),\\n          r0,\\n          r1: after ? after.r : null,\\n          done0,\\n          done: after ? after.done : null,\\n          framing,\\n          canvas: { w: rect.width, h: rect.height },\\n          view: { w: window.innerWidth, h: window.innerHeight },\\n          errors: (eng.errors || []).slice(0, 6),\\n          gpu: eng.renderer && eng.renderer.gpuErrors ? eng.renderer.gpuErrors.slice(0, 6) : [],\\n370→          active: window.AIHub ? window.AIHub.active : null,\\n          seeded: window.AIHub ? window.AIHub.seeded : null,\\n        };\\n      });\\n      await page.screenshot({ path: join(SCRATCH, `launch-${n}.png`) });\\n      const mean = execFileSync('magick', [join(SCRATCH, `launch-${n}.png`), '-format', '%[fx:mean]', 'info:'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim();\\n      state.mean = Number(mean);\\n      state.pageErrors = errors;\\n      runs.push(state);\\n      await context.close();\\n380→    }\\n  } finally {\\n    await browser.close();\\n  }\\n  const lines = runs.map((run, i) => `run ${i + 1}\\\\n${JSON.stringify(run, null, 2)}`).join('\\\\n');\\n  writeFileSync(join(SCRATCH, 'launch.txt'), lines + '\\\\n');\\n  const a = runs[0];\\n  const b = runs[1];\\n  const cover = (run) => run.canvas.w >= run.view.w - 2 && run.canvas.h >= run.view.h - 2;\\n  const ox = (run) => {\\n390→    const f = run.framing || {};\\n    return (f.offsetX || 0) === 0 && (f.offsetY || 0) === 0;\\n  };\\n  check('launch no page errors', runs.every((run) => run.pageErrors.length === 0 && run.errors.length === 0 && run.gpu.length === 0));\\n  check('launch music 0.1', runs.every((run) => Math.abs(run.music - 0.1) < 0.001));\\n  check('launch fill', runs.every((run) => cover(run) && ox(run)));\\n  check('launch painted', runs.every((run) => run.mean > 0.02));\\n  check('launch drain', runs.every((run) => run.done0 === false && (run.done === true || (run.r1 != null && run.r1 < run.r0 - 0.05))));\\n  check('launch agree', a.fingerprint === b.fingerprint && a.r1 =