{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5b905c69-d1eb-46f2-9864-9c09af609057-89","content":"{\"type\":\"TaskOutput\",\"Result\":{\"task_id\":\"a823d3cb-ccb0-45d9-9ead-17046fe8dbb8\",\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040 && PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 node tests/run.mjs browser\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"exit_code\":0,\"started\":\"2026-11-05T07:55:22Z\",\"ended\":\"2026-11-05T07:56:31Z\",\"duration_secs\":69.354502753,\"output\":\"(node:65662) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n16 passed, 0 failed\\n\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/terminal/call-90e8078e-8725-434b-9939-75490c4367d5-54.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"truncation_hint\":\"[truncated - use read_file on output_file for full content]\",\"raw_output_bytes\":184}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"9dd92e05-7009-4ffb-b561-e0a1af44eb4b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_347","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The browser suite passed all 16 tests.\n\nThe browser screenshots were overwritten with the old HUD. Rebuilding is required to refresh them and confirm the fixes. The plan is to rebuild, rerun browser, then launch, then hub.\n\nThe node suite will be rerun and saved to tests.txt before the browser test. This avoids memory pressure from running both suites together.\n\nThe browser suite now takes about 70 seconds. The node suite and browser will run in one sequential command to save memory. Afterward I will inspect title.png, hud.png, and audio.txt before launching. I also need to check whether the testing counts should be updated.\n\nFive real bugs were confirmed: hover fighting keyboard focus, HUD anchor clipping title and clock, shown vitals stuck at zero, stats payload shape, and pad confirm toggling glyphs. The pad confirm issue is a test bug, not a game bug. These findings will be recorded in the testing feedback.\n\nThe About/testing feedback currently lists six specific bugs and seven total issues. Additional findings from this session include a session embed newline build bug, a launch drain check false pass, tool labels overlapping, hover failing to detect absolute mouse moves, held pad buttons advancing the title after attract, and HUD anchors placing the title and clock off screen.\n\nThe existing seven-issue count was already accurate. The two syringe assertions were test bugs, not game bugs. The honest total remains seven.\n\nThe About/testing feedback will be updated to include the three newly caught game bugs: HUD anchor offsets, shown vitals stuck at zero, and finish stats shape. Earlier shell bugs are excluded from this continuation.\n\nThe new HUD bugs are serious but not game-breaking. The original four critical issues remain unchanged.\n\nThe total issue count will be updated to 10, with the four critical items unchanged. about.js must be edited before the final rebuild so the bundled HTML reflects the new numbers. The exit interview will also be updated to match.\n\nThe in-game About page truncates feedback lines to 57 characters. The tests only verify that fields are present, not that the full text fits. The JSON stores the complete answers.\n\nThe in-game About page is truncated to eight lines of 57 characters each. The four long testing feedback paragraphs will be unreadable there. This conflicts with the requirement that every field and question must display fully.\n\nThe About page can fit roughly eleven lines, not eight. Each testing answer will be word-wrapped into 57-character segments so the full feedback is visible without truncation.\n\nThe About page currently displays only eight of fourteen source fields. Tightening the line spacing to eleven pixels would fit all fourteen fields and the wrapped testing feedback on a single page.\n\nLine spacing will be set to twelve pixels so all fourteen source fields fit on the About page. This leaves room for the footer and keeps the text readable.\n\nAbout page line spacing is being tightened to eleven pixels starting at y=40. Feedback answers will be wrapped to fifty-four characters so the full text fits without truncation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-87ae68ed-f7f6-4936-a755-2cd27e632de2-90","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040 && node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { ABOUT_FIELDS, TESTING_FEEDBACK, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK } from \"./src/content/about.js\";\nfunction wrap(s, n=54) {\n  const words = s.split(/\\s+/);\n  const lines = [];\n  let cur = \"\";\n  for (const w of words) {\n    const next = cur ? cur + \" \" + w : w;\n    if (next.length > n) { if (cur) lines.push(cur); cur = w; }\n    else cur = next;\n  }\n  if (cur) lines.push(cur);\n  return lines;\n}\nconst pages = [\n  ABOUT_FIELDS.map(([k,v]) => k + \": \" + v),\n  TESTING_FEEDBACK,\n  ENGINE_FEEDBACK,\n  PROMPT_FEEDBACK,\n];\nfor (const [i, page] of pages.entries()) {\n  const lines = page.flatMap((row) => wrap(row));\n  console.log(\"page\", i, \"blocks\", page.length, \"lines\", lines.length, \"longest\", Math.max(...lines.map(l => l.length)));\n}\n'","description":"Count wrapped About page lines"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":710,"output_tokens":2750,"cache_read_input_tokens":141312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"85a59ba9-a1cd-46aa-a984-04388c7e6cf2"}
