{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_351","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking PLAN section 13 hub URLs against the hub test and reviewing session client send size.\n\nChecking encodeFast size and host snapshot send limits for protocol issues. Reviewing game.js server path bugs before the hub. Confirmed client `allow` returns skip nothing important, host finish stats are correct, and card enter handles ready responses properly. Noted that swallowed encodeFast errors could block snapshots while pings still send.\n\nServer ready() waits for welcome before acting. Clients start four WebGPU contexts within the 20-second budget. The server interval sends pings immediately. createOp uses a seeded random generator.\n\nVerifying createOp uses its own RNG rather than Math.random. Shared-world gameplay does not require AIHub.seeded checks. The interval catch block prevents page errors from reaching the window.\n\nbeginOp must not throw because hub.fail would register a protocol error. I will verify SESSION_OPS and createOp are safe. The max snapshot size test passes. I am checking docs/AUTHORING.md, title-roll.json, and whether PROGRESS should be written after verification.\n\nHub tests may take up to twelve minutes. I will start them only after browser screenshots look good. The client send logic is correct: non-hosts return before the host branch, and hosts send pings instead of inputs. Some scenarios allow five percent message loss.\n\nBridge traffic counts may include attempted sends before loss, but five percent loss over many packets should still leave received traffic positive. I will check bridge stats to confirm dropped messages are counted. I am waiting for the browser command to finish and will draft the exit interview by re-reading about.js. I will also check TASK.md for the HTML filename location.\n\nChecking the pixel-engine hash method. The build script embeds session data correctly. I will verify the session bytes after building. A potential bug in drawAbout silently drops lines when y exceeds h minus twenty. The about page is not captured in browser screenshots.\n\nI will verify the about page visually after the main browser test finishes. A short Playwright script can open the about page without another full browser run.\n\nI will not add an extra about-page screenshot to the current browser run. The verification checklist already covers title, arenas, bust, HUD, and results.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ddbdf47d-6421-4fd9-9907-2dbf407f0cba-96","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["f86fd56c-1cc3-4141-9aef-c3fc681376bc"],"timeout_ms":120000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":967,"output_tokens":1447,"cache_read_input_tokens":147584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"e87a5328-7de4-4dfc-987a-e7eaec26523e"}
