 Add story scenes, gibberish voices, music, results, and saves so episodes 1–3 play through.\\n- [ ] Add title, menus, last-device prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode sliders, attract mode, the touch gate, and About pages.\\n- [ ] Add the remaining operations, The Second Look, all strains, and the campaign playthrough test.\\n- [ ] Add couch Consult, then the hub session, card, and net code; run all five harness scenarios.\\n50→- [ ] Tune to the balance table, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, emit the root HTML, and save a green `node tests/run.mjs` log plus the two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"42→## Task checklist\\n- [x] Download the kit and hub files, create the named dev folder, boot an empty scene from `file://`, and add the test runner plus the fresh-profile music default of 0.1.\\n- [x] Implement the pure sim and Operation 1 (drain, forceps, suture, gel, syringe) with the tissue view, hand, and HUD; test those tools.\\n- [x] Add scalpel, laser, scanner, operations 2 and 3, Code Blue, The Quiet, and the bot; assert idle-fail and skill-0.7 clear.\\n- [x] Add story scenes, gibberish voices, music, results, and saves so episodes 1–3 play through.\\n- [ ] Add title, menus, last-device prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode sliders, attract mode, the touch gate, and About pages.\\n- [ ] Add the remaining operations, The Second Look, all strains, and the campaign playthrough test.\\n- [ ] Add couch Consult, then the hub session, card, and net code; run all five harness scenarios.\\n50→- [ ] Tune to the balance table, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, emit the root HTML, and save a green `node tests/run.mjs` log plus the two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":42,\"limit\":10,\"raw_output\":\"## Task checklist\\n- [x] Download the kit and hub files, create the named dev folder, boot an empty scene from `file://`, and add the test runner plus the fresh-profile music default of 0.1.\\n- [x] Implement the pure sim and Operation 1 (drain, forceps, suture, gel, syringe) with the tissue view, hand, and HUD; test those tools.\\n- [x] Add scalpel, laser, scanner, operations 2 and 3, Code Blue, The Quiet, and the bot; assert idle-fail and skill-0.7 clear.\\n- [x] Add story scenes, gibberish voices, music, results, and saves so episodes 1–3 play through.\\n- [ ] Add title, menus, last-device prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode sliders, attract mode, the touch gate, and About pages.\\n- [ ] Add the remaining operations, The Second Look, all strains, and the campaign playthrough test.\\n- [ ] Add couch Consult, then the hub session, card, and net code; run all five harness scenarios.\\n- [ ] Tune to the balance table, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, emit the root HTML, and save a green `node tests/run.mjs` log plus the two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":56}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-16195d61-cb47-4fa7-b5e9-2e674da8b21c-110","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Authoring The Second Opinion Clinic\\n\\nThe operation sim is plain data. A new case is an object in `src/content/ops.js`. A new scene is an object in `src/content/story.js`. The bot plays any entity `toolFor` understands, so a case does not need its own script.\\n\\n## Add an operation\\n\\nPush an object onto `OPS` in `src/content/ops.js`.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key (`op11`). `n` is its story number. `title`, `patient`, `age`, `job`, `hook`, and `objective` are the briefing lines.\\n10→- `arena` is one of `forearm`, `stomach`, `ferry`, `bone`, `liver`, `kidney`, `lung`, `heart`, `chest`, `spine`. The view colours that name.\\n- `time` is seconds. `vitals` is `{ start, drain }` or `start` as an array when there are several tables. `doses` is the syringe count.\\n- `tools` lists the tools this case unlocks. The eight hand tools are scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, syringe, gel, laser, and scanner. Dressing is a close-up tool the sim already knows.\\n- `gifts` is `quiet`, `look`, or both. Leave it empty when the case unlocks a gift on a stage instead.\\n- `par` is the skill-1 bot score on seed 1. Measure it with `node tests/run.mjs cal` and paste that integer. Do not lower it to make a rank easier.\\n- `stages` is an array. Each stage has `say` (one HUD line) and `spawn` (entity specs). Optional `strain` starts a named strain. Optional `codeblue` or `massage` runs that beat. A stage clears when its required entities are done, or when the strain says so.\\n- Entity specs are `{ id, kind, x, z, ... }`. Kinds include pool, hook, wound, gel, polyp, cyst, fragment, plate, eye, tumor, core, pore, magnet, and dressing. `hidden` and `hiddenBy` keep a piece under another. `table` sends it to another table.\\n- `follow` and `reyes` are rank lines: `{ S, A, B, C }`.\\n- Couch seats come from the Consult screen. Set `partner: true` only when a second surgeon is part of the case.\\n\\n20→Run `node tests/run.mjs sim` after the new case. Idle input must lose. The skill-0.7 bot must clear it.\\n\\n## Add a scene\\n\\nPush an object onto `SCENES` in `src/content/story.js`, in play order.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key. `set` is the room name the busts stand in. `title` is the heading.\\n- `op` is an operation id, or omit it for a scene that ends the night.\\n- `lines` is 8 to 16 rows. Each row is `{ who, say }`. `who` is a cast id. `say` is one line, at most 57 characters, using only letters, digits, and `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >`. The HUD uppercases it. Write `...` with three dots.\\n\\n30→The campaign runner walks `SCENES` from first to last and writes the save.\\n\\n## Add a strain\\n\\nAdd a branch in `src/sim/strains.js`.\\n\\n- `startStrain(sim, name)` spawns the strain's pieces and sets `sim.strain`.\\n- `tickStrains(sim, dt)` moves it. Call the existing note helpers (`noteEyeLaser`, `noteSob`, `notePlate`) from the tool that hits the piece.\\n- A stage lists `strain: 'your-name'`. The stage clears when `sim.flags.strainDead` is set.\\n- Keep the strain's numbers in `src/core/config.js` (`strainSpeed`, `strainHp`) so Dev Mode can slide them.\\n40→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Authoring The Second Opinion Clinic\\n\\nThe operation sim is plain data. A new case is an object in `src/content/ops.js`. A new scene is an object in `src/content/story.js`. The bot plays any entity `toolFor` understands, so a case does not need its own script.\\n\\n## Add an operation\\n\\nPush an object onto `OPS` in `src/content/ops.js`.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key (`op11`). `n` is its story number. `title`, `patient`, `age`, `job`, `hook`, and `objective` are the briefing lines.\\n10→- `arena` is one of `forearm`, `stomach`, `ferry`, `bone`, `liver`, `kidney`, `lung`, `heart`, `chest`, `spine`. The view colours that name.\\n- `time` is seconds. `vitals` is `{ start, drain }` or `start` as an array when there are several tables. `doses` is the syringe count.\\n- `tools` lists the tools this case unlocks. The eight hand tools are scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, syringe, gel, laser, and scanner. Dressing is a close-up tool the sim already knows.\\n- `gifts` is `quiet`, `look`, or both. Leave it empty when the case unlocks a gift on a stage instead.\\n- `par` is the skill-1 bot score on seed 1. Measure it with `node tests/run.mjs cal` and paste that integer. Do not lower it to make a rank easier.\\n- `stages` is an array. Each stage has `say` (one HUD line) and `spawn` (entity specs). Optional `strain` starts a named strain. Optional `codeblue` or `massage` runs that beat. A stage clears when its required entities are done, or when the strain says so.\\n- Entity specs are `{ id, kind, x, z, ... }`. Kinds include pool, hook, wound, gel, polyp, cyst, fragment, plate, eye, tumor, core, pore, magnet, and dressing. `hidden` and `hiddenBy` keep a piece under another. `table` sends it to another table.\\n- `follow` and `reyes` are rank lines: `{ S, A, B, C }`.\\n- Couch seats come from the Consult screen. Set `partner: true` only when a second surgeon is part of the case.\\n\\n20→Run `node tests/run.mjs sim` after the new case. Idle input must lose. The skill-0.7 bot must clear it.\\n\\n## Add a scene\\n\\nPush an object onto `SCENES` in `src/content/story.js`, in play order.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key. `set` is the room name the busts stand in. `title` is the heading.\\n- `op` is an operation id, or omit it for a scene that ends the night.\\n- `lines` is 8 to 16 rows. Each row is `{ who, say }`. `who` is a cast id. `say` is one line, at most 57 characters, using only letters, digits, and `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >`. The HUD uppercases it. Write `...` with three dots.\\n\\n30→The campaign runner walks `SCENES` from first to last and writes the save.\\n\\n## Add a strain\\n\\nAdd a branch in `src/sim/strains.js`.\\n\\n- `startStrain(sim, name)` spawns the strain's pieces and sets `sim.strain`.\\n- `tickStrains(sim, dt)` moves it. Call the existing note helpers (`noteEyeLaser`, `noteSob`, `notePlate`) from the tool that hits the piece.\\n- A stage lists `strain: 'your-name'`. The stage clears when `sim.flags.strainDead` is set.\\n- Keep the strain's numbers in `src/core/config.js` (`strainSpeed`, `strainHp`) so Dev Mode can slide them.\\n40→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/docs/AUTHORING.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Authoring The Second Opinion Clinic\\n\\nThe operation sim is plain data. A new case is an object in `src/content/ops.js`. A new scene is an object in `src/content/story.js`. The bot plays any entity `toolFor` understands, so a case does not need its own script.\\n\\n## Add an operation\\n\\nPush an object onto `OPS` in `src/content/ops.js`.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key (`op11`). `n` is its story number. `title`, `patient`, `age`, `job`, `hook`, and `objective` are the briefing lines.\\n- `arena` is one of `forearm`, `stomach`, `ferry`, `bone`, `liver`, `kidney`, `lung`, `heart`, `chest`, `spine`. The view colours that name.\\n- `time` is seconds. `vitals` is `{ start, drain }` or `start` as an array when there are several tables. `doses` is the syringe count.\\n- `tools` lists the tools this case unlocks. The eight hand tools are scalpel, forceps, suture, drain, syringe, gel, laser, and scanner. Dressing is a close-up tool the sim already knows.\\n- `gifts` is `quiet`, `look`, or both. Leave it empty when the case unlocks a gift on a stage instead.\\n- `par` is the skill-1 bot score on seed 1. Measure it with `node tests/run.mjs cal` and paste that integer. Do not lower it to make a rank easier.\\n- `stages` is an array. Each stage has `say` (one HUD line) and `spawn` (entity specs). Optional `strain` starts a named strain. Optional `codeblue` or `massage` runs that beat. A stage clears when its required entities are done, or when the strain says so.\\n- Entity specs are `{ id, kind, x, z, ... }`. Kinds include pool, hook, wound, gel, polyp, cyst, fragment, plate, eye, tumor, core, pore, magnet, and dressing. `hidden` and `hiddenBy` keep a piece under another. `table` sends it to another table.\\n- `follow` and `reyes` are rank lines: `{ S, A, B, C }`.\\n- Couch seats come from the Consult screen. Set `partner: true` only when a second surgeon is part of the case.\\n\\nRun `node tests/run.mjs sim` after the new case. Idle input must lose. The skill-0.7 bot must clear it.\\n\\n## Add a scene\\n\\nPush an object onto `SCENES` in `src/content/story.js`, in play order.\\n\\n- `id` is a short key. `set` is the room name the busts stand in. `title` is the heading.\\n- `op` is an operation id, or omit it for a scene that ends the night.\\n- `lines` is 8 to 16 rows. Each row is `{ who, say }`. `who` is a cast id. `say` is one line, at most 57 characters, using only letters, digits, and `. , : ; ! ? - + % / ( ) [ ] ' \\\" # & * = < >`. The HUD uppercases it. Write `...` with three dots.\\n\\nThe campaign runner walks `SCENES` from first to last and writes the save.\\n\\n## Add a strain\\n\\nAdd a branch in `src/sim/strains.js`.\\n\\n- `startStrain(sim, name)` spawns the strain's pieces and sets `sim.strain`.\\n- `tickStrains(sim, dt)` moves it. Call the existing note helpers (`noteEyeLaser`, `noteSob`, `notePlate`) from the tool that hits the piece.\\n- A stage lists `strain: 'your-name'`. The stage clears when `sim.flags.strainDead` is set.\\n- Keep the strain's numbers in `src/core/config.js` (`strainSpeed`, `strainHp`) so Dev Mode can slide them.\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":74}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"11a53527-d43e-42d3-82ed-703bbe234859"}
