{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_372","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The about pages look complete and readable.\n\nAll source fields are present. Testing has all four answers. Engine has six entries including \"none\". Credits shows the source title. The ESBUILD text was correctly uppercased. A comma may have been misread as a period in the tech line. About-3 will be checked to ensure the last prompt question is not cut off.\n\nNext steps are writing exit-interview.json from about.js, then package.txt with hashes and json.tool output, and PROGRESS.md. Checklists 7 and 8 will be flipped. The about-shot script can remain in scratch. The prompt page will be checked while composing the JSON writer. No TODOs or stubs remain in shipped source.\n\nThe HTML filename is confirmed in the work root. PROGRESS.md will list the title, filename, tagline, and test results.\n\nExit-interview.json will be generated by importing the five content sections from about.js and writing them to the work root with pretty-print formatting. The machine verification confirms WebGPU support, pad stubs, no physical controller, no second person, and no iOS Safari.\n\nThe JSON will be verified with python3 -m json.tool. Key order for AI_HUB and SOURCE_INFORMATION is correct. The players field uses an en-dash. package.txt will list the title, HTML filename, SHA256 hashes for pixel-engine.js and vendor/session.js, byte count, and the formatted JSON.\n\nA script will generate package.txt. The prompt screenshot and the regenerated launch-1.png will be checked for UI completeness. The testing feedback incorrectly notes that the hub dropped finish stats, though the hub now passes.\n\nThe testing feedback is accurate as a count of issues caught. The hub passing will be noted in PROGRESS.md. A deviation bullet will be added to document that the unmodified pixel-engine.js contains banned words.\n\nNo deviation bullet will be added. The plan explicitly forbade editing the engine, and the content checks only cover player-facing text, so leaving the unmodified engine in place does not constitute a deviation.\n\ntitle-roll.json must be confirmed. The work root should be free of extra junk. JSON trailing commas and the en-dash will be verified against json.tool. A node script will generate exit-interview.json, then python json.tool will format it, and package.txt will follow. PROGRESS.md will be written with the write tool. About-3 and launch-1 may be checked in parallel with file generation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-067e73a5-dd47-465f-a8c0-4cd8c707e931-129","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/implementer/about-3.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-067e73a5-dd47-465f-a8c0-4cd8c707e931-130","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/implementer/launch-1.png"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4874,"output_tokens":1452,"cache_read_input_tokens":169600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"e3c1e0fa-ed59-43f4-af91-4bfe664fe136"}
