{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_377","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The Second Opinion Clinic** is playable from `file://` as `The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html`. The tagline is \"The truth, stat.\"\n\nThe operation HUD now shows vitals, the clock, and composure, and the title screen reads in full. About lists every source field and every feedback answer. `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md` are in this folder.\n\nVerified here: `node tests/run.mjs` (117 passed), browser menus and prompts (16 passed), two agreeing `file://` launches, and all five AI Hub harnesses. Fresh-profile music is 0.1. No physical pad, second person, iOS Safari, or TV.\n\n**Source information.** Date 2026-11-04 22:40:40. Source: Trauma Center: Second Opinion. Plan: PLAN.md. Genre: Simulation. Perspective: fixed overhead surgical view. Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (build 2026-11-02), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, esbuild 0.28.2. Art: engine pixel-toon, original OR sets, primitive busts, canvas tissue. Animation: engine clock plus sim-driven tool motion, heart pulse, and code-blue needle. Audio: original chiptune, SoundDef effects, formant gibberish voices, no audio files. Online: couch consult and AI Hub shared-world for 1 to 4 players. Testing: Node sim suite, Playwright on software WebGPU, hub harness on 127.0.0.1. Research: the planner read the source Wikipedia page, the hub protocol, and the engine kit, and ran engine spikes; this build followed PLAN.md and the engine docs. Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux. Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh. Usage: added on import.\n\n**Testing feedback.** Testing caught 10 issues. Four were game-breaking: hooks never left the field, the magnet could not be extracted, Op 5 never closed, and the transplant skipped its forced rewind. The most helpful test was the skill-1 bot play of every operation. The least helpful was a menu screenshot with no input behind it.\n\n**Engine feedback.** Song data and `renderSound` were testable in Node, and the HUD grid matched the fill-mode canvas. A held entity id is a string, so a numeric comparison never saw the grab. The surgery sim, eight tools, strains, couch seats, and shared-world host loop had to be built here. Pad buttons versus keyboard keys took the longest. Nothing in the engine was changed. A per-button \"read it yourself\" flag would have helped.\n\n**Prompt feedback.** The plan named the beats, tools, and pass lines. Two boot documents disagreed about swapping screens. One bot clearing every operation at rank S, without lowering par, was the hardest part. Ask for the exit-interview counts after the suite has run, and name one file as the only source of the balance numbers."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":324,"output_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":182016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"81401f50-7f5f-4699-9dc6-81adf31b5c97"}
