{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_396","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The HUD anchor is not text alignment relative to the x,y point.\n\nThe docs confirm x and y are offsets from the screen corner. The COMP text at top-right with offset 8,4 matches the screenshot. This is correct placement.\n\nThe clock is centered manually. The developer view tools are being checked against the criteria. All five cheat tools are present and wired. The action tools are also implemented.\n\nSpawn pool is implemented, but the other spawn variants are missing. The jump tool only supports story operations. It does not support stages or scenes. The view tool lacks frame step and FPS stats.\n\nThe missing tools are a genuine gap. The anti-overreach rule forbids refuting for unrequired extensions, but criterion 3 explicitly names those tools. The four categories exist, yet their contents are incomplete.\n\nThe verification instructions bias toward refuting and hunting for real bugs. A missing dev tool explicitly required by the acceptance criterion is a genuine gap, not a nit.\n\nThe missing dev tools are explicitly required by the contract, so they can be refuted. I will also hunt for more serious gameplay bugs. I will inspect session.js for hub issues, verify story line fonts, confirm the HTML file works as a single file, and check that server copies never start the engine.\n\nThe harness passed all five tests, confirming the hub integration works at the harness level. I am now checking whether live.mjs drives a real game or merely injects state during the drain test. The tests.txt file only records \"117 passed\", so I must verify that this reflects an actual run.\n\nA spot-check run is permitted only if the captured evidence is uncertain. The results screen correctly uses rank for follow-up lines and displays the rank stamp. I am now inspecting the HTML file to confirm it is a single file with an inline script.\n\nThe authoring document exists. The continueShift logic is correct: it clamps the next scene index to the final scene when all scenes have been viewed, and newShift properly resets save state and enters scene zero. I am now inspecting score.js to verify the rank cap for unscripted blue and pristine conditions, and to confirm whether a perfect skill score of 1.0 yields an S rank without god mode.\n\nThe par test passes because the criterion defines par as the full-skill bot's own score. The bot runs at skill 1 without god mode, so the equality check is valid.\n\nI am now checking whether the skill 0.7 clock check excludes bosses when comparing timeLeft to timeMax.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45c418e1-0810-426e-a51d-b210df90c08c-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Math\\.random","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45c418e1-0810-426e-a51d-b210df90c08c-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"new Engine|Engine\\.start|server|AIHub\\.active|send\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/net/session.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-45c418e1-0810-426e-a51d-b210df90c08c-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/game.js","limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7584,"output_tokens":1792,"cache_read_input_tokens":117760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"b85c35ea-5dd2-4ca0-a718-7e99fdbf43e1"}
