{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-58562099-b99f-4385-812b-eac0a0d09105-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→  function post(type, fields) {\\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\\n    try {\\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n210→  function emit(type, args) {\\n    var list = handlers[type];\\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n      try {\\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\\n      } catch (e) {\\n220→        setTimeout(function () {\\n          throw e;\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function onMessage(event) {\\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\\n    var m = event.data;\\n230→    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      welcomed = true;\\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\\n      for (var key in m) {\\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\\n        hub[key] = m[key];\\n      }\\n240→      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\\n      if (m.limits) {\\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\\n        tokens = limits.burst;\\n      }\\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\\n      return;\\n250→    }\\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\\n      try {\\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\\n      } catch (e) {}\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\\n260→      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\\n        return p.id !== m.id;\\n      });\\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\\n270→      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\",\"content_concise\":\"200→  function post(type, fields) {\\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\\n    try {\\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n210→  function emit(type, args) {\\n    var list = handlers[type];\\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n      try {\\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\\n      } catch (e) {\\n220→        setTimeout(function () {\\n          throw e;\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function onMessage(event) {\\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\\n    var m = event.data;\\n230→    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      welcomed = true;\\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\\n      for (var key in m) {\\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\\n        hub[key] = m[key];\\n      }\\n240→      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\\n      if (m.limits) {\\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\\n        tokens = limits.burst;\\n      }\\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\\n      return;\\n250→    }\\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\\n      try {\\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\\n      } catch (e) {}\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\\n260→      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\\n        return p.id !== m.id;\\n      });\\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\\n270→      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/vendor/session.js\",\"offset\":200,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  function post(type, fields) {\\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\\n    try {\\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\\n    } catch (e) {\\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function emit(type, args) {\\n    var list = handlers[type];\\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n      try {\\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\\n      } catch (e) {\\n        setTimeout(function () {\\n          throw e;\\n        });\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function onMessage(event) {\\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\\n    var m = event.data;\\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\\n      if (welcomed) return;\\n      welcomed = true;\\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\\n      for (var key in m) {\\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\\n        hub[key] = m[key];\\n      }\\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\\n      if (m.limits) {\\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\\n        tokens = limits.burst;\\n      }\\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\\n      try {\\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\\n      } catch (e) {}\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\\n        return p.id !== m.id;\\n      });\\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\\n      ended = true;\\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\\n    } else {\\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\\n      var detail = {};\\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\\n\",\"total_lines\":488}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"38ed8c6c-b3ab-48d0-b517-30cd0d375f1c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_406","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `hub.me` value originates from the welcome message field.\n\n`me` is a numeric player ID. The `i === me` check skips the local seat when both values are numbers. If `me` is 0, client seat 0 never updates.\n\nHost mouse input overwrites x and z via `pullSession`. Stick input survives in `sx` and `sz`. Host pad works. Host mouse does not move. Client pad input reaches the host. The host simulates movement. The client view of its own hand does not update.\n\nThe harness auto-plays. It may inject inputs through the gamepad or protocol, which would let the host receive them and complete the game. The client-side cursor freeze might not fail the harness if it checks state on the host. This remains a player-facing bug. Missing view tools in dev mode will only be listed as a secondary gap if confirmed.\n\nThe missing frame step is a secondary gap because the criterion explicitly requires view tools in §8. The cursor bug remains the primary issue. Re-reading `applySnap` confirms the local seat stays at its initial position since `applyDecoded` never updates it. The host player sees their hand move because they step the simulation directly.\n\nNon-host players see tissue updates but their own hand remains frozen at the spawn point. They cannot aim because they cannot see where their hand is. This makes client play unusable and confirms a core multiplayer defect. I should also check whether non-host views use a different simulation.\n\nConfirmed that `pullSession` mutates the same simulation object, so views reflect those changes. In session mode, `update` calls `pullSession` but never merges local stick input into the seat. The host's own inputs also overwrite mouse coordinates with `place:true`.\n\nThe harness likely drives the game through synthetic keys and direct protocol injection rather than the page mouse. It checks `__hubCheck.pass`, so the broken host mouse path does not cause a failure. Keyboard stick input may still work for the host because `pullSession` preserves `sx` from `humanInput`.\n\nHost keyboard stick input works in session mode. Client keyboard aim is invisible because the host moves the seat but the client ignores it. This is enough to refute.\n\nI will not list extra dev-mode gaps to avoid wasting time. The cursor bug is the only real issue.\n\nA second bug exists in local play: pad inputs block mouse.\n\nThe pad-blocking-mouse bug will be included because it breaks last-device mouse aim. The missing settings rows are skipped since the criterion only requires working screens, not every row. The missing dev tools—frame step, FPS/stats, jump to stage or scene, and spawn kinds other than pool—are a single gap under §8. It is unclear if this is over-reach.\n\nThe missing frame step is strictly unmet because the criterion explicitly requires the view tools in §8. I will list it as a gap. The input bugs remain the primary defects.\n\nThe HUD tool wheel is not required to be clickable. Criterion 3 only mandates its presence, not interactivity. The always-visible composure HUD satisfies the criterion. The authoring note exists at docs/AUTHORING.md.\n\nThe title \"The Second Opinion Clinic\" is a valid riff and not a direct match to the forbidden names, so it does not constitute a failure. The 117 passed tests are sufficient evidence; rerunning the full balance suite is unnecessary.\n\nThe test evidence appears genuine. Two runs agree. Painted frames and music playback are visible. The drain state changed. Screenshots show a real surgery view.\n\nI am now checking whether `me` could be null during play. If it were, the `i === me` guard would not block updates. The welcome message may set `hub.me` before `openSession` resolves.\n\n`hub.me` is confirmed to be set before `openSession` runs, so the null-ID theory is ruled out. The pad-blocking-mouse bug will be listed as a second finding alongside the cursor freeze.\n\nThe missing local prediction is the same bug. The harness never checks client cursor position, so tests do not cover this path. The defect is in the code and can be verified by reading.\n\nThe `i === me` guard also prevents the client from updating its own tool state. Non-host clients only send input and do not step the simulation.\n\nThe client tool wheel stays locked to the initial tool because `applySnap` skips the local seat. The host simulates actions at its own position, but the client sees tissue changes at a frozen cursor that does not match the host's hand. This makes client play completely unplayable.\n\nThe two-pad test passes locally. The verdict is refuted with high confidence and no blocking issues. The missing frame step and FPS are minor gaps, so they will be omitted to avoid false refutation.\n\nThe missing frame step and scene/stage jump will be listed as gaps. The criterion explicitly names them in §8, and the UI currently lacks both paths. The view tools are also missing: no frame step, no FPS display, and the dev tool cannot jump to arbitrary stages or story scenes.\n\nThe pad-stealing-mouse bug is confirmed as a design inconsistency. The code sets the device to mouse when a pad exists, but then ignores mouse input entirely. This contradicts the last-device prompt and the \"mouse aims\" requirement.\n\nThe pad-blocking-mouse bug is confirmed by a concrete example: an idle pad with axes at zero discards mouse placement and drain inputs, leaving the pool untouched. The terminal token must be exactly \"Refuted\". No extra verification is needed.\n\nThe gamepad button clearing is confirmed to work correctly. I am now writing the verdict files. The hub bug requires three fixes: applying the local seat from snapshots, integrating local input into the seat each frame, and stopping the aimed x/z overwrite before sending.\n\nI am finalizing the verdict JSON schema and mapping exact line numbers to each finding. The pad-stealing-mouse bug is at clinic.js:165, the hub cursor overwrite at clinic.js:380-384, the session skip at session.js:73-76, the fixedUpdate guard at clinic.js:156, and the missing dev tools at clinic.js:274-278.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The launch and sim logs are real, but the input wiring drops mouse aim whenever a pad is connected and never moves a hub client’s own hand. I’ll record that as a refute."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1093396f-8999-4070-9aa1-177d8a84a827-77","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-verdict-9c48352445aa-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js:165\",\n      \"detail\": \"If any pad is connected, fixedUpdate always feeds seat i from padInputs and drops humanInput, so a mouse move/click (or WASD) after the prompt has switched to mouse/key does not move or use the tool. Expected: last device aims and uses; actual: idle pad axes win and the pool never drains.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/net/session.js:73\",\n      \"detail\": \"A non-host hand never moves: fixedUpdate returns when a session exists, applySnap skips i === me, and pullSession (clinic.js:380) overwrites aimed x/z with the current seat. Expected: client tip follows stick/mouse and host mouse aim reaches the sim; actual: client hand stays at spawn and host place-aim is a no-op.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"gap\",\n      \"location\": \"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js:274\",\n      \"detail\": \"Dev Mode is missing PLAN §8 tools criterion 3 requires: jump is ops only (no stage, no story scene), view has no frame step or FPS/sim stats, and Actions spawn only a pool.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"clinic.js:165 prefers padInputs over humanInput; session.js:73 skips the local seat and clinic.js:380 clobbers mouse x/z; devRows() has no frame-step/scene jump. tests.txt 117 passed does not drive these paths.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Refuted. The Node suite, file:// launches, and five hub harnesses are real and the package matches criterion 1, but two input paths produce the wrong result and Dev Mode omits tools criterion 3 names.\\n\\n**Pad steals the tool.** `fixedUpdate` (`clinic.js:165`) assigns `inputs[i] = this.padInputs[i]` whenever that pad exists, before the mouse/keyboard `humanInput`. `buildSeatInputs` writes a pad row every frame a pad is connected, even with zero axes. Moving the mouse sets `device` to `mouse` and fills `humanInput` with `place`/`x`/`z`/`use`, then that object is discarded. With a connected pad, holding the mouse on a pool does not drain it. The mouse-drain browser check never installs a pad, so it does not catch this.\\n\\n**Hub clients cannot see their own hand.** Non-host copies do not step the sim (`clinic.js:156`). `applySnap` (`session.js:73`) writes every seat except `i === me`, and `applyDecoded` never copies seat poses. `pullSession` (`clinic.js:380`) then replaces the aimed `x`/`z` with the seat's current position, so host mouse `place` input is a no-op. Stick `sx`/`sz` can move the host sim, but the client reticle stays at spawn. Harness `pass=true` does not read that seat.\\n\\n**Dev Mode is short of §8.** Balance sliders, the five cheats, op jump, and most actions exist. Missing from the UI: jump to a stage or story scene, frame step, FPS/sim stats, and spawn of anything but a pool (`clinic.js:274`–`278`, `pickDev`).\\n\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1093396f-8999-4070-9aa1-177d8a84a827-78","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-classifier-9c48352445aa-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"Refuted. The Node suite, file:// launches, and five hub harnesses are real and the package matches criterion 1, but two input paths produce the wrong result and Dev Mode omits tools criterion 3 names.\n\n**Pad steals the tool.** `fixedUpdate` (`clinic.js:165`) assigns `inputs[i] = this.padInputs[i]` whenever that pad exists, before the mouse/keyboard `humanInput`. `buildSeatInputs` writes a pad row every frame a pad is connected, even with zero axes. Moving the mouse sets `device` to `mouse` and fills `humanInput` with `place`/`x`/`z`/`use`, then that object is discarded. With a connected pad, holding the mouse on a pool does not drain it. The mouse-drain browser check never installs a pad, so it does not catch this.\n\n**Hub clients cannot see their own hand.** Non-host copies do not step the sim (`clinic.js:156`). `applySnap` (`session.js:73`) writes every seat except `i === me`, and `applyDecoded` never copies seat poses. `pullSession` (`clinic.js:380`) then replaces the aimed `x`/`z` with the seat's current position, so host mouse `place` input is a no-op. Stick `sx`/`sz` can move the host sim, but the client reticle stays at spawn. Harness `pass=true` does not read that seat.\n\n**Dev Mode is short of §8.** Balance sliders, the five cheats, op jump, and most actions exist. Missing from the UI: jump to a stage or story scene, frame step, FPS/sim stats, and spawn of anything but a pool (`clinic.js:274`–`278`, `pickDev`).\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1012,"output_tokens":4921,"cache_read_input_tokens":146432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"822c0419-d66a-46bc-a193-f5800d5c5271"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1093396f-8999-4070-9aa1-177d8a84a827-77","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": true,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js:165\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"If any pad is connected, fixedUpdate always feeds seat i from padInputs and drops humanInput, so a mouse move/click (or WASD) after the prompt has switched to mouse/key does not move or use the tool. Expected: last device aims and uses; actual: idle pad axes win and the pool never drains.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"bug\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/net/session.js:73\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"A non-host hand never moves: fixedUpdate returns when a session exists, applySnap skips i === me, and pullSession (clinic.js:380) overwrites aimed x/z with the current seat. Expected: client tip follows stick/mouse and host mouse aim reaches the sim; actual: client hand stays at spawn and host place-aim is a no-op.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"gap\\\",\\n      \\\"location\\\": \\\"The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js:274\\\",\\n      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"Dev Mode is missing PLAN §8 tools criterion 3 requires: jump is ops only (no stage, no story scene), view has no frame step or FPS/sim stats, and Actions spawn only a pool.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"clinic.js:165 prefers padInputs over humanInput; session.js:73 skips the local seat and clinic.js:380 clobbers mouse x/z; devRows() has no frame-step/scene jump. tests.txt 117 passed does not drive these paths.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Refuted. The Node suite, file:// launches, and five hub harnesses are real and the package matches criterion 1, but two input paths produce the wrong result and Dev Mode omits tools criterion 3 names.\\\\n\\\\n**Pad steals the tool.** `fixedUpdate` (`clinic.js:165`) assigns `inputs[i] = this.padInputs[i]` whenever that pad exists, before the mouse/keyboard `humanInput`. `buildSeatInputs` writes a pad row every frame a pad is connected, even with zero axes. Moving the mouse sets `device` to `mouse` and fills `humanInput` with `place`/`x`/`z`/`use`, then that object is discarded. With a connected pad, holding the mouse on a pool does not drain it. The mouse-drain browser check never installs a pad, so it does not catch this.\\\\n\\\\n**Hub clients cannot see their own hand.** Non-host copies do not step the sim (`clinic.js:156`). `applySnap` (`session.js:73`) writes every seat except `i === me`, and `applyDecoded` never copies seat poses. `pullSession` (`clinic.js:380`) then replaces the aimed `x`/`z` with the seat's current position, so host mouse `place` input is a no-op. Stick `sx`/`sz` can move the host sim, but the client reticle stays at spawn. Harness `pass=true` does not read that seat.\\\\n\\\\n**Dev Mode is short of §8.** Balance sliders, the five cheats, op jump, and most actions exist. Missing from the UI: jump to a stage or story scene, frame step, FPS/sim stats, and spawn of anything but a pool (`clinic.js:274`–`278`, `pickDev`).\\\\n\\\"\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-verdict-9c48352445aa-1-0.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-verdict-9c48352445aa-1-0.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/ho