{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_427","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The drawHud function calls hud.clear and hud.measure.\n\nTests for clinic.update need a minimal stub with no-op hud methods. The view and camera must be present to avoid null errors. playScore requires an audio stub.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bacdf574-af75-4a18-89e9-30d173289696-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/aim.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bacdf574-af75-4a18-89e9-30d173289696-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/view/stage.js","offset":150,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4338,"output_tokens":517,"cache_read_input_tokens":83328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"2512e0e1-1c3f-422e-acf8-cea1be7e934d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bacdf574-af75-4a18-89e9-30d173289696-48","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Tissue height. The heart dome rises about 2 units; other arenas stay low. */\\nexport function heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse = 0) {\\n  const r2 = x * x * 0.08 + z * z * 0.1;\\n  if (arena === 'heart') {\\n    const dome = 2.15 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 18 - (z * z) / 12);\\n    return dome + Math.sin(pulse) * 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'chest') {\\n    const heart = 1.7 * Math.exp(-((x - 0.4) ** 2) / 10 - ((z + 0.2) ** 2) / 8);\\n10→    const lung = 0.55 * Math.exp(-((x + 1.6) ** 2) / 14 - (z * z) / 16);\\n    return heart + lung + Math.sin(pulse * 0.7) * 0.05;\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'lung') return 0.45 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 22 - (z * z) / 14) + Math.sin(pulse * 0.6) * 0.08;\\n  if (arena === 'liver') return 0.7 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 20 - ((z - 0.2) ** 2) / 12);\\n  if (arena === 'bone') return 0.35 + 0.25 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 30);\\n  if (arena === 'spine') return 0.4 + 0.15 * Math.cos(x * 1.4) * Math.exp(-(z * z) / 10);\\n  return 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n}\\n\\n20→/**\\n * Mouse aim: iterate the ray onto the raised surface (four steps).\\n * origin/dir are {x,y,z}. Returns the surface point.\\n */\\nexport function aimOnSurface(arena, origin, dir, pulse = 0) {\\n  let y = 0;\\n  let x = origin.x;\\n  let z = origin.z;\\n  const dy = dir.y || -1e-6;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n30→    const t = (y - origin.y) / dy;\\n    x = origin.x + dir.x * t;\\n    z = origin.z + dir.z * t;\\n    y = heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse);\\n  }\\n  return { x, y, z };\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Tissue height. The heart dome rises about 2 units; other arenas stay low. */\\nexport function heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse = 0) {\\n  const r2 = x * x * 0.08 + z * z * 0.1;\\n  if (arena === 'heart') {\\n    const dome = 2.15 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 18 - (z * z) / 12);\\n    return dome + Math.sin(pulse) * 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'chest') {\\n    const heart = 1.7 * Math.exp(-((x - 0.4) ** 2) / 10 - ((z + 0.2) ** 2) / 8);\\n10→    const lung = 0.55 * Math.exp(-((x + 1.6) ** 2) / 14 - (z * z) / 16);\\n    return heart + lung + Math.sin(pulse * 0.7) * 0.05;\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'lung') return 0.45 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 22 - (z * z) / 14) + Math.sin(pulse * 0.6) * 0.08;\\n  if (arena === 'liver') return 0.7 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 20 - ((z - 0.2) ** 2) / 12);\\n  if (arena === 'bone') return 0.35 + 0.25 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 30);\\n  if (arena === 'spine') return 0.4 + 0.15 * Math.cos(x * 1.4) * Math.exp(-(z * z) / 10);\\n  return 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n}\\n\\n20→/**\\n * Mouse aim: iterate the ray onto the raised surface (four steps).\\n * origin/dir are {x,y,z}. Returns the surface point.\\n */\\nexport function aimOnSurface(arena, origin, dir, pulse = 0) {\\n  let y = 0;\\n  let x = origin.x;\\n  let z = origin.z;\\n  const dy = dir.y || -1e-6;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n30→    const t = (y - origin.y) / dy;\\n    x = origin.x + dir.x * t;\\n    z = origin.z + dir.z * t;\\n    y = heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse);\\n  }\\n  return { x, y, z };\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/aim.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/** Tissue height. The heart dome rises about 2 units; other arenas stay low. */\\nexport function heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse = 0) {\\n  const r2 = x * x * 0.08 + z * z * 0.1;\\n  if (arena === 'heart') {\\n    const dome = 2.15 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 18 - (z * z) / 12);\\n    return dome + Math.sin(pulse) * 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'chest') {\\n    const heart = 1.7 * Math.exp(-((x - 0.4) ** 2) / 10 - ((z + 0.2) ** 2) / 8);\\n    const lung = 0.55 * Math.exp(-((x + 1.6) ** 2) / 14 - (z * z) / 16);\\n    return heart + lung + Math.sin(pulse * 0.7) * 0.05;\\n  }\\n  if (arena === 'lung') return 0.45 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 22 - (z * z) / 14) + Math.sin(pulse * 0.6) * 0.08;\\n  if (arena === 'liver') return 0.7 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 20 - ((z - 0.2) ** 2) / 12);\\n  if (arena === 'bone') return 0.35 + 0.25 * Math.exp(-(x * x) / 30);\\n  if (arena === 'spine') return 0.4 + 0.15 * Math.cos(x * 1.4) * Math.exp(-(z * z) / 10);\\n  return 0.12 * Math.exp(-r2);\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Mouse aim: iterate the ray onto the raised surface (four steps).\\n * origin/dir are {x,y,z}. Returns the surface point.\\n */\\nexport function aimOnSurface(arena, origin, dir, pulse = 0) {\\n  let y = 0;\\n  let x = origin.x;\\n  let z = origin.z;\\n  const dy = dir.y || -1e-6;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\\n    const t = (y - origin.y) / dy;\\n    x = origin.x + dir.x * t;\\n    z = origin.z + dir.z * t;\\n    y = heightAt(arena, x, z, pulse);\\n  }\\n  return { x, y, z };\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":36}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bacdf574-af75-4a18-89e9-30d173289696-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→  tissue.material.color?.setHex?.(hex);\\n}\\n\\nexport function syncView(view, app, pulse) {\\n  const sim = app.sim;\\n  const operating = !!sim && (app.mode === 'op' || app.mode === 'pause' || app.mode === 'dev' || app.mode === 'results' || app.mode === 'attract' || app.mode === 'session');\\n  view.room.visible = !operating;\\n  view.tissue.visible = operating;\\n  view.lamp.visible = !operating;\\n  if (operating) paintTissue(view.tissue, sim.arena || 'forearm', pulse);\\n160→\\n  const show = operating ? sim.entities.filter((e) => !e.hidden && (e.table == null || e.table === sim.active)) : [];\\n  view.ents.forEach((body, i) => {\\n    const ent = show[i];\\n    body.visible = !!ent && !ent.done;\\n    if (!ent || ent.done) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', ent.x, ent.z, pulse) + 0.18 + (ent.r || 0) * 0.05;\\n    body.position.set(ent.x, y, ent.z);\\n    const s = Math.max(0.35, ent.r || (ent.kind === 'hook' ? 0.45 : 0.7));\\n    body.scale.setScalar(s);\\n170→    body.material.color?.setHex?.(KIND_COLOR[ent.kind] || 0xc45a58);\\n  });\\n\\n  view.hands.forEach((hand, i) => {\\n    const seat = operating ? sim.seats[i] : null;\\n    hand.visible = !!seat;\\n    if (!seat) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', seat.x, seat.z, pulse) + 0.42;\\n    hand.position.set(seat.x, y, seat.z);\\n  });\\n180→\\n  const story = app.mode === 'story' || app.mode === 'brief' || app.mode === 'credits' || app.mode === 'title' || app.mode === 'card';\\n  const speaker = app.speaker || (app.mode === 'title' ? 'ilya' : app.mode === 'card' ? 'reyes' : '');\\n  view.busts.forEach((bust, i) => {\\n    bust.group.visible = story;\\n    if (!story) return;\\n    const talking = bust.id === speaker;\\n    bust.group.position.set((i - 2.5) * 0.85, 0, talking ? -0.2 : -1.3);\\n    bust.group.scale.setScalar(talking ? 1.15 : 0.82);\\n    const bob = talking ? 1 + Math.sin(pulse * 6) * 0.04 : 1;\",\"content_concise\":\"150→  tissue.material.color?.setHex?.(hex);\\n}\\n\\nexport function syncView(view, app, pulse) {\\n  const sim = app.sim;\\n  const operating = !!sim && (app.mode === 'op' || app.mode === 'pause' || app.mode === 'dev' || app.mode === 'results' || app.mode === 'attract' || app.mode === 'session');\\n  view.room.visible = !operating;\\n  view.tissue.visible = operating;\\n  view.lamp.visible = !operating;\\n  if (operating) paintTissue(view.tissue, sim.arena || 'forearm', pulse);\\n160→\\n  const show = operating ? sim.entities.filter((e) => !e.hidden && (e.table == null || e.table === sim.active)) : [];\\n  view.ents.forEach((body, i) => {\\n    const ent = show[i];\\n    body.visible = !!ent && !ent.done;\\n    if (!ent || ent.done) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', ent.x, ent.z, pulse) + 0.18 + (ent.r || 0) * 0.05;\\n    body.position.set(ent.x, y, ent.z);\\n    const s = Math.max(0.35, ent.r || (ent.kind === 'hook' ? 0.45 : 0.7));\\n    body.scale.setScalar(s);\\n170→    body.material.color?.setHex?.(KIND_COLOR[ent.kind] || 0xc45a58);\\n  });\\n\\n  view.hands.forEach((hand, i) => {\\n    const seat = operating ? sim.seats[i] : null;\\n    hand.visible = !!seat;\\n    if (!seat) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', seat.x, seat.z, pulse) + 0.42;\\n    hand.position.set(seat.x, y, seat.z);\\n  });\\n180→\\n  const story = app.mode === 'story' || app.mode === 'brief' || app.mode === 'credits' || app.mode === 'title' || app.mode === 'card';\\n  const speaker = app.speaker || (app.mode === 'title' ? 'ilya' : app.mode === 'card' ? 'reyes' : '');\\n  view.busts.forEach((bust, i) => {\\n    bust.group.visible = story;\\n    if (!story) return;\\n    const talking = bust.id === speaker;\\n    bust.group.position.set((i - 2.5) * 0.85, 0, talking ? -0.2 : -1.3);\\n    bust.group.scale.setScalar(talking ? 1.15 : 0.82);\\n    const bob = talking ? 1 + Math.sin(pulse * 6) * 0.04 : 1;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/view/stage.js\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  tissue.material.color?.setHex?.(hex);\\n}\\n\\nexport function syncView(view, app, pulse) {\\n  const sim = app.sim;\\n  const operating = !!sim && (app.mode === 'op' || app.mode === 'pause' || app.mode === 'dev' || app.mode === 'results' || app.mode === 'attract' || app.mode === 'session');\\n  view.room.visible = !operating;\\n  view.tissue.visible = operating;\\n  view.lamp.visible = !operating;\\n  if (operating) paintTissue(view.tissue, sim.arena || 'forearm', pulse);\\n\\n  const show = operating ? sim.entities.filter((e) => !e.hidden && (e.table == null || e.table === sim.active)) : [];\\n  view.ents.forEach((body, i) => {\\n    const ent = show[i];\\n    body.visible = !!ent && !ent.done;\\n    if (!ent || ent.done) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', ent.x, ent.z, pulse) + 0.18 + (ent.r || 0) * 0.05;\\n    body.position.set(ent.x, y, ent.z);\\n    const s = Math.max(0.35, ent.r || (ent.kind === 'hook' ? 0.45 : 0.7));\\n    body.scale.setScalar(s);\\n    body.material.color?.setHex?.(KIND_COLOR[ent.kind] || 0xc45a58);\\n  });\\n\\n  view.hands.forEach((hand, i) => {\\n    const seat = operating ? sim.seats[i] : null;\\n    hand.visible = !!seat;\\n    if (!seat) return;\\n    const y = heightAt(sim.arena || 'forearm', seat.x, seat.z, pulse) + 0.42;\\n    hand.position.set(seat.x, y, seat.z);\\n  });\\n\\n  const story = app.mode === 'story' || app.mode === 'brief' || app.mode === 'credits' || app.mode === 'title' || app.mode === 'card';\\n  const speaker = app.speaker || (app.mode === 'title' ? 'ilya' : app.mode === 'card' ? 'reyes' : '');\\n  view.busts.forEach((bust, i) => {\\n    bust.group.visible = story;\\n    if (!story) return;\\n    const talking = bust.id === speaker;\\n    bust.group.position.set((i - 2.5) * 0.85, 0, talking ? -0.2 : -1.3);\\n    bust.group.scale.setScalar(talking ? 1.15 : 0.82);\\n    const bob = talking ? 1 + Math.sin(pulse * 6) * 0.04 : 1;\\n\",\"total_lines\":192}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"84697523-d02f-4ebc-b2d4-1820c44d120d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_428","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Planning mouse aim input handling for session mode.\n\nStubbing `rayAt` to fire a ray straight down from a fixed point so mouse aim hits a known location.\n\nThe host will move seat 1 via mouse aim, then pull the session state to snap it into place. The client will predict seat 1 movement using WASD or stick input, and applySnap will correct drift. Need to verify applySnap directly through session messages, and ensure predictSeat targets the correct seat index.\n\nThe client's `predictLocal` now targets `hub.me` instead of `drive`. It calls `predictSeat` using `session.local`, which is populated after `pullSession` so the input matches what gets sent. Key stick input is already copied into `humanInput` and flows through this path.\n\nMouse aim snaps the seat immediately via `predictSeat` place. Drift correction eases by 0.35 when the host snapshot is more than one unit away. The client sends include `place`, so `hub.sent` can be checked after 80 ms. The token bucket starts at 16 tokens, so early sends succeed.\n\nThe client sends every 66 ms of wall-clock time. The host only emits pings until it receives a start event and sets its timer to zero. The test sequence creates the host hub, opens a session, attaches the clinic, emits start, and runs one update so local place is set.\n\nThe host test now advances time to 80 ms and checks that the seat lands within 0.3 units of the aimed x coordinate. The fake RNG must return a function so `beginOp` can generate a deterministic seed. The client will be tested separately with `isHost: false` and `me: 1`, where emitting start triggers `beginOp` to create the simulation state.\n\nThe client must predict seat movement inside `update`, not `fixedUpdate`, because the host and client should not share state when the session stops. `applySnap` will only ease the local seat’s position by 0.35 if drift exceeds one unit; the local tool state is preserved for the player’s own seat, while other seats are corrected from the snapshot.\n\nExtracting `moveSeat` into a pure `predictSeat` helper and a `moveSeats` loop so the client can predict seat positions independently. A test case with 3-unit drift confirms the eased position lands at 1.05 rather than snapping fully to 3.\n\nThe client will call `predictSeat` only for its own seat, leaving other seats untouched. The host timer runs `moveSeats` to update all seats, merging local inputs with network data; remote seats without input remain idle.\n\nThe client will simulate a mouse-aimed place by feeding that message directly to the host. The `x: loc.x || 0` fallback is being replaced with nullish coalescing. In `fixedUpdate`, `seatInputs` now routes human seats to bot logic unless they are the current drive, and pad inputs are fetched only for the active drive.\n\nWhen the device is mouse or key, the drive seat uses `humanInput` even if a pad input exists for it. Other human seats still use their own pads. When the device is a pad, the drive seat uses `padInputs[drive]` rather than always pad 0.\n\nWhen the device is a pad, the drive seat’s `humanInput` is built from its own `padInputs[drive]`, with keyboard tool overlays preserved. On couch mode, pad 0 controls seat 0.\n\nThe last input event determines the active device. If a mouse user and pad 0 both want control, the mouse wins and seat 0 uses mouse input while seat 1 still uses pad 1.\n\nIn dev mode, paused frames step via pickDev instead of fixedUpdate. timeLeft drops unless freeze is active.\n\nFPS will display on the view tab continuously rather than only when focused.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0a964ff9-135a-43c9-b5c2-eecf2ce4a396-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function tickClock|freezeClock|timeLeft","glob":"**/op.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1909,"output_tokens":2310,"cache_read