(action === 'freeze') sim.freezeClock = !sim.freezeClock;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"34d6f219-d452-4d59-a0c3-d833d4b03b14"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_429","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"sim.t is still increasing even with the freeze active.\n\nConfirmed that step() increments sim.t before tickClock, so the timer advances even when frozen. Dev jump stage and scene setup are verified. Need to check operation stage counts for the longest list and add scroll to the HUD so all rows remain reachable. The browser suite does not open the jump tab.\n\nA scroll window for the dev list will keep the focused row visible without breaking the pause menu layout. The clean() function strips characters but preserves titles.\n\nThe jump list header \"LIST OPS\" can be nudged left or right to switch between operation, stage, and scene modes. The constructor initializes the current jump kind to 'op'. Spawn specifications for entities like pool and bleeder are being defined.\n\nSpawn specs for laceration, hook, and strain are now defined. The dev cheat spawn handler will also cover the strain alias. Strain names will cycle through a list so repeated spawns produce different variants rather than always defaulting to introit.\n\nStrain spawns will default to introit unless a specific name is provided. The VIEW stats row fits within 42 characters, so no truncation is needed. FPS will remain on its own separate row. When forceBot is active and the device uses mouse input, the human player is disabled and the bot takes over; the skill slider still applies because seat 0 receives botSkill 1 from createOp.\n\nThe skill slider is effectively useless for seat 0 because createOp always sets seat.botSkill to 1. The bot input logic uses seat.botSkill first, so the slider value never reaches the bot. This contradicts the PLAN requirement that the slider controls bot plays.\n\nThe bot skill logic is being fixed so the slider actually controls the bot. When Bot Plays is active, all seats use this.botSkill. Otherwise, non-human seats fall back to seat.botSkill, and human seats use this.botSkill. Partner bots in operations will keep their 0.85 skill.\n\nThe implementation plan is now concrete. It covers editing op.js, clinic.js, and session.js, adding tests in run.mjs, running node tests, and rebuilding for browser launch. A TODO placeholder for banned words also needs checking.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3378413c-4375-4999-92a5-71ef3965ed0d-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/ops.js","offset":150,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3378413c-4375-4999-92a5-71ef3965ed0d-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^\\s+\\{ say:","glob":"**/ops.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2737,"output_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":89344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"0cf384fd-bc3b-4782-976a-ca4123bf8405"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3378413c-4375-4999-92a5-71ef3965ed0d-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→    gifts: [],\\n    par: 6010,\\n    follow: follow({}, 'All three made the morning paper. Alive.'),\\n    reyes: follow({}, 'You went quiet. I noticed.'),\\n    stages: [\\n      {\\n        say: 'Table A. Leg gash.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('a1', 'wound', -0.4, 0.2, { len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0, table: 0 }),\\n          line('a2', 'pool', 1.2, -0.4, { r: 0.65, table: 0 }),\\n160→        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Table B. Debris and burns.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('bdeb', 'debris', -0.6, 0.1, { pull: 1.1, dx: 0.2, dz: 1, table: 1 }),\\n          line('bgel', 'gel', 0.8, -0.3, { w: 1.5, h: 0.9, table: 1 }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n170→        say: 'Table C. Chest.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('c1', 'incision', -0.8, 0.3, { len: 1.0, dx: 1, dz: 0, table: 2 }),\\n          line('c2', 'pool', 0.6, 0.2, { r: 0.6, bleed: true, table: 2 }),\\n          line('c3', 'wound', -0.2, -0.8, { len: 1.0, dx: 1, dz: 0.1, table: 2 }),\\n          line('c4', 'polyp', 1.4, 0.8, { table: 2 }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      { say: 'The room goes quiet. Hold your gift.', quiet: true, flag: 'awakened', until: 'flag' },\\n      {\",\"content_concise\":\"150→    gifts: [],\\n    par: 6010,\\n    follow: follow({}, 'All three made the morning paper. Alive.'),\\n    reyes: follow({}, 'You went quiet. I noticed.'),\\n    stages: [\\n      {\\n        say: 'Table A. Leg gash.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('a1', 'wound', -0.4, 0.2, { len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0, table: 0 }),\\n          line('a2', 'pool', 1.2, -0.4, { r: 0.65, table: 0 }),\\n160→        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Table B. Debris and burns.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('bdeb', 'debris', -0.6, 0.1, { pull: 1.1, dx: 0.2, dz: 1, table: 1 }),\\n       