116,114,97,105,110,39,32,125,44,10,52,51,57,58,32,32,32,32,32,32,123,32,115,97,121,58,32,39,78,79,32,83,73,71,78,65,76,39,44,32,99,111,100,101,98,108,117,101,58,32,116,114,117,101,44,32,117,110,116,105,108,58,32,39,102,108,97,103,39,44,32,102,108,97,103,58,32,39,98,108,117,101,68,111,110,101,39,32,125,44,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":20,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/ops.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":91,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Midline. Keep it straight.', spawn: [line('cut', 'incision', -0.8, 0.2, { len: 1.6, dx: 1, dz: 0 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":178,\"content\":\"      { say: 'The room goes quiet. Hold your gift.', quiet: true, flag: 'awakened', until: 'flag' },\"},{\"line_number\":226,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Gel along the seams.', spawn: [line('cement', 'gel', 0, 0.1, { w: 2.2, h: 0.8 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":227,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Artery. Suture it now.', spawn: [line('art', 'bleeder', -0.3, -1.1, { len: 1.0, dx: 1, dz: 0.1 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":228,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Paddles. Two good shocks.', codeblue: true, until: 'flag', flag: 'blueDone' },\"},{\"line_number\":263,\"content\":\"      { say: 'It knocked.', strain: 'introit', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":264,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Close the tears.', until: 'kinds', kinds: ['wound', 'pool'] },\"},{\"line_number\":306,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Open.', spawn: [line('kcut', 'incision', -0.5, 1.0, { len: 1.3, dx: 1, dz: 0 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":318,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Lift the failing kidney.', spawn: [line('oldk', 'organ', 0, 0.1, { pull: 1.2, dx: 0.1, dz: 1 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":319,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Donor kidney. The ice starts now.', cold: 120, spawn: [line('newk', 'organ', 2.4, -1.2, { pull: 1.3, dx: -0.4, dz: 1 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"      { say: 'A small cut. Then it weeps.', spawn: [line('lcut', 'incision', -0.4, 1.2, { len: 0.8, dx: 1, dz: 0 })] },\"},{\"line_number\":368,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Eyes open in turn.', strain: 'lacrimosa', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":399,\"content\":\"      { say: 'On the beat. Diastole only.', spawn: [line('hcut', 'incision', -0.3, 1.3, { len: 0.7, dx: 1, dz: 0, window: 'diastole' })] },\"},{\"line_number\":400,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Seven plates.', strain: 'dies', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":401,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Fibrillation. Two shocks.', codeblue: true, until: 'flag', flag: 'blueDone' },\"},{\"line_number\":402,\"content\":\"      { say: 'Massage. Left, then right.', massage: true, until: 'flag', flag: 'massaged' },\"},{\"line_number\":436,\"content\":\"      { say: 'NO SIGNAL', lie: true, strain: 'sanctus', until: 'strain', spawn: [line('ring9a', 'ring', 2.2, -1.2, { optional: true })] },\"},{\"line_number\":437,\"content\":\"      { say: 'NO SIGNAL', strain: 'reprise', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":438,\"content\":\"      { say: 'NO SIGNAL', strain: 'miserere', until: 'strain' },\"},{\"line_number\":439,\"content\":\"      { say: 'NO SIGNAL', codeblue: true, until: 'flag', flag: 'blueDone' },\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"241f7a8c-db2a-429d-a79b-31426203d081"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_430","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Operation 9 likely has four to six stages.\n\nHeader plus six stages fits the layout. Dev mode jump behavior is confirmed: entering an already-entered stage re-spawns, story scenes save correctly, and simulation state persists during scene jumps. FPS tracking will run in update during dev. Session client fixedUpdate returns early so the host alone steers; client prediction uses render delta time.\n\nOnly non-host clients predict movement. The host runs the simulation on its timer and applies hand placement at each tick, snapping to the latest position. Client prediction updates every frame for instant feel. Host mouse input is processed within 34 milliseconds of the timer step.\n\nThe host place bug was caused by stripped placement data, which prevented the snap from reaching the simulation. The fix ensures the next timer tick applies the host placement correctly. A verifier checking one frame without waiting for the tick would see a no-op; the real path is the following step. Predicting the host seat locally in pullSession was considered but rejected to avoid double-movement.\n\nClient-side prediction is confirmed safe for hand placement because the snap is idempotent, but stick input would double speed if predicted on the host. The client sim drifts between snapshots for non-local entities, yet applyDecoded corrects them and the own seat only eases when drift exceeds one unit. Snapshots are not required for the local tip test.\n\nThe client update order will be reversed so input is read before pulling session state. This prevents the aim from being wiped by incoming snapshots. The gentle correction threshold is one unit of drift; beyond that, the client eases back toward the host position by thirty-five percent.\n\nThe client update order is now `readInput`, then `pullSession`, then `predictLocal`. `pullSession` will preserve the local seat’s x and z coordinates so they are not overwritten by incoming snapshots. FPS is tracked as a weighted average of the current frame rate.\n\nThe local session state is built from the current aim and seat data. Mouse placement uses the hit coordinates as x and z, while keyboard input leaves those positions at the seat and only sends stick and button values to the host.\n\nClient prediction integrates stick input each frame. The host seat only moves on the timer, so tests must wait for that step. Client movement is instant and does not need the timer. Both paths will be tested.\n\nA test for `applySnap` will encode the client simulation, overwrite a seat position in the snap to zero, and emit it via the hub. The resulting three-unit drift exceeds the one-unit correction threshold, so the client should ease back toward the host position.\n\nThe applySnap test will encode the simulation after moving the client seat, then overwrite the encoded position to zero so the client eases back toward that origin. A small drift of 0.4 units will be left unchanged.\n\nFor devCheat laceration, the entity kind will be mapped to 'wound' because makeEntity does not set suture slots; the test will assert the menu row displays 'laceration'.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a9e54f7c-9f93-4574-ae18-8e3474e4ded9-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/ops.js","offset":37,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3070,"output_tokens":1946,"cache_read_input_tokens":92032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"7fb22656-5536-44a2-9220-96f49fddc063"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a9e54f7c-9f93-4574-ae18-8e3474e4ded9-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"37→    stages: [\\n      {\\n        say: 'Two pools. Hooks under both.',\\n40→        spawn: [\\n          line('p1', 'pool', -3.1, -1.1, { r: 0.7 }),\\n          line('p2', 'pool', -2.48, -1.1, { r: 0.65 }),\\n          { ...hooks(1)[0], hidden: true, hiddenBy: 'p1' },\\n          { ...hooks(2)[1], hidden: true, hiddenBy: 'p2' },\\n          ...hooks(11).slice(2),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Lacerations. Close them.',\\n50→        spawn: [\\n          line('w1', 'wound', -1.4, 0.8, { len: 1.2, dx: 1, dz: 0 }),\\n          line('w2', 'wound', 1.2, 0.7, { len: 1.1, dx: 1, dz: 0.15 }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Gel the rust. Syringe if he fades.',\\n        unlock: ['syringe'],\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('g1', 'gel', 0.2, -0.4, { w: 1.6, h: 1.0 }),\\n60→          line('ring', 'ring', 2.2, 1.2, { optional: true }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n      {\\n        say: 'Twelve. I counted twelve.',\\n        spawn: [\\n          line('dress', 'dressing', -0.4, 1.4, { len: 1.5, dx: 1, dz: 0.1 }),\\n          line('h12', 'hook', 2.6, -0.8, { pull: 1.0, curve: 0.8, dx: -0.2, dz: 1 }),\\n        ],\\n      },\\n70→    ],\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'op2',\\n    n: 2,\\n    title: 'The Vanishing Act',\\n    patient: 'The Great Zamboni',\\n    age: 51,\\n    job: 'Stage magician',\\n    hook: 'He swallowed the act and will not say which half.',\\n80→    objective: 'Find every prop, then the thing that is not a prop.',\\n    arena: 'stomach',\\n    time: 300,\\n    vitals: { start: 80, drain: 0.15 },\\n    doses: 3,\\n    tools: ['scalpel', 'drain', 'forceps', 'scanner', 'laser', 'suture', 'gel', 'syringe'],\\n    gifts: ['quiet'],\\n    par: 6290,\\n    follow: follow({}, 'The coin turned up in the laundry.'),\\n    reyes: follow({}, 'T