,101,44,32,97,110,100,32,65,98,111,117,116,32,112,97,103,101,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"3. **Drama, sound, and 10-foot play.** Episodes 1–10 and the ending are straight melodrama in the original cast's voices: at most two lines, at most 60 characters, characters the engine font can draw. Surgery is a fixed first-person close-up; story uses talking-head close-ups and wider room shots. Every note, effect, and voice is synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish keyed to the line; a fresh profile sets music to 0.1. The mouse tip hits the raised tissue surface, not a flat floor. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs when that setting is on, key and mouse icons after a key or click. Each pad is read on its own, analog triggers included, and pad buttons do not also press keyboard keys. Screens that exist and work with a pad and with a mouse: title (dark theatre, lamp, EKG, \\\"press to start\\\"), main menu, briefing chart, operation HUD (vitals, clock, composure, comm, tool wheel), results (rank stamp and a follow-up that depends o [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. **gating:** Browser tests, still via the one test command or a filter it documents, assert: pad-stub, keyboard, and mouse each move a menu focus (hover moves focus); prompts swap when the device changes and the Xbox setting swaps glyphs; attract starts after 10 idle seconds and a key or pad exits without touching the save; a Pixel 7 profile shows `Controller or keyboard required`, the settings control, no joystick, and attract running; pause Dev Mode changes a live slider and reset restores it; two stub pads produce two independent tips. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/browser.txt`.\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"- [x] Add title, menus, last-device prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode sliders, attract mode, the touch gate, and About pages.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"c3338cca-88c9-4fdf-8e89-b9db6e0dc12e"}
