wright install`.\\n- Do not read or write sibling agent folders. Do not kill processes you did not start.\\n- Defining mechanics were checked against Wikipedia and StrategyWiki (timed first-person surgery, vitals and clock fails, distinct tools, zigzag suture, precision ranks, nurse prompts, one doctor who slows time and another whose gift differs, defibrillator, pathogen bosses, story between ops). PLAN.md's original names and hold-to-activate gifts replace the source IP on purpose; that is in scope, a star gesture is not.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nKeep the operation rules as plain data plus pure functions so Node can step them with no browser. The view, HUD, and audio only read that state. One bot driver serves attract mode, the partner hand, balance, and the campaign test. Build in PLAN.md §15 order so something is playable early. Bundle last into the single root HTML; do not minify or rewrite the hub session client. Inline the script so `file://` works. The module split in PLAN.md §11 is guidance, not a required layout.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Download the kit and hub files, create the named dev folder, boot an empty scene from `file://`, and add the test runner plus the fresh-profile music default of 0.1.\\n- [x] Implement the pure sim and Operation 1 (drain, forceps, suture, gel, syringe) with the tissue view, hand, and HUD; test those tools.\\n- [x] Add scalpel, laser, scanner, operations 2 and 3, Code Blue, The Quiet, and the bot; assert idle-fail and skill-0.7 clear.\\n- [x] Add story scenes, gibberish voices, music, results, and saves so episodes 1–3 play through.\\n- [x] Add title, menus, last-device prompts, settings, pause, Dev Mode sliders, attract mode, the touch gate, and About pages.\\n- [x] Add the remaining operations, The Second Look, all strains, and the campaign playthrough test.\\n- [x] Add couch Consult, then the hub session, card, and net code; run all five harness scenarios.\\n- [x] Tune to the balance table, write the authoring note, fill About and `exit-interview.json`, emit the root HTML, and save a green `node tests/run.mjs` log plus the two launch captures under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- The zip may be newer than engine 0.46.0, which PLAN.md's spikes used. Read `CHANGELOG.md` and `GUIDE.md`. Do not edit the engine; adapt the game if an API moved.\\n- Several agents share this machine. Bind `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks, and stop only that PID. earlyoom kills the largest browser when memory runs out; keep one or two browsers open.\\n- The HTML filename depends on the RNG title. Write the chosen name in `PROGRESS.md` and `{SCRATCH}/package.txt`.\\n- Skill-1.0 rank S is defined by setting par from that bot's score. A balance run that uses god mode, or a par set below that score, does not pass criterion 2.\\n\",\"total_lines\":56}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"354fa418-1b2a-460a-a5cc-6b6f182851d2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_501","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The code already implements the three fixes.\n\nThe verifier still rejects the candidate. The HTML bundle may be stale. The tests may not cover the behavior. Or a subtle bug remains.\n\nThe skeptic's line numbers refer to pre-fix code. The current fixedUpdate no longer contains the pad branch. This suggests the verifier is running against stale files or a re-injected rejection harness.\n\nThe static read might still see the bug if `device` defaults to `'pad'`. `seatInput` then returns `padInputs` first, and `fixedUpdate` relies on that same flag. The device type only flips to mouse after input events, so the old pad-branch behavior could persist.\n\nEngine call order is being checked. If fixedUpdate runs before readInput, the device flag could lag behind input events. The browser test already shows mouse drain works correctly with idle pads. Session mode also returns early from fixedUpdate and restricts predictLocal to non-host clients.\n\nThe pullSession line number is also stale. The current code at line 435 preserves aim.x via nullish coalescing, while the old version at line 380 overwrote it with seat data. The evaluator's instruction to confirm or regenerate scratch artifacts against the current HTML suggests the rejection may stem from a stale build or outdated test harness.\n\nThe prior completion claim was likely premature. The verifier audits committed tests and saved evidence rather than rebuilding them. A fresh static read of the source should not report the old line numbers if the fixes are already present. This suggests the HTML bundle or test snapshot is still stale.\n\nThe current rejection is a cached stale report re-injected by the harness. I will treat it as the active task and verify whether the three gaps remain unfixed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4b09b8db-c129-4d06-a59a-99957352f773-9","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Dev Mode|frame step|Frame Step|jump","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4b09b8db-c129-4d06-a59a-99957352f773-10","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function testHands|function testSessionHands|padInputs|jumpKind|FRAME STEP|Spawn laceration","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4b09b8db-c129-4d06-a59a-99957352f773-11","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"seatInput|padInputs\\[i\\]|jumpKind|predictSeat|FRAME STEP","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8332,"output_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":38528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"fe948f83-d362-4086-b74c-740bfa2a6177"}
