g `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a4620ef2-fccf-4e5b-a7dd-83d2be9430a7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_507","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The code is genuinely fixed. The skeptic report cites pre-fix line numbers.\n\nThe harness rejected the fixes again. It re-evaluated after compaction and still cited the old bug text. This is concerning.\n\nThe skeptic may be hallucinating the old bug from prompt history. Current line 165 is `const inputs = {};`, so the report likely reflects a cached or mixed-up AST.\n\nThe system prompt itself contains the old bug description, which likely explains the verifier's stale view. Fresh targeted tests will provide current stdout proof. The hand-in files need verification before the round ends with a completion claim. I am also considering whether to strengthen seatInput to prevent static misreads.\n\nThe seatInput method is being reviewed to confirm the fix. It returns padInputs only when a pad is connected, and otherwise routes to humanInput or botInput.\n\nThe device state persists across frames. It only switches from pad to mouse when the engine detects movement, so idle pads do not revert the device type.\n\nThe Playwright mouse-down test passed. The browser correctly keeps the device as mouse after a click with no pointer movement, so humanInput rebuilds each frame and the drain continues. I will run tests to confirm and check evidence files before completing.\n\nThe harness prioritized fixing every gap, so a simple test re-run may not suffice. The skeptic is clearly reading a stale file view. I will run the simulation tests to gather fresh proof for this turn. I am checking how long the balance test takes before running the full suite.\n\nI will run the tests via `node tests/run.mjs` since the test functions are not exported. I need to verify that scratch files exist to confirm evidence is in place. Once the tests pass and the evidence is confirmed, I will mark the remaining todos complete and write a clear completion statement. The test run itself will be kept as an in-progress task.\n\nI will report the current status honestly. The three flagged behaviors are implemented and tested, but the harness alone decides acceptance.\n\nA quick re-review of the current code found no new real bugs. The readInput session early return occurs after buildSeatInputs, and fixedUpdate correctly returns immediately during a session.\n\nHost mouse aim is stored in state.local and applied on the next tick. The host stick uses sx instead of x, so pad device input does not overwrite it. Host stick aim remains safe even when humanInput lacks an x coordinate.\n\nThe host place-aim no-op is fixed. pullSession now preserves aim.x instead of overwriting it with seat.x.\n\napplySnap no longer skips the local player; it eases their position.\n\nI am checking that dev mode HUD tools are actually drawn, not just listed in devRows(). The old file view may have shown settings rows at line 274 rather than the dev tools.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6d5d014-2a07-471a-8aab-d9e2ba857e69-27","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"devTab|devRows|DRAW DEV|mode === 'dev'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/ui/hud.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b6d5d014-2a07-471a-8aab-d9e2ba857e69-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"action === 'spawn'|action === 'stage'|action === 'win'|action === 'blue'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5731,"output_tokens":1680,"cache_read_input_tokens":66432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"2c199a95-c603-447a-999c-b64c04809b29"}
