{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_514","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will write a clear completion message.\n\nThe three skeptic items are fixed and tests pass. I will describe the current behavior directly instead of using contrastive negation.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The three flagged behaviors are already in the shipped game, and the suite that drives them just passed again: `141 passed, 0 failed`.\n\nLast device aims and uses the tool. With an idle pad connected, the drive seat follows the mouse or the keys. The other couch pad still moves on its own stick. A pad that is the last device uses that stick.\n\nIn a hub session the client tip follows the mouse or the stick, and a large snapshot drift eases back while a small one stays. The host's place-aim is stepped into the sim on the session timer.\n\nDev Mode jumps any operation, stage, or story scene. Actions complete, win, fail, trigger Code Blue, spawn a pool, bleeder, laceration, hook, or strain, and copy the op JSON. View has hitboxes, Bot Plays with a skill slider, sim speed from 0.1 to 3, frame step, FPS, and sim stats.\n\nHand-in in this folder: `PROGRESS.md`, `exit-interview.json` (`usage` is `added on import`, genre Simulation, players `1–4`, series Trauma Center), and `The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html`. The embedded session client matches the vendor file (16707 bytes). Launch, browser, hub, audio, and 1920×1080 shots are already saved beside that suite log."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":564,"output_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":79360,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"e4fa408b-f2e9-4677-beb6-920d590de1d8"}
