{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_547","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The last device aims and uses the tool. A client hand follows the mouse or the stick, the host's place-aim reaches the sim, and Dev Mode can jump a stage, spawn, and step one frame.\n\n`seatInput` keeps the drive seat on the mouse or the keys unless the pad was the last device. An idle connected pad still moves the other couch seat. `pullSession` keeps an aimed `x`/`z`, and `applySnap` eases only that player's seat when the snapshot is more than 1 unit away. Dev Mode, opened from pause, lists operations, stages, and scenes, and its actions and view tools include spawn, frame step, FPS, and sim stats.\n\nThe rebuilt HTML is `The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html`. The embedded session client is still the vendor file, 16707 bytes. `node tests/run.mjs` is `149 passed, 0 failed`, including those paths driven through `readInput`. The browser suite on that file is `16 passed, 0 failed`: the idle-pad mouse drain goes from radius 0.7 to done with the device still `mouse`."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":882,"output_tokens":280,"cache_read_input_tokens":133120,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"fcf9bb73-ff1f-4df8-8e1e-f3ce094e4fea"}
