{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_559","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bugs do not remain. The evaluator would have required fixes if they had.\n\nA lone factual overlap remains: `fixedUpdate` returns early when `this.session` is set. The hand actually moves in `update` via `predictLocal`. A skeptical reader might wrongly claim the hand never moves and that `applySnap` is skipped or overwritten, but both claims are false.\n\nThe evaluator's combined bug description is a false trinity. Only the first premise is true; the other two are false. One fix would be to predict inside fixedUpdate when a session exists, avoiding double-prediction in update.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-93d4ede8-490f-474e-bd76-e100ccdad9a1-113","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040\" && node tests/run.mjs hands","description":"Re-run hand, session, and Dev Mode tests"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3643,"output_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":154112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"e73eba5a-4b92-4468-9532-282ab29b645a"}
