{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_572","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to examine predictSeat, pickDev jump logic, and tests to determine whether they drive the real execution path or merely set internal state.\n\nI also need to verify whether laceration maps to wound kind and if client prediction actually moves the seat via step or moveSeats. I spotted a potential bug in applySnap: it only corrects local seat when drift exceeds 1 by 35%, while local prediction should handle movement itself. I should read predictSeat to confirm. For host mouse, pullSession preserves aimed x/z when aim.x is set, and hostInputs merges state.local place and coordinates; this works if humanInput carries place and x. I need to read the test to confirm the host place reaches the simulation.\n\nDev mode pauses automatic simulation stepping, so frame step remains the only manual advancement path. The pickDev implementation for jumping to a specific stage and scene still needs to be written.\n\nThe applySnap correction is intentional: it only nudges the client when drift exceeds one unit, leaving small prediction errors alone. A seatInput fix ensures mouse and keyboard input takes precedence over pad input whenever a drive device is connected.\n\nMouse input reaches the drive seat and advances the simulation correctly. I still need to verify whether the tests are theater.\n\nI am reading run.mjs around lines 470-750. The test expects laceration to map to wound kind after spawning, so makeEntity must perform that mapping. I need to verify whether the dev jump test actually triggers pause menu confirmation or merely sets devTab directly. Tests import source modules rather than the bundle, and FINAL_RESPONSE confirms HTML was rebuilt.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2e411b4a-a66f-4cd3-801f-dae168cb6ed4-87","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function predictSeat|export function predictSeat","path":"/home