":[{\"line_number\":1126,\"content\":\"    if (spec.kind === 'strain') {\"},{\"line_number\":1130,\"content\":\"    if (spec.kind === 'laceration') spec.kind = 'wound';\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/strains.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"  if (s.name === 'introit') tickIntroit(sim, s, dt, speed);\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"cf59a95e-05ea-4d5d-a43d-638ad22157ad"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_574","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The prior gaps appear genuinely fixed.\n\nSeat input now prefers human input on non-pad devices. Tests verify the pool drains and keys move seats correctly.\n\nSession pulling preserves aimed x/z. Predicted seat positions use real movement logic. Drift easing applies when drift exceeds one unit. Tests check seat position and sent packets against a stubbed ray point.\n\nDev mode supports stage jumps, frame stepping, FPS display, and spawning different object kinds.\n\nTests exercise the pause menu and dev menu through real key events. The host update order appears correct. A bug was spotted: predictLocal only runs when !isHost.\n\nHost hand movement comes from the host timer step and local inputs, not predictLocal. The host sees its own hand lag one tick between 34ms updates, which is acceptable.\n\nA client update ordering issue was spotted: readInput builds humanInput from the ray before pullSession copies aim.\n\nThe shellCtx rayAt stub is intentional for tests. Production uses the real engine ray.\n\nI should verify the HTML bundle includes the latest fixes.\n\nDev scene jumps skip saving. They set story mode and check attract.\n\nScene jump selection maps focus 2 to scene index 1. The test passed and confirmed the correct scene ID.\n\nFrame stepping remains active during simHold.\n\nLocal play still steps in fixedUpdate. Session updates rely on prediction and the host timer.\n\nHost local inputs take precedence over network inputs when merging.\n\nClient place packets include local x and z coordinates. The applySnap identity check works correctly because hub.me is a number. predictLocal uses hub.me as the seat index, which aligns with createOp seat counts. I need to verify whether the devCheat strain spawn actually starts a real strain or merely sets a test flag.\n\nThe devCheat strain spawn creates a real strain entity named 'introit', which the test validates. Laceration maps to the wound kind in the simulation, which is correct. Frame stepping during dev mode does not advance if the phase has already won. I will grep the compiled HTML or bundle for predictSeat, lastIsPad, and FRAME STEP to confirm the latest fixes are actually present in the deliverable.\n\nThe LIST OPS label change is correct. When jumpKind is 'op', the first row shows 'LIST OPS' and left or right cycles through the list.\n\nA potential client-side bug was spotted: mouse prediction uses the engine update delta time, but moveSeat place ignores that dt and snaps directly to x and z. Stick input correctly applies dt.\n\nMouse delta correctly sets the pointed flag, so idle pads do not hijack input. The 0.28 deadzone filters out tiny axis noise from connected pads.\n\nIf a pad axis sits slightly above the deadzone while the mouse is active, the mouse wins because it is checked first in the device selection chain. If the pointer stops moving and the pad stays idle, the device flag does not reset; the seat input continues using the last active device.\n\ntryLook still indexes inputs by seat ID rather than string, but this is a pre-existing issue and was not introduced by the current refactor.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f69627ff-593e-410d-9417-07d5b78662d9-94","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"predictSeat|lastIsPad|FRAME STEP|LIST STAGES","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f69627ff-593e-410d-9417-07d5b78662d9-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"predictSeat|FRAME STEP","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/dist/bundle.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f69627ff-593e-410d-9417-07d5b78662d