  }\\n790→  if (want.has('content')) testContent();\\n  if (want.has('audio')) testAudio();\\n  if (want.has('browser') || want.has('launch') || want.has('hub')) {\\n    const live = await import('./live.mjs');\\n    if (want.has('browser')) await live.browser(root, check);\\n    if (want.has('launch')) await live.launch(root, check);\\n    if (want.has('hub')) await live.hub(root, check);\\n  }\\n  if (fails.length) {\\n    for (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f);\\n800→  }\\n  console.log(`${passed} passed, ${fails.length} failed`);\\n  process.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n}\\n\\nmain();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":777,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"async function main() {\\n  if (want.has('sim') || want.has('cal') || want.has('hands')) {\\n    if (!want.has('hands')) {\\n      testTools();\\n      testGifts();\\n      testRankSlidersCodec();\\n      testBalance(arg === 'cal');\\n    }\\n    if (want.has('sim') || want.has('hands')) {\\n      testHands();\\n      testSessionHands();\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (want.has('content')) testContent();\\n  if (want.has('audio')) testAudio();\\n  if (want.has('browser') || want.has('launch') || want.has('hub')) {\\n    const live = await import('./live.mjs');\\n    if (want.has('browser')) await live.browser(root, check);\\n    if (want.has('launch')) await live.launch(root, check);\\n    if (want.has('hub')) await live.hub(root, check);\\n  }\\n  if (fails.length) {\\n    for (const f of fails) console.log('FAIL ' + f);\\n  }\\n  console.log(`${passed} passed, ${fails.length} failed`);\\n  process.exit(fails.length ? 1 : 0);\\n}\\n\\nmain();\\n\",\"total_lines\":805}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"86410254-d956-4cbf-8430-666d6f361b57"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_575","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests look honest. The HTML contains the fix.\n\nChecking for a real remaining bug or regression. The client drift correction logic looks correct. It gently nudges the local tip back when drift exceeds one unit.\n\nA potential bug in testHandsOnInput was found. On the first frame, the device becomes mouse. On the next frame, pointerMoved is false because the pointer position matches the previous frame. The device stays mouse instead of switching to pointer.\n\nThe test passed and the pool drained correctly. The 151 tests versus 117 previously suggests 34 new checks were added, though roughly 16 of those appear to be counted already.\n\nThe 34 new tests likely account for the jump from 117 to 151. A spot-check of the hands tests would confirm the captured results.\n\nRunning `node tests/run.mjs hands` is cheap because it skips the expensive balance suite. This spot-check will verify whether the captured test results match the current code.\n\nThe hands-only run should finish in seconds. The applySnap rounding and message handler ordering look correct. A pre-existing host pump catch swallows errors, but that is not a new regression.\n\nScene jumps correctly pause the operation simulation. The story scene list index mapping needs verification. The test presses ArrowRight twice from the operation list, then ArrowDown twice to select a scene. The second scene ID must be 'rounds'. The test passed, so this mapping is likely correct.\n\nThe couch consult keyboard and pad regression is fixed. Seat 0 now uses the mouse input while seat 1 uses its pad, preventing both seats from moving right. This also resolves the independent tips issue when the last device was not the pad. When a pad is active, keyboard input is correctly ignored. All gaps appear resolved.\n\nThe predictLocal guard requires mode to be session. syncSessionMode sets this before readInput and pullSession run. The test manually sets the mode first. In real play the start event creates the simulation and time becomes non-negative. This ordering looks correct.\n\nThe client prediction and host snapshot share the same simulation state. This is safe because the snapshot can correct any seat movement that prediction makes.\n\nThe local seat tool is not set by applySnap. It is set by predictSeat from input.tool. If the mouse does not send a tool, the seat keeps its previous tool. This is acceptable.\n\nFor host mouse placement, the shell ray starts at (2.2, 6, -0.8) with downward direction. The intersection calculation yields x = 2.2 and z = -0.8. Then the y coordinate is set to heightAt.\n\nThe host placement ray converges to x ≈ 2.2, satisfying the test tolerance. The seat snaps to this aim after roughly four steps because moveSeats runs every frame with place enabled. A potential naming bug was spotted: the client \"stick\" test actually uses KeyD, which sets sx rather than a true stick input.\n\nA bug was found in pad input handling for client seats other than zero. The code copies humanInput from padInputs[0], which is the local player's own controller. This means a client seat with device set to 'pad' receives its own pad input instead of the host's intended pad data.\n\nThe suspected pad input bug is not a real defect. Each client treats its own pad as index zero, so the local seat receives the correct input. The couch local mapping is also correct. Tests cover this for non-zero seats. This issue is not refuted.\n\nFrame step advances the simulation even when no human input is present, so the dev mode test passes. The FPS display updates correctly from the 1/60 second delta. The jump stage index calculation is also correct, mapping focus 2 to stage index 1.\n\nThe applySnap zero-position edge case is safe. A snapshot seat at x=0 correctly triggers drift correction because 0 is not nullish. The easing math passes the test bounds. The fix is considered genuinely resolved.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e157dcd2-5141-4ddd-af8f-a4cc895dce8d-98","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"id: '","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/content/story.js","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e157dcd2-5141-4ddd-af8f-a4cc895dce8d-99","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node tests/run.mjs hands","description":"Re-run the new hand and dev-mode tests","block_until_ms":60000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3496,"output_tokens":2756,"cache_read_input_tokens":193920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"edd7ea4e-d3c0-4cff-9866-b75ddacd47bd"}
