* (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\\n520→```js\\nconst LOOK = (sat = 1, vig = .3, spread = 0) => ({\\n  scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: vig } }, { id: 'adjust', params: { saturation: sat, contrast: 1 } }, { id: 'chromatic', params: { spread } }],\\n  actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: .85, crease: .2 }, filters: [] },\\n  environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0, crease: 0 }, filters: [] },\\n});\\n```\\nThe split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔. Tag every tool, hand, strain and character with `setLookLayer(obj, 'actors')`.\\n\\n**Camera in surgery:** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 9.6, 3.1], target: [0, 0, 0.1], fov: 44, minZoom: 1, maxZoom: 1 }`.\\n530→\\n- ✔ Without the min/max lock the mouse wheel zooms the \\\"fixed\\\" camera, and wheel is our tool cycle.\\n- ✔ Enter and WASD don't disturb a fixed rig.\\n- ✔ Move the camera for parallax, dives and whip-pans by setting `ctx.camera.camera.position` and `.lookAt()` each frame; it sticks and `rayAt` follows. Add ±0.25 units of drift toward the tip.\\n- For narrow windows multiply the camera's distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)`.\\n\\n**Lighting.**\\n\\n- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\\n- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\\n540→- Never `new PointLight`; use `ctx.lights`.\\n\\n**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\\n\\n- ✔ Copying the base into the buffer and painting 60 blood discs measured about 0.5 ms a frame.\\n- Mapping ✔: `px = (x / 16 + .5) · W`, `py = (z / 9 + .5) · H`, and **flip the plane's UV v** (`uv.setY(i, 1 - uv.getY(i))`), or the paint lands mirrored.\\n- Set `magFilter`/`minFilter` Nearest and `needsUpdate` after each paint.\\n- Each frame: write the prebuilt base into the buffer, then paint scars, pools, wounds, stitches, gel and burns from sim state. Displace the mesh by `heightAt` plus heartbeat, breathing and bulges, then `computeVertexNormals()`.\\n\\nBase painting recipe (✔ the look, shown for the heart; each arena has its own ramp and shape):\\n550→```js\\nconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5];\\nconst RAMP = [0x3c0d24, 0x5e1430, 0x8a1f38, 0xb5343f, 0xd65c4f];      // dark to light, 5 steps\\n// per texel: m = shape mask (0 outside the organ); light = 0.25 + 0.75*m + (fbm(x*.9, z*.9) - .5)*.9 + tilt;\\n// index = floor(clamp(light)*5 + BAYER[(px&3) + (py&3)*4]/16*.9 - .2) into RAMP (ordered dither between bands)\\n// outside the organ: a dark cavity colour (0x1c0a18) with noise blotches of RAMP[0]\\n// then: fat blobs (0xe9c46a) where fbm(x*1.6, z*2.4) > .66 near edges\\n//       vessels: random-walk branches (heading += noise*.55, step .09, width 2 then 1, branch at 4.5%), arteries 0xf08a5d, veins 0x2e1a52\\n//       wet sheen: a few hundred single 0xf6d0c0 texels on the light-facing side\\n```\\n560→\\n| Arena | Ramp feel, shape |\\n|---|---|\\n| forearm | tan skin ramp, hair flecks, teal drape window |\\n| stomach | pink-salmon, folded rugae lines |\\n| 3 tables | one skin ramp each, small windows |\\n| bone | dark muscle with a white bone silhouette |\\n| liver | deep maroon, two big lobes |\\n| kidney bed | fat-yellow bed, kidney bean mesh (plum to red tween) |\\n| lung | grey-pink, dotted alveoli, breathing |\\n570→| heart | the recipe above |\\n| whole chest | ribs, lung and heart together |\\n| spine | pale ivory and cool shadow |\\n\\nFrame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\\n\\n**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\\n\\n```js\\nexport const handDef = model({ id:'glove-hand', about:'Gloved surgeon hand gripping a shaft, wrist toward +Z', tags:['character','hand'], floats:true,\\n580→  palette:{ glove:'sky', fold:'blue', sleeve:'teal' }, parts:[\\n  { name:'palm', box:[.72,.3,.8], at:[0,0,0], c:'glove' }, { name:'knuck', box:[.74,.16,.14], at:[0,.12,-.34], c:'fold' },\\n  ...[-.27,-.09,.09,.27].flatMap((x,i)=>[{ name:`f${i}a`, box:[.16,.16,.34], at:[x,.05,-.56], rot:[18,0,0], c:'glove' },{ name:`f${i}b`, box:[.15,.15,.26], at:[x,-.09,-.76], rot:[58,0,0], c:'glove' }]),\\n  { name:'thumb', box:[.18,.18,.5], at:[-.44,-.04,-.26], rot:[10,-28,0], c:'glove' },\\n  { name:'cuff', cyl:[.62,.62,.3], at:[0,0,.54], rot:[90,0,0], c:'fold' }, { name:'wrist', cyl:[.56,1.6,.56], at:[0,0,1.46], rot:[90,0,0], c:'glove' },\\n  { name:'sleeve', cyl:[.8,2.6,.8], at:[0,0,3.4], rot:[90,0,0], c:'sleeve' } ]});\\n```\\n\\n- ✔ Placement that read well: tool at `(x, surface + .05, z)`, rotation `(-.5, -.7, 0)`; hand at `tip + (.88, 1.1, 1.25)`, rotation `(-.46, -.72, .2)`.\\n- Seats 2 to 4 enter from other corners. Glove colour follows the seat: palette `red`, `blue`, `green`, `sand` in 3D; `info.players[i].color` exactly on the HUD (`hud.text` colours take numbers).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":470,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"  - **Comm bust:** a tiny real 3D bust of the speaker placed near the camera at the top-left corner, with `castShadow = false`, so in-op talk uses the same models and mouth animation.\\n- **Results:** the chart drops in. Lines tally one at a time with ticks: time, vitals, technique, streak, mistakes. Rank stamp slams with shake, then a Reyes comment, then the patient's follow-up line for that rank.\\n- **Pause (Options/Esc):** Resume, Retry Stage, Restart, Settings, **Dev Mode**, Quit to Menu. Use your own pause flag and stop stepping the sim. ✔ Don't use `engine.paused`: `update()` stops running and your menu dies. Disabled in a session.\\n- **Settings** (own HUD screen, navigable by pad):\\n  - Music (**10% default**), Sound, Voices.\\n  - Button glyphs (PlayStation/Xbox), Aim Assist, Cursor Speed, Rumble, Gift Hold/Toggle.\\n  - Look (engine looks), Pixel Size, Screen Shake, Reduce Flashes, Text Speed, Difficulty, Fullscreen, Reset.\\n- **About/Credits:** paged, big text. Pages: Source Information; Testing Feedback; Engine Feedback; Prompt Feedback; Credits. All field labels and answers as your brief lists them. Data in `src/content/about.js`, filled in last. Credits condense the kit's `CREDITS.md` (engine MIT, three.js, Rapier, Kenney furniture CC0) and the game's own \\\"all art and audio written in code\\\".\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect before `Engine.start`: no `(any-pointer: fine)`, `maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad. ✔ Phones report art like 136×276 at 8×, so the HUD would be a narrow column.\\n\\n- Show a DOM overlay with the exact text `Controller or keyboard required`, plus the engine's ⚙: ✔ `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` shows it on a phone profile and a tap opens the DOM panel.\\n- `touch: false` always: ✔ no joystick appears.\\n- The attract mode loops behind the message.\\n- If a key is pressed or a pad connects, drop the gate and play normally.\\n\\n**Attract mode.** 10 s with no input on Title or any menu screen starts it. Input means a key, click, mouse move, stick beyond deadzone, pad button or touch; each resets the timer.\\n\\n- A looping reel of real sim segments of 20 to 30 s each, played by the bot with cheats (god vitals, free Composure): a talking-head snippet, Op 1 hooks, Op 2 scan and laser, Op 3 table swaps, Bone Mend, Introit with The Quiet, Second Look rewind, Lacrimosa, Dies Irae with Code Blue, then Pile-Up with four hands.\\n- Banner `DEMO - PRESS ANY BUTTON`. Any input exits at once to Title and is swallowed.\\n- It must never touch saves or settings.\\n\\n**Dev Mode** (from Pause; tabs on L1/R1, Q/E or click):\\n\\n- **BALANCE:** live sliders, Reset to Defaults (list in section 12).\\n- **CHEATS:** God Vitals, Infinite Composure, Freeze Clock, Unlimited Mistakes, Unlock All.\\n- **JUMP:** any op and stage, any story scene.\\n- **ACTIONS:** Complete Stage, Win Op, Fail Op, Trigger Code Blue, Spawn (pool, bleeder, laceration, hook, strain), Copy Op JSON to console.\\n- **VIEW:** hitbox overlay (entity circles and ids), Bot Plays (with skill slider), Sim Speed 0.1× to 3×, Frame Step, FPS and sim stats.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Art direction: what works\\n\\nThe engine's native style is low-poly 3D turned into pixel art. My mock of the heart arena with this recipe looked like a shipped game. Keep to these numbers unless you can beat them.\\n\\n**Framing.** `aspect: 'fill'` always. ✔ It gives no black bars:\\n\\n| Viewport | Art resolution | Scale |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1920×1080 | 480×270 | ×4 |\\n| 3840×2160 | 480×270 | ×8 |\\n| 1280×720 | 427×240 | ×3 |\\n| 1024×768 | 342×256 | ×3 |\\n| 800×600 | 400×300 | ×2 |\\n| 600×400 | 600×400 | ×1 |\\n\\nWithout it, 1280×720 letterboxes to 960×540. Lay out all HUD from anchors.\\n\\n**The look** (✔ crisp outlines on tools and creatures, none on tissue):\\n```js\\nconst LOOK = (sat = 1, vig = .3, spread = 0) => ({\\n  scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: vig } }, { id: 'adjust', params: { saturation: sat, contrast: 1 } }, { id: 'chromatic', params: { spread } }],\\n  actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: .85, crease: .2 }, filters: [] },\\n  environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0, crease: 0 }, filters: [] },\\n});\\n```\\nThe split look renders two passes (about a third of the frame rate on software WebGPU here). That's fine: your brief puts performance out of scope. `sixteen_bit` dithers the whole frame and hurts readability ✔. Tag every tool, hand, strain and character with `setLookLayer(obj, 'actors')`.\\n\\n**Camera in surgery:** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 9.6, 3.1], target: [0, 0, 0.1], fov: 44, minZoom: 1, maxZoom: 1 }`.\\n\\n- ✔ Without the min/max lock the mouse wheel zooms the \\\"fixed\\\" camera, and wheel is our tool cycle.\\n- ✔ Enter and WASD don't disturb a fixed rig.\\n- ✔ Move the camera for parallax, dives and whip-pans by setting `ctx.camera.camera.position` and `.lookAt()` each frame; it sticks and `rayAt` follows. Add ±0.25 units of drift toward the tip.\\n- For narrow windows multiply the camera's distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)`.\\n\\n**Lighting.**\\n\\n- Field ✔: sun intensity 1.0 from `[.25, 1, .35]`, ambient 0.55 warm white (`0xfff0e0`), one point light at `[0, 5.2, .4]`, intensity 5, radius 15. Much more than that washes the tissue out.\\n- OR-7 wide ✔: sun 0.35, ambient 0.28 cool (`0x8fa8c8`), lamp point light over the table at intensity 14, radius 7, a monitor glow. A dark room with a pool of light is the mood.\\n- Never `new PointLight`; use `ctx.lights`.\\n\\n**The tissue canvas** is the game's signature. Each table has a 480×270 RGBA `DataTexture` on a 192×108 `PlaneGeometry` in `toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map })` with `receiveShadow`.\\n\\n- ✔ Copying the base into the buffer and painting 60 blood discs measured about 0.5 ms a frame.\\n- Mapping ✔: `px = (x / 16 + .5) · W`, `py = (z / 9 + .5) · H`, and **flip the plane's UV v** (`uv.setY(i, 1 - uv.getY(i))`), or the paint lands mirrored.\\n- Set `magFilter`/`minFilter` Nearest and `needsUpdate` after each paint.\\n- Each frame: write the prebuilt base into the buffer, then paint scars, pools, wounds, stitches, gel and burns from sim state. Displace the mesh by `heightAt` plus heartbeat, breathing and bulges, then `computeVertexNormals()`.\\n\\nBase painting recipe (✔ the look, shown for the heart; each arena has its own ramp and shape):\\n```js\\nconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5];\\nconst RAMP = [0x3c0d24, 0x5e1430, 0x8a1f38, 0xb5343f, 0xd65c4f];      // dark to light, 5 steps\\n// per texel: m = shape mask (0 outside the organ); light = 0.25 + 0.75*m + (fbm(x*.9, z*.9) - .5)*.9 + tilt;\\n// index = floor(clamp(light)*5 + BAYER[(px&3) + (py&3)*4]/16*.9 - .2) into RAMP (ordered dither between bands)\\n// outside the organ: a dark cavity colour (0x1c0a18) with noise blotches of RAMP[0]\\n// then: fat blobs (0xe9c46a) where fbm(x*1.6, z*2.4) > .66 near edges\\n//       vessels: random-walk branches (heading += noise*.55, step .09, width 2 then 1, branch at 4.5%), arteries 0xf08a5d, veins 0x2e1a52\\n//       wet sheen: a few hundred single 0xf6d0c0 texels on the light-facing side\\n```\\n\\n| Arena | Ramp feel, shape |\\n|---|---|\\n| forearm | tan skin ramp, hair flecks, teal drape window |\\n| stomach | pink-salmon, folded rugae lines |\\n| 3 tables | one skin ramp each, small windows |\\n| bone | dark muscle with a white bone silhouette |\\n| liver | deep maroon, two big lobes |\\n| kidney bed | fat-yellow bed, kidney bean mesh (plum to red tween) |\\n| lung | grey-pink, dotted alveoli, breathing |\\n| heart | the recipe above |\\n| whole chest | ribs, lung and heart together |\\n| spine | pale ivory and cool shadow |\\n\\nFrame every arena with raised teal drapes (boxes, `y` 0.4), steel clamps and retractors. Pools, blood and wounds use 2 or 3 flat colours with animated sparkle texels, plus particles for droplets, smoke and foam (`ctx.particles.register`; sizes are whole art pixels).\\n\\n**The hand and instruments.** Each is `model()` data with the tip at the origin, pointing −Z. A gloved hand plus forearm from below the frame sells first-person presence, and its cast shadow gives depth ✔.\\n\\n```js\\nexport const handDef = model({ id:'glove-hand', about:'Gloved surgeon hand gripping a shaft, wrist toward +Z', tags:['character','hand'], floats:true,\\n  palette:{ glove:'sky', fold:'blue', sleeve:'teal' }, parts:[\\n  { name:'palm', box:[.72,.3,.8], at:[0,0,0], c:'glove' }, { name:'knuck', box:[.74,.16,.14], at:[0,.12,-.34], c:'fold' },\\n  ...[-.27,-.09,.09,.27].flatMap((x,i)=>[{ name:`f${i}a`, box:[.16,.16,.34], at:[x,.05,-.56], rot:[18,0,0], c:'glove' },{ name:`f${i}b`, box:[.15,.15,.26], at:[x,-.09,-.76], rot:[58,0,0], c:'glove' }]),\\n  { name:'thumb', box:[.18,.18,.5], at:[-.44,-.04,-.26], rot:[10,-28,0], c:'glove' },\\n  { name:'cuff', cyl:[.62,.62,.3], at:[0,0,.54], rot:[90,0,0], c:'fold' }, { name:'wrist', cyl:[.56,1.6,.56], at:[0,0,1.46], rot:[90,0,0], c:'glove' },\\n  { name:'sleeve', cyl:[.8,2.6,.8], at:[0,0,3.4], rot:[90,0,0], c:'sleeve' } ]});\\n```\\n\\n- ✔ Placement that read well: tool at `(x, surface + .05, z)`, rotation `(-.5, -.7, 0)`; hand at `tip + (.88, 1.1, 1.25)`, rotation `(-.46, -.72, .2)`.\\n- Seats 2 to 4 enter from other corners. Glove colour follows the seat: palette `red`, `blue`, `green`, `sand` in 3D; `info.players[i].color` exactly on the HUD (`hud.text` colours take numbers).\\n\",\"total_lines\":893}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"a72e0614-837b-4c3c-8f59-7729cbdb40be"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_584","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to verify whether the three prior bugs are actually fixed.I need to carefully review the prior bugs to confirm they are actually fixed.\n\nBug 1 involves pad\n\nChecking gap 1: pad input overriding mouse inputs override human and keyboard. The seatInput input in fixedUpdate. method is being examined The seatInput code  to see if it prioritizes pad axes over humanis being reviewed to input. see if this is fixed.\n\nThe seatInput method now checks `this.device === 'pad'` to prioritize pad input. fixedUpdate\n\nThe seatInput logic is also being reviewed. appears to fix gap 1. It prioritizes human input when the drive seat's last device is not a pad, and only falls back to pad inputs when both conditions are met.\n\nThe fixedUpdate loop now applies seatInput to every seat. The last-device logic is confirmed: when the device is mouse or keyboard, the drive \n\nThe condition orderingseat uses humanInput is correct. The drive even if pad data exists. seat with a mouse input buildSeatInputs also copies pad axes into matches the humanInput humanInput whenever branch first. Idle  the device is pad.pad inputs are intentionally preserved when the last device was a pad.\n\nThe device switch logic is being scrutinized. `pads.any` might remain true for idle pads, which could cause unwanted\n\n`lastIsPad` is global, switching back to pad input. The tests also not per-seat. When  bypass `readInput` the last device was by setting inputs directly,a pad, every seat with so the actual human-to-pad a pad input receives transition path may it. The drive seat  not be fully covered.without a pad falls back to humanInput, which copies padInputs[0] when the device is pad.\n\nThe tests may be setting device and humanInput directly, which could hide the real input transition path.\n\nBug 2 is still present. fixedUpdate returns\n\nThe humanInput assignment early when a session exists, so the simulation logic is correct for never steps locally all three device modes. during a session. This prevents non-host hands Gap 1 is fixed only if tests exercise it. from moving. Idle pad axes may still be a problem.\n\nHost stepping now happens in sessionTick via hostInputs. Clients use predictLocal instead.\n\nMouse input correctly\n\napplySnap blends the ignores pad data, so local player's position the pool drains properly. only when the distance exceeds one unit. Other The concern is whether seats receive a direct idle connected pads copy of x and z.\n\npullSession set `pads.any`, which now prefers aimed coordinates over the current seat would keep the device position if aim.x is stuck on pad mode and set.\n\nI still need  prevent mouse or keyto verify whether client activation. tips follow mouse or stick input, and whether host mouse aim reaches the simulation. I will read predictSeat next.\n\nThe host's local simulation state is updated through sessionTick, which copies the synced session.sim into this.sim. HostInputs merges local input into the host's own seat. A potential ordering bug exists in update(): readInput runs before the session check, so humanInput may be set before pullSession processes it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a03851e-bb13-4878-a0cb-cdd7d8b9c4a9-6","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/input/devices.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a03851e-bb13-4878-a0cb-cdd7d8b9c4a9-7","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"seatInput|humanInput|padInputs|frameStep|devTab|jumpKind|spawn|last device|idle pad|predictSeat|place","glob":"**/tests/**/*.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4a03851e-bb13-4878-a0cb-cdd7d8b9c4a9-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"last device|Dev Mode|frame step|idle pad|client tip|host place","glob":"**/PLAN.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11476,"output_tokens":1308,"cache_read_input_tokens":33536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"3ce29532-382f-4a6f-8fe4-08e3ae727920"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4a03851e-bb13-4878-a0cb-cdd7d8b9c4a9-6","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\\n\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n10→  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n20→\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n30→  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n40→/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n50→  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n60→    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n70→    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n80→}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n90→\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n100→    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n110→  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\\n\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n10→  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n20→\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n30→  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n40→/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n50→  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n60→    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n70→    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n80→}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n90→\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n100→    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n110→  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/input/devices.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\\n\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":117}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4a03851e-bb13-4878-a0cb-cdd7d8b9c4a9-7","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,52,48,95,95,120,50,52,101,98,98,51,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,48,52,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,52,48,