{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_591","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" encodeFast test zeroes seat x, which triggers this correction and brings the seat toward the held position. Small drift is also rounded into the near snapshot.\n\nThe encodeFast test assumes a scale of 20; a different value would break it, so the test suite must be run to confirm. The dev mode jump story path enters scene 1 without saving and sets mode to 'story', which the test expects. The prior gap whereSeat 0 defaults to human. The mouse test uses jump was restricted to ops only is now  this seat.fixed because jumpKind cycles through op, stage, and scene modes and pickJump handles all three, with tests covering both direct calls and input paths. The VIEW tab now includes frame step and FPS/sim stats.\n\nThe frameStep and FPS logic is confirmed correct. The test advances the simulation and checks that the frame rate exceeds ten, which passes because the fixed delta is one-sixtieth of a second.\n\nA potential bug was spotted in the spawn action: it may set sim.strain without actually spawning an entity. The plan lists five spawn kinds, but the strain case might be missing its actual entity creation.\n\nChecking applyDecoded and the client snap path for bugs. Verifying tests.txt is not truncated. Confirming whether run.mjs prints individual check names. Need to verify the suite actually runs the new tests, since tests.txt might be stale evidence.\n\nStrain is a gameplay flag rather than an entity, so the test checks sim.strain.name","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7da8cd31-ac8c-4901-84fe-973aa51fb5fe-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/codec.js","offset":1,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7da8cd31-ac8c-4901-84fe-973