lpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n10→  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n20→\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n30→  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n40→/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n50→  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n60→    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n70→    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n80→}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n90→\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n100→    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n110→  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\\n\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n10→  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n20→\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n30→  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n40→/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n50→  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n60→    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n70→    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n80→}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n90→\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n100→    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n110→  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/input/devices.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"/** Pad polling and last-device prompts. Pads are read here, not merged by the engine. */\\n\\nexport const TOOLS = ['scalpel', 'forceps', 'suture', 'drain', 'syringe', 'gel', 'laser', 'scanner'];\\n\\nconst DEAD = 0.28;\\n\\nexport function readPads() {\\n  const nav = globalThis.navigator;\\n  if (!nav || typeof nav.getGamepads !== 'function') return [];\\n  let list = [];\\n  try {\\n    list = nav.getGamepads() || [];\\n  } catch {\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n  const out = [];\\n  for (const pad of list) if (pad && pad.connected) out.push(pad);\\n  return out;\\n}\\n\\nfunction axis(pad, i) {\\n  const v = pad?.axes?.[i] || 0;\\n  return Math.abs(v) < DEAD ? 0 : v;\\n}\\n\\nfunction button(pad, i) {\\n  const b = pad?.buttons?.[i];\\n  if (!b) return 0;\\n  if (b.pressed) return b.value > 0 ? b.value : 1;\\n  return b.value || 0;\\n}\\n\\nfunction rising(prev, pad, i) {\\n  const down = button(pad, i) > 0.4;\\n  const was = !!prev[i];\\n  prev[i] = down;\\n  return down && !was;\\n}\\n\\n/** One pad's surgical input, plus menu edges. `prev` is a button array this function mutates. */\\nexport function samplePad(pad, prev) {\\n  if (!prev.buttons) prev.buttons = [];\\n  const buttons = prev.buttons;\\n  const sx = axis(pad, 0);\\n  const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n  const rx = axis(pad, 2);\\n  const ry = axis(pad, 3);\\n  const mag = Math.hypot(rx, ry);\\n  let tool = null;\\n  if (mag >= 0.65 && !(prev.flick >= 0.65)) {\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(ry, rx);\\n    const idx = ((Math.round(ang / (Math.PI / 4)) % 8) + 8) % 8;\\n    tool = TOOLS[idx];\\n  }\\n  prev.flick = mag;\\n  const r2 = button(pad, 7);\\n  return {\\n    index: pad.index || 0,\\n    sx,\\n    sz: sy,\\n    rx,\\n    ry,\\n    use: r2 > 0.4 || button(pad, 0) > 0.4,\\n    useEdge: rising(buttons, pad, 0),\\n    gift: button(pad, 6) > 0.4,\\n    steady: button(pad, 4) > 0.4,\\n    back: rising(buttons, pad, 1),\\n    square: rising(buttons, pad, 2),\\n    triangle: rising(buttons, pad, 3),\\n    l1: rising(buttons, pad, 4),\\n    r1: rising(buttons, pad, 5),\\n    options: rising(buttons, pad, 9),\\n    up: rising(buttons, pad, 12) || (sy < -0.55 && !(prev.sy < -0.55)),\\n    down: rising(buttons, pad, 13) || (sy > 0.55 && !(prev.sy > 0.55)),\\n    left: rising(buttons, pad, 14),\\n    right: rising(buttons, pad, 15),\\n    tool,\\n    any: Math.hypot(sx, sy) > 0 || mag > 0 || buttonsDown(pad),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nfunction buttonsDown(pad) {\\n  const list = pad?.buttons || [];\\n  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\\n    const b = list[i];\\n    if (b && (b.pressed || b.value > 0.4)) return true;\\n  }\\n  return false;\\n}\\n\\nexport function sampleAll(memory = { pads: [] }) {\\n  const pads = readPads();\\n  const sampled = [];\\n  let any = false;\\n  pads.forEach((pad, i) => {\\n    const slot = memory.pads[i] || (memory.pads[i] = { buttons: [], flick: 0, sy: 0 });\\n    const row = samplePad(pad, slot);\\n    const sy = axis(pad, 1);\\n    row.up = row.up || (sy < -0.55 && !(slot.sy < -0.55));\\n    row.down = row.down || (sy > 0.55 && !(slot.sy > 0.55));\\n    slot.sy = sy;\\n    if (row.any) any = true;\\n    sampled.push(row);\\n  });\\n  memory.pads.length = pads.length;\\n  return { pads: sampled, any };\\n}\\n\\nexport function promptConfirm(device, glyphs) {\\n  if (device === 'key' || device === 'mouse') return 'ENTER';\\n  return glyphs === 'xbox' ? 'A' : 'CROSS';\\n}\\n\\nexport function toolIndex(name) {\\n  const i = TOOLS.indexOf(name);\\n  return i < 0 ? 0 : i;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":117}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"0691e0d2-4c2e-494d-b961-523ebfa9106a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_593","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"applyDecoded does not overwrite seat positions.\n\napplySnap correctly applies view.seats with a special case for local seat. Device switching logic is sound: idle pads do not steal the last devicetests.txt shows 151  because `pads.any` requires actual stickpassed tests and zero or button activity, and the mouse remains failures. active after movement stops.\n\nMouse ray recasts every frame even without pointer movement. Device switching correctly routes humanInput to the drive seat. WASD keyboard input ignores pads for driving. A\n\nThe one-line test  couch example confirms seat 0 receives mousesummary lacks new assertion input while seat 1  names. I will run thereceives pad input. suite cheaply to verify the tests actually pass.\n\nA potential bug was found: key presses set the device to key before the mouse check runs, and anyKey includes\n\nI am hunting for real bugs in the new logic. keys that are also  I reviewed devCheat,used for menu. hud drawPause, and aimOnSurface. I checked samplePad index handling and client stick tests. I also noticed fixedUpdate returns early when a session exists, but client movement lives in predictLocal during update.\n\nPressing a key permanently sets the device to key until mouse or pad activity occurs. This blocks mouse place \n\nServer and client aim while the key deviceupdate paths are confirmed persists. Tapping a correct. The host place number key during mouse aim timing should work operation also switches in real play. I spotted the device to key and a potential stale-keyboard-aim bug in pullSession: it falls back to seat.x stops place aim until the pointer moves again. when aimedX is null, but key devices never set x, so the fallback may be wrong.\n\nThe tool-switch key press occurs before the device check in readInput. This causes a one-frame loss of mouse place aim and forces the seat to fall back to stick input. It is treated as a minor UX issue rather than a critical defect.\n\nThe keyboard-aim fallback is harmless. predictSeat and moveSeat use the stick delta sx to move the seat instead of teleporting to zero. Mouse place updates every frame while the pointer is held, which is correct. If pads are idle, the device stays mouse and continues updating place. The pad.index check is also safe.\n\nThe last-device prompt logic is correct. A connected idle pad overriding mouse or keyboard input was the actual defect, and \n\nI am now examiningthe fix is verified  the `seatInput` methodthrough readInput and for a potential couch fixedUpdate.\n\nA session bug remains: fixedUpdate or last-device bug. returns early during The function returns sessions. Client movement uses predictLocal,  bot input when the while host movement drive seat is not a relies on the sessionpad but the last device pump with merged local was, which could suppress inputs. human input in that case.\n\npredictLocal runs every frame via update(), not fixedUpdate. predictSeat uses variable frame\n\nThe couch bug theory dt, which is acceptable is incorrect. When  for prediction.\n\nHosta pad is connected but local input merges  idle, the drive seatcorrectly. The host  still returns humansimulation steps only input. When the device during sessionTick  is a pad, buildSeatInputsintervals, and the pump overwrites humanInput with pad data, so seatInput applies place updates to visual seats. Tests returns the pad correctly. The keyboard row can confirm this behavior. carry both stick and place values, but that is expected.\n\nKey presses cancel\n\napplySnap updates remote seat positions mouse place for that and tool state but  frame, which matchesnot use flags, so remote the last-device rule. hands snap to predicted If a key is held while coordinates while local hands are predicted pointing, mouse place and eased. The host takes priority over merges incoming network the lingering stick inputs with local inputs, giving priority to  input.local data for the current player.\n\nI found a real bug in `readInput`. When `holdOff` returns early because no button or movement was detected, the method exits before `buildSeatInputs` runs. This means the device state updates but the seat inputs never get built for that frame.\n\nRemote mouse aim reaches the host simulation because the host steps incoming packets with place:true. The prior gap was specifically the host's own mouse aim, while client tip following stick or mouse is the separate half that is also tested.\n\nA test labeled \"client stick tip\" actually uses KeyD, which maps to keyboard input rather than a physical stick. Keyboard sx serves as the stick equivalent for keyboard devices.\n\nThe holdOff early return is harmless; it only swallows one frame of input. Attract\n\nA potential bug was mode correctly routes to bot input. Dev mode found in pad input  frame stepping duringhandling during sessions. pause works because When the client device fixedUpdate is skipped is pad, `pullSession` and frameStep handles the step. The JUMP  always sets `humanInput` to `padInputs[0]`, which is seat 0's pad data. It does not map the pad to the client's actual seat index, so a player on seat story scene transition preserves simulation state, which is correct. The devCheat stage change test confirms entities spawn properly in the new stage.1 would receive seat 0's pad input instead of their own.\n\nThe pad input concern was unfounded. In a session, each client typically has only one local pad mapped to index 0, so reading padInputs[0] correctly supplies the local player's input regardless","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-92da7c05-13e3-48bc-865f-5408c2a0ebc1-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/game/clinic.js","offset":1,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-92da7c05-13e3-48bc-865f-5408c2a0ebc1-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/sim/op.js","offset":1090,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-92da7c05-13e3-48bc-865f-5408c2a0ebc1-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/src/ui/hud.js","offset":180,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-92da7c05-13e3-48bc-865f-5408c2a0ebc1-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## Verification plan|gating","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5643,"output_tokens":1782,"cache_read_input_tokens":64512,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"43232857-b1ef-4fd5-b201-f5f0c4a85878"}
