ic same-seed hash, codec round-trip and peak snapshot size, every op failing with no input and clearing with the skill-0.7 bot, and the Resident balance table in criterion 2. Run `node tests/run.mjs` from the dev folder. It must print only failures and one count line, and exit 0. Save the stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.txt`.\"},{\"line_number\":19,\"content\":\"2. **gating:** The same command's content checks assert: no `TODO` / placeholder / stub strings, none of the forbidden names, every About field present, story lines within the length and font limits, and a bot playthrough from the first scene through the last op to credits that writes saves and unlocks the log. Those assertions are in the run captured in `{SCRATCH}/tests.txt`.\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"3. **gating:** Load the root HTML twice in headless Chromium (WebGPU software flags from PLAN.md §13, fresh profile, viewport 960×540 or 1920×1080). Each run: zero page errors, `engine` GPU error list empty, canvas art size matches fill-mode for that viewport, painted coverage is most of the frame, music volume is 0.1, and a scripted drain or forceps action at a known target changes that entity's sim state. Screenshot each run to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and write the read state to `{SCRATCH}/launch.txt`. If Chromium cannot start, save the launcher's own error to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.txt` and treat steps 1–2 as the bar. Do not treat a blank successful screenshot as this fallback.\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"4. **gating:** Browser tests, still via the one test command or a filter it documents, assert: pad-stub, keyboard, and mouse each move a menu focus (hover moves focus); prompts swap when the device changes and the Xbox setting swaps glyphs; attract starts after 10 idle seconds and a key or pad exits without touching the save; a Pixel 7 profile shows `Controller or keyboard required`, the settings control, no joystick, and attract running; pause Dev Mode changes a live slider and reset restores it; two stub pads produce two independent tips. Capture to `{SCRATCH}/browser.txt`.\"},{\"line_number\":22,\"content\":\"5. **gating:** Serve the built page and the unmodified hub harness with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, then run the five PLAN.md §13 harness URLs. Each must reach `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Stop that server by its PID. Save results to `{SCRATCH}/hub.txt`.\"},{\"line_number\":23,\"content\":\"6. **gating:** Hash `pixel-engine.js` against the zip and the embedded session client against the fetched file; both equal. `exit-interview.json` parses and matches criterion 1. Record hashes and `python3 -m json.tool` output in `{SCRATCH}/package.txt`.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"5ce8cca6-6128-48c4-8639-4ae39a0345e0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_594","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" of their seat ID. The prior bug assumption does not apply.\n\nClient keyboard movement correctly uses sx, and the host pump doesAll 151 tests passed. not skip stepping because the session is started and time is valid. The client input accumulator reaches the 66 ms threshold, so it sends packets as expected.\n\nThe `allow()` token bucket may block the first sessionTick send if tokens are low. The function returns early from the entire tick when tokens are insufficient, not just from skipping the send.\n\nThe one-line pass output is correct per the verification plan. I need to confirm the captured run includes the new tests. Re-running the full suite would be expensive, so I will check if the prior capture already covers them.\n\napplySnap tests confirm large drifts ease the seat by 35% while small\n\nI will run `node tests/run.mjs drifts are ignored. applyDecoded also restores hands` to spot-check timeLeft and score from snapshots, but  the prior gaps. Thisthat is unrelated to this test. Dev mode is a cheap filter that uses its own pause flag and does not step runs only the hands the simulation. and session hands tests.\n\nFrame step runs once per press and does not trigger fixedUpdate. FPS and simulation statistics appear as menu rows in the dev menu rather than on screen. The devRows test verifies these\n\nI am now inspecting entries. the client stick logic for hidden bugs. The KeyD input path during sessions may have a subtle issue in how it builds seat inputs and returns early.\n\nI need to verify that the HUD actually renders the dev mode rows from `devRows`, since the prior gap required the feature to be visible on screen. The jump-to-scene input path is now tested and confirmed: scene index 1 corresponds to 'rounds'.\n\nClient stick movement checks out. The default cursor speed is high enough to clear the 0.05 threshold.\n\nMouse placement on the client needs `aimOnSurface`. I am scanning `aim.js` for a bug where straight-down rays return the origin x instead of the hit point.\n\nThe host test ray uses a default origin near (2.2, 6, -0.8). I need to verify that vertical aim calculations use this origin correctly.\n\nArrowDown input does\n\nA potential bug in the FIELD clamp logic not move the seat during also needs investigation. dev mode because fixedUpdate is skipped. The stage jump test only checks\n\nThe FIELD clamp hypothesis is resolved. The test that stage index 1  asserts local.x beforeis reached, not that clamping, so FIELD.x the seat moves. must be at least 2.2 for the pass to succeed.\n\nI also need to verify the root HTML bundle was rebuilt. The playable artifact inlines clinic.js and session.js, so a stale bundle would ship the old buggy code.\n\nThe tests import source modules directly, so they can pass while the shipped HTML bundle is stale. I need to verify that dist/bundle.js and the root HTML actually contain the new seatInput\n\nArrowDown input during logic. dev mode does not affect the dev menu. The spawn laceration cheat correctly maps laceration to wound. I am checking whether the spawn function accepts hook as a kind.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe8a5039-c50e-4958-99e8-612bcc0aadc5-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"jumpKind|predictSeat|lastIsPad|FRAME STEP","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040/dist/bundle.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe8a5039-c50e-4958-99e8-612bcc0aadc5-22","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"jumpKind|predictSeat|FRAME STEP|lastIsPad","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-fe8a5039-c50e-4958-99e8-612bcc0a