{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_595","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe spawn function likely accepts hook as a kind without error. The 151-pass result is consistent with roughly 34 new checks added to the prior 117. I will run the hands tests to confirm they pass.\n\nI will run the hands test suite directly to confirm it passes. I am also scanning for any missed bugs before executing it.The bundle includes fixes. I will run the hands tests to confirm they pass and search harder for a real bug.\n\napplySnap also overwrites the simulation phase from the view snapshot. This is a bug because the local simulation should not be driven\n\nChecking whether startStrain by remote phase data. properly sets sim.strain when spawning introit on op1. Verifying the input path test hits the correct menu items. A minor HUD text overlap was noted but dismissed as a non-issue.\n\nThe plan calls for hitbox circles and IDs. The current code only renders text IDs on the HUD. The prior gap did not flag missing circles. I am checking if this was an accepted text-only implementation.\n\nThe `strainDead` flag is never cleared after being set from a remote snapshot, but this is a minor issue outside the current gap. The client hand snaps to its spawn position via prediction on the first mouse update, and the test correctly verifies movement from\n\nThe prior gap only that spawn point. I cited jump ops, frame am now checking whether step, and spawn pools. `aimOnSurface` returns the ray origin's xz Hitbox circles were coordinates, since  not flagged as a defect.the test only validates I will not raise this horizontal plane intersection as a new objection  at y=surface withoutunless it is a demonstrable checking the z coordinate. defect in the shipped behavior.\n\nI will run the test to verify `aimOnSurface` returns the expected x coordinate. I am \n\nThe verification plan'salso checking whether gating items do not mouse input lacks a explicitly require  default tool, whichentity circles. PLAN.md could prevent the drain §8 acceptance criteria action from working. for Dev Mode VIEW include In consult mode, seat hitbox overlays with 0 uses mouse input while seat 1 uses pad. circles and IDs. This suggests the missing circles may be an unmet gating criterion.\n\nI will grep stage.js for hitbox circles. If they were never implemented, the prior round likely accepted text-only IDs. I must verify this before \n\nThe pad idle-zero deciding whether to issue is harmless becauseraise it as a new defect. the test explicitly sets pad sx to -1. The drive input path is safe since readInput and fixedUpdate run in separate engine passes, so state persists correctly. I am now checking whether the engine loop order places fixedUpdate before update, which would delay input by one frame.\n\nThe objective and ","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23243886-bc9f-4efd-89b9-51ed05ad02d0-23","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"input\\.tool|seat\\.tool","glob":"**/src/sim/op.js","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2473,"output_tokens":3656,"cache_read_input_tokens":70528,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"af7a0684-3057-4056-8796-8f2abb987b50"}
