{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_600","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Operation 1 begins with the first tool in theSeat 0 is assigned to the human user when not in consult mode. tools list.\n\nSession mode logic\n\nConsult mode makes checks out. A bug was all seats human. The mouse test uses beginOp without consult, so seat 0 is human. It passes only if the coordinates hit pool p1. I am running it found: the host clinic now. I also checked the session client and input paths for real bugs. The samplePad index logic is fine. Session mode returns early after buildSeatInputs, so keyboard stick input update calls pullSession, does not conflict with menus. which sets local state\n\nHost update logic is correct. The session mode stays set because from mouse input, but hub.time() is zero when the update runs. The first pump at t=0 initializes the simulation properly. The client start handler sets  the host's sessionTickstate.started and state.me. also runs on an interval.\n\nHosts correctly skip applying snaps to themselves. Client snapshots only sync position, not actions, which is standard\n\nThe client runs beginOp locally on start, creating snapshot netcode. A its own operation without waiting for a snapshot. This is acceptable for prediction. The  potential real bug client correctly assigns me as seat 1 and creates two seats. In consultwas spotted: local player mode, predictSeat always moves the seat regardless of human status. easing in `applySnap` only triggers when error exceeds 1.\n\nThe client and host use the same random seed for deal generation, which is acceptable for tests. I need to verify that applySnap\n\n`applyDecoded` overwrites and encodeFast are the real implementations so the test does not accidentally match  entity positions, time,buggy code. I also noticed that sessionTick catches errors without rethrowing them. and score from the host snapshot before local seat correction. This can fight prediction for entities, but the hand position gap is already handled.\n\nDev mode FPS and simulation stats may already be visible in the HUD menu list, which would satisfy the prior requirement.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1eb5c303-5e73-49d2-a1ee-74e521979cf6-29","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"sim\\.t\\b|\\.t =","glob":"**/src/sim/op.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1eb5c303-5e73-49d2-a1ee-74e521979cf6-30","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mode === 'dev'|devRows|listItems","glob":"**/src/ui/hud.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3102,"output_tokens":1062,"cache_read_input_tokens":78080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"94b55e03-0f77-4e24-bfbd-ed7bffe47049"}
