{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_603","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" In `samplePad`, the `any` flag is false when no stick, trigger, or button is active.SCENES[1] is 'rounds'. Focus 2 is index 1.\n\nThe `any` flag stays false for idle pads because `axis()` deadzones values below 0.28. Button noise is out of scope.\n\nA device-switching bug was found: when switching from keyboard to pad, the code returns `humanInput` immediately without merging the new pad state. When switching from mouse to pad, `humanInput` still carries both keyboard stick axes and mouse place, but `moveSeat` checks `place` first.\n\nWhen the mouse is the last active device, its `place` flag overrides WASD stick input because `moveSeat` checks `place` first. The device stays locked to key while WASD is held, so the stick continues moving the seat.\n\nThe three gaps appear\n\nI need to verify the genuinely fixed. The 151 passing tests by running hands directly, review will focus on since the captured  demonstrable defectsfile might be fabricated in the changed code or incomplete. I also rather than minor nits. need to check how entity IDs are generated.\n\nI will inspect the round diff for newly introduced bugs. I also need to verify the hands and session-hands tests actually run and pass, since the test runner only executes them when the `hands` flag is passed.\n\nI'm investigating a potential bug in `applySnap` and `predict`. The client mouse tip test aims at x=2.2, but if the seat spawns too close, the assertion `abs(x - spawnX) > ","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a63893f-5585-4901-b388-6b606a0d48e3-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## Verification plan|## Acceptance criteria|gating","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3%2Fwork/01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4/goal/plan.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a63893f-