{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_614","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" not tested, only mouse. The client `predictLocal` correctly applies `dt` for stick movement but snaps place updates without it. The host hand now advances on pump instead of staying frozen; the prior bug where it never moved is fixed.The bundle includes the fixes. The first grep missed the HTML\n\nThe `sessionTick`  file because it wastry/catch is defensive too large or the path and harmless because glob did not include the test expects movement. the root HTML. The client snap logic correctly ignores small errors while blending large ones; the test confirms a 0.35-unit easing and a 0.4 offset match the code.\n\nThe HTML file is present. A quick hands test will confirm the fix. I am also checking a subtle bug where a session mode return might skip a bump.\n\n`fixedUpdate` returns early when a session exists, so couch games skip local stepping. The host drives the simulation and clients predict only their own seat. Other players and tools are corrected via `applySnap`. This is correct netcode.\n\nThe session return correctly skips the menu bump. Seat inputs build before the session check, and KeyD moves via sx. Host mouse ordering is correct: seat inputs are built first, then readInput runs, then pullSession follows. A NaN edge case with aimedX is irrelevant.\n\nDev mode correctly\n\napplySnap correctly freezes the simulation updates entities before during menu browsing seats via applyDecoded. so frame stepping works. The client only predicts seat movement locally, The win-op selection not tool application. transitions the phase Tool effects require the host snap to return to won and then shifts entity state. The prior the mode to results. gap about client tip following stick or mouse refers to position tracking, not tool activation.\n\nThe client `use` flag is sent in the same input packet as `place`, so it reaches the host without a separate test gap. The diff only verifies checklist items, not a weakened","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-22b6bad0-b146-4db9-8c24-5b1b4e8d7035-43","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node tests/run.mjs hands","description":"Run hand, dev-mode, and session tests","block_until_ms":60000}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1465,"output_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":98688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"523a4b2a-fa81-4048-b48b-7b45ed9e9dcd"}
