{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_620","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"34 hands tests passed.Running hands tests as a quick spot-check.\n\nThree prior gaps are fixed in source and bundled HTML. Client hand tests confirm predictLocal movement and host placement reaching the simulation. Idle pad input drains the pool correctly. Dev mode input path passes.\n\nTests passed with 151 successes. Now investigating a subtle pad-input bug where stick noise near menu edges could falsely trigger device-to-pad mapping.\n\nDrift easing tests passed. Host mouse aim using ctx.camera.rayAt is accepted as a prior gap. A potential real bug in applySnap is being re-examined.\n\nThe `button()` function is safe because `buttonsDown` requires values above 0.4, and analog rest values stay below that threshold. The fixes look solid. Now examining a potential bug in the INPUT PATH mouse test.\n\nThe applySnap device routing logic is verified. Mouse inputs flow correctly to seatInput. Idle pad zero values are ignored when the device is mouse. Drive seat defaults to 0 and KeyE\n\nThe mouse test sets swaps it in partner a horizontal delta  operations.and holds MouseLeft. The `wasPressed` check reads from the pressed set, so the button state must be verified.\n\nThe seat routing logic for mouse and drive seats is confirmed correct. The SESSION client test where a pad defaults to mouse also passes.\n\nThe old bug was that `fixedUpdate` always fed pad inputs to a seat when any pad was connected, dropping human input. The fix keeps the device as mouse once the pointer stops moving, because `isDown` remains true while `wasPressed` becomes false. The test would fail on the old code since the default device is 'pad'.\n\nAnother potential bug was examined: `fixedUpdate` returns early when a session exists, which would leave client prediction in `update()` alone. The test proves `update()` moves the\n\nThe test intentionally hand, and the real  includes a mouse deltaengine must call it  on the first frame every frame. This isso the device switches acceptable architecture. from the default pad to mouse. Without that initial movement, the seat would remain on idle pad and fail to drain. Once the pointer stops moving, the idle pad produces no input, so the device stays mouse and the seat continues draining.\n\nThe engine lifecycle is standard: both fixed and variable update steps are called each frame. Dev mode live sliders were accepted in the prior round and will not be re-checked unless a defect appears.\n\nThe mouse test asserts the device stays 'mouse', which would catch any regression that incorrectly reverts to pad whenever a pad is connected. I will run it to confirm it passes. The AIHub global leak concern is resolved because\n\nSpawn pool tests confirm testSessionHands cleans up after itself, and spawned entities are fixedUpdate checks the local session rather usable. HUD view stats than a global AIHub. fit within the visible Clinic update also correctly skips pullSession window. The jump list when no session exists. contains four stages.\n\nChecking that the bundled HTML matches the source by grepping for a distinctive line in `applySnap`. The client hand follows the mouse through `predictSeat` updates to simulation seats, and the view reads from those same seats. Unit tests verify the simulation seats directly.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2117ffc3-f3c0-4dae-a14a-b5ec3b8f97f3-41","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hypot\\(dx, dz\\) > 1|idle pad yields","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/work/The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2117ffc3-f3c0-4dae-a14a-b5ec3b8f97f3-42","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node tests/run.mjs hands","description":"Run the new hand and dev-mode tests","block_until_ms":60000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4549,"output_tokens":1202,"cache_read_input_tokens":93440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"09d13439-0116-4409-a64b-e04feb574de6"}
