{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_626","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51efbe34-b81b-422a-91d8-7dcce631e570-46","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-verdict-9c48352445aa-2-2.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"tests/run.mjs hands: 34 passed, 0 failed; clinic.js:327-330 and :439-469 plus session.js:69-101 and :212 drive idle-pad yield, client predict, host place, and Dev Mode jump/spawn/frame-step, also present in the root HTML.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Not refuted. All three prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules, covered by tests that call those modules, and present in the root HTML bundle.\\n\\n- Idle pad: `seatInput` returns `humanInput` for the drive seat unless the last device is `pad` (`clinic.js:327-330`). `samplePad` sets `any` only for a live stick or button, so a connected idle pad does not steal `device`. `testHandsOnInput` stubs `getGamepads` with a zeroed pad, aims with the mouse, and asserts the Op 1 pool shrinks while `device` stays `mouse`; WASD still moves the seat with `device === 'key'`.\\n- Session hands: `fixedUpdate` still returns when a session exists, but `pullSession` keeps aimed `x`/`z` (`clinic.js:439-457`) and `predictLocal` steps the local seat (`clinic.js:464-469`, `op.js:361-364`). Host `hostInputs` merges `state.local` over the net packet and `step` applies `place` (`session.js:93-101`, `:212`). `applySnap` eases only the local seat, and only when the error is greater than 1 (`session.js:69-88`). `testSessionHands` checks host place reaches the sim, the client tip follows mouse and KeyD, and large versus small snap drift.\\n- Dev Mode: jump cycles op/stage/scene and starts a stage or `rounds` (`clinic.js:299-311`, `:765-782`). Actions spawn pool, bleeder, laceration (as wound), hook, and introit (`clinic.js:26-37`, `op.js:1123-1131`). View lists frame step, FPS, and sim stats and `frameStep` advances `sim.t` (`clinic.js:283-292`, `:335-339`). The input-path test opens Dev Mode from pause and drives those rows with keys. The VIEW tab is drawn by `hud.js:206-217`.\\n\\n`node tests/run.mjs hands` printed `34 passed, 0 failed`. That matches the captured default log rising from 117 to `151 passed, 0 failed` in the implementer `tests.txt`. The same `lastIsPad`, spawn, frame-step, and `predictSeat` strings are in the root HTML.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-51efbe34-b81b-422a-91d8-7dcce631e570-47","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-classifier-9c48352445aa-2-skeptic-2.md","content":"Not refuted. All three prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules, covered by tests that call those modules, and present in the root HTML bundle.\n\n- Idle pad: `seatInput` returns `humanInput` for the drive seat unless the last device is `pad` (`clinic.js:327-330`). `samplePad` sets `any` only for a live stick or button, so a connected idle pad does not steal `device`. `testHandsOnInput` stubs `getGamepads` with a zeroed pad, aims with the mouse, and asserts the Op 1 pool shrinks while `device` stays `mouse`; WASD still moves the seat with `device === 'key'`.\n- Session hands: `fixedUpdate` still returns when a session exists, but `pullSession` keeps aimed `x`/`z` (`clinic.js:439-457`) and `predictLocal` steps the local seat (`clinic.js:464-469`, `op.js:361-364`). Host `hostInputs` merges `state.local` over the net packet and `step` applies `place` (`session.js:93-101`, `:212`). `applySnap` eases only the local seat, and only when the error is greater than 1 (`session.js:69-88`). `testSessionHands` checks host place reaches the sim, the client tip follows mouse and KeyD, and large versus small snap drift.\n- Dev Mode: jump cycles op/stage/scene and starts a stage or `rounds` (`clinic.js:299-311`, `:765-782`). Actions spawn pool, bleeder, laceration (as wound), hook, and introit (`clinic.js:26-37`, `op.js:1123-1131`). View lists frame step, FPS, and sim stats and `frameStep` advances `sim.t` (`clinic.js:283-292`, `:335-339`). The input-path test opens Dev Mode from pause and drives those rows with keys. The VIEW tab is drawn by `hud.js:206-217`.\n\n`node tests/run.mjs hands` printed `34 passed, 0 failed`. That matches the captured default log rising from 117 to `151 passed, 0 failed` in the implementer `tests.txt`. The same `lastIsPad`, spawn, frame-step, and `predictSeat` strings are in the root HTML.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":243,"output_tokens":3934,"cache_read_input_tokens":101376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"4580026d-0f36-42db-84f5-dbf73aba2cd1"}
