{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_629","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"tests.txt is 12 seconds newer than run.\n\nThe timing is consistent with editing tests before running the suite. A full suite of 151 tests including a campaign playthrough could finish in about 12 seconds if the simulation runs quickly in Node.js. Clinic.js was created at 01:53, and tests were written at 02:03.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The three prior gaps are fixed in the shipped clinic and session code, and the new tests that drive those paths pass. I'll record that verdict."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c9d2a221-aa2c-42f2-868b-caa2a59111bd-48","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-verdict-9c48352445aa-2-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"node tests/run.mjs hands → 34 passed, 0 failed; implementer tests.txt is 151 passed (117+34) and newer than clinic.js/session.js; bundle and root HTML contain lastIsPad, predictSeat, jumpKind, and the 0.35 snap ease.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Not refuted. All three prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules and in the root HTML bundle, and the new tests drive those paths.\\n\\n- **Idle pad vs last device** (`src/game/clinic.js:320-332`, `src/input/devices.js:78`). `seatInput` returns `humanInput` when the drive seat's last device is not a pad. `sampleAll` sets `any` only for a stick past the deadzone or a button, so a connected idle pad does not flip `device`. `testHands` / `testHandsOnInput` drain pool `p1` and move the seat with mouse and KeyD while `getGamepads` returns a zeroed pad, and assert `device` stays `mouse` or `key`.\\n- **Session hands** (`src/game/clinic.js:439-469`, `src/net/session.js:69-101`). `fixedUpdate` still returns when a session exists, but `update` copies aimed `x`/`z` in `pullSession` and `predictSeat` moves the local seat. The host merges `state.local` over the net input and `step` applies `place`. `applySnap` only eases the local seat when the error is greater than 1. `testSessionHands` checks host place-aim, the client mouse tip, the place packet, large-drift ease, and a small snap that does not yank the tip.\\n- **Dev Mode** (`src/game/clinic.js:279-340`, `743-783`, `src/ui/hud.js:206-217`). Jump cycles ops, stages, and story scenes. Actions spawn pool, bleeder, laceration (as `wound`), hook, and strain `introit`. View has frame step, FPS, and sim stats, and the HUD draws those rows. Both the direct `pickDev` path and the pause-menu input path assert stage 1, scene `rounds`, the five spawns, and `sim.t` advancing.\\n\\n`node tests/run.mjs hands` printed `34 passed, 0 failed`. That is the whole delta from the previous 117 to the captured `151 passed, 0 failed` line, written after `tests/run.mjs`. No plan criterion was weakened.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c9d2a221-aa2c-42f2-868b-caa2a59111bd-49","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-224040__x24ebb3/tmp/grok-goal-9c48352445aa/goal-classifier-9c48352445aa-2-skeptic-1.md","content":"Not refuted. All three prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules and in the root HTML bundle, and the new tests drive those paths.\n\n- **Idle pad vs last device** (`src/game/clinic.js:320-332`, `src/input/devices.js:78`). `seatInput` returns `humanInput` when the drive seat's last device is not a pad. `sampleAll` sets `any` only for a stick past the deadzone or a button, so a connected idle pad does not flip `device`. `testHands` / `testHandsOnInput` drain pool `p1` and move the seat with mouse and KeyD while `getGamepads` returns a zeroed pad, and assert `device` stays `mouse` or `key`.\n- **Session hands** (`src/game/clinic.js:439-469`, `src/net/session.js:69-101`). `fixedUpdate` still returns when a session exists, but `update` copies aimed `x`/`z` in `pullSession` and `predictSeat` moves the local seat. The host merges `state.local` over the net input and `step` applies `place`. `applySnap` only eases the local seat when the error is greater than 1. `testSessionHands` checks host place-aim, the client mouse tip, the place packet, large-drift ease, and a small snap that does not yank the tip.\n- **Dev Mode** (`src/game/clinic.js:279-340`, `743-783`, `src/ui/hud.js:206-217`). Jump cycles ops, stages, and story scenes. Actions spawn pool, bleeder, laceration (as `wound`), hook, and strain `introit`. View has frame step, FPS, and sim stats, and the HUD draws those rows. Both the direct `pickDev` path and the pause-menu input path assert stage 1, scene `rounds`, the five spawns, and `sim.t` advancing.\n\n`node tests/run.mjs hands` printed `34 passed, 0 failed`. That is the whole delta from the previous 117 to the captured `151 passed, 0 failed` line, written after `tests/run.mjs`. No plan criterion was weakened.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":216,"output_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":111104,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d19-7772-a082-6fbf4c1e0ec4","uuid":"ad1c2c4b-09c9-4b47-978c-0ac57d760b57"}
