{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_633","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game is a single HTML file that runs in a browser.\n\nThe game is \"The Second Opinion Clinic\", a surgical action title inspired by Trauma Center: Second Opinion. It runs from a local HTML file using keyboard or mouse controls.\n\nThe HTML filename is long and includes a date stamp. It requires a browser with WebGPU support.\n\nPress Enter, click, or the X button on the title screen to choose On Call for the story or Consult for local co-op. Move tools with the mouse, WASD, or left stick. Use left click, J, or R2 to activate them. Pick tools with 1–8 or the right stick. Press Esc or Options to pause; Dev Mode is there too.\n\nThe title is a first-person surgical drama with story operations, couch co-op, and AI Hub multiplayer.\n\nThe title sentence is trimmed to 22 words. The third bullet is being shortened to keep the total under 80.\n\nThe final draft is 70 words. The title sentence is 16 words. The three bullets are 8, 22, and 24 words.\n\nThe file is in the work folder root, not inside a subfolder. The response will use only three bullets plus the lead sentence, omitting any preamble.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The Second Opinion Clinic is a playable single-file browser game: timed surgery, a hospital story, and co-op for up to four players.\n\n- Open `The-Second-Opinion-Clinic-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-224040.html` in a browser with WebGPU.\n- Press Enter, click, or Cross on the title, then choose On Call for the story or Consult for local co-op.\n- Aim with the mouse, WASD, or the left stick; operate with left click, J, or R2. Esc or Options pauses into Dev Mode."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1609,"output_tokens":2993,"cache_read_input_tokens":35584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa39-3d